               |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `nonParameterMappings` | `Record<string, MappingValue>` |         | Properties set without a parameter. See Set properties without a parameter. |","table":"table-6"},"1262":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-68","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option                  | Type                                     | Default | Description                                                             |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `actionLevelValidation` | `Array<{ condition; displayMetadata? }>` |         | Conditions that must all pass to submit the action. See Who can submit. |","table":"table-6"},"1263":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-69","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option              | Type            | Default                                                          | Description                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameterOrdering` | `Array<string>` | Configured parameters first, then properties in definition order | The form's parameter order. Must list every parameter; the chosen-object parameter is added first if you leave it out. |","table":"table-6"},"1264":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-70","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option     | Type                   | Default | Description                                             |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sections` | `Array<ActionSection>` |         | Group parameters into form sections. See Form sections. |","table":"table-6"},"1265":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-71","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option          | Type                | Default | Description                |\n| --------------- | ------------------- | ------- | -------------------------- |\n| `defaultFormat` | `\"FORM\" \\| \"TABLE\"` |         | The form's default layout. |","table":"table-6"},"1266":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-72","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option               | Type      | Default | Description                                      |\n| -------------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `enableLayoutSwitch` | `boolean` |         | Let users switch between form and table layouts. |","table":"table-6"},"1267":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-73","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option               | Type                                                   | Default | Description                    |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `tableConfiguration` | `{ columnWidthByParameterRid; enableFileImport; ... }` |         | Settings for the table layout. |","table":"table-6"},"1268":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-74","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option               | Type                                                                                          | Default | Description                                                |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `submissionMetadata` | `{ successMessage: string; submitButtonDisplayMetadata?; undoButtonConfiguration?: boolean }` |         | The submit button and the message shown after it succeeds. |","table":"table-6"},"1269":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-75","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option | Type                                        | Default | Description        |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------ |\n| `icon` | `{ locator: BlueprintIcon; color: string }` |         | The action's icon. |","table":"table-6"},"1270":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-76","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"| Option       | Type                                                                                    | Default | Description                          |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `permission` | `\"roles\" \\| \"publicProject\" \\| { type: \"ontologyPackage\"; ontologyPackageRid: string }` |         | The permission model for the action. |","table":"table-6"},"1271":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-77","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#helper-options","content":"`defineDeleteObjectAction` reads only `objectType`, `apiName`, `displayName`, `description`, `status`, `actionLevelValidation`, `icon`, and `permission`."},"1272":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-78","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"`parameterConfiguration` is keyed by parameter ID, which for property parameters is the property's API name. A key that is not a property adds a new parameter, and needs `customParameterType`."},"1273":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-79","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option        | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` | The parameter's label. Defaults to the property's display name. |","table":"table-7"},"1274":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-80","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option        | Type     | Description                    |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `description` | `string` | Help text under the parameter. |","table":"table-7"},"1275":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-81","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option     | Type                                                        | Description                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `required` | `boolean \\| { listLength: { min?: number; max?: number } }` | Whether a value is required. Defaults to `true` when the property sets `nullability.noNulls`, and for arrays to a minimum length of 1 when it sets `noEmptyCollections`. |","table":"table-7"},"1276":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-82","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option          | Type            | Description                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| --------------- | --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `allowedValues` | `AllowedValues` | The values the parameter accepts, such as `{ type: \"oneOf\", oneOf }`, `{ type: \"range\", min?, max? }`, or `{ type: \"text\", minLength?, maxLength?, regex? }`. Defaults to what the property type allows. |","table":"table-7"},"1277":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-83","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option         | Type                         | Description        |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `defaultValue` | `OntologyIrParameterPrefill` | A prefilled value. |","table":"table-7"},"1278":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-84","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option              | Type                                   | Description               |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `defaultVisibility` | `\"editable\" \\| \"disabled\" \\| \"hidden\"` | How the parameter starts. |","table":"table-7"},"1279":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-85","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option                 | Type                         | Description                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `conditionalOverrides` | `Array<ConditionalOverride>` | Change the visibility, whether a value is required, the default, or the allowed values when a condition passes. |","table":"table-7"},"1280":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-86","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option       | Type                  | Description                 |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `renderHint` | `ParameterRenderHint` | Which input control to use. |","table":"table-7"},"1281":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-87","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option                   | Type                                       | Description                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `structFieldValidations` | `Record<string, StructFieldConfiguration>` | For struct parameters, per-field settings, including `defaultValue`. Set a field's `defaultValue` to `null` to turn off the default that modify helpers infer. |","table":"table-7"},"1282":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-88","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Option                | Type                  | Description                                                                            |\n| --------------------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `customParameterType` | `ActionParameterType` | The type of a parameter that is not a property, such as `\"string\"` or `\"booleanList\"`. |","table":"table-7"},"1283":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-89","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"A conditional override is one of:"},"1284":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-90","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Override                                   | Effect when `condition` passes                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"visibility\", condition, then? }` | Sets visibility to `then`: `\"editable\"`, `\"disabled\"`, or `\"hidden\"`. |","table":"table-8"},"1285":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-91","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Override                                 | Effect when `condition` passes |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"disabled\", condition, then? }` | Disables the parameter.        |","table":"table-8"},"1286":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-92","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Override                          | Effect when `condition` passes |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"required\", condition }` | Makes the parameter required.  |","table":"table-8"},"1287":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-93","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Override                                            | Effect when `condition` passes |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"defaultValue\", condition, defaultValue }` | Uses a different default.      |","table":"table-8"},"1288":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-94","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#configure-parameters","content":"| Override                                        | Effect when `condition` passes |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"constraint\", condition, constraint }` | Uses different allowed values. |","table":"table-8"},"1289":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-95","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#conditions","content":"Validation rules and overrides take a `ConditionDefinition`:"},"1290":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-96","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#conditions","content":"| Condition                 | Passes when                                                                          |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"group\", name }` | The user is in the group chosen for the input `name` when the ontology is installed. |","table":"table-9"},"1291":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-97","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#conditions","content":"| Condition                                     | Passes when                                                                                                                        |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"parameter\", parameterId, matches }` | The parameter's value equals `matches`, such as `{ type: \"staticValue\", staticValue: { type: \"string\", string: \"Engineering\" } }`. |","table":"table-9"},"1292":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-98","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#conditions","content":"| Condition                             | Passes when                      |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"and\" \\| \"or\", conditions }` | All or any of `conditions` pass. |","table":"table-9"},"1293":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-99","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#who-can-submit","content":"`actionLevelValidation` is a list of rules that must all pass before a user can submit. `displayMetadata.failureMessage` is shown when a rule fails."},"1294":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-100","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#who-can-submit","content":"This action can only be submitted by members of the HR group, shows `skills` only when the department is Engineering, limits `department` to two values, and records who made the edit:"},"1295":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-101","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"`nonParameterMappings` sets a property from something other than user input. The property gets no parameter."},"1296":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-102","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"| Value                     | Sets the property to                       |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"currentUser\" }` | The ID of the user who submits the action. |","table":"table-10"},"1297":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-103","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"| Value                     | Sets the property to              |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"currentTime\" }` | The time the action is submitted. |","table":"table-10"},"1298":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-104","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"| Value                       | Sets the property to                                            |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"uuid\", linkId? }` | A new UUID. Properties that share a `linkId` get the same UUID. |","table":"table-10"},"1299":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-105","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"| Value                                  | Sets the property to |\n| -------------------------------------- | -------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"staticValue\", staticValue }` | A fixed value.       |","table":"table-10"},"1300":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-106","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#set-properties-without-a-parameter","content":"| Value                                  | Sets the property to                                        |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"parameterId\", parameterId }` | The value of another parameter, such as a custom parameter. |","table":"table-10"},"1301":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-107","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#form-sections","content":"Each entry in `sections` has an `id`, a `displayName`, and the `parameters` it holds, plus optional `description`, `defaultVisibility` (`\"visible\"` or `\"hidden\"`), `columnCount` (`1` or `2`), `showTitleBar`, `collapsedByDefault`, `style` (`\"box\"` or `\"minimal\"`), and `conditionalOverrides`."},"1302":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-108","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#define-an-action-from-rules","content":"`defineAction` takes the parameters and logic rules directly, for actions the helpers do not cover. The rules use the Ontology IR rule types, such as `addObjectRule`, `modifyObjectRule`, `deleteObjectRule`, `addOrModifyObjectRuleV2`, and `addInterfaceRule`."},"1303":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions-109","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/links-and-actions#define-an-action-from-rules","content":"`defineAction` throws when there are no rules, when parameter IDs repeat, or when a rule or section references a parameter that is not defined."},"1304":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"page","content":"Local development","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Ontology as code"],"tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development"},"1305":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-0","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","content":"Use @osdk/vite-plugin-oac to compile your ontology, generate an SDK, and serve a seeded mock Foundry API from the Vite dev server."},"1306":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-1","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"1307":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-2","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#requirements","content":"Requirements"},"1308":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-3","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#install","content":"Install"},"1309":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-4","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"Configure Vite"},"1310":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-5","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data","content":"Seed data"},"1311":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-6","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"Connect your app"},"1312":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-7","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"Limitations"},"1313":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-8","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"Seed data for the local Ontology server"},"1314":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-9","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","content":"`@osdk/vite-plugin-oac` lets you build an app against your ontology-as-code definitions before they exist in Foundry. On every change to `.ontology/`, it compiles the ontology again, regenerates an SDK into `.osdk/src`, and answers OSDK requests from the Vite dev server with data from a seed file."},"1315":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-10","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","content":"In `@osdk/vite-plugin-oac` 0.85.0, the step that converts the IR to Ontology metadata reads a `blockData` key, but `@osdk/maker` 0.82.0 writes the IR under `ontology`. The conversion fails with `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'interfaceTypes')`, so no SDK is generated and the mock serves no types. Check the changelog for a fix before you adopt the plugin."},"1316":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-11","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Step                    | Tool                                            | Output                                      |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| 1. Compile the ontology | `pnpm exec maker -i <ontologyDir>/ontology.mts` | `node_modules/.osdk/.oac/.ontology.ir.json` |","table":"table-0"},"1317":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-12","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Step                                   | Tool                                    | Output                                   |\n| -------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| 2. Convert the IR to Ontology metadata | `@osdk/generator-converters.ontologyir` | `node_modules/.osdk/.oac/.ontology.json` |","table":"table-0"},"1318":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-13","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Step               | Tool                                          | Output                                       |\n| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| 3. Generate an SDK | `pnpm exec osdk unstable typescript generate` | `.osdk/src`, then `pnpm exec tsc` in `.osdk` |","table":"table-0"},"1319":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-14","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Step                                | Tool         | Output                                                           |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 4. Start the mock (dev server only) | `@osdk/faux` | Ontology metadata and `seed.ts` data, served from the dev server |","table":"table-0"},"1320":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-15","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"The plugin writes the SDK to a temporary directory first, then copies only the files whose contents changed into `.osdk/src` and deletes files that are no longer generated."},"1321":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-16","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Command             | What runs                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `vite` (dev server) | All four steps before the server starts, then all four again on every add, change, or delete under the ontology directory. After each successful run, the browser does a full reload. Failures are logged, and the server keeps running. |","table":"table-1"},"1322":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-17","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#how-it-works","content":"| Command      | What runs                                                                                 |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `vite build` | Steps 1 to 3 in the `buildStart` hook. The build fails if any step fails. No mock server. |","table":"table-1"},"1323":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-18","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#requirements","content":"**pnpm.** The plugin runs `maker`, `osdk`, and `tsc` with `pnpm exec`, so pnpm must be on your `PATH` and each binary must be installed in your project."},"1324":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-19","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#requirements","content":"**Vite** and a Node.js version that can import `.mts` files natively: 22.18 or later, or 23.6 or later."},"1325":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-20","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#requirements","content":"**A `tsconfig.json` in `.osdk`.** After generating, the plugin runs `tsc` with `.osdk` as the working directory and fails if it exits with an error."},"1326":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-21","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#install","content":"The app itself needs `@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api`, which the generated SDK imports, plus `@osdk/react` if you use React. `@osdk/faux` is only needed for the seed file's types."},"1327":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-22","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"Add `ontologyAsCode` to your Vite config:"},"1328":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-23","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"Pass `ontologyDir` as an absolute path: the plugin ignores a changed file unless its path starts with `ontologyDir`, and Vite's watcher reports absolute paths. The `resolve.alias` entry is one way to import the generated SDK as `@my-app/sdk`; add a matching `paths` entry to your app's `tsconfig.json` so TypeScript resolves it too."},"1329":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-24","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                    |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ontologyDir` | `string` |         | Required. The directory that holds `ontology.mts` and `seed.ts`. Created if it does not exist. |","table":"table-2"},"1330":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-25","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"| Option        | Type                                     | Default  | Description                                                            |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `loggerLevel` | `\"debug\" \\| \"info\" \\| \"warn\" \\| \"error\"` | `\"info\"` | The lowest level the plugin logs. Messages are prefixed with `[osdk]`. |","table":"table-2"},"1331":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-26","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"| Option          | Type                                        | Default | Description                                                                                                                         |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hooks.preSeed` | `(ontology: FauxOntology) => Promise<void>` |         | Runs after the plugin registers the generated metadata with the mock and before it applies the seed. Errors are logged and ignored. |","table":"table-2"},"1332":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-27","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"Create `.osdk/tsconfig.json` for the `tsc` step. The generated code uses ES module imports with `.js` extensions:"},"1333":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-28","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#configure-vite","content":"Add `.osdk/src` to `.gitignore`, or commit it so the app builds without running the plugin. Do not edit it by hand."},"1334":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-29","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data","content":"The mock starts empty. The plugin loads `seed.ts` from the ontology directory after every regeneration and calls its default export with the mock's `FauxFoundry`. The file is required: without it, each regeneration logs an error and the browser does not reload."},"1335":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-30","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data","content":"`registerObject` takes the object's API name in `__apiName`, its primary key in `__primaryKey`, and property values in their wire format, such as ISO 8601 strings for dates. `registerLink(source, linkName, target, reverseLinkName)` takes both sides' link names and sets the foreign key for you, so this seed sets Ada's `officeId` to `\"lon\"` and her `leadId` to `2`."},"1336":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-31","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data","content":"Every regeneration rebuilds the mock from the seed, so edits made through actions last only until the next change to `.ontology/`."},"1337":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-32","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"The mock answers on the dev server's own origin, and passes any request it does not handle on to Vite. Create the client with the dev server's origin, the mock's Ontology RID, and the token the mock accepts:"},"1338":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-33","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"| Value                    | Why                                       |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `window.location.origin` | The mock runs inside the Vite dev server. |","table":"table-3"},"1339":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-34","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"| Value                                                            | Why                                                                                                                                   |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ri.ontology.main.ontology.00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000` | The RID of the mock's only ontology. Do not use the generated SDK's `$ontologyRid`; a locally generated SDK sets it to a placeholder. |","table":"table-3"},"1340":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-35","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"| Value             | Why                                                 |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"myAccessToken\"` | The mock rejects any other bearer token with `401`. |","table":"table-3"},"1341":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-36","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"From there, use the client as you would against Foundry. With `@osdk/react`, pass it to `OsdkProvider` and query the generated types:"},"1342":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-37","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#connect-your-app","content":"See Create a client for `OsdkProvider`, and Load objects for the hooks."},"1343":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-38","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"The mock is an approximation of Foundry built from the generated metadata."},"1344":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-39","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"| Area    | Behavior                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Actions | Create, modify, and delete object rules work. Add and delete link rules are only partly supported. Interface create, modify, and delete rules throw `not implemented`. |","table":"table-4"},"1345":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-40","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"| Area                 | Behavior                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Numeric primary keys | The mock accepts an object parameter only as a string, while the client sends the primary key as it is. Modify and delete actions on object types with numeric primary keys, such as `employeeId`, fail validation with `INVALID`. Use string primary keys for types you edit locally. |","table":"table-4"},"1346":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-41","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"| Area       | Behavior                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Interfaces | Only shared-property-type properties reach the generated SDK and the mock, every interface property is optional, and object types do not record which interfaces they implement. Interface-defined properties are missing. |","table":"table-4"},"1347":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-42","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"| Area      | Behavior                                                                  |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Functions | The generated metadata has no queries, so there are no functions to call. |","table":"table-4"},"1348":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-43","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#limitations","content":"| Area              | Behavior                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Schema migrations | The plugin runs `maker` without `--write-locks`. If an interface uses schema migrations, commit an up-to-date `ontology-schema-lock.json` or compilation fails. |","table":"table-4"},"1349":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-44","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"`@osdk/seed-helpers` and `@osdk/seed-compiler` build seed data for a different local server: the Ontology server that `@osdk/integration-testing` starts, which loads seed JSON into SQLite. They do not seed the Vite plugin's mock. To use them in tests, see Integration testing."},"1350":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-45","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"`seed-compiler` merges a directory of seed files into one JSON file:"},"1351":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-46","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"| Option       | Description                                                                                                 |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--metadata` | Required. The `ontology-metadata.json` that the SDK generator writes with `--experimentalOntologyMetadata`. |","table":"table-5"},"1352":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-47","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"| Option       | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--seed-dir` | Required. A directory of seed files. Every top-level `.mts` file whose name does not start with `$` is loaded, in file name order. |","table":"table-5"},"1353":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-48","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"| Option           | Description                               |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `-o`, `--output` | Required. Where to write the merged JSON. |","table":"table-5"},"1354":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development-49","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/local-development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/local-development#seed-data-for-the-local-ontology-server","content":"Each seed file default-exports the result of `createSeedWithMetadata` from `@osdk/seed-helpers`, or its `output`. All files are merged through one builder, so primary keys must be unique across the whole directory, and a link can reference objects created in any file:"},"1355":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"page","content":"Object types","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Ontology as code"],"tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types"},"1356":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-0","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","content":"Define object types with defineObject from @osdk/maker, including property types, primary keys, titles, value types, and datasources."},"1357":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-1","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"Define an object type"},"1358":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-2","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#primary-key-and-title","content":"Primary key and title"},"1359":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-3","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#properties","content":"Properties"},"1360":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-4","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"Property types"},"1361":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-5","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#struct-properties","content":"Struct properties"},"1362":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-6","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"Value types"},"1363":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-7","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#status","content":"Status"},"1364":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-8","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"Datasources"},"1365":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-9","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"Property security"},"1366":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-10","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"Derived properties"},"1367":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-11","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","content":"An object type describes one kind of thing in your ontology, such as an employee or an office: its properties, which property identifies each object, and where its data comes from. Define one with `defineObject` from `@osdk/maker` in your `.ontology/ontology.mts` file."},"1368":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-12","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"`defineObject` registers the type and returns its definition with the namespaced API name, so `employee.apiName` is `com.example.Employee` when you compile with `--apiNamespace com.example`. Pass the returned value wherever another definition needs the object type, such as a link or an action."},"1369":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-13","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                    |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `apiName` | `string` |         | Required. The API name, without the namespace. |","table":"table-0"},"1370":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-14","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                                   |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` |         | Required. The singular name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-0"},"1371":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-15","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option              | Type     | Default | Description                                 |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `pluralDisplayName` | `string` |         | Required. The plural name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-0"},"1372":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-16","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option                      | Type     | Default | Description                                                |\n| --------------------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `primaryKeyPropertyApiName` | `string` |         | Required. The property whose value identifies each object. |","table":"table-0"},"1373":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-17","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option                 | Type     | Default | Description                                          |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `titlePropertyApiName` | `string` |         | Required. The property shown as each object's title. |","table":"table-0"},"1374":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-18","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option       | Type                                 | Default | Description                                        |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------ | ------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `properties` | `Record<string, PropertyDefinition>` |         | The properties, keyed by API name. See Properties. |","table":"table-0"},"1375":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-19","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` |         | A description shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-0"},"1376":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-20","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#define-an-object-type","content":"| Option | Type                               