 with options."},"1406":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-50","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type    | Value       | Notes |\n| ------- | ----------- | ----- |\n| Boolean | `\"boolean\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1407":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-51","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type     | Value                                      | Notes |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------ | ----- |\n| Integers | `\"byte\"`, `\"short\"`, `\"integer\"`, `\"long\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1408":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-52","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type     | Value                              | Notes                                                                                                         |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Decimals | `\"float\"`, `\"double\"`, `\"decimal\"` | `{ type: \"decimal\", precision?: number, scale?: number }` sets precision and scale, which default to 5 and 2. |","table":"table-2"},"1409":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-53","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type   | Value      | Notes                                                     |\n| ------ | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| String | `\"string\"` | `{ type: \"string\", ... }` sets search options; see below. |","table":"table-2"},"1410":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-54","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type          | Value                   | Notes |\n| ------------- | ----------------------- | ----- |\n| Date and time | `\"date\"`, `\"timestamp\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1411":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-55","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type       | Value          | Notes |\n| ---------- | -------------- | ----- |\n| Attachment | `\"attachment\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1412":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-56","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type       | Value                      | Notes |\n| ---------- | -------------------------- | ----- |\n| Geospatial | `\"geopoint\"`, `\"geoshape\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1413":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-57","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type  | Value              | Notes                                                             |\n| ----- | ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Media | `\"mediaReference\"` | Each `mediaReference` property gets its own media set datasource. |","table":"table-2"},"1414":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-58","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type        | Value             | Notes |\n| ----------- | ----------------- | ----- |\n| Time series | `\"geotimeSeries\"` |       |","table":"table-2"},"1415":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-59","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type    | Value                                                                                    | Notes                                                                                  |\n| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Marking | `{ type: \"marking\", markingType: \"MANDATORY\" \\| \"CBAC\", markingInputGroupName: string }` | `markingInputGroupName` names the marking input chosen when the ontology is installed. |","table":"table-2"},"1416":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-60","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type   | Value                                              | Notes                  |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Struct | `{ type: \"struct\", structDefinition, mainValue? }` | See Struct properties. |","table":"table-2"},"1417":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-61","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"| Type   | Value                                                                                       | Notes                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Vector | `{ type: \"vector\", dimension: number, supportsSearchWith, embeddingModel?, quantization? }` | `supportsSearchWith` is `\"COSINE_SIMILARITY\"`, `\"DOT_PRODUCT\"`, or `\"EUCLIDEAN_DISTANCE\"`. `dimension` must be an integer of at least 1, and a vector property cannot be an array. |","table":"table-2"},"1418":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-62","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-types","content":"The object form of `string` accepts `isLongText`, `supportsEfficientLeadingWildcard`, `supportsExactMatching`, `supportsFullTextRegex`, `supportsPhonetic`, `enableAsciiFolding`, and `analyzerOverride`:"},"1419":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-63","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#struct-properties","content":"A struct property groups named fields into one value. Each field is a type name, or an object with `fieldType` and `displayMetadata`. Fields cannot be structs, markings, or vectors. `mainValue` names the field or fields that represent the struct when it is shown as a single value, such as a title."},"1420":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-64","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"A value type is a reusable, versioned type with constraints, such as \"a string that looks like an email address\". Define it with `defineValueType`, then reference it from a property with `valueType`. Value types are written to `value-types.json` as well as the IR."},"1421":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-65","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                          |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `apiName` | `string` |         | Required. The value type's API name. |","table":"table-3"},"1422":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-66","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                          |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `displayName` | `string` |         | Required. The name shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-3"},"1423":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-67","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option    | Type     | Default | Description                                                                                                      |\n| --------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `version` | `string` |         | Required. A semantic version. You can define several versions of the same API name; each version must be unique. |","table":"table-3"},"1424":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-68","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option | Type                     | Default | Description                                  |\n| ------ | ------------------------ | ------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `type` | `{ type, constraints? }` |         | Required. The base type and its constraints. |","table":"table-3"},"1425":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-69","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option        | Type     | Default | Description                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` |         | A description shown in Foundry. |","table":"table-3"},"1426":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-70","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option   | Type                                                                                         | Default    | Description          |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | -------------------- |\n| `status` | `\"active\" \\| { type: \"deprecated\"; message: string; deadline: string; replacedBy?: string }` | `\"active\"` | Deprecate a version. |","table":"table-3"},"1427":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-71","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"| Option            | Type      | Default | Description                                |\n| ----------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `namespacePrefix` | `boolean` | `false` | Prefix the API name with `--apiNamespace`. |","table":"table-3"},"1428":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-72","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#value-types","content":"`type.type` is one of `boolean`, `binary`, `byte`, `short`, `integer`, `long`, `float`, `double`, `decimal`, `string`, `date`, `timestamp`, `array`, `map`, `optional`, or `structV2`. Each entry in `constraints` has a `constraint` for that base type and an optional `failureMessage`. String constraints are `regex`, `oneOf`, `length`, `isUuid`, and `isRid`:"},"1429":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-73","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#status","content":"`status` is `\"active\"`, `\"experimental\"`, `\"example\"`, or `{ type: \"deprecated\", message, deadline }`, where `deadline` is an ISO 8601 date or date-time. An experimental, example, or deprecated object type can only contain properties with the same status, and a link to it must have a matching status. See Link status."},"1430":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-74","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"`datasources` says where property values come from. Without it, a dataset backs every property. Give an object type one base datasource (`dataset`, `stream`, `restrictedView`, or `direct`) plus any number of `derived` datasources; `defineObject` throws if you list more than one `dataset`, `stream`, or `restrictedView`. Properties not mapped by a `derived` datasource come from the base datasource."},"1431":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-75","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"| `type`      | Options                                            | Description                     |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `\"dataset\"` | `objectSecurityPolicy?`, `propertySecurityGroups?` | A dataset backs the properties. |","table":"table-4"},"1432":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-76","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"| `type`     | Options            | Description                                                                                 |\n| ---------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"stream\"` | `retentionPeriod?` | A stream backs the properties. `retentionPeriod` is an ISO 8601 duration, such as `\"P90D\"`. |","table":"table-4"},"1433":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-77","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"| `type`             | Options | Description                             |\n| ------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `\"restrictedView\"` |         | A restricted view backs the properties. |","table":"table-4"},"1434":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-78","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"| `type`     | Options                                            | Description                           |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `\"direct\"` | `objectSecurityPolicy?`, `propertySecurityGroups?` | A direct source backs the properties. |","table":"table-4"},"1435":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-79","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#datasources","content":"| `type`      | Options                             | Description                                                      |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"derived\"` | `linkDefinition`, `propertyMapping` | Properties computed from linked objects. See Derived properties. |","table":"table-4"},"1436":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-80","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"On `dataset` and `direct` datasources, `propertySecurityGroups` restricts who can read a set of properties, and `objectSecurityPolicy` restricts who can read the objects. Each takes a `name`, an optional `granularPolicy` condition, and optional `appliedMarkings` and `assumedMarkings` maps from a marking input name to `\"CBAC\"` or `\"MANDATORY\"`."},"1437":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-81","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"A `granularPolicy` condition is one of:"},"1438":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-82","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"| Condition                 | Passes when                                                                          |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"group\", name }` | The user is in the group chosen for the input `name` when the ontology is installed. |","table":"table-5"},"1439":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-83","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"| Condition                             | Passes when                                  |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"groupProperty\", property }` | The user is in a group listed in `property`. |","table":"table-5"},"1440":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-84","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"| Condition                               | Passes when                                                         |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"markingProperty\", property }` | The user satisfies the markings in the marking property `property`. |","table":"table-5"},"1441":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-85","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#property-security","content":"| Condition                             | Passes when                      |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"and\" \\| \"or\", conditions }` | All or any of `conditions` pass. |","table":"table-5"},"1442":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-86","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"A `derived` datasource computes properties from objects reached through one or more links. `linkDefinition` lists the links to follow in order, and `propertyMapping` maps each derived property to either a property on the linked object or an aggregation."},"1443":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-87","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"| Aggregation         | Derived property must be | Description                   |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"count\" }` | Any                      | The number of linked objects. |","table":"table-6"},"1444":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-88","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"| Aggregation                          | Derived property must be | Description                       |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------ | --------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"sum\" \\| \"avg\", property }` | Numeric                  | The sum or average of `property`. |","table":"table-6"},"1445":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-89","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"| Aggregation                          | Derived property must be | Description                                  |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"min\" \\| \"max\", property }` | Primitive                | The smallest or largest value of `property`. |","table":"table-6"},"1446":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-90","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"| Aggregation                                                          | Derived property must be | Description                                  |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"approximateCardinality\" \\| \"exactCardinality\", property }` | Primitive                | The number of distinct values of `property`. |","table":"table-6"},"1447":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-91","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"| Aggregation                                                | Derived property must be | Description                                      |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"collectList\" \\| \"collectSet\", property, limit }` | An array                 | Up to `limit` values of `property`, at most 100. |","table":"table-6"},"1448":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-92","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"Aggregations skip linked objects where the property is null. Generated create and create-or-modify actions leave derived properties out of their parameters."},"1449":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-93","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"The link must be defined before the object that uses it. When the object is not defined yet, refer to it from the link by its API name:"},"1450":{"id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types-94","page_id":"/ontology-as-code/object-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ontology-as-code/object-types#derived-properties","content":"When you compile with `--apiNamespace`, the string reference must include the namespace, such as `\"com.example.Office\"`."},"1451":{"id":"/overview","page_id":"/overview","type":"page","content":"What is OSDK","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/overview"},"1452":{"id":"/overview-0","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview","content":"The Ontology SDK gives TypeScript apps a typed client for your Foundry Ontology's objects, links, actions, functions, and interfaces."},"1453":{"id":"/overview-1","page_id":"/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"1454":{"id":"/overview-2","page_id":"/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/overview#packages","content":"Packages"},"1455":{"id":"/overview-3","page_id":"/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/overview#a-first-query","content":"A first query"},"1456":{"id":"/overview-4","page_id":"/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"Why use `@osdk/react`"},"1457":{"id":"/overview-5","page_id":"/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/overview#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1458":{"id":"/overview-6","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview","content":"The Ontology SDK (OSDK) lets you read and write your Foundry Ontology from TypeScript with types generated from your own object types, actions, and functions. Use it in browser apps, Node.js services, and scripts, and add `@osdk/react` to get cached, reactive hooks in React."},"1459":{"id":"/overview-7","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"You pick the Ontology resources your app needs in Developer Console, and Foundry generates an npm package for them, such as `@my-app/sdk`. The generated package contains typed definitions only. The runtime that sends requests, pages results, and applies actions lives in `@osdk/client`, and you pass definitions to it:"},"1460":{"id":"/overview-8","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"| Ontology concept | Generated export     | How you use it                                                                    |\n| ---------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object type      | `Employee`, `Office` | `client(Employee).where(...).fetchPage()`, or `useOsdkObjects(Employee)` in React |","table":"table-0"},"1461":{"id":"/overview-9","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"| Ontology concept | Generated export       | How you use it                                             |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Link type        | `$link` on each object | `employee.$link.office.fetchOne()`, or `useLinks` in React |","table":"table-0"},"1462":{"id":"/overview-10","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"| Ontology concept | Generated export | How you use it                                                                         |\n| ---------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Action type      | `modifyEmployee` | `client(modifyEmployee).applyAction(...)`, or `useOsdkAction(modifyEmployee)` in React |","table":"table-0"},"1463":{"id":"/overview-11","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"| Ontology concept | Generated export                | How you use it                                                       |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Function (query) | A function definition per query | `client(fn).executeFunction(...)`, or `useOsdkFunction(fn)` in React |","table":"table-0"},"1464":{"id":"/overview-12","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"| Ontology concept | Generated export             | How you use it                                                                     |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Interface        | One definition per interface | `client(MyInterface).fetchPage()` returns objects of every type that implements it |","table":"table-0"},"1465":{"id":"/overview-13","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"Because the SDK holds metadata rather than generated implementation code, its size grows with the number of types you include, unused definitions tree-shake away, and fixes to the client ship as a dependency bump without regenerating your SDK. The generated package also exports namespaces such as `$Objects`, `$Actions`, and `$Queries`, so `import * as Sdk from \"@my-app/sdk\"` gives you autocomplete over everything in it."},"1466":{"id":"/overview-14","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#how-it-works","content":"Dates and timestamps arrive as ISO 8601 strings. OSDK does not bundle a date library, so parse them with the one your app already uses."},"1467":{"id":"/overview-15","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package        | Role                                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `@osdk/client` | The runtime. `createClient` returns the `client` you call with definitions to fetch objects, follow links, apply actions, and execute functions. |","table":"table-1"},"1468":{"id":"/overview-16","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package     | Role                                                                                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/api` | Shared type definitions that `@osdk/client` and generated SDKs both depend on. Install it alongside `@osdk/client`. |","table":"table-1"},"1469":{"id":"/overview-17","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package                       | Role                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Generated SDK (`@my-app/sdk`) | Your Ontology's object types, interfaces, actions, and functions, generated in Developer Console and installed from your Foundry npm registry. |","table":"table-1"},"1470":{"id":"/overview-18","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package       | Role                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/oauth` | Token providers: `createPublicOauthClient` for browser apps, `createConfidentialOauthClient` for servers, `createAuthlessClient` for public apps. |","table":"table-1"},"1471":{"id":"/overview-19","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package       | Role                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/react` | `OsdkProvider` and hooks such as `useOsdkObjects`, `useOsdkObject`, `useLinks`, `useOsdkAction`, and `useOsdkFunction`, backed by a normalized cache. |","table":"table-1"},"1472":{"id":"/overview-20","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package                  | Role                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/react-components` | Ontology-aware React components, such as `ObjectTable`, `FilterList`, and `ActionForm`, built on `@osdk/react`. |","table":"table-1"},"1473":{"id":"/overview-21","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package            | Role                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/create-app` | A CLI that scaffolds a React, Vue, or Expo app with authentication, client setup, and your SDK already wired in. |","table":"table-1"},"1474":{"id":"/overview-22","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#packages","content":"| Package                | Role                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/react-devtools` | A development panel and Vite plugin for inspecting the queries, cache entries, and actions of a running `@osdk/react` app. |","table":"table-1"},"1475":{"id":"/overview-23","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#a-first-query","content":"Create a client once, then pass it a definition from your SDK. `createClient` takes the Foundry URL, your Ontology RID, and a token provider, here the OAuth client from `@osdk/oauth`:"},"1476":{"id":"/overview-24","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#a-first-query","content":"In React, wrap your app in `OsdkProvider` with the same client, and read the data with a hook. The hook loads the page, caches it, and re-renders the component when the objects change:"},"1477":{"id":"/overview-25","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#a-first-query","content":"See Create a client for `OsdkProvider` setup and the full `createClient` reference."},"1478":{"id":"/overview-26","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"You can call `@osdk/client` from any data layer, including TanStack Query. `@osdk/react` adds behavior that a generic request cache cannot reproduce because it understands Ontology objects:"},"1479":{"id":"/overview-27","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Normalized object cache.** Each object, such as `Employee:42`, is stored once. When it changes, every list, link, and detail view that contains it re-renders with the new values."},"1480":{"id":"/overview-28","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Deduplicated requests.** Components that ask for the same objects with the same options share one cache entry and one request."},"1481":{"id":"/overview-29","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Updates after actions.** An action's response lists the objects it added, modified, and deleted. The cache reloads those objects and re-evaluates affected lists against their `where` clauses, with no manual invalidation."},"1482":{"id":"/overview-30","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Optimistic updates with rollback.** Pass `$optimisticUpdate` to `applyAction` to show the expected result immediately. If the action fails, the cache restores the previous state."},"1483":{"id":"/overview-31","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Live data.** `streamUpdates: true` keeps a list current over a WebSocket subscription instead of polling."},"1484":{"id":"/overview-32","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"**Function dependencies.** `useOsdkFunction` reruns a function when objects it depends on change, using `dependsOn` for object types or `dependsOnObjects` for specific instances."},"1485":{"id":"/overview-33","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#why-use-osdkreact","content":"Use `@osdk/react` for Ontology data and keep a general-purpose library such as TanStack Query for non-Foundry APIs. The two work side by side. Caching explains how the cache stores and shares entries."},"1486":{"id":"/overview-34","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#next-steps","content":"Scaffold a React app with `@osdk/create-app` and run your first query and action."},"1487":{"id":"/overview-35","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#next-steps","content":"Add OSDK packages and your generated SDK to an existing app."},"1488":{"id":"/overview-36","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#next-steps","content":"Fetch lists and single objects with `useOsdkObjects` and `useOsdkObject`."},"1489":{"id":"/overview-37","page_id":"/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/overview#next-steps","content":"Build with Ontology-aware tables, filters, and action forms."},"1490":{"id":"/quickstart","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"page","content":"Quickstart","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/quickstart"},"1491":{"id":"/quickstart-0","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart","content":"Scaffold a React app with @osdk/create-app, sign in to Foundry, and run your first OSDK query and action."},"1492":{"id":"/quickstart-1","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"Before you start"},"1493":{"id":"/quickstart-2","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#create-the-app","content":"Create the app"},"1494":{"id":"/quickstart-3","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"Run the CLI"},"1495":{"id":"/quickstart-4","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#install-dependencies","content":"Install dependencies"},"1496":{"id":"/quickstart-5","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#start-the-dev-server","content":"Start the dev server"},"1497":{"id":"/quickstart-6","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"What the CLI generates"},"1498":{"id":"/quickstart-7","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#run-your-first-query","content":"Run your first query"},"1499":{"id":"/quickstart-8","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#apply-your-first-action","content":"Apply your first action"},"1500":{"id":"/quickstart-9","page_id":"/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/quickstart#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1501":{"id":"/quickstart-10","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart","content":"Use `@osdk/create-app` to generate a React and Vite app that already signs users in, creates an OSDK client, and installs your generated SDK. By the end of this page you have a local app that lists `Employee` objects and applies the `modifyEmployee` action."},"1502":{"id":"/quickstart-11","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart","content":"To add OSDK to an app you already have, see Installation instead."},"1503":{"id":"/quickstart-12","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"You need Node.js and an application in Foundry Developer Console. The CLI asks for these values, so collect them first:"},"1504":{"id":"/quickstart-13","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value       | Example                               | Where to find it in Developer Console |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Foundry URL | `https://example.palantirfoundry.com` | The URL of your Foundry stack.        |","table":"table-0"},"1505":{"id":"/quickstart-14","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value           | Example                                                   | Where to find it in Developer Console                                              |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Application RID | `ri.third-party-applications.main.application.1c66b352-…` | The application's Developer Console URL, `/workspace/developer-console/app/<rid>`. |","table":"table-0"},"1506":{"id":"/quickstart-15","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value           | Example                            | Where to find it in Developer Console |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| OAuth client ID | `2650385ab6c5e0df3b44aff776b00a42` | **OAuth & scopes**.                   |","table":"table-0"},"1507":{"id":"/quickstart-16","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value        | Example                                | Where to find it in Developer Console |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Ontology RID | `ri.ontology.main.ontology.1df1ce4c-…` | **Ontology SDK**.                     |","table":"table-0"},"1508":{"id":"/quickstart-17","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value            | Example       | Where to find it in Developer Console                                               |\n| ---------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| SDK package name | `@my-app/sdk` | The npm install instructions of a generated SDK version. Must match `@<scope>/sdk`. |","table":"table-0"},"1509":{"id":"/quickstart-18","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"| Value            | Example                                                                                                | Where to find it in Developer Console |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| npm registry URL | `https://example.palantirfoundry.com/artifacts/api/repositories/<repository-rid>/contents/release/npm` | The SDK's npm install instructions.   |","table":"table-0"},"1510":{"id":"/quickstart-19","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"In Developer Console, also:"},"1511":{"id":"/quickstart-20","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"Add the object types, link types, actions, and functions your app uses to the application's SDK, then generate a new version on **SDK versions** with the **npm** package type and the latest generator. Generate a new version whenever you change the resources."},"1512":{"id":"/quickstart-21","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"On **OAuth & scopes**, add `http://localhost:8080/auth/callback` as a redirect URL. The generated app runs on port 8080 and handles the sign-in redirect at that path."},"1513":{"id":"/quickstart-22","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#before-you-start","content":"Get a Foundry token with access to the SDK's npm registry. The generated `.npmrc` reads it from the `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` environment variable when you install packages."},"1514":{"id":"/quickstart-23","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"Run `@osdk/create-app` and pass the project directory name:"},"1515":{"id":"/quickstart-24","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"`npm create @osdk/app@latest` runs the same CLI. The prompts, in order:"},"1516":{"id":"/quickstart-25","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                                   | Default       | Flag                   |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Project name (letters, digits, `-`, `_`) | `my-osdk-app` | positional `[project]` |","table":"table-1"},"1517":{"id":"/quickstart-26","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                                         | Default | Flag         |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------ |\n| Framework: React, React (Public), Expo, or Vue |         | `--template` |","table":"table-1"},"1518":{"id":"/quickstart-27","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                                   | Default | Flag           |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------- | -------------- |\n| Foundry URL (must start with `https://`) |         | `--foundryUrl` |","table":"table-1"},"1519":{"id":"/quickstart-28","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                           | Default | Flag                                         |\n| -------------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| Do you know your production URL? |         | `--applicationUrl` or `--skipApplicationUrl` |","table":"table-1"},"1520":{"id":"/quickstart-29","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt          | Default | Flag            |\n| --------------- | ------- | --------------- |\n| Application RID |         | `--application` |","table":"table-1"},"1521":{"id":"/quickstart-30","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt          | Default | Flag         |\n| --------------- | ------- | ------------ |\n| OAuth client ID |         | `--clientId` |","table":"table-1"},"1522":{"id":"/quickstart-31","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                                              | Default | Flag         |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------ |\n| Will you use an OSDK? (No means Platform APIs only) |         | `--skipOsdk` |","table":"table-1"},"1523":{"id":"/quickstart-32","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt       | Default | Flag         |\n| ------------ | ------- | ------------ |\n| Ontology RID |         | `--ontology` |","table":"table-1"},"1524":{"id":"/quickstart-33","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt           | Default | Flag            |\n| ---------------- | ------- | --------------- |\n| SDK package name |         | `--osdkPackage` |","table":"table-1"},"1525":{"id":"/quickstart-34","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt           | Default | Flag                |\n| ---------------- | ------- | ------------------- |\n| npm registry URL |         | `--osdkRegistryUrl` |","table":"table-1"},"1526":{"id":"/quickstart-35","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                                      | Default | Flag          |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------- |\n| Include a CORS proxy for local development? | No      | `--corsProxy` |","table":"table-1"},"1527":{"id":"/quickstart-36","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt       | Default                                                                         | Flag       |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| OAuth scopes | `api:read-data api:write-data api:use-ontologies-read api:use-ontologies-write` | `--scopes` |","table":"table-1"},"1528":{"id":"/quickstart-37","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"Choose **React** for this guide. Answer **Yes** to the CORS proxy unless your Foundry administrator has allowed `http://localhost:8080` as a CORS origin."},"1529":{"id":"/quickstart-38","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-the-cli","content":"To skip every prompt, pass all values as flags:"},"1530":{"id":"/quickstart-39","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#install-dependencies","content":"Export your token so npm can reach your SDK's registry, then install:"},"1531":{"id":"/quickstart-40","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#install-dependencies","content":"A `401` or `404` for `@my-app/sdk` means `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` is missing, expired, or lacks access to the registry."},"1532":{"id":"/quickstart-41","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#start-the-dev-server","content":"Open `http://localhost:8080`. The app sends you to Foundry to sign in, Foundry redirects back to `/auth/callback`, and the app returns you to the home page. If Foundry reports an invalid redirect URL, add `http://localhost:8080/auth/callback` on **OAuth & scopes** in Developer Console."},"1533":{"id":"/quickstart-42","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\".env.development\" />"},"1534":{"id":"/quickstart-43","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\".env.production\" />"},"1535":{"id":"/quickstart-44","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\".npmrc\" />"},"1536":{"id":"/quickstart-45","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"foundry.config.json\" />"},"1537":{"id":"/quickstart-46","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"index.html\" />"},"1538":{"id":"/quickstart-47","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"package.json\" />"},"1539":{"id":"/quickstart-48","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"vite.config.ts\" />"},"1540":{"id":"/quickstart-49","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"resources.json\" />"},"1541":{"id":"/quickstart-50","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"AuthCallback.tsx\" />"},"1542":{"id":"/quickstart-51","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"client.ts\" />"},"1543":{"id":"/quickstart-52","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"env.test.ts\" />"},"1544":{"id":"/quickstart-53","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"Home.tsx\" />"},"1545":{"id":"/quickstart-54","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"main.tsx\" />"},"1546":{"id":"/quickstart-55","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"router.tsx\" />"},"1547":{"id":"/quickstart-56","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"ErrorBoundary.tsx\" />"},"1548":{"id":"/quickstart-57","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"Header.tsx\" />"},"1549":{"id":"/quickstart-58","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"Loading.tsx\" />"},"1550":{"id":"/quickstart-59","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"NextSteps.tsx\" />"},"1551":{"id":"/quickstart-60","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"<File name=\"Osdk.tsx\" />"},"1552":{"id":"/quickstart-61","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File                                  | Purpose                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `.env.development`, `.env.production` | `VITE_FOUNDRY_API_URL`, `VITE_FOUNDRY_CLIENT_ID`, `VITE_FOUNDRY_REDIRECT_URL`, and `VITE_FOUNDRY_ONTOLOGY_RID` for each mode. With the CORS proxy, the development API URL is `http://localhost:8080`. |","table":"table-2"},"1553":{"id":"/quickstart-62","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File         | Purpose                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `index.html` | Copies the env values into `<meta>` tags such as `osdk-foundryUrl` and `osdk-clientId`, so you can change configuration without rebuilding JavaScript. |","table":"table-2"},"1554":{"id":"/quickstart-63","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File            | Purpose                                                                                                       |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/client.ts` | Reads the meta tags, creates `auth` with `createPublicOauthClient`, and exports `client` from `createClient`. |","table":"table-2"},"1555":{"id":"/quickstart-64","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File           | Purpose                                                     |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.tsx` | Renders the router inside `<OsdkProvider client={client}>`. |","table":"table-2"},"1556":{"id":"/quickstart-65","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File             | Purpose                                                    |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/router.tsx` | Maps `/` to `Home` and `/auth/callback` to `AuthCallback`. |","table":"table-2"},"1557":{"id":"/quickstart-66","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File                   | Purpose                                                                    |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/AuthCallback.tsx` | Calls `auth.signIn()` to finish the OAuth redirect, then navigates to `/`. |","table":"table-2"},"1558":{"id":"/quickstart-67","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File             | Purpose                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `vite.config.ts` | Serves on port 8080, proxies `/api` and `/multipass/api` to Foundry when you chose the CORS proxy, and defines `process.env.NODE_ENV`. See Use OSDK with Vite. |","table":"table-2"},"1559":{"id":"/quickstart-68","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File     | Purpose                                                                                        |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.npmrc` | Points your SDK's npm scope at the Foundry registry and authenticates with `${FOUNDRY_TOKEN}`. |","table":"table-2"},"1560":{"id":"/quickstart-69","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File                  | Purpose                                                                                            |\n| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `foundry.config.json` | Deployment settings for Foundry website hosting with `@osdk/cli`. Delete it if you host elsewhere. |","table":"table-2"},"1561":{"id":"/quickstart-70","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"| File              | Purpose                                                              |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/env.test.ts` | A test that checks `.env.production` is filled in before you deploy. |","table":"table-2"},"1562":{"id":"/quickstart-71","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"The generated `src/client.ts` looks like this:"},"1563":{"id":"/quickstart-72","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#what-the-cli-generates","content":"Authentication explains the sign-in flow and the callback route. Create a client covers `createClient` and `OsdkProvider`."},"1564":{"id":"/quickstart-73","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-your-first-query","content":"Create a component that lists employees with `useOsdkObjects`. Replace `Employee`, `department`, and `fullName` with an object type and properties from your SDK:"},"1565":{"id":"/quickstart-74","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-your-first-query","content":"Render it from `src/Home.tsx`:"},"1566":{"id":"/quickstart-75","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#run-your-first-query","content":"The list keeps rendering while it loads and reloads, so show the loading indicator next to the data instead of in place of it. See Load objects for filters, pagination, and live updates."},"1567":{"id":"/quickstart-76","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#apply-your-first-action","content":"Add a button that applies `modifyEmployee`. `useOsdkAction` tracks the pending state and the last error, and `applyAction` rethrows, so attach a `catch`:"},"1568":{"id":"/quickstart-77","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#apply-your-first-action","content":"When the action succeeds, the list updates without a refetch call: the action response tells the cache which objects changed. See Apply actions for validation, batches, and optimistic updates."},"1569":{"id":"/quickstart-78","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next-steps","content":"Filter, sort, paginate, and stream updates with `useOsdkObjects`."},"1570":{"id":"/quickstart-79","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next-steps","content":"Validate parameters and show optimistic results."},"1571":{"id":"/quickstart-80","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next-steps","content":"Drop in `ObjectTable`, `FilterList`, and `ActionForm`."},"1572":{"id":"/quickstart-81","page_id":"/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/quickstart#next-steps","content":"Inspect your app's queries and cache while you develop."},"1573":{"id":"/troubleshooting","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Help"],"tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting"},"1574":{"id":"/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting","content":"Fixes for common OSDK errors, including a missing OsdkProvider, mismatched package versions, CORS, auth failures, and Vite build issues."},"1575":{"id":"/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#no-osdkprovider-found-did-you-forget-to-wrap-your-component-tree-with-osdkprovider","content":"`No OsdkProvider found. Did you forget to wrap your component tree with <OsdkProvider>?`"},"1576":{"id":"/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#name-is-not-exported-by-osdkclientobservablejs","content":"`\"<name>\" is not exported by @osdk/client/…/observable.js`"},"1577":{"id":"/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#peer-dependency-warnings-for-osdkclient-or-osdkapi","content":"Peer dependency warnings for `@osdk/client` or `@osdk/api`"},"1578":{"id":"/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#rollup-failed-to-resolve-import-osdkfoundryadmin","content":"`Rollup failed to resolve import \"@osdk/foundry.admin\"`"},"1579":{"id":"/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#referenceerror-process-is-not-defined","content":"`ReferenceError: process is not defined`"},"1580":{"id":"/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"CORS errors in local development"},"1581":{"id":"/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"`401 Unauthorized`"},"1582":{"id":"/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"`403 Forbidden` or `PERMISSION_DENIED`"},"1583":{"id":"/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#invalid-ontology-rid","content":"`Invalid ontology RID`"},"1584":{"id":"/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#meta-tag-osdk-clientid-contains-placeholder-value","content":"`Meta tag osdk-clientId contains placeholder value`"},"1585":{"id":"/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#rendered-more-hooks-than-during-the-previous-render","content":"`Rendered more hooks than during the previous render`"},"1586":{"id":"/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#actions-take-about-a-second-in-development","content":"Actions take about a second in development"},"1587":{"id":"/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#data-does-not-update-after-a-change-made-elsewhere","content":"Data does not update after a change made elsewhere"},"1588":{"id":"/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#deprecation-warnings-for-osdkreactexperimental","content":"Deprecation warnings for `@osdk/react/experimental`"},"1589":{"id":"/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/troubleshooting#the-devtools-panel-does-not-appear","content":"The devtools panel does not appear"},"1590":{"id":"/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting","content":"Find the error message or symptom you see, then apply the fix. Each section names the cause first."},"1591":{"id":"/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#no-osdkprovider-found-did-you-forget-to-wrap-your-component-tree-with-osdkprovider","content":"A component called an `@osdk/react` hook, or used the client from `useOsdkClient`, outside an `OsdkProvider`. Outside a provider, every hook gets a placeholder client that throws this error."},"1592":{"id":"/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#no-osdkprovider-found-did-you-forget-to-wrap-your-component-tree-with-osdkprovider","content":"Render `OsdkProvider` once at the root, above every component that uses OSDK hooks:"},"1593":{"id":"/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#no-osdkprovider-found-did-you-forget-to-wrap-your-component-tree-with-osdkprovider","content":"If only some components fail, they render outside the provider, for example in a header or a portal mounted next to `<App />`. Move `OsdkProvider` up so it wraps them."},"1594":{"id":"/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#no-osdkprovider-found-did-you-forget-to-wrap-your-component-tree-with-osdkprovider","content":"In tests, wrap the component under test in a provider. See Testing."},"1595":{"id":"/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#name-is-not-exported-by-osdkclientobservablejs","content":"You might also see the same error for `unstable-do-not-use.js` or a path in `@osdk/api`. `@osdk/react` imports its runtime from `@osdk/client/observable`, and your installed `@osdk/client` or `@osdk/api` comes from a different release than your `@osdk/react`."},"1596":{"id":"/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#name-is-not-exported-by-osdkclientobservablejs","content":"`@osdk/api`, `@osdk/client`, and `@osdk/react` share one version number. Install the same version of all three, and keep prereleases together:"},"1597":{"id":"/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#name-is-not-exported-by-osdkclientobservablejs","content":"Check what is installed with `npm ls @osdk/api @osdk/client @osdk/react`. Do not delete the failing import or downgrade one package on its own. See Version compatibility."},"1598":{"id":"/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#peer-dependency-warnings-for-osdkclient-or-osdkapi","content":"The peer ranges that `@osdk/react` declares, such as `^2.15.0`, are broader than what works. Pin `@osdk/api`, `@osdk/client`, and `@osdk/react` to the same version instead of ignoring the warning."},"1599":{"id":"/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#peer-dependency-warnings-for-osdkclient-or-osdkapi","content":"If the warning comes from your generated SDK, the SDK was built against a newer `@osdk/client` than you have. Upgrade the three OSDK packages, or generate a new SDK version. If npm still cannot resolve peers, use `overrides` as shown in Installation."},"1600":{"id":"/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#rollup-failed-to-resolve-import-osdkfoundryadmin","content":"The same error can name `@osdk/foundry.core`. You import from `@osdk/react/platform-apis`, which depends on two optional peer packages that are not installed."},"1601":{"id":"/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#rollup-failed-to-resolve-import-osdkfoundryadmin","content":"Install them:"},"1602":{"id":"/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#rollup-failed-to-resolve-import-osdkfoundryadmin","content":"If you do not use the platform API hooks, remove the imports from `@osdk/react/platform-apis` instead. See Platform APIs."},"1603":{"id":"/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#referenceerror-process-is-not-defined","content":"OSDK packages read `process.env.NODE_ENV`, and Vite does not replace it by default. Add `\"process.env.NODE_ENV\": JSON.stringify(mode)` to `define` in your Vite config. See Use OSDK with Vite for the full config."},"1604":{"id":"/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"The browser console shows an error like `Access to fetch at 'https://<your-stack>/api/...' from origin 'http://localhost:8080' has been blocked by CORS policy`. Your Foundry environment does not allow requests from your dev server's origin."},"1605":{"id":"/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"Fix it in one of two ways:"},"1606":{"id":"/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"**Allow the origin.** Ask your Foundry administrator to allow `http://localhost:8080` for CORS on your environment."},"1607":{"id":"/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"**Proxy through Vite.** Forward `/api` and `/multipass/api` to Foundry from the dev server, and set `VITE_FOUNDRY_API_URL=http://localhost:8080`. Requests then go to your own origin, so CORS does not apply. See Proxy Foundry requests in development."},"1608":{"id":"/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#cors-errors-in-local-development","content":"Apps created with `@osdk/create-app` include the proxy when you answer yes to the CORS proxy prompt or pass `--corsProxy`. The proxy runs only under `vite dev`, so keep the real Foundry URL in `.env.production`."},"1609":{"id":"/troubleshooting-35","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"The request had no valid token. Check, in order:"},"1610":{"id":"/troubleshooting-36","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"**Client ID.** The client ID passed to `createPublicOauthClient` matches the one on your application's **OAuth & scopes** page in Developer Console."},"1611":{"id":"/troubleshooting-37","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"**Redirect URL.** The redirect URL matches one listed on the same page exactly, including protocol, port, and path, such as `http://localhost:8080/auth/callback`."},"1612":{"id":"/troubleshooting-38","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"**Callback route.** Your app renders a route at the redirect path, so the OAuth client can complete sign-in."},"1613":{"id":"/troubleshooting-39","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"**Token provider.** The client receives the OAuth client as its token provider: `createClient(foundryUrl, ontologyRid, auth)`."},"1614":{"id":"/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#401-unauthorized","content":"To detect an expired session in UI code, check `error.statusCode === 401` on a `PalantirApiError`. See Loading and errors."},"1615":{"id":"/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"The token is valid but cannot do what you asked. Common causes:"},"1616":{"id":"/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"**Missing scopes.** The OAuth client requests `api:read-data`, `api:write-data`, `api:use-ontologies-read`, and `api:use-ontologies-write` by default. Other APIs need more. For example, the user and marking hooks in `@osdk/react/platform-apis` need `api:admin-read`. Add the scope to the application in Developer Console, then request it:"},"1617":{"id":"/troubleshooting-43","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"Changing `scopes` signs users in again so the new token carries them. See Scopes."},"1618":{"id":"/troubleshooting-44","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"**Resources outside the application's scope.** The object type, action, or function is not included in the application's Ontology SDK resources in Developer Console."},"1619":{"id":"/troubleshooting-45","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"**User permissions.** The signed-in user cannot see the data or apply the action. Requests made with a public OAuth client act as the signed-in user and never exceed that user's access."},"1620":{"id":"/troubleshooting-46","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#403-forbidden-or-permission_denied","content":"A `NOT_FOUND` error, such as `ObjectNotFound`, can also mean the user lacks access to an object that exists."},"1621":{"id":"/troubleshooting-47","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#invalid-ontology-rid","content":"`createClient` throws this when its second argument does not start with `ri.`. The value is often empty, an API name, or a placeholder from an env file. Pass the full Ontology RID, such as `ri.ontology.main.ontology.<uuid>`. Find it on the **Ontology SDK** page of your application in Developer Console, or import `$ontologyRid` from your generated SDK."},"1622":{"id":"/troubleshooting-48","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#meta-tag-osdk-clientid-contains-placeholder-value","content":"Apps created with `@osdk/create-app` read their configuration from `<meta>` tags that Vite fills in from `.env` files. This error means a variable, such as `VITE_FOUNDRY_CLIENT_ID`, is not set for the current mode. Add it to `.env.development` or `.env.production` and restart the dev server."},"1623":{"id":"/troubleshooting-49","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#rendered-more-hooks-than-during-the-previous-render","content":"A component called an `@osdk/react` hook conditionally. Call every hook on every render, and use `enabled` to skip the request:"},"1624":{"id":"/troubleshooting-50","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#actions-take-about-a-second-in-development","content":"In development, actions that have an `$optimisticUpdate` wait 1000 ms after the server responds so you can see the optimistic state. The console logs `[@osdk/client] Applied a 1000ms dev-mode delay…` the first time it happens. Production builds never delay. To turn it off in development:"},"1625":{"id":"/troubleshooting-51","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#data-does-not-update-after-a-change-made-elsewhere","content":"The cache updates itself after actions you apply through `useOsdkAction`. It cannot see changes made by other systems, by `@osdk/client` calls outside the hooks, or by REST calls. Invalidate the affected data, or use `streamUpdates: true` on lists that must stay live. See Caching and reactivity and Cache invalidation."},"1626":{"id":"/troubleshooting-52","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#deprecation-warnings-for-osdkreactexperimental","content":"The hooks from `@osdk/react/experimental` are now exported from `@osdk/react`, and `OsdkProvider2` is now `OsdkProvider`. Change the imports:"},"1627":{"id":"/troubleshooting-53","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#deprecation-warnings-for-osdkreactexperimental","content":"The `experimental` entry point will be removed in a future major version."},"1628":{"id":"/troubleshooting-54","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#the-devtools-panel-does-not-appear","content":"| Symptom   | Fix                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| No panel. | Confirm `osdkDevTools()` from `@osdk/react-devtools/vite` is in your Vite `plugins` and you run `vite dev`. Pass `osdkDevTools({ verbose: true })` and look for `Injected devtools into HTML` in the terminal. |","table":"table-0"},"1629":{"id":"/troubleshooting-55","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#the-devtools-panel-does-not-appear","content":"| Symptom              | Fix                                                                                                                   |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Panel shows no data. | The screen must read data through `@osdk/react` hooks under `OsdkProvider`. The panel does not see raw `fetch` calls. |","table":"table-0"},"1630":{"id":"/troubleshooting-56","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#the-devtools-panel-does-not-appear","content":"| Symptom                              | Fix                                                                                                      |\n| ------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Component inspection is unavailable. | Something loaded React before the devtools script. Remove scripts in `index.html` that load React first. |","table":"table-0"},"1631":{"id":"/troubleshooting-57","page_id":"/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/troubleshooting#the-devtools-panel-does-not-appear","content":"See the devtools troubleshooting table for more."},"1632":{"id":"/widgets","page_id":"/widgets","type":"page","content":"Custom widgets","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Custom widgets"],"tags":[],"url":"/widgets"},"1633":{"id":"/widgets-0","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets","content":"Build React or plain TypeScript widgets that run inside Foundry UIs such as Workshop, exchange parameters and events with the host, and call the OSDK."},"1634":{"id":"/widgets-1","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"1635":{"id":"/widgets-2","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#packages","content":"Packages"},"1636":{"id":"/widgets-3","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#create-a-widget-set-project","content":"Create a widget set project"},"1637":{"id":"/widgets-4","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"Run the CLI"},"1638":{"id":"/widgets-5","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#install-dependencies","content":"Install dependencies"},"1639":{"id":"/widgets-6","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#start-developer-mode","content":"Start developer mode"},"1640":{"id":"/widgets-7","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"Project layout"},"1641":{"id":"/widgets-8","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#run-locally","content":"Run locally"},"1642":{"id":"/widgets-9","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#start-the-dev-server","content":"Start the dev server"},"1643":{"id":"/widgets-10","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#open-the-setup-url","content":"Open the setup URL"},"1644":{"id":"/widgets-11","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#edit-your-code","content":"Edit your code"},"1645":{"id":"/widgets-12","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#code-workspaces","content":"Code Workspaces"},"1646":{"id":"/widgets-13","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#use-the-osdk-in-a-widget","content":"Use the OSDK in a widget"},"1647":{"id":"/widgets-14","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"Build a widget without React"},"1648":{"id":"/widgets-15","page_id":"/widgets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1649":{"id":"/widgets-16","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets","content":"A custom widget is a web page you build with Vite that Foundry embeds inside a host UI such as Workshop. The host passes values into the widget as parameters, the widget sends events back to update them, and the widget can read and write your Ontology through the OSDK."},"1650":{"id":"/widgets-17","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"Widgets ship in a **widget set**, a Foundry resource with a RID such as `ri.widgetregistry..widget-set.<id>`. One project builds one widget set, and each HTML entrypoint in its Vite config becomes one widget in the set. You deploy the set as numbered versions, and the host loads the scripts and stylesheets that the version's manifest lists."},"1651":{"id":"/widgets-18","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"Each widget declares its contract in a config file built with `defineConfig`: an ID and name, the parameters the host can set, and the events the widget can emit. At build time, `@osdk/widget.vite-plugin` turns those configs into the manifest at `.palantir/widgets.config.json`, which tells Foundry what to show in the widget's setup panel. See Parameters and events."},"1652":{"id":"/widgets-19","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"At runtime the host injects `window.__PALANTIR_WIDGET_API__` into the widget's page, and the two sides exchange typed messages through it:"},"1653":{"id":"/widgets-20","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message        | Direction      | Payload                   | When                                                          |\n| -------------- | -------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widget.ready` | Widget to host | `{ apiVersion: \"1.0.0\" }` | The widget is listening and wants its first parameter values. |","table":"table-0"},"1654":{"id":"/widgets-21","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message                  | Direction      | Payload                                            | When                                             |\n| ------------------------ | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `host.update-parameters` | Host to widget | `{ parameters }`, one async value per parameter ID | Parameter values or their loading states change. |","table":"table-0"},"1655":{"id":"/widgets-22","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message             | Direction      | Payload                         | When                                         |\n| ------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `widget.emit-event` | Widget to host | `{ eventId, parameterUpdates }` | The widget fires one of its declared events. |","table":"table-0"},"1656":{"id":"/widgets-23","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message         | Direction      | Payload                                               | When                               |\n| --------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `widget.resize` | Widget to host | `{ width, height }` of the document body's border box | The widget's content changes size. |","table":"table-0"},"1657":{"id":"/widgets-24","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"| Message         | Direction      | Payload | When                                                                            |\n| --------------- | -------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widget.reload` | Widget to host | `{}`    | The widget needs a full reload, such as a Vite full-page reload in development. |","table":"table-0"},"1658":{"id":"/widgets-25","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#how-it-works","content":"`FoundryWidget` from `@osdk/widget.client-react` sends `widget.ready`, `widget.resize`, and `widget.reload` for you and exposes the rest through a hook. See React widgets."},"1659":{"id":"/widgets-26","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package            | Use it for                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `@osdk/widget.api` | The contract itself: message, manifest, and parameter value types, `BrowserPermission`, and `MANIFEST_FILE_LOCATION`. `@osdk/widget.client` re-exports the parts you need, so you rarely import it directly. |","table":"table-1"},"1660":{"id":"/widgets-27","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package               | Use it for                                                                                                                                                         |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `@osdk/widget.client` | `defineConfig` for widget configs, `createFoundryWidgetClient` for widgets without React, and `createFoundryWidgetTokenProvider` for OSDK clients inside a widget. |","table":"table-1"},"1661":{"id":"/widgets-28","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package                     | Use it for                                                                                     |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/widget.client-react` | The `FoundryWidget` provider and the `useFoundryWidgetContext` hook. Supports React 18 and 19. |","table":"table-1"},"1662":{"id":"/widgets-29","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package                    | Use it for                                                                                               |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/widget.vite-plugin` | Generates the manifest during `vite build` and runs developer mode during `vite`. Supports Vite 6 and 7. |","table":"table-1"},"1663":{"id":"/widgets-30","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package               | Use it for                                                                      |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/create-widget` | A CLI that scaffolds a React widget set project with all of the above wired in. |","table":"table-1"},"1664":{"id":"/widgets-31","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#packages","content":"| Package     | Use it for                                                                                                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/cli` | `osdk widgetset deploy` and `osdk widgetset version` for publishing and managing versions. See Build and publish. |","table":"table-1"},"1665":{"id":"/widgets-32","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#create-a-widget-set-project","content":"Before you start, you need:"},"1666":{"id":"/widgets-33","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#create-a-widget-set-project","content":"A widget set in Foundry and its RID, `ri.widgetregistry..widget-set.<id>`."},"1667":{"id":"/widgets-34","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#create-a-widget-set-project","content":"A Foundry token in the `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` environment variable. Developer mode, `osdk widgetset deploy`, and installing your SDK package from Foundry's npm registry all read it."},"1668":{"id":"/widgets-35","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#create-a-widget-set-project","content":"To call the Ontology, the name of your widget set's SDK package, such as `@my-app/sdk`, and the URL of the npm registry that hosts it. The registry URL has the form `https://<stack>/artifacts/api/repositories/ri.artifacts.main.repository.<id>/contents/release/npm`."},"1669":{"id":"/widgets-36","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"`npm create @osdk/widget@latest` runs the same CLI. It prompts for each value you do not pass as a flag:"},"1670":{"id":"/widgets-37","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt       | Flag                   | Accepted values                                              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Project name | positional `[project]` | Letters, digits, `-`, and `_`. Defaults to `my-osdk-widget`. |","table":"table-2"},"1671":{"id":"/widgets-38","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                            | Flag          | Accepted values                                                                                                                  |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Overwrite the existing directory? | `--overwrite` | Asked only if the directory exists. `--overwrite` removes its files; `--no-overwrite` keeps them and writes over matching paths. |","table":"table-2"},"1672":{"id":"/widgets-39","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt    | Flag         | Accepted values                                                       |\n| --------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Framework | `--template` | `widget-react`, listed as **OSDK React**: React, Vite, and Blueprint. |","table":"table-2"},"1673":{"id":"/widgets-40","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt       | Flag           | Accepted values                                                                                |\n| ------------ | -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| OSDK version | `--sdkVersion` | `2.x`, the only version the React template supports. Not prompted unless the value is invalid. |","table":"table-2"},"1674":{"id":"/widgets-41","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt      | Flag           | Accepted values                                                            |\n| ----------- | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Foundry URL | `--foundryUrl` | Must start with `https://`, such as `https://example.palantirfoundry.com`. |","table":"table-2"},"1675":{"id":"/widgets-42","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt                     | Flag         | Accepted values                                                                                              |\n| -------------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Will you be using an OSDK? | `--skipOsdk` | Passing `--osdkPackage` or `--osdkRegistryUrl` answers yes. `--skipOsdk` answers no and conflicts with both. |","table":"table-2"},"1676":{"id":"/widgets-43","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt            | Flag            | Accepted values                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| OSDK package name | `--osdkPackage` | Must match `@<scope>/sdk`, such as `@my-app/sdk`. |","table":"table-2"},"1677":{"id":"/widgets-44","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt           | Flag                | Accepted values                                              |\n| ---------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| npm registry URL | `--osdkRegistryUrl` | The Foundry Artifacts URL ending in `/contents/release/npm`. |","table":"table-2"},"1678":{"id":"/widgets-45","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt         | Flag          | Accepted values                       |\n| -------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Widget set RID | `--widgetSet` | `ri.widgetregistry..widget-set.<id>`. |","table":"table-2"},"1679":{"id":"/widgets-46","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"| Prompt | Flag           | Accepted values                                                                             |\n| ------ | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| None   | `--repository` | Optional code repository RID, written to `foundry.config.json` for `osdk widgetset deploy`. |","table":"table-2"},"1680":{"id":"/widgets-47","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-the-cli","content":"To skip every prompt:"},"1681":{"id":"/widgets-48","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#install-dependencies","content":"The generated `.npmrc` sends `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` to your Foundry npm registry, so a `401` or `404` for your SDK package means the token is missing, expired, or lacks access."},"1682":{"id":"/widgets-49","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#start-developer-mode","content":"The terminal prints a setup URL. Open it to load your local widgets in Foundry, as described in Run locally."},"1683":{"id":"/widgets-50","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\".gitignore\" />"},"1684":{"id":"/widgets-51","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\".npmrc\" />"},"1685":{"id":"/widgets-52","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"README.md\" />"},"1686":{"id":"/widgets-53","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"eslint.config.mjs\" />"},"1687":{"id":"/widgets-54","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"foundry.config.json\" />"},"1688":{"id":"/widgets-55","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"index.html\" />"},"1689":{"id":"/widgets-56","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"package.json\" />"},"1690":{"id":"/widgets-57","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"tsconfig.json\" />"},"1691":{"id":"/widgets-58","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"tsconfig.node.json\" />"},"1692":{"id":"/widgets-59","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"vite.config.ts\" />"},"1693":{"id":"/widgets-60","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"client.ts\" />"},"1694":{"id":"/widgets-61","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"main.config.ts\" />"},"1695":{"id":"/widgets-62","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"main.css\" />"},"1696":{"id":"/widgets-63","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"main.tsx\" />"},"1697":{"id":"/widgets-64","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"useDarkTheme.ts\" />"},"1698":{"id":"/widgets-65","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"vite-env.d.ts\" />"},"1699":{"id":"/widgets-66","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"Widget.module.css\" />"},"1700":{"id":"/widgets-67","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"<File name=\"Widget.tsx\" />"},"1701":{"id":"/widgets-68","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File                  | Purpose                                                                                                               |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `foundry.config.json` | The Foundry URL and widget set settings that the Vite plugin and `osdk widgetset deploy` read. See Build and publish. |","table":"table-3"},"1702":{"id":"/widgets-69","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File     | Purpose                                                                                                                          |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.npmrc` | Points your SDK package's scope at your Foundry registry and authenticates with `${FOUNDRY_TOKEN}`. Only generated with an OSDK. |","table":"table-3"},"1703":{"id":"/widgets-70","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File             | Purpose                                                                                                                                         |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `vite.config.ts` | Adds `@vitejs/plugin-react` and `@osdk/widget.vite-plugin`, serves on port 8080 with CORS enabled, and lists `./index.html` as the build input. |","table":"table-3"},"1704":{"id":"/widgets-71","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File         | Purpose                                            |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `index.html` | The widget's entrypoint. It loads `/src/main.tsx`. |","table":"table-3"},"1705":{"id":"/widgets-72","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File                 | Purpose                                                                                                                                |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.config.ts` | The widget config: ID `widgetId`, a `greetingName` string parameter, a `counterValue` number parameter, and a `setCounterValue` event. |","table":"table-3"},"1706":{"id":"/widgets-73","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File           | Purpose                                                                                                                                                        |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.tsx` | Renders `Widget` inside `FoundryWidget`, and inside `OsdkProvider` when you use an OSDK. Importing `main.config.ts` here is what lets the Vite plugin find it. |","table":"table-3"},"1707":{"id":"/widgets-74","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File            | Purpose                                               |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/client.ts` | Creates the OSDK client. Only generated with an OSDK. |","table":"table-3"},"1708":{"id":"/widgets-75","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File             | Purpose                                                                                                               |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/Widget.tsx` | Reads both parameters, increments the counter every second by emitting `setCounterValue`, and renders a reset button. |","table":"table-3"},"1709":{"id":"/widgets-76","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| File                  | Purpose                                                                             |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/useDarkTheme.ts` | Tracks `prefers-color-scheme: dark` so the widget can apply Blueprint's dark theme. |","table":"table-3"},"1710":{"id":"/widgets-77","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"Without an OSDK, the CLI omits `.npmrc` and `src/client.ts`, and `package.json` drops `@osdk/client`, `@osdk/react`, and the SDK package."},"1711":{"id":"/widgets-78","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"The `package.json` scripts:"},"1712":{"id":"/widgets-79","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| Script | Command | Description                               |\n| ------ | ------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `dev`  | `vite`  | Starts the dev server and developer mode. |","table":"table-4"},"1713":{"id":"/widgets-80","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| Script  | Command             | Description                                                                     |\n| ------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `build` | `tsc && vite build` | Typechecks, builds to `dist/`, and writes `dist/.palantir/widgets.config.json`. |","table":"table-4"},"1714":{"id":"/widgets-81","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| Script | Command                                                        | Description        |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `lint` | `eslint . --report-unused-disable-directives --max-warnings 0` | Lints the project. |","table":"table-4"},"1715":{"id":"/widgets-82","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| Script | Command                        | Description |\n| ------ | ------------------------------ | ----------- |\n| `test` | `vitest run --passWithNoTests` | Runs tests. |","table":"table-4"},"1716":{"id":"/widgets-83","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#project-layout","content":"| Script    | Command        | Description                          |\n| --------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `preview` | `vite preview` | Serves the production build locally. |","table":"table-4"},"1717":{"id":"/widgets-84","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#run-locally","content":"Developer mode loads widget code from your dev server into Foundry, so you can preview changes against real host data without deploying a version."},"1718":{"id":"/widgets-85","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#start-the-dev-server","content":"Export `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` and run `npm run dev`. The plugin stops with `FOUNDRY_TOKEN environment variable not found` if the variable is missing. Instead of the usual local URL, Vite prints:"},"1719":{"id":"/widgets-86","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#open-the-setup-url","content":"The setup page loads each HTML entrypoint so Vite parses its widget config, then builds a development manifest whose scripts point at your dev server. It sends that manifest for the widget set in `foundry.config.json` to Foundry, enables developer mode, and redirects you to the widget set's preview page at `<foundryUrl>/workspace/custom-widgets/preview/<widgetSetRid>`."},"1720":{"id":"/widgets-87","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#open-the-setup-url","content":"If a widget's config is never found, the page gives up after 10 attempts with `Timed out waiting for widget config files to be parsed. Are you sure a widget config is imported?`."},"1721":{"id":"/widgets-88","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#edit-your-code","content":"Component changes reach the embedded widget through Vite hot module replacement. A change to a widget config file does not: the terminal warns that the config changed, and you open the setup URL again to send the new parameters and events to Foundry."},"1722":{"id":"/widgets-89","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#edit-your-code","content":"You do not need to publish a widget set before developing on it. To place the widget in a Workshop module, publish a version once so the widget appears in Workshop's **Widget setup** panel. See Build and publish."},"1723":{"id":"/widgets-90","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#code-workspaces","content":"In Foundry Code Workspaces, run Vite in the `code-workspaces` mode instead:"},"1724":{"id":"/widgets-91","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#code-workspaces","content":"In this mode the plugin reads the Foundry URL from `FOUNDRY_PROXY_URL`, the token from the file named by `FOUNDRY_PROXY_TOKEN`, and the dev server address from `DEV_SERVER_DOMAIN` and `DEV_SERVER_BASE_PATH`, all set by the workspace. Open the preview panel to enter developer mode, and refresh it after you change a widget config. The plugin warns when you run `npm run dev` inside a workspace, or the `code-workspaces` mode outside one."},"1725":{"id":"/widgets-92","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#use-the-osdk-in-a-widget","content":"Inside Foundry, a widget authenticates through the host instead of OAuth. Create the client against the page origin with the widget token provider:"},"1726":{"id":"/widgets-93","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#use-the-osdk-in-a-widget","content":"`createFoundryWidgetTokenProvider` resolves to a placeholder that Foundry replaces with real credentials on each request. Pass the client to `FoundryWidget`, which needs it to resolve object set parameters, and to `OsdkProvider` so `@osdk/react` hooks work inside the widget:"},"1727":{"id":"/widgets-94","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#use-the-osdk-in-a-widget","content":"From there, query with the hooks in Query objects or read object sets the host passes in, as shown in React widgets. At build time, the Vite plugin also lists every installed package whose `package.json` has an `osdk.packageRid` field, with its version, in the manifest's `inputSpec`."},"1728":{"id":"/widgets-95","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"`createFoundryWidgetClient` from `@osdk/widget.client` speaks the same protocol without a framework. Outside a Foundry host or developer mode, it throws `Invariant failed: [FoundryWidgetClient] Missing __PALANTIR_WIDGET_API__ in window`."},"1729":{"id":"/widgets-96","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member        | Description                                                                     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `subscribe()` | Starts forwarding host messages to `hostEventTarget`. Call it before `ready()`. |","table":"table-5"},"1730":{"id":"/widgets-97","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member          | Description                     |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `unsubscribe()` | Stops forwarding host messages. |","table":"table-5"},"1731":{"id":"/widgets-98","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member    | Description                                                        |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `ready()` | Sends `widget.ready` so the host sends the first parameter values. |","table":"table-5"},"1732":{"id":"/widgets-99","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member                                     | Description                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `emitEvent(eventId, { parameterUpdates })` | Sends `widget.emit-event`. Typed against the events in your config. |","table":"table-5"},"1733":{"id":"/widgets-100","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member                      | Description            |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `resize({ width, height })` | Sends `widget.resize`. |","table":"table-5"},"1734":{"id":"/widgets-101","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member     | Description            |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- |\n| `reload()` | Sends `widget.reload`. |","table":"table-5"},"1735":{"id":"/widgets-102","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member                 | Description                                         |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sendMessage(message)` | Sends any widget message. Prefer the methods above. |","table":"table-5"},"1736":{"id":"/widgets-103","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#build-a-widget-without-react","content":"| Member            | Description                                                                                           |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hostEventTarget` | An `EventTarget` that dispatches `host.update-parameters` with the message payload in `event.detail`. |","table":"table-5"},"1737":{"id":"/widgets-104","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#next-steps","content":"Every parameter type, event, permission, and how they map to the manifest."},"1738":{"id":"/widgets-105","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#next-steps","content":"Read parameters, emit events, and handle loading states with `FoundryWidget`."},"1739":{"id":"/widgets-106","page_id":"/widgets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets#next-steps","content":"Configure the Vite plugin, build the manifest, and deploy versions."},"1740":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"page","content":"Parameters and events","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Custom widgets"],"tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events"},"1741":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-0","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","content":"Declare a widget's parameters, events, and browser permissions with defineConfig, and see how each field maps to the widgets.config.json manifest."},"1742":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-1","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#define-a-config","content":"Define a config"},"1743":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-2","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"Config fields"},"1744":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-3","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"Parameter types"},"1745":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-4","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"Loading states"},"1746":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-5","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"Events"},"1747":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-6","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"Permissions"},"1748":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-7","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"How the config maps to the manifest"},"1749":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-8","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","content":"A widget config declares what the host can pass into your widget and what the widget can send back. Write one per widget with `defineConfig` from `@osdk/widget.client`. The config also types your React hooks, and the Vite plugin turns it into the manifest Foundry reads."},"1750":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-9","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#define-a-config","content":"Export the config as the file's default export, name the file `*.config.ts` (or `.js`, `.tsx`, `.jsx`), and import it from the widget's entrypoint script. The Vite plugin finds configs through that import; see Build and publish."},"1751":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-10","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#define-a-config","content":"`defineConfig` returns its argument unchanged. Its `const` type parameter keeps parameter IDs, types, and `parameterUpdateIds` as literal types, which is what lets `useFoundryWidgetContext` and `emitEvent` type-check against your config."},"1752":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-11","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field | Type     | Default  | Description                                                                                                                 |\n| ----- | -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | `string` | Required | Unique within the widget set. camelCase: letters and digits only, starting with a lowercase letter. At most 100 characters. |","table":"table-0"},"1753":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-12","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field  | Type     | Default  | Description                                         |\n| ------ | -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `name` | `string` | Required | The name shown in the host. At most 100 characters. |","table":"table-0"},"1754":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-13","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field         | Type     | Default | Description                                |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `description` | `string` |         | Shown in the host. At most 250 characters. |","table":"table-0"},"1755":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-14","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field  | Type         | Default  | Description                                                  |\n| ------ | ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `type` | `\"workshop\"` | Required | The host the widget targets. `\"workshop\"` is the only value. |","table":"table-0"},"1756":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-15","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field        | Type                                  | Default  | Description                                                          |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameters` | `Record<string, ParameterDefinition>` | Required | Values the host passes in, keyed by parameter ID. Use `{}` for none. |","table":"table-0"},"1757":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-16","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field    | Type                              | Default  | Description                                                       |\n| -------- | --------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `events` | `Record<string, EventDefinition>` | Required | Events the widget can emit, keyed by event ID. Use `{}` for none. |","table":"table-0"},"1758":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-17","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field         | Type                  | Default | Description                                                      |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `permissions` | `BrowserPermission[]` |         | Extra browser capabilities the widget requests. See Permissions. |","table":"table-0"},"1759":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-18","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"| Field                     | Type      | Default                    | Description                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------------------- | --------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `refreshHostDataOnAction` | `boolean` | Plugin default, else unset | Asks the host to refresh the Ontology data it passes in, currently object set parameters, when the widget is thought to have applied an action through the Ontology APIs. |","table":"table-0"},"1760":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-19","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#config-fields","content":"TypeScript cannot check ID formats and lengths, so the Vite plugin validates them when it loads the config and fails the build or developer mode with messages such as `Widget id \"my-widget\" does not match allowed pattern (must be camelCase)`."},"1761":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-20","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"Every parameter needs a `type` and a `displayName`, the label shown in the host's setup panel. Parameter IDs follow the same camelCase rule and 100-character limit as widget IDs."},"1762":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-21","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`     | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes |\n| ---------- | ------------ | ------------------- | ----- |\n| `\"string\"` |              | `string`            |       |","table":"table-1"},"1763":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-22","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`     | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes |\n| ---------- | ------------ | ------------------- | ----- |\n| `\"number\"` |              | `number`            |       |","table":"table-1"},"1764":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-23","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`      | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes |\n| ----------- | ------------ | ------------------- | ----- |\n| `\"boolean\"` |              | `boolean`           |       |","table":"table-1"},"1765":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-24","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`   | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes                      |\n| -------- | ------------ | ------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `\"date\"` |              | `string`            | An ISO date, `YYYY-MM-DD`. |","table":"table-1"},"1766":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-25","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`        | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes            |\n| ------------- | ------------ | ------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `\"timestamp\"` |              | `string`            | An ISO datetime. |","table":"table-1"},"1767":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-26","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`       | Extra fields | Value in the widget | Notes           |\n| ------------ | ------------ | ------------------- | --------------- |\n| `\"scenario\"` |              | `string`            | A Scenario RID. |","table":"table-1"},"1768":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-27","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`    | Extra fields | Value in the widget             | Notes                                    |\n| --------- | ------------ | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `\"array\"` | `subType`    | An array of the `subType` value | `subType` is any of the six types above. |","table":"table-1"},"1769":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-28","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`        | Extra fields  | Value in the widget        | Notes                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------- | ------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"objectSet\"` | `allowedType` | `{ objectSetRid: string }` | `allowedType` is an object type or interface from your generated SDK, such as `Employee` or `Worker`. In React, the value also carries a hydrated `objectSet`; see React widgets. |","table":"table-1"},"1770":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-29","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"| `type`           | Extra fields | Value in the widget        | Notes                                                                            |\n| ---------------- | ------------ | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"mapTileLayer\"` |              | `{ tileSourceId: string }` | Read-only: a tile source ID for the Foundry Tiles APIs. Events cannot update it. |","table":"table-1"},"1771":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-30","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"An `objectSet` parameter needs the RID that generated SDKs embed in each type definition. If it is missing, the plugin fails with `ObjectSet parameter \"employees\" must have a valid rid in its metadata, make sure your OSDK was generated with a generator version >=2.6.2`. The older `objectType` field is deprecated; use `allowedType`."},"1772":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-31","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#parameter-types","content":"Dates and timestamps stay strings. Parse them with the date library your widget already uses."},"1773":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-32","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"The host sends each parameter as an async value, so your widget can show what is still loading. The `type` field moves through these states:"},"1774":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-33","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"| `type`          | `value` | `error` | Meaning                                     |\n| --------------- | ------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"not-started\"` |         |         | The host has not started loading the value. |","table":"table-2"},"1775":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-34","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"| `type`      | `value` | `error` | Meaning                        |\n| ----------- | ------- | ------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `\"loading\"` |         |         | The first load is in progress. |","table":"table-2"},"1776":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-35","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"| `type`     | `value`                   | `error` | Meaning                                                               |\n| ---------- | ------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"loaded\"` | The value, or `undefined` |         | The value is ready. `undefined` means the host variable has no value. |","table":"table-2"},"1777":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-36","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"| `type`        | `value`            | `error` | Meaning                 |\n| ------------- | ------------------ | ------- | ----------------------- |\n| `\"reloading\"` | The previous value |         | A new value is loading. |","table":"table-2"},"1778":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-37","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"| `type`     | `value`                | `error` | Meaning         |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- | ------- | --------------- |\n| `\"failed\"` | The last value, if any | `Error` | Loading failed. |","table":"table-2"},"1779":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-38","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#loading-states","content":"The types are exported from `@osdk/widget.client` as `AsyncValue`, `AsyncLoadedValue`, `AsyncFailedValue`, and so on. React widgets covers how `FoundryWidget` combines them."},"1780":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-39","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"An event tells the host to update one or more of the widget's parameters. Declare each event with a label and the parameters it updates:"},"1781":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-40","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"| Field         | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `displayName` | `string` | The event name shown in the host, where builders attach behavior to it. |","table":"table-3"},"1782":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-41","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"| Field                | Type       | Description                                                                                                                |\n| -------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameterUpdateIds` | `string[]` | The parameter IDs the event sets. Each must be a parameter in the same config, and none can be a `mapTileLayer` parameter. |","table":"table-3"},"1783":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-42","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"When you emit the event, `parameterUpdates` must contain a value for every ID in `parameterUpdateIds`, typed like the parameter's value:"},"1784":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-43","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#events","content":"To fire an event without updating anything, set `parameterUpdateIds: []` and emit `parameterUpdates: {}`. Listing a `mapTileLayer` parameter is a type error, and the plugin rejects it with `Event \"selectTile\" cannot update read-only map tile layer parameter \"tiles\"`."},"1785":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-44","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"A widget runs in a sandboxed frame. Request extra capabilities with `permissions`:"},"1786":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-45","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value      | Requests                         |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `\"camera\"` | The `camera` permissions policy. |","table":"table-4"},"1787":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-46","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value          | Requests                             |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `\"microphone\"` | The `microphone` permissions policy. |","table":"table-4"},"1788":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-47","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value        | Requests                           |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `\"autoplay\"` | The `autoplay` permissions policy. |","table":"table-4"},"1789":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-48","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value               | Requests                            |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `\"allow-downloads\"` | The `allow-downloads` sandbox flag. |","table":"table-4"},"1790":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-49","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value           | Requests                        |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `\"allow-forms\"` | The `allow-forms` sandbox flag. |","table":"table-4"},"1791":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-50","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value            | Requests                         |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `\"allow-modals\"` | The `allow-modals` sandbox flag. |","table":"table-4"},"1792":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-51","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"| Value            | Requests                         |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `\"allow-popups\"` | The `allow-popups` sandbox flag. |","table":"table-4"},"1793":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-52","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#permissions","content":"The same values are available as constants on `BrowserPermission` from `@osdk/widget.api`, such as `BrowserPermission.CAMERA`. A request does not guarantee access: the user may still need to accept a browser prompt, depending on the permission and browser settings."},"1794":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-53","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"`vite build` writes one manifest per widget set to `.palantir/widgets.config.json` in the build output. Each widget's config becomes an entry under `widgetSet.widgets`, keyed by widget ID. For the config at the top of this page, the manifest looks like this:"},"1795":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-54","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field  | Source                                    |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.rid` | `widgetSet.rid` in `foundry.config.json`. |","table":"table-5"},"1796":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-55","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field      | Source                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.version` | `widgetSet.autoVersion` in `foundry.config.json`; by default the `version` in `package.json`. See Versioning. |","table":"table-5"},"1797":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-56","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field | Source                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widgets.<id>` | One entry per HTML entrypoint, keyed by the config's `id`. Two widgets with the same ID fail the build with `Duplicate widget ID`. |","table":"table-5"},"1798":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-57","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field                                       | Source                  |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `id`, `name`, `description`, `events`, `permissions` | Copied from the config. |","table":"table-5"},"1799":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-58","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field | Source                                     |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `type`         | `\"workshop\"` becomes `\"workshopWidgetV1\"`. |","table":"table-5"},"1800":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-59","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field                  | Source                                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `entrypointJs`, `entrypointCss` | The script and stylesheet tags in the built HTML file, in order, with the leading `/` removed. |","table":"table-5"},"1801":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-60","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field | Source                                                                                                                                                          |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameters`   | Copied from the config, except `objectSet`: `allowedType` becomes the type's RID, and `objectTypeRids` holds the object type RID, or is empty for an interface. |","table":"table-5"},"1802":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-61","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field            | Source                                                                    |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `refreshHostDataOnAction` | The config's value, else the plugin's `defaults.refreshHostDataOnAction`. |","table":"table-5"},"1803":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-62","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field              | Source                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `inputSpec.discovered.sdks` | The `rid` and `version` of every installed package whose `package.json` has an `osdk.packageRid`. |","table":"table-5"},"1804":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-63","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"| Manifest field                        | Source                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `inputSpec.discovered.authorizations` | `authorizations.read` and `authorizations.requiredRead` from `resources.json` in the project root, when that file exists. |","table":"table-5"},"1805":{"id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events-64","page_id":"/widgets/parameters-and-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/parameters-and-events#how-the-config-maps-to-the-manifest","content":"Fields without a value, such as an unset `permissions`, are left out of the JSON. In developer mode the plugin sends Foundry the same widget entries, but with `entrypointJs` pointing at your dev server."},"1806":{"id":"/widgets/publish","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"page","content":"Build and publish","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Custom widgets"],"tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish"},"1807":{"id":"/widgets/publish-0","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish","content":"Configure @osdk/widget.vite-plugin, build a widget set and its manifest, deploy versions with osdk widgetset deploy, and manage them."},"1808":{"id":"/widgets/publish-1","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#add-the-vite-plugin","content":"Add the Vite plugin"},"1809":{"id":"/widgets/publish-2","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"How the plugin finds configs"},"1810":{"id":"/widgets/publish-3","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"Build multiple widgets"},"1811":{"id":"/widgets/publish-4","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"Build"},"1812":{"id":"/widgets/publish-5","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"`foundry.config.json`"},"1813":{"id":"/widgets/publish-6","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#versioning","content":"Versioning"},"1814":{"id":"/widgets/publish-7","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#deploy","content":"Deploy"},"1815":{"id":"/widgets/publish-8","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#build-1","content":"Build"},"1816":{"id":"/widgets/publish-9","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"Deploy"},"1817":{"id":"/widgets/publish-10","page_id":"/widgets/publish","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/publish#manage-versions","content":"Manage versions"},"1818":{"id":"/widgets/publish-11","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish","content":"Publishing a widget set takes two commands: `vite build` produces your widget files and a manifest, and `osdk widgetset deploy` uploads them to Foundry as a new version. This page covers the Vite plugin, `foundry.config.json`, versioning, and the CLI."},"1819":{"id":"/widgets/publish-12","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#add-the-vite-plugin","content":"`@osdk/widget.vite-plugin` writes the manifest during `vite build` and runs developer mode during `vite`. Projects from `@osdk/create-widget` already include it."},"1820":{"id":"/widgets/publish-13","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#add-the-vite-plugin","content":"The plugin supports Vite 6 and 7. It takes one optional argument:"},"1821":{"id":"/widgets/publish-14","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#add-the-vite-plugin","content":"| Option                             | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                           |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaults.refreshHostDataOnAction` | `boolean` |         | The `refreshHostDataOnAction` value for every widget whose config does not set it. See Config fields. |","table":"table-0"},"1822":{"id":"/widgets/publish-15","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"Each HTML file in `build.rollupOptions.input` is one widget. For each one, the plugin looks for a widget config among the modules its entry script imports:"},"1823":{"id":"/widgets/publish-16","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"The file name, minus its extension, ends in `.config`, such as `main.config.ts`."},"1824":{"id":"/widgets/publish-17","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"The file lives under `src/` and the entrypoint script imports it directly. Developer mode only tracks direct imports."},"1825":{"id":"/widgets/publish-18","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"The default export is the config from `defineConfig`."},"1826":{"id":"/widgets/publish-19","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#how-the-plugin-finds-configs","content":"If you do not need the config object at runtime, a side-effect import such as `import \"./main.config.js\";` is enough. Each entrypoint must import exactly one config."},"1827":{"id":"/widgets/publish-20","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"Add an HTML file per widget, each loading its own script that imports its own config:"},"1828":{"id":"/widgets/publish-21","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"index.html\" />"},"1829":{"id":"/widgets/publish-22","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"second.html\" />"},"1830":{"id":"/widgets/publish-23","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"vite.config.ts\" />"},"1831":{"id":"/widgets/publish-24","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"main.tsx\" />"},"1832":{"id":"/widgets/publish-25","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"main.config.ts\" />"},"1833":{"id":"/widgets/publish-26","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"second.tsx\" />"},"1834":{"id":"/widgets/publish-27","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"<File name=\"second.config.ts\" />"},"1835":{"id":"/widgets/publish-28","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"Then list every HTML file as a build input. Both the array and object forms of `input` work:"},"1836":{"id":"/widgets/publish-29","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build-multiple-widgets","content":"The build writes one manifest with an entry per widget, keyed by each config's `id`, so every widget in the set needs a different ID."},"1837":{"id":"/widgets/publish-30","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"The template's `build` script runs `tsc && vite build`. Vite writes your HTML, scripts, and styles to its output directory, `dist/` by default, and the plugin then adds the manifest:"},"1838":{"id":"/widgets/publish-31","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"<File name=\"index.html\" />"},"1839":{"id":"/widgets/publish-32","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"<File name=\"index-[hash].js\" />"},"1840":{"id":"/widgets/publish-33","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"<File name=\"index-[hash].css\" />"},"1841":{"id":"/widgets/publish-34","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"<File name=\"widgets.config.json\" />"},"1842":{"id":"/widgets/publish-35","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"To write the manifest, the plugin reads each built HTML file for its script and stylesheet tags, evaluates each widget config in a separate Vite server, computes the version, and scans `package.json` dependencies for SDK packages. Parameters and events shows the result field by field."},"1843":{"id":"/widgets/publish-36","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"Build errors from the plugin:"},"1844":{"id":"/widgets/publish-37","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                 | Cause                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `foundry.config.json file not found.` | No `foundry.config.json` in the working directory or any parent. |","table":"table-1"},"1845":{"id":"/widgets/publish-38","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                             | Cause                                               |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `No widget config files found for entrypoint ...` | The entrypoint does not import a `*.config` module. |","table":"table-1"},"1846":{"id":"/widgets/publish-39","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                                   | Cause                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Multiple widget config files found for entrypoint ...` | The entrypoint's bundle includes more than one `*.config` module. |","table":"table-1"},"1847":{"id":"/widgets/publish-40","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                            | Cause                                  |\n| -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `No default export found in ...` | The config file has no default export. |","table":"table-1"},"1848":{"id":"/widgets/publish-41","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                      | Cause                      |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `Duplicate widget ID: ...` | Two configs share an `id`. |","table":"table-1"},"1849":{"id":"/widgets/publish-42","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                            | Cause                                                                                              |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Entrypoint chunk not found for input file: ...` | The built HTML's script paths do not match a bundle entry. Keep Vite's `base` at its default, `/`. |","table":"table-1"},"1850":{"id":"/widgets/publish-43","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                                 | Cause                                                                                      |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `Unexpected inline content found in Vite HTML output` | The built HTML has an inline `<script>` or `<link>` with content. Load scripts with `src`. |","table":"table-1"},"1851":{"id":"/widgets/publish-44","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                                | Cause                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Unexpected ... attribute found in Vite HTML output` | A `<script>` has attributes other than `src`, `type`, and `crossorigin`, or a stylesheet `<link>` has attributes other than `rel`, `href`, and `crossorigin`. |","table":"table-1"},"1852":{"id":"/widgets/publish-45","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                                          | Cause                                                         |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Invalid script type attribute found in Vite HTML output: ...` | A `<script>` `type` other than `module` or `text/javascript`. |","table":"table-1"},"1853":{"id":"/widgets/publish-46","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"| Error                                             | Cause                                                     |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `The version string ... is not SemVer compliant.` | The computed version is not valid SemVer. See Versioning. |","table":"table-1"},"1854":{"id":"/widgets/publish-47","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#build","content":"Config validation errors, such as a widget ID that is not camelCase, are listed in Parameters and events."},"1855":{"id":"/widgets/publish-48","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"The plugin and `osdk widgetset` commands read `foundry.config.json` from the working directory or the nearest parent. `@osdk/create-widget` writes it for you:"},"1856":{"id":"/widgets/publish-49","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field        | Type     | Default  | Description                                                        |\n| ------------ | -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `foundryUrl` | `string` | Required | Your Foundry stack. Developer mode and the CLI send requests here. |","table":"table-2"},"1857":{"id":"/widgets/publish-50","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field           | Type     | Default  | Description                                                                |\n| --------------- | -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.rid` | `string` | Required | The widget set RID, written to the manifest and used as the deploy target. |","table":"table-2"},"1858":{"id":"/widgets/publish-51","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field                 | Type     | Default  | Description                                              |\n| --------------------- | -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.directory` | `string` | Required | The build output to deploy. Match Vite's `build.outDir`. |","table":"table-2"},"1859":{"id":"/widgets/publish-52","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field                  | Type     | Default | Description                                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.repository` | `string` |         | A code repository RID to publish through instead of the widget set. See Deploy. |","table":"table-2"},"1860":{"id":"/widgets/publish-53","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"| Field                   | Type                                                                         | Default        | Description                         |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `widgetSet.autoVersion` | `{ type: \"package-json\" }` or `{ type: \"git-describe\", tagPrefix?: string }` | `package-json` | How the build computes the version. |","table":"table-2"},"1861":{"id":"/widgets/publish-54","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#foundryconfigjson","content":"The file is validated on load. Unknown top-level fields fail with `does not match the expected schema`."},"1862":{"id":"/widgets/publish-55","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#versioning","content":"Every deployed version needs a SemVer version string. The build computes it once and writes it to the manifest's `widgetSet.version`; `osdk widgetset deploy` reads it from there and has no version flag."},"1863":{"id":"/widgets/publish-56","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#versioning","content":"The default. The version is the `version` field of the nearest `package.json`. Bump it, then rebuild before you deploy:"},"1864":{"id":"/widgets/publish-57","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#versioning","content":"The version comes from `git describe --tags --first-parent --dirty`:"},"1865":{"id":"/widgets/publish-58","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#versioning","content":"With an empty `tagPrefix`, the build uses the most recent tag reachable from `HEAD` and strips a leading `v`, so `v1.4.0` becomes `1.4.0`. With a prefix such as `widgets/`, it only matches tags that start with the prefix and strips it, so `widgets/1.4.0` becomes `1.4.0`. Commits after the tag and uncommitted changes add a suffix such as `1.4.0-3-g1a2b3c4-dirty`. The build fails if git is missing, the directory is not a repository, or no tag matches."},"1866":{"id":"/widgets/publish-59","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy","content":"`osdk widgetset deploy` from `@osdk/cli` zips the build output and publishes it as a new version."},"1867":{"id":"/widgets/publish-60","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"The CLI reads the version from `.palantir/widgets.config.json` in the directory, zips everything in the directory, and uploads it. When `repository` is set, it uploads to that code repository on behalf of the widget set, which works only if the repository is authorized to publish the widget set. It passes the current git branch along, unless HEAD is detached or the project is not a git repository."},"1868":{"id":"/widgets/publish-61","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"Every option defaults to the matching `foundry.config.json` field where one exists:"},"1869":{"id":"/widgets/publish-62","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option        | Default         | Description         |\n| ------------- | --------------- | ------------------- |\n| `--widgetSet` | `widgetSet.rid` | The widget set RID. |","table":"table-3"},"1870":{"id":"/widgets/publish-63","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option         | Default      | Description                                  |\n| -------------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `--foundryUrl` | `foundryUrl` | The Foundry URL. Must start with `https://`. |","table":"table-3"},"1871":{"id":"/widgets/publish-64","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option        | Default               | Description                                                               |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--directory` | `widgetSet.directory` | The directory to upload. It must contain `.palantir/widgets.config.json`. |","table":"table-3"},"1872":{"id":"/widgets/publish-65","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option         | Default                | Description                               |\n| -------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `--repository` | `widgetSet.repository` | A code repository RID to publish through. |","table":"table-3"},"1873":{"id":"/widgets/publish-66","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option         | Default                | Description                 |\n| -------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `--branchName` | The current git branch | The branch to publish from. |","table":"table-3"},"1874":{"id":"/widgets/publish-67","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option    | Default | Description                                    |\n| --------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `--token` |         | A Foundry token. Conflicts with `--tokenFile`. |","table":"table-3"},"1875":{"id":"/widgets/publish-68","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option        | Default | Description                        |\n| ------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `--tokenFile` |         | A file containing a Foundry token. |","table":"table-3"},"1876":{"id":"/widgets/publish-69","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"| Option            | Default | Description                       |\n| ----------------- | ------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `--verbose`, `-v` |         | Verbose logging. Repeat for more. |","table":"table-3"},"1877":{"id":"/widgets/publish-70","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"Without `--token` or `--tokenFile`, the CLI reads `FOUNDRY_TOKEN`. The deprecated `FOUNDRY_SDK_AUTH_TOKEN` still works with a warning. The token must be a JWT."},"1878":{"id":"/widgets/publish-71","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#deploy-1","content":"After the first version is published, the widget appears in Workshop's **Widget setup** panel. Until then you can still preview it with developer mode."},"1879":{"id":"/widgets/publish-72","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#manage-versions","content":"The same options select the widget set and credentials:"},"1880":{"id":"/widgets/publish-73","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#manage-versions","content":"| Command                       | Description                                                                           |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk widgetset version list` | Lists published versions, newest first, for the current git branch or `--branchName`. |","table":"table-4"},"1881":{"id":"/widgets/publish-74","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#manage-versions","content":"| Command                                 | Description                                |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `osdk widgetset version info <version>` | Prints the details of one version as JSON. |","table":"table-4"},"1882":{"id":"/widgets/publish-75","page_id":"/widgets/publish","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/publish#manage-versions","content":"| Command                                   | Description                                                                                                 |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `osdk widgetset version delete <version>` | Deletes a version after a confirmation prompt. `--yes` or `-y` skips the prompt. Deletion cannot be undone. |","table":"table-4"},"1883":{"id":"/widgets/react","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"page","content":"React widgets","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Guides","Custom widgets"],"tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react"},"1884":{"id":"/widgets/react-0","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react","content":"Render a widget with FoundryWidget, read typed parameters and loading states with useFoundryWidgetContext, and emit events back to the host."},"1885":{"id":"/widgets/react-1","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#install","content":"Install"},"1886":{"id":"/widgets/react-2","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Render `FoundryWidget`"},"1887":{"id":"/widgets/react-3","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"Read parameters"},"1888":{"id":"/widgets/react-4","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"Loading states"},"1889":{"id":"/widgets/react-5","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#emit-events","content":"Emit events"},"1890":{"id":"/widgets/react-6","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"Object set parameters"},"1891":{"id":"/widgets/react-7","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#listen-to-host-messages","content":"Listen to host messages"},"1892":{"id":"/widgets/react-8","page_id":"/widgets/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/widgets/react#render-outside-foundry","content":"Render outside Foundry"},"1893":{"id":"/widgets/react-9","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react","content":"`@osdk/widget.client-react` connects a React tree to the Foundry host. `FoundryWidget` handles the message protocol, and `useFoundryWidgetContext` gives every component typed parameter values and an `emitEvent` function derived from your widget config."},"1894":{"id":"/widgets/react-10","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#install","content":"Projects from `@osdk/create-widget` already include these packages. To add them to an existing Vite and React project:"},"1895":{"id":"/widgets/react-11","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#install","content":"`@osdk/widget.client-react` supports React 18 and 19 and lists `@osdk/client` as a peer dependency. Add `@osdk/client`, `@osdk/react`, and your SDK package to call the Ontology."},"1896":{"id":"/widgets/react-12","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Wrap the widget's root in `FoundryWidget` and pass its config. Importing the config in the entrypoint is also what lets the Vite plugin find it."},"1897":{"id":"/widgets/react-13","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"| Prop     | Type                              | Default  | Description                                                                     |\n| -------- | --------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `config` | The return type of `defineConfig` | Required | The widget config. Every parameter and event type in the context comes from it. |","table":"table-0"},"1898":{"id":"/widgets/react-14","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"| Prop       | Type              | Default  | Description |\n| ---------- | ----------------- | -------- | ----------- |\n| `children` | `React.ReactNode` | Required | The widget. |","table":"table-0"},"1899":{"id":"/widgets/react-15","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"| Prop     | Type                         | Default | Description                                                                                                                                                      |\n| -------- | ---------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `client` | `Client` from `@osdk/client` |         | An OSDK client, used to hydrate object set parameters and to serialize object sets you emit. Required by the types when the config has an `objectSet` parameter. |","table":"table-0"},"1900":{"id":"/widgets/react-16","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"| Prop            | Type                         | Default                       | Description                                                                |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------- | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `initialValues` | Async value per parameter ID | Every parameter `not-started` | Starting values for `asyncParameterValues` before the host's first update. |","table":"table-0"},"1901":{"id":"/widgets/react-17","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"On mount, `FoundryWidget`:"},"1902":{"id":"/widgets/react-18","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Subscribes to host messages and sends `widget.ready`, so the host sends the first parameter values."},"1903":{"id":"/widgets/react-19","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Observes the size of `document.body` and sends `widget.resize` with its border-box width and height on every change."},"1904":{"id":"/widgets/react-20","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Sends `widget.reload` before a Vite full-page reload in development."},"1905":{"id":"/widgets/react-21","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Wraps `children` in an error boundary. An uncaught render error shows its stack trace, plus troubleshooting tips when `NODE_ENV` is not `production`. Add your own error boundary inside `FoundryWidget` to show a custom message instead."},"1906":{"id":"/widgets/react-22","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-foundrywidget","content":"Render one `FoundryWidget` per widget, at the root. It creates the widget client once, when it mounts."},"1907":{"id":"/widgets/react-23","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"`useFoundryWidgetContext` returns the context for the nearest `FoundryWidget`. The context is not generic at runtime, so bind your config's type once with `withTypes` and import that hook everywhere:"},"1908":{"id":"/widgets/react-24","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"`useFoundryWidgetContext<typeof MainConfig>()` is equivalent. Outside a `FoundryWidget`, the hook returns a default context; see Render outside Foundry."},"1909":{"id":"/widgets/react-25","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"| Field               | Type                                 | Description                                                                                                              |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `parameters.values` | Each parameter's value, all optional | The latest values, typed from the config: `headerText` is `string \\| undefined`, `todoItems` is `string[] \\| undefined`. |","table":"table-1"},"1910":{"id":"/widgets/react-26","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"| Field              | Type                                                                | Description                                                        |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `parameters.state` | `\"not-started\" \\| \"loading\" \\| \"loaded\" \\| \"reloading\" \\| \"failed\"` | One loading state for the widget's parameters. See Loading states. |","table":"table-1"},"1911":{"id":"/widgets/react-27","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"| Field                  | Type                                                                  | Description                                                                             |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `asyncParameterValues` | Per parameter ID: `{ type, value }`, where `value` is an `AsyncValue` | The individual state of each parameter, for widgets that load parameters independently. |","table":"table-1"},"1912":{"id":"/widgets/react-28","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"| Field       | Type                                      | Description                                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `emitEvent` | `(eventId, { parameterUpdates }) => void` | Sends one of the config's events. See Emit events. |","table":"table-1"},"1913":{"id":"/widgets/react-29","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#read-parameters","content":"| Field             | Type                     | Description                                                   |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hostEventTarget` | `FoundryHostEventTarget` | The raw stream of host messages. See Listen to host messages. |","table":"table-1"},"1914":{"id":"/widgets/react-30","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"`parameters.state` summarizes the parameters in the host's most recent update, in this order of precedence:"},"1915":{"id":"/widgets/react-31","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"| State      | When                                                                        |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"failed\"` | Any parameter failed. `parameters.values` keeps the values that did arrive. |","table":"table-2"},"1916":{"id":"/widgets/react-32","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"| State       | When                                         |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"loading\"` | Any parameter is loading for the first time. |","table":"table-2"},"1917":{"id":"/widgets/react-33","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"| State         | When                                                             |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"reloading\"` | Any parameter is reloading. Values keep their previous contents. |","table":"table-2"},"1918":{"id":"/widgets/react-34","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"| State           | When                                   |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `\"not-started\"` | Any parameter has not started loading. |","table":"table-2"},"1919":{"id":"/widgets/react-35","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"| State      | When                    |\n| ---------- | ----------------------- |\n| `\"loaded\"` | Every parameter loaded. |","table":"table-2"},"1920":{"id":"/widgets/react-36","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"While the state is `not-started` or `loading`, `parameters.values` is `{}`, so give every read a fallback and keep rendering. Show progress next to the content instead of replacing it:"},"1921":{"id":"/widgets/react-37","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#loading-states","content":"To react to one parameter without waiting on the others, read `asyncParameterValues`:"},"1922":{"id":"/widgets/react-38","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#emit-events","content":"`emitEvent(eventId, { parameterUpdates })` sends a `widget.emit-event` message. TypeScript limits `eventId` to the config's events and requires a value for every ID in the event's `parameterUpdateIds`. The call returns nothing and does not report whether the host acted on the event."},"1923":{"id":"/widgets/react-39","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#emit-events","content":"In the example above, `handleAdd` emits `updateTodoItems` with the new list. The widget does not keep its own copy: when the host writes the update to the variable bound to `todoItems`, the new list arrives through `parameters.values` and the widget re-renders. The template's counter works the same way, reading `counterValue` and emitting `setCounterValue` with the next number."},"1924":{"id":"/widgets/react-40","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"For an `objectSet` parameter, the host sends an object set RID. Pass an OSDK `client` to `FoundryWidget`, and the value in `parameters.values` gains an `objectSet` you can query, typed by the parameter's `allowedType`."},"1925":{"id":"/widgets/react-41","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"Query the set with `useObjectSet` from `@osdk/react`. Hydrated object sets are cached per parameter, so the `objectSet` reference only changes when the host sends a new RID, and it is safe to pass straight to hooks. To emit an object set, pass an `ObjectSet` from `@osdk/client`:"},"1926":{"id":"/widgets/react-42","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"`emitEvent` turns each `ObjectSet` into a temporary object set RID with an extra request before it sends the event. Because of that step:"},"1927":{"id":"/widgets/react-43","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"If you emit the same event again before the request finishes, only the last call is sent."},"1928":{"id":"/widgets/react-44","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"Errors, such as a failed request, are not reported to the caller."},"1929":{"id":"/widgets/react-45","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"Emitting an object set without a `client` on `FoundryWidget` fails, and so does receiving one."},"1930":{"id":"/widgets/react-46","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#object-set-parameters","content":"See Work with object sets for filtering, pivoting, and combining the sets you receive."},"1931":{"id":"/widgets/react-47","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#listen-to-host-messages","content":"`hostEventTarget` dispatches every `host.update-parameters` message, with the raw payload in `event.detail`. Use it to log or react to updates beyond what `parameters` exposes:"},"1932":{"id":"/widgets/react-48","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-outside-foundry","content":"`FoundryWidget` needs the host API that Foundry injects. Outside Foundry and developer mode, it throws `Invariant failed: [FoundryWidgetClient] Missing __PALANTIR_WIDGET_API__ in window` when it renders."},"1933":{"id":"/widgets/react-49","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-outside-foundry","content":"Components below it still render on their own: without a `FoundryWidget` ancestor, `useFoundryWidgetContext` returns a default context whose `parameters.state` is `not-started`, whose `parameters.values` is `{}`, and whose `emitEvent` does nothing. Because widget components already handle empty values, you can render them directly in unit tests and Storybook."},"1934":{"id":"/widgets/react-50","page_id":"/widgets/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/widgets/react#render-outside-foundry","content":"To start `asyncParameterValues` in a known state before the host's first update, pass `initialValues` to `FoundryWidget`. It does not affect `parameters.values` or `parameters.state`, which stay `{}` and `not-started` until the first `host.update-parameters` message."},"1935":{"id":"/ai/agents","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"page","content":"Agents","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","Build with AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents"},"1936":{"id":"/ai/agents-0","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"Converse with AIP Agents through the Platform SDK, start sessions for agents in your generated SDK, and read injected clients with @osdk/agents."},"1937":{"id":"/ai/agents-1","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"Chat with an AIP Agent"},"1938":{"id":"/ai/agents-2","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"Send a message"},"1939":{"id":"/ai/agents-3","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#stream-the-answer","content":"Stream the answer"},"1940":{"id":"/ai/agents-4","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"Start a session for a generated agent"},"1941":{"id":"/ai/agents-5","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#send-events-to-a-session","content":"Send events to a session"},"1942":{"id":"/ai/agents-6","page_id":"/ai/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"Reach the clients from agent code"},"1943":{"id":"/ai/agents-7","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"An agent is configured in Foundry and runs its own model calls, tools, and retrieval; your app sends it input and reads its answers. Use this page to call an AIP Agent built in AIP Agent Studio, to start a session for an agent included in your generated SDK, or to reach the OSDK clients from code inside an agent."},"1944":{"id":"/ai/agents-8","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"Every API on this page is pre-release. The AIP Agents platform endpoints are marked beta, the generated-SDK session method is `experimental_createSession`, the Agents session endpoints are marked alpha, and `@osdk/agents` is at version 0.x with its client helpers under `/experimental`."},"1945":{"id":"/ai/agents-9","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"| You want to                                  | Use                                       |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Chat with an agent built in AIP Agent Studio | `Sessions` from `@osdk/foundry.aipagents` |","table":"table-0"},"1946":{"id":"/ai/agents-10","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"| You want to                                             | Use                                                              |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Start a session for an agent your generated SDK exports | `client(agent).experimental_createSession()` from `@osdk/client` |","table":"table-0"},"1947":{"id":"/ai/agents-11","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"| You want to                                           | Use                                            |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| Call the Ontology from code that runs inside an agent | `getClient()` from `@osdk/agents/experimental` |","table":"table-0"},"1948":{"id":"/ai/agents-12","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"| You want to                                           | Use                         |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Chat with a language model directly, without an agent | `generateText` or `useChat` |","table":"table-0"},"1949":{"id":"/ai/agents-13","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents","content":"The `AipAgentChat` component chats with a language model, not with an AIP Agent."},"1950":{"id":"/ai/agents-14","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"`@osdk/foundry.aipagents` is the Platform SDK package for AIP Agents. It works with the `Client` from `createClient` or a `PlatformClient`; see Platform SDK setup."},"1951":{"id":"/ai/agents-15","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"| Function                                               | Required scope         | Description                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Sessions.create(client, agentRid, { agentVersion? })` | `api:aip-agents-write` | Starts a session. Omit `agentVersion` for the latest published version. |","table":"table-1"},"1952":{"id":"/ai/agents-16","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"| Function                                                        | Required scope         | Description                                        |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Sessions.blockingContinue(client, agentRid, sessionRid, body)` | `api:aip-agents-write` | Sends a message and resolves with the full answer. |","table":"table-1"},"1953":{"id":"/ai/agents-17","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"| Function                                                         | Required scope         | Description                                                                                    |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Sessions.streamingContinue(client, agentRid, sessionRid, body)` | `api:aip-agents-write` | Sends a message and resolves with a `Response` whose body streams the answer as Markdown text. |","table":"table-1"},"1954":{"id":"/ai/agents-18","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"| Function                                                                  | Required scope         | Description                                                   |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Sessions.cancel(client, agentRid, sessionRid, { messageId, response? })` | `api:aip-agents-write` | Cancels a streamed exchange, optionally replacing the answer. |","table":"table-1"},"1955":{"id":"/ai/agents-19","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"| Function                                                                        | Required scope        | Description                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `Sessions.list(client, agentRid)`, `Sessions.get(client, agentRid, sessionRid)` | `api:aip-agents-read` | Reads sessions this client created. |","table":"table-1"},"1956":{"id":"/ai/agents-20","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#chat-with-an-aip-agent","content":"Each function takes query parameters as its last argument. Pass `{ preview: true }` while the endpoints are in beta. Find the agent RID in AIP Agent Studio."},"1957":{"id":"/ai/agents-21","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"| Request field | Type               | Description         |\n| ------------- | ------------------ | ------------------- |\n| `userInput`   | `{ text: string }` | The user's message. |","table":"table-2"},"1958":{"id":"/ai/agents-22","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"| Request field     | Type                             | Description                                                             |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameterInputs` | `Record<string, ParameterValue>` | Values for the agent's application variables. Pass `{}` if it has none. |","table":"table-2"},"1959":{"id":"/ai/agents-23","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"| Request field      | Type                  | Description                                                     |\n| ------------------ | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contextsOverride` | `Array<InputContext>` | Replaces the context the agent would retrieve for this message. |","table":"table-2"},"1960":{"id":"/ai/agents-24","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"| Request field | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `messageId`   | `string` | Streaming only. An id you choose, so you can cancel the exchange. |","table":"table-2"},"1961":{"id":"/ai/agents-25","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"| Request field    | Type     | Description                      |\n| ---------------- | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `sessionTraceId` | `string` | An id for tracing this exchange. |","table":"table-2"},"1962":{"id":"/ai/agents-26","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-a-message","content":"`blockingContinue` resolves with `agentMarkdownResponse`, `parameterUpdates`, `totalTokensUsed`, `interruptedOutput`, and `sessionTraceId`."},"1963":{"id":"/ai/agents-27","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#stream-the-answer","content":"`streamingContinue` resolves with a `Response`. Read its body as text:"},"1964":{"id":"/ai/agents-28","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#stream-the-answer","content":"A session handles one exchange at a time: wait for the answer, or cancel it with `Sessions.cancel` and the same `messageId`, before sending the next message. Cancelling does not close the stream, so also stop reading it."},"1965":{"id":"/ai/agents-29","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"When your generated SDK includes agents, it exports each one alongside your object types, and all of them as `$Agents`. Pass one to the client and call `experimental_createSession` with the agent's arguments:"},"1966":{"id":"/ai/agents-30","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"| Behavior  | Details                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Arguments | A record keyed by argument name. OSDK objects and object sets are converted to the agent's argument types, including nested values. Omit the argument for agents that take none. |","table":"table-3"},"1967":{"id":"/ai/agents-31","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"| Behavior     | Details                                  |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------- |\n| Return value | `AgentSession`, with the session's `id`. |","table":"table-3"},"1968":{"id":"/ai/agents-32","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"| Behavior | Details                                                                                                          |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Version  | The version pinned in your generated SDK. Override it with `client({ ...employeeAssistant, version: \"2.0.0\" })`. |","table":"table-3"},"1969":{"id":"/ai/agents-33","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"| Behavior            | Details                                                                       |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Unsupported clients | Throws before sending a request on branch, scenario, and transaction clients. |","table":"table-3"},"1970":{"id":"/ai/agents-34","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"| Behavior | Details                                                                                      |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Scopes   | Loads the agent definition (`api:agents-read`) and creates the session (`api:agents-write`). |","table":"table-3"},"1971":{"id":"/ai/agents-35","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#start-a-session-for-a-generated-agent","content":"Creating a session runs agent logic and can modify platform data."},"1972":{"id":"/ai/agents-36","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-to-a-session","content":"After creation, interact with the session through `AgentSessions` in `@osdk/foundry.agents`. These endpoints are alpha and take `{ preview: true }`."},"1973":{"id":"/ai/agents-37","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-to-a-session","content":"| Function                                  | Description                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sendEvent(client, sessionId, { event })` | Sends an event of a type the agent declared when it was published. `result.type` is `\"accepted\"`, with a `consistencyKey`, or `\"sessionNotReady\"`; retry the latter after a short delay. |","table":"table-4"},"1974":{"id":"/ai/agents-38","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-to-a-session","content":"| Function                                                  | Description                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getSessionState(client, sessionId, { consistencyKey? })` | Reads the session. `type` is `\"available\"`, with `status`, `agentState`, `arguments`, and context items; `\"behind\"` when it has not yet caught up to `consistencyKey`; or `\"notReady\"`. |","table":"table-4"},"1975":{"id":"/ai/agents-39","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-to-a-session","content":"| Function                 | Description                                |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `get(client, sessionId)` | Reads the session's agent RID and version. |","table":"table-4"},"1976":{"id":"/ai/agents-40","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#send-events-to-a-session","content":"The event types and payload shapes are defined by the agent, so check its published definition."},"1977":{"id":"/ai/agents-41","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"`@osdk/agents` is for code that runs inside a Foundry agent, not for apps that call one. Foundry injects an Ontology `Client` and a `PlatformClient` into each invocation; `@osdk/agents/experimental` reads them."},"1978":{"id":"/ai/agents-42","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"| Export        | Description                                                                                                  |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `getClient()` | The Ontology SDK `Client` for the current invocation. Throws if no Ontology is imported into the repository. |","table":"table-5"},"1979":{"id":"/ai/agents-43","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"| Export                | Description                                      |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `getPlatformClient()` | The `PlatformClient` for the current invocation. |","table":"table-5"},"1980":{"id":"/ai/agents-44","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"| Export                      | Description                                                        |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `withClients(clients, run)` | Runs `run` with `clients` as the current clients. Use it in tests. |","table":"table-5"},"1981":{"id":"/ai/agents-45","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"| Export                                          | Description                                                                                     |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ScopeResources`, `ScopeAuthorization`, `Scope` | Resource and authorization scope declarations, re-exported from `@osdk/functions/experimental`. |","table":"table-5"},"1982":{"id":"/ai/agents-46","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"The `AgentConfig` type from `@osdk/agents` describes the `export const config` an agent declares alongside its code: `locator: string`, plus optional `apiName`, `sources: Array<string>`, and an experimental `scope`."},"1983":{"id":"/ai/agents-47","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"The clients exist only while an invocation runs. Call `getClient()` and `getPlatformClient()` inside your handlers, not at module load and not from work that outlives the invocation."},"1984":{"id":"/ai/agents-48","page_id":"/ai/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/agents#reach-the-clients-from-agent-code","content":"To call a language model from agent code, pass `getPlatformClient()` to `foundryModel`."},"1985":{"id":"/ai/chat","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"page","content":"Generate and stream text","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","Build with AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat"},"1986":{"id":"/ai/chat-0","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat","content":"Call Foundry-hosted language models with generateText and streamText from @osdk/aip-core, in Node.js or the browser."},"1987":{"id":"/ai/chat-1","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#install","content":"Install"},"1988":{"id":"/ai/chat-2","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#create-a-model","content":"Create a model"},"1989":{"id":"/ai/chat-3","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"Model identifiers"},"1990":{"id":"/ai/chat-4","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#generate-text","content":"Generate text"},"1991":{"id":"/ai/chat-5","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"Prompts, messages, and system instructions"},"1992":{"id":"/ai/chat-6","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#stream-text","content":"Stream text"},"1993":{"id":"/ai/chat-7","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"Stream result"},"1994":{"id":"/ai/chat-8","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"Sampling options"},"1995":{"id":"/ai/chat-9","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#cancel-a-request","content":"Cancel a request"},"1996":{"id":"/ai/chat-10","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"Usage and finish reason"},"1997":{"id":"/ai/chat-11","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"Errors and warnings"},"1998":{"id":"/ai/chat-12","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"Use the AI SDK"},"1999":{"id":"/ai/chat-13","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"Call a provider SDK directly"},"2000":{"id":"/ai/chat-14","page_id":"/ai/chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/chat#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"2001":{"id":"/ai/chat-15","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat","content":"`@osdk/aip-core` sends chat completions to the Foundry Language Model Service (LMS) with the same auth, governance, and usage tracking as the rest of your OSDK app. Use `generateText` for a complete answer and `streamText` to render tokens as they arrive."},"2002":{"id":"/ai/chat-16","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat","content":"`@osdk/aip-core` is at version 0.x, and its API can change in any minor release. The current release runs one model call per request: there is no built-in multi-step tool loop, no structured (JSON) output, and only text content parts are sent. Image and file parts are dropped with a warning."},"2003":{"id":"/ai/chat-17","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#install","content":"`@osdk/client` is a peer dependency. `@osdk/aip-core` brings in `@osdk/language-models` itself."},"2004":{"id":"/ai/chat-18","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#create-a-model","content":"Every call takes a model handle from `foundryModel`. It needs a `PlatformClient` from `createPlatformClient` and the model's LMS API name."},"2005":{"id":"/ai/chat-19","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#create-a-model","content":"Pass a client from `createPlatformClient`, not the `Client` from `createClient`: `foundryModel` reads `baseUrl`, `fetch`, and `tokenProvider` from the client, and an Ontology `Client` does not expose them. Reuse the same token provider for both clients so the user signs in once."},"2006":{"id":"/ai/chat-20","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#create-a-model","content":"OAuth applications must request the `api:use-language-models-execute` scope. The default scopes of `createPublicOauthClient` do not include it, so list every scope your app needs. See Authentication for the other token providers."},"2007":{"id":"/ai/chat-21","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"`model` accepts an API name string or a `ModelIdentifier`:"},"2008":{"id":"/ai/chat-22","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"| Value    | Example    | Use it for                                                                        |\n| -------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `string` | `\"gpt-4o\"` | A built-in LMS model, by API name. Shorthand for `{ type: \"lmsModel\", apiName }`. |","table":"table-0"},"2009":{"id":"/ai/chat-23","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"| Value                           | Example                                   | Use it for             |\n| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"lmsModel\", apiName }` | `{ type: \"lmsModel\", apiName: \"gpt-4o\" }` | The same, spelled out. |","table":"table-0"},"2010":{"id":"/ai/chat-24","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"| Value                                             | Example                                                                           | Use it for                                       |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"registeredModel\", registeredModelRid }` | `{ type: \"registeredModel\", registeredModelRid: \"ri.language-model-service...\" }` | A model your organization registered in Foundry. |","table":"table-0"},"2011":{"id":"/ai/chat-25","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#model-identifiers","content":"Which models you can call depends on your enrollment. Look up API names in Model Catalog in Foundry. The handle's `modelId` is `foundry/<apiName or rid>`, useful for logging."},"2012":{"id":"/ai/chat-26","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#generate-text","content":"`generateText` sends one request and resolves with the full response."},"2013":{"id":"/ai/chat-27","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"Give the conversation as either `prompt` or `messages`. Passing both throws. At least one of `system`, `prompt`, or `messages` is required."},"2014":{"id":"/ai/chat-28","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| Option   | Type                            | Description                        |\n| -------- | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `prompt` | `string \\| Array<ModelMessage>` | A string becomes one user message. |","table":"table-1"},"2015":{"id":"/ai/chat-29","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| Option     | Type                  | Description                    |\n| ---------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `messages` | `Array<ModelMessage>` | The full conversation history. |","table":"table-1"},"2016":{"id":"/ai/chat-30","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| Option   | Type                                                        | Description                                                                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `system` | `string \\| SystemModelMessage \\| Array<SystemModelMessage>` | Instructions prepended before the conversation. An empty string is ignored. |","table":"table-1"},"2017":{"id":"/ai/chat-31","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"A `ModelMessage` is one of:"},"2018":{"id":"/ai/chat-32","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| `role`     | `content` |\n| ---------- | --------- |\n| `\"system\"` | `string`  |","table":"table-2"},"2019":{"id":"/ai/chat-33","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| `role`   | `content`                                                                                                           |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"user\"` | `string`, or an array of `{ type: \"text\", text }` parts. Image and file parts are accepted by the type but dropped. |","table":"table-2"},"2020":{"id":"/ai/chat-34","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| `role`        | `content`                                            |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"assistant\"` | `string`, or an array of text and `tool-call` parts. |","table":"table-2"},"2021":{"id":"/ai/chat-35","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"| `role`   | `content`                                          |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"tool\"` | An array of `tool-result` parts. See Tool calling. |","table":"table-2"},"2022":{"id":"/ai/chat-36","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#prompts-messages-and-system-instructions","content":"To hold a multi-turn conversation, keep the history and append each answer before the next question:"},"2023":{"id":"/ai/chat-37","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-text","content":"`streamText` returns immediately and starts the request. Read tokens from `textStream`, or every event from `fullStream`. The other fields are promises that resolve when the stream ends."},"2024":{"id":"/ai/chat-38","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-text","content":"Use `getReader()` in browsers: not every browser supports `for await` over a `ReadableStream`."},"2025":{"id":"/ai/chat-39","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field        | Type                     | Description       |\n| ------------ | ------------------------ | ----------------- |\n| `textStream` | `ReadableStream<string>` | Text deltas only. |","table":"table-3"},"2026":{"id":"/ai/chat-40","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field        | Type                              | Description                |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `fullStream` | `ReadableStream<TextStreamChunk>` | Every event, listed below. |","table":"table-3"},"2027":{"id":"/ai/chat-41","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field  | Type              | Description      |\n| ------ | ----------------- | ---------------- |\n| `text` | `Promise<string>` | The full answer. |","table":"table-3"},"2028":{"id":"/ai/chat-42","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field           | Type                           | Description                                |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `reasoningText` | `Promise<string \\| undefined>` | Reasoning text, for models that return it. |","table":"table-3"},"2029":{"id":"/ai/chat-43","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field       | Type                       | Description                        |\n| ----------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `toolCalls` | `Promise<Array<ToolCall>>` | Tool calls requested by the model. |","table":"table-3"},"2030":{"id":"/ai/chat-44","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field          | Type                    | Description             |\n| -------------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `finishReason` | `Promise<FinishReason>` | Why generation stopped. |","table":"table-3"},"2031":{"id":"/ai/chat-45","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field                 | Type                          | Description                                               |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `usage`, `totalUsage` | `Promise<LanguageModelUsage>` | Token counts. Identical while each call is a single step. |","table":"table-3"},"2032":{"id":"/ai/chat-46","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field      | Type                                   | Description                                          |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `warnings` | `Promise<Array<Warning> \\| undefined>` | Ignored inputs. Resolves even when the stream fails. |","table":"table-3"},"2033":{"id":"/ai/chat-47","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| Field                 | Type                                                                              | Description                                                                          |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `request`, `response` | `Promise<RequestMetadata \\| undefined>`, `Promise<ResponseMetadata \\| undefined>` | The request body sent, and the response id, model, timestamp, and assistant message. |","table":"table-3"},"2034":{"id":"/ai/chat-48","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"`fullStream` emits these `TextStreamChunk` events:"},"2035":{"id":"/ai/chat-49","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| `type`         | Fields        | When                       |\n| -------------- | ------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `\"text-delta\"` | `id`, `delta` | Each piece of answer text. |","table":"table-4"},"2036":{"id":"/ai/chat-50","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| `type`              | Fields        | When                          |\n| ------------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `\"reasoning-delta\"` | `id`, `delta` | Each piece of reasoning text. |","table":"table-4"},"2037":{"id":"/ai/chat-51","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| `type`        | Fields                            | When                                                                         |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"tool-call\"` | `toolCallId`, `toolName`, `input` | Once per tool call, after the model finishes, with `input` parsed from JSON. |","table":"table-4"},"2038":{"id":"/ai/chat-52","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| `type`     | Fields                                     | When              |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------ | ----------------- |\n| `\"finish\"` | `finishReason`, `rawFinishReason`, `usage` | Once, at the end. |","table":"table-4"},"2039":{"id":"/ai/chat-53","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"| `type`    | Fields  | When                                                                        |\n| --------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"error\"` | `error` | The request or stream failed. The stream then errors with the same `Error`. |","table":"table-4"},"2040":{"id":"/ai/chat-54","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#stream-result","content":"`streamText` also takes `onChunk`, `onError`, and `onFinish` callbacks. `onFinish` receives `finishReason`, `text`, `reasoningText`, `toolCalls`, `usage`, `totalUsage`, `warnings`, `request`, and `response`."},"2041":{"id":"/ai/chat-55","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"`generateText` and `streamText` share these options:"},"2042":{"id":"/ai/chat-56","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option            | Type     | Description                 |\n| ----------------- | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| `maxOutputTokens` | `number` | Maximum tokens to generate. |","table":"table-5"},"2043":{"id":"/ai/chat-57","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option        | Type     | Description                                |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `temperature` | `number` | Randomness. `0` is the most deterministic. |","table":"table-5"},"2044":{"id":"/ai/chat-58","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option | Type     | Description                 |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| `topP` | `number` | Nucleus sampling threshold. |","table":"table-5"},"2045":{"id":"/ai/chat-59","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option            | Type     | Description                                 |\n| ----------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `presencePenalty` | `number` | Penalizes tokens that have appeared at all. |","table":"table-5"},"2046":{"id":"/ai/chat-60","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option             | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `frequencyPenalty` | `number` | Penalizes tokens by how often they have appeared. |","table":"table-5"},"2047":{"id":"/ai/chat-61","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option          | Type            | Description                               |\n| --------------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `stopSequences` | `Array<string>` | Stops generation at any of these strings. |","table":"table-5"},"2048":{"id":"/ai/chat-62","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option | Type     | Description                                                |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seed` | `number` | Seed for repeatable sampling, where the model supports it. |","table":"table-5"},"2049":{"id":"/ai/chat-63","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option    | Type                                  | Description                        |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `headers` | `Record<string, string \\| undefined>` | Extra HTTP headers on the request. |","table":"table-5"},"2050":{"id":"/ai/chat-64","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"| Option        | Type          | Description          |\n| ------------- | ------------- | -------------------- |\n| `abortSignal` | `AbortSignal` | Cancels the request. |","table":"table-5"},"2051":{"id":"/ai/chat-65","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#sampling-options","content":"Models differ in which options they honor. The LMS proxy does not accept `topK`, so there is no such option."},"2052":{"id":"/ai/chat-66","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#cancel-a-request","content":"Pass an `AbortSignal`. `generateText` rejects, and `streamText` errors its streams and rejects its promises. Calling `cancel()` on `textStream` or `fullStream` also aborts the request."},"2053":{"id":"/ai/chat-67","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#cancel-a-request","content":"Check `signal.aborted` rather than `error.name`: the client's `fetch` wraps the abort in its own error type."},"2054":{"id":"/ai/chat-68","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"`generateText` resolves with a `GenerateTextResult`:"},"2055":{"id":"/ai/chat-69","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field  | Type     | Description      |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------- |\n| `text` | `string` | The answer text. |","table":"table-6"},"2056":{"id":"/ai/chat-70","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field           | Type                  | Description                                |\n| --------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `reasoningText` | `string \\| undefined` | Reasoning text, for models that return it. |","table":"table-6"},"2057":{"id":"/ai/chat-71","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field     | Type                 | Description                                    |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `content` | `Array<ContentPart>` | Text, reasoning, and tool-call parts in order. |","table":"table-6"},"2058":{"id":"/ai/chat-72","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field       | Type              | Description                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `toolCalls` | `Array<ToolCall>` | Tool calls requested by the model. |","table":"table-6"},"2059":{"id":"/ai/chat-73","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field         | Type                | Description                                   |\n| ------------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `toolResults` | `Array<ToolResult>` | Always empty: tools are not executed for you. |","table":"table-6"},"2060":{"id":"/ai/chat-74","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field          | Type           | Description             |\n| -------------- | -------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `finishReason` | `FinishReason` | Normalized stop reason. |","table":"table-6"},"2061":{"id":"/ai/chat-75","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field             | Type                  | Description                                       |\n| ----------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `rawFinishReason` | `string \\| undefined` | The provider's own value, such as `\"tool_calls\"`. |","table":"table-6"},"2062":{"id":"/ai/chat-76","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field   | Type                 | Description                 |\n| ------- | -------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `usage` | `LanguageModelUsage` | Token counts for this call. |","table":"table-6"},"2063":{"id":"/ai/chat-77","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field        | Type                 | Description      |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `totalUsage` | `LanguageModelUsage` | Same as `usage`. |","table":"table-6"},"2064":{"id":"/ai/chat-78","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field   | Type                | Description                           |\n| ------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `steps` | `Array<StepResult>` | One entry per model call. Always one. |","table":"table-6"},"2065":{"id":"/ai/chat-79","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field      | Type                          | Description               |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `warnings` | `Array<Warning> \\| undefined` | Inputs that were ignored. |","table":"table-6"},"2066":{"id":"/ai/chat-80","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"| Field                 | Type                                  | Description                                                                           |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `request`, `response` | `RequestMetadata`, `ResponseMetadata` | The request body, plus response `id`, `modelId`, `timestamp`, `body`, and `messages`. |","table":"table-6"},"2067":{"id":"/ai/chat-81","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"`FinishReason` is one of `\"stop\"`, `\"length\"` (hit `maxOutputTokens`), `\"tool-calls\"`, `\"content-filter\"`, `\"error\"`, or `\"other\"`."},"2068":{"id":"/ai/chat-82","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"`LanguageModelUsage` has `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens`, each `number | undefined`, plus optional `reasoningTokens` and `cachedInputTokens`. Fields are `undefined` when the model does not report usage."},"2069":{"id":"/ai/chat-83","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#usage-and-finish-reason","content":"`generateText` also accepts `onStepFinish(step)` and `onFinish(event)`, where `event` adds `steps` and `totalUsage` to the step result."},"2070":{"id":"/ai/chat-84","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"Failed requests reject with `PalantirApiError` from `@osdk/client`, which carries `statusCode`, `errorName`, and `message`. A `403` usually means the token lacks `api:use-language-models-execute` or your user cannot use the model."},"2071":{"id":"/ai/chat-85","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"Unsupported input does not throw. It is skipped and reported in `warnings`:"},"2072":{"id":"/ai/chat-86","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"| Input                                 | Behavior |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| Image or file parts in a user message | Dropped. |","table":"table-7"},"2073":{"id":"/ai/chat-87","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"| Input                                           | Behavior |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| Reasoning or file parts in an assistant message | Dropped. |","table":"table-7"},"2074":{"id":"/ai/chat-88","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"| Input                  | Behavior |\n| ---------------------- | -------- |\n| Media in a tool result | Dropped. |","table":"table-7"},"2075":{"id":"/ai/chat-89","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"| Input                                                  | Behavior                    |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------- |\n| A tool whose `inputSchema` is not a JSON Schema object | Sent with empty parameters. |","table":"table-7"},"2076":{"id":"/ai/chat-90","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#errors-and-warnings","content":"| Input                                       | Behavior                          |\n| ------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Tool-call arguments that are not valid JSON | Passed through as the raw string. |","table":"table-7"},"2077":{"id":"/ai/chat-91","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"If your app already uses the AI SDK, `@osdk/aip-core/ai-sdk` provides a Foundry provider for it. You get the AI SDK's own `generateText`, `streamText`, and `tool()` helpers, including its multi-step tool loop. The provider implements the v3 provider specification, so use `ai` version 6."},"2078":{"id":"/ai/chat-92","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"`foundry(model)` and `foundry.languageModel(model)` accept the same API name or `ModelIdentifier` as `foundryModel`. The provider also ignores `topK` and JSON response formats, and reports them as warnings."},"2079":{"id":"/ai/chat-93","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"`@osdk/language-models` is the lower-level package `@osdk/aip-core` is built on. It returns Foundry's provider-compatible proxy URLs, so you can point an OpenAI, Anthropic, or Google SDK at Foundry instead of the provider. Use it when you need a provider feature `@osdk/aip-core` does not cover yet, such as the OpenAI Responses API or embeddings."},"2080":{"id":"/ai/chat-94","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"| Function                   | Returns                                   |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `getOpenAiBaseUrl(client)` | `<foundryUrl>/api/v2/llm/proxy/openai/v1` |","table":"table-8"},"2081":{"id":"/ai/chat-95","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"| Function                      | Returns                                   |\n| ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `getAnthropicBaseUrl(client)` | `<foundryUrl>/api/v2/llm/proxy/anthropic` |","table":"table-8"},"2082":{"id":"/ai/chat-96","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"| Function                   | Returns                                |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `getGoogleBaseUrl(client)` | `<foundryUrl>/api/v2/llm/proxy/google` |","table":"table-8"},"2083":{"id":"/ai/chat-97","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"| Function              | Returns                                                                           |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `createFetch(client)` | The client's `fetch`, which sets a fresh `Authorization` header on every request. |","table":"table-8"},"2084":{"id":"/ai/chat-98","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"| Function                  | Returns                                   |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `getFoundryToken(client)` | `Promise<string>` with the current token. |","table":"table-8"},"2085":{"id":"/ai/chat-99","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"Each function accepts an Ontology `Client` or a `PlatformClient`."},"2086":{"id":"/ai/chat-100","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#call-a-provider-sdk-directly","content":"`createFetch` replaces the `Authorization` header on each request, so the client keeps working after the token from `getFoundryToken` expires. The proxy accepts each provider's native request format; Foundry's LLM-provider compatible APIs documentation lists the supported endpoints."},"2087":{"id":"/ai/chat-101","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#next-steps","content":"Tool calling: let the model query the Ontology and propose actions."},"2088":{"id":"/ai/chat-102","page_id":"/ai/chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/chat#next-steps","content":"React chat UIs: stream into React with `useChat`."},"2089":{"id":"/ai","page_id":"/ai","type":"page","content":"AI overview","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","Build with AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai"},"2090":{"id":"/ai-0","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai","content":"Packages for adding LLM features to OSDK apps with Foundry's Language Model Service, what each one does, and what you need before you start."},"2091":{"id":"/ai-1","page_id":"/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai#packages","content":"Packages"},"2092":{"id":"/ai-2","page_id":"/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"Which to use"},"2093":{"id":"/ai-3","page_id":"/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"2094":{"id":"/ai-4","page_id":"/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"Current limits"},"2095":{"id":"/ai-5","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai","content":"Add text generation, tool calling, chat UIs, and agents to an OSDK app using models hosted by Foundry's Language Model Service (LMS). Requests run with the signed-in user's permissions and Foundry's governance and usage tracking, so you never ship a provider API key."},"2096":{"id":"/ai-6","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai","content":"These packages are pre-release. `@osdk/aip-core`, `@osdk/language-models`, and `@osdk/agents` are at version 0.x, and the React APIs ship from `/experimental` entry points. Expect breaking changes in minor releases."},"2097":{"id":"/ai-7","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package          | Import           | What it does                                                                                               | Maturity |\n| ---------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| `@osdk/aip-core` | `@osdk/aip-core` | `foundryModel`, `generateText`, `streamText`, tool definitions, and the `LmsChatTransport` chat transport. | 0.x      |","table":"table-0"},"2098":{"id":"/ai-8","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package          | Import                  | What it does                                                    | Maturity |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| `@osdk/aip-core` | `@osdk/aip-core/ai-sdk` | `createFoundryAI`, a Foundry provider for the AI SDK version 6. | 0.x      |","table":"table-0"},"2099":{"id":"/ai-9","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package                 | Import                  | What it does                                                                                                              | Maturity |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| `@osdk/language-models` | `@osdk/language-models` | Proxy base URLs and an authenticated `fetch` for the OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google SDKs. `@osdk/aip-core` is built on it. | 0.x      |","table":"table-0"},"2100":{"id":"/ai-10","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package       | Import                         | What it does                                                    | Maturity     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| `@osdk/react` | `@osdk/react/experimental/aip` | `useChat`, a hook that streams a conversation into React state. | Experimental |","table":"table-0"},"2101":{"id":"/ai-11","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package                  | Import                                               | What it does                                              | Maturity     |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| `@osdk/react-components` | `@osdk/react-components/experimental/aip-agent-chat` | `AipAgentChat`, a prebuilt chat panel built on `useChat`. | Experimental |","table":"table-0"},"2102":{"id":"/ai-12","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package                   | Import                    | What it does                                                                                 | Maturity       |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.aipagents` | `@osdk/foundry.aipagents` | Platform SDK for agents built in AIP Agent Studio: sessions, blocking and streaming replies. | Beta endpoints |","table":"table-0"},"2103":{"id":"/ai-13","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#packages","content":"| Package        | Import                                      | What it does                                                                                           | Maturity |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------- |\n| `@osdk/agents` | `@osdk/agents`, `@osdk/agents/experimental` | `AgentConfig` and the injected `getClient` and `getPlatformClient` for code that runs inside an agent. | 0.x      |","table":"table-0"},"2104":{"id":"/ai-14","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                                       | Start with                |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Summarize, classify, or draft text from a script or server | `generateText` in Node.js |","table":"table-1"},"2105":{"id":"/ai-15","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                          | Start with   |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------ |\n| Show an answer token by token | `streamText` |","table":"table-1"},"2106":{"id":"/ai-16","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                                   | Start with   |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------ |\n| Let the model look up Ontology data or propose actions | Tool calling |","table":"table-1"},"2107":{"id":"/ai-17","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                              | Start with     |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| Add a chat panel to a React app with no custom UI | `AipAgentChat` |","table":"table-1"},"2108":{"id":"/ai-18","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                   | Start with |\n| ---------------------- | ---------- |\n| Build your own chat UI | `useChat`  |","table":"table-1"},"2109":{"id":"/ai-19","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                                     | Start with              |\n| -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| Use the AI SDK's helpers, Zod tools, and multi-step loop | `@osdk/aip-core/ai-sdk` |","table":"table-1"},"2110":{"id":"/ai-20","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                                                         | Start with              |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| Call an OpenAI, Anthropic, or Google SDK feature that `@osdk/aip-core` lacks | `@osdk/language-models` |","table":"table-1"},"2111":{"id":"/ai-21","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"| Goal                                            | Start with |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| Talk to an agent configured in AIP Agent Studio | Agents     |","table":"table-1"},"2112":{"id":"/ai-22","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#which-to-use","content":"`@osdk/language-models` is not superseded: `@osdk/aip-core` depends on it for the proxy URL. Use `@osdk/aip-core` for a provider-neutral API, and `@osdk/language-models` when you want a provider's own SDK."},"2113":{"id":"/ai-23","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#prerequisites","content":"| Requirement            | Details                                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| AIP on your enrollment | AIP must be enabled, and your users need permission to use AIP builder capabilities. |","table":"table-2"},"2114":{"id":"/ai-24","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#prerequisites","content":"| Requirement | Details                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| OAuth scope | Third-party applications must request `api:use-language-models-execute`. The default scopes of `createPublicOauthClient` do not include it. Agents need `api:aip-agents-read` and `api:aip-agents-write`, or `api:agents-read` and `api:agents-write` for generated agents. |","table":"table-2"},"2115":{"id":"/ai-25","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#prerequisites","content":"| Requirement        | Details                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A `PlatformClient` | `foundryModel`, `createFoundryAI`, and `AipAgentChat` take a client from `createPlatformClient`, not the Ontology `Client`. Create it with the same token provider. |","table":"table-2"},"2116":{"id":"/ai-26","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#prerequisites","content":"| Requirement | Details                                                                                                                                  |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A model     | Use a model API name, such as `\"gpt-4o\"`, or a registered model RID. Available models vary by enrollment; look them up in Model Catalog. |","table":"table-2"},"2117":{"id":"/ai-27","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"| Limit                                                       | Applies to                   |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| One model call per request; you run the tool loop yourself. | `generateText`, `streamText` |","table":"table-3"},"2118":{"id":"/ai-28","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"| Limit                                                                  | Applies to                   |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Tool `inputSchema` must be JSON Schema; Zod schemas are not converted. | `generateText`, `streamText` |","table":"table-3"},"2119":{"id":"/ai-29","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"| Limit                                                       | Applies to                  |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Text only: image and file parts are dropped with a warning. | `@osdk/aip-core`, `useChat` |","table":"table-3"},"2120":{"id":"/ai-30","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"| Limit                                 | Applies to                                |\n| ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| No structured JSON output, no `topK`. | `@osdk/aip-core`, `@osdk/aip-core/ai-sdk` |","table":"table-3"},"2121":{"id":"/ai-31","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"| Limit                                         | Applies to                |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| No tools, multi-step loops, or stream resume. | `useChat`, `AipAgentChat` |","table":"table-3"},"2122":{"id":"/ai-32","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"The AI SDK provider lifts the first two: the AI SDK runs the loop and converts Zod schemas."},"2123":{"id":"/ai-33","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"`generateText`, `streamText`, models, messages, and usage."},"2124":{"id":"/ai-34","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"Query the Ontology and propose actions from model tool calls."},"2125":{"id":"/ai-35","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"`useChat`, custom transports, and streaming rendering."},"2126":{"id":"/ai-36","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"AIP Agents, generated agent sessions, and `@osdk/agents`."},"2127":{"id":"/ai-37","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"A prebuilt chat panel for React."},"2128":{"id":"/ai-38","page_id":"/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai#current-limits","content":"`llms.txt`, per-page Markdown, and AGENTS.md for coding assistants."},"2129":{"id":"/ai/llms","page_id":"/ai/llms","type":"page","content":"Use these docs with AI","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","AI-assisted development"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai/llms"},"2130":{"id":"/ai/llms-0","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms","content":"Give coding assistants accurate OSDK context with llms.txt, per-page Markdown, and the package AGENTS.md files."},"2131":{"id":"/ai/llms-1","page_id":"/ai/llms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/llms#from-any-page","content":"From any page"},"2132":{"id":"/ai/llms-2","page_id":"/ai/llms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/llms#markdown-for-every-url","content":"Markdown for every URL"},"2133":{"id":"/ai/llms-3","page_id":"/ai/llms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"llms.txt"},"2134":{"id":"/ai/llms-4","page_id":"/ai/llms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"Docs inside your node_modules"},"2135":{"id":"/ai/llms-5","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms","content":"Every page on this site is also published as plain Markdown, so you can hand OSDK documentation to ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, or your own agent without scraping HTML."},"2136":{"id":"/ai/llms-6","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#from-any-page","content":"Each page header has two controls:"},"2137":{"id":"/ai/llms-7","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#from-any-page","content":"| Control           | What it does                                                       |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Copy Markdown** | Copies the page as Markdown, ready to paste into a chat or prompt. |","table":"table-0"},"2138":{"id":"/ai/llms-8","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#from-any-page","content":"| Control       | What it does                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Open** menu | Opens the page in ChatGPT, Claude, or Cursor with a prompt that points at the Markdown version, or opens the source on GitHub. |","table":"table-0"},"2139":{"id":"/ai/llms-9","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#markdown-for-every-url","content":"Append `.md` to any docs URL to get the Markdown version:"},"2140":{"id":"/ai/llms-10","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"The site follows the llms.txt convention:"},"2141":{"id":"/ai/llms-11","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"| File        | Contents                                                                                        | Use it when                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `/llms.txt` | An index of every page, grouped by section, with a one-line summary and a link to its Markdown. | Your tool fetches pages on demand. |","table":"table-1"},"2142":{"id":"/ai/llms-12","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"| File             | Contents                  | Use it when                                        |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/llms-full.txt` | Every page, concatenated. | You want the whole SDK in a single context window. |","table":"table-1"},"2143":{"id":"/ai/llms-13","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"In chat, type `@Docs`, choose **Add new doc**, and enter `https://palantir.github.io/osdk-ts/llms-full.txt`. Mention it with `@Docs` in later prompts."},"2144":{"id":"/ai/llms-14","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"Add the index to your project's `CLAUDE.md` so Claude fetches the pages it needs:"},"2145":{"id":"/ai/llms-15","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#llmstxt","content":"Fetch `https://palantir.github.io/osdk-ts/llms.txt`, pick the relevant pages, then fetch their `.md` links. Use `llms-full.txt` when the agent can't make follow-up requests."},"2146":{"id":"/ai/llms-16","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"The React packages ship agent instructions and documentation in their npm tarballs, so assistants working in your repository can read docs that match your installed version:"},"2147":{"id":"/ai/llms-17","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"| Package       | Files                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/react` | `AGENTS.md` (install rules, version matching, correct and incorrect patterns) and `docs/` (the React guides on this site) |","table":"table-2"},"2148":{"id":"/ai/llms-18","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"| Package                  | Files                                                                             |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/react-components` | `AGENTS.md` and `docs/` (one page per component, including generated prop tables) |","table":"table-2"},"2149":{"id":"/ai/llms-19","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"Point your assistant at them directly:"},"2150":{"id":"/ai/llms-20","page_id":"/ai/llms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/llms#docs-inside-your-node_modules","content":"The files in `node_modules` match the version you have installed. This site always documents the latest release."},"2151":{"id":"/ai/react","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"page","content":"React chat UIs","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","Build with AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai/react"},"2152":{"id":"/ai/react-0","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react","content":"Build streaming chat interfaces with useChat from @osdk/react/experimental/aip, custom chat transports, or the prebuilt AipAgentChat component."},"2153":{"id":"/ai/react-1","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#choose-an-approach","content":"Choose an approach"},"2154":{"id":"/ai/react-2","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#install","content":"Install"},"2155":{"id":"/ai/react-3","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#create-the-model-once","content":"Create the model once"},"2156":{"id":"/ai/react-4","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#build-a-chat-with-usechat","content":"Build a chat with `useChat`"},"2157":{"id":"/ai/react-5","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"How streaming renders"},"2158":{"id":"/ai/react-6","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#options","content":"Options"},"2159":{"id":"/ai/react-7","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"Return value"},"2160":{"id":"/ai/react-8","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"Messages"},"2161":{"id":"/ai/react-9","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"Custom transports"},"2162":{"id":"/ai/react-10","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"Stream chunks"},"2163":{"id":"/ai/react-11","page_id":"/ai/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/react#use-the-prebuilt-component","content":"Use the prebuilt component"},"2164":{"id":"/ai/react-12","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react","content":"`useChat` streams a conversation with a Foundry-hosted model into React state: you render `messages` and call `sendMessage`. For a finished UI, drop in the `AipAgentChat` component instead."},"2165":{"id":"/ai/react-13","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react","content":"`useChat` is exported from the experimental entry point `@osdk/react/experimental/aip`, and `AipAgentChat` from `@osdk/react-components/experimental/aip-agent-chat`. Both can change in any minor release. The current version is text-only: it does not send tools, run multi-step loops, or resume a dropped stream, and it does not render reasoning text."},"2166":{"id":"/ai/react-14","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#choose-an-approach","content":"| Approach       | You write   | Use it when                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `AipAgentChat` | One element | You want a complete chat panel with a composer, message list, and optional model picker. |","table":"table-0"},"2167":{"id":"/ai/react-15","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#choose-an-approach","content":"| Approach  | You write | Use it when                                               |\n| --------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useChat` | The UI    | You need your own layout, message rendering, or controls. |","table":"table-0"},"2168":{"id":"/ai/react-16","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#choose-an-approach","content":"| Approach                            | You write                | Use it when                                                              |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `useChat` with a custom `transport` | The UI and the transport | You need to observe or change the stream, such as recording token usage. |","table":"table-0"},"2169":{"id":"/ai/react-17","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#install","content":"`@osdk/react` already depends on `@osdk/aip-core`; install it directly because your code imports `foundryModel` from it. `useChat` does not read from `OsdkProvider`, so it works inside or outside one."},"2170":{"id":"/ai/react-18","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#create-the-model-once","content":"`useChat` needs a model from `foundryModel`, which takes a `PlatformClient` and the model's LMS API name. Create it at module scope so it stays the same object across renders. A new model object rebuilds the hook's transport."},"2171":{"id":"/ai/react-19","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#create-the-model-once","content":"If your app already has an Ontology client, pass the same `auth` to `createClient` so the user signs in once. Model selection and scopes are covered in Generate and stream text."},"2172":{"id":"/ai/react-20","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#build-a-chat-with-usechat","content":"The list keeps rendering while a reply streams and after an error, so earlier messages never disappear."},"2173":{"id":"/ai/react-21","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"`sendMessage` appends the user message and sets `status` to `\"submitted\"`."},"2174":{"id":"/ai/react-22","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"On the first text token, an assistant message is added and `status` becomes `\"streaming\"`. Its single text part grows as tokens arrive."},"2175":{"id":"/ai/react-23","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"Updates are batched every 50 ms by default, so a fast stream does not render once per token. Change it with `experimentalThrottle`."},"2176":{"id":"/ai/react-24","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"When the stream ends, `status` returns to `\"ready\"` and `onFinish` fires with the final message."},"2177":{"id":"/ai/react-25","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#how-streaming-renders","content":"`stop()` aborts the request and keeps the partial reply; `status` returns to `\"ready\"` with no error. A failed request sets `status` to `\"error\"`, fills `error`, and calls `onError`. `sendMessage` resolves in every case; it does not reject."},"2178":{"id":"/ai/react-26","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option  | Type            | Default | Description                                                          |\n| ------- | --------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `model` | `LanguageModel` |         | The model from `foundryModel`. Required unless you pass `transport`. |","table":"table-1"},"2179":{"id":"/ai/react-27","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option   | Type     | Default | Description                                                                        |\n| -------- | -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `system` | `string` |         | System prompt sent with every request. Replaces any system messages in `messages`. |","table":"table-1"},"2180":{"id":"/ai/react-28","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option                                                                                                   | Type | Default | Description                             |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---- | ------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `temperature`, `maxOutputTokens`, `topP`, `presencePenalty`, `frequencyPenalty`, `stopSequences`, `seed` |      |         | Sampling options, as in `generateText`. |","table":"table-1"},"2181":{"id":"/ai/react-29","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option    | Type                                  | Default | Description                         |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `headers` | `Record<string, string \\| undefined>` |         | Extra HTTP headers on each request. |","table":"table-1"},"2182":{"id":"/ai/react-30","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option | Type     | Default   | Description                                                            |\n| ------ | -------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`   | `string` | Generated | Chat id. Changing it starts a new, empty store seeded from `messages`. |","table":"table-1"},"2183":{"id":"/ai/react-31","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option     | Type                       | Default | Description                           |\n| ---------- | -------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `messages` | `ReadonlyArray<UIMessage>` | `[]`    | Initial messages. Read once per `id`. |","table":"table-1"},"2184":{"id":"/ai/react-32","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option      | Type                       | Default                     | Description                                                                                               |\n| ----------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `transport` | `ChatTransport<UIMessage>` | `new LmsChatTransport(...)` | Replaces the default transport. When set, `model`, `system`, sampling options, and `headers` are ignored. |","table":"table-1"},"2185":{"id":"/ai/react-33","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option                 | Type     | Default | Description                                              |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `experimentalThrottle` | `number` | `50`    | Minimum milliseconds between re-renders while streaming. |","table":"table-1"},"2186":{"id":"/ai/react-34","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option    | Type                     | Default | Description                                                     |\n| --------- | ------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onError` | `(error: Error) => void` |         | Called when a request or stream fails. Not called for `stop()`. |","table":"table-1"},"2187":{"id":"/ai/react-35","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"| Option     | Type                                     | Default | Description                          |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `onFinish` | `(event: { message, messages }) => void` |         | Called once after a reply completes. |","table":"table-1"},"2188":{"id":"/ai/react-36","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#options","content":"Changing `model` or a sampling option takes effect on the next message and keeps the conversation, which is how a model picker works."},"2189":{"id":"/ai/react-37","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field | Type     | Description  |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------ |\n| `id`  | `string` | The chat id. |","table":"table-2"},"2190":{"id":"/ai/react-38","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field      | Type                       | Description                                        |\n| ---------- | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `messages` | `ReadonlyArray<UIMessage>` | The conversation, including the reply in progress. |","table":"table-2"},"2191":{"id":"/ai/react-39","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field    | Type         | Description                                            |\n| -------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `status` | `ChatStatus` | `\"ready\"`, `\"submitted\"`, `\"streaming\"`, or `\"error\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"2192":{"id":"/ai/react-40","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field   | Type                 | Description                                    |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `error` | `Error \\| undefined` | The last failure, while `status` is `\"error\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"2193":{"id":"/ai/react-41","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field         | Type                                         | Description                                     |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `sendMessage` | `(input: SendMessageInput) => Promise<void>` | Sends `{ text }`, or `{ role: \"user\", parts }`. |","table":"table-2"},"2194":{"id":"/ai/react-42","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field        | Type                                                  | Description                                                                                                   |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `regenerate` | `(options?: { messageId?: string }) => Promise<void>` | Removes the last assistant message, or the one with `messageId` and everything after it, and generates again. |","table":"table-2"},"2195":{"id":"/ai/react-43","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field  | Type         | Description                   |\n| ------ | ------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `stop` | `() => void` | Aborts the reply in progress. |","table":"table-2"},"2196":{"id":"/ai/react-44","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field         | Type                                       | Description                                                                                               |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `setMessages` | `(messages \\| (prev) => messages) => void` | Replaces the conversation. Ignored while `status` is `\"submitted\"` or `\"streaming\"`; call `stop()` first. |","table":"table-2"},"2197":{"id":"/ai/react-45","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field        | Type         | Description                                  |\n| ------------ | ------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `clearError` | `() => void` | Resets `status` from `\"error\"` to `\"ready\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"2198":{"id":"/ai/react-46","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"| Field          | Type                  | Description                                                                               |\n| -------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resumeStream` | `() => Promise<void>` | Reconnects to a dropped stream. The LMS transport cannot reconnect, so this does nothing. |","table":"table-2"},"2199":{"id":"/ai/react-47","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#return-value","content":"Clear the conversation with `setMessages([])`, or render a new chat by changing `id`."},"2200":{"id":"/ai/react-48","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"A `UIMessage` is what the UI renders:"},"2201":{"id":"/ai/react-49","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"| Field | Type     | Description                           |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | `string` | Stable id. Use it as the React `key`. |","table":"table-3"},"2202":{"id":"/ai/react-50","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"| Field  | Type                                | Description   |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `role` | `\"system\" \\| \"user\" \\| \"assistant\"` | Who wrote it. |","table":"table-3"},"2203":{"id":"/ai/react-51","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"| Field   | Type                   | Description                                                                                     |\n| ------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parts` | `Array<UIMessagePart>` | `{ type: \"text\", text }`, `{ type: \"reasoning\", text }`, or `{ type: \"file\", url, mediaType }`. |","table":"table-3"},"2204":{"id":"/ai/react-52","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"| Field      | Type                      | Description        |\n| ---------- | ------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `metadata` | `Record<string, unknown>` | Optional app data. |","table":"table-3"},"2205":{"id":"/ai/react-53","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#messages","content":"Only text parts reach the model. `getUIMessageText(message)` from `@osdk/aip-core` joins a message's text parts. To restore a saved conversation, pass it as `messages` with a stable `id`, and persist the final list from `onFinish`."},"2206":{"id":"/ai/react-54","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"A transport turns the conversation into a stream of `UIMessageChunk` events. The default, `LmsChatTransport` from `@osdk/aip-core`, calls `streamText` and takes the same model, `system`, sampling, and `headers` options as `useChat`. Write your own to observe or change the stream."},"2207":{"id":"/ai/react-55","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"A `ChatTransport` has two methods:"},"2208":{"id":"/ai/react-56","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"| Method                                                                         | Description                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sendMessages({ trigger, chatId, messageId, messages, abortSignal, headers })` | Returns `Promise<ReadableStream<UIMessageChunk>>`. `trigger` is `\"submit-message\"` or `\"regenerate-message\"`; `messageId` is the id for the assistant reply. Honor `abortSignal` so `stop()` works. |","table":"table-4"},"2209":{"id":"/ai/react-57","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"| Method                          | Description                            |\n| ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `reconnectToStream({ chatId })` | Returns a stream to resume, or `null`. |","table":"table-4"},"2210":{"id":"/ai/react-58","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"This transport wraps `LmsChatTransport` and reports token usage from the `\"finish\"` chunk:"},"2211":{"id":"/ai/react-59","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#custom-transports","content":"Keep the transport stable with `useMemo` or module scope, for the same reason as the model."},"2212":{"id":"/ai/react-60","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"`LmsChatTransport` emits these chunks in order. `useChat` reads `\"text-delta\"` and `\"error\"`; the others are there for custom transports and consumers."},"2213":{"id":"/ai/react-61","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`    | Fields      | Meaning            |\n| --------- | ----------- | ------------------ |\n| `\"start\"` | `messageId` | The reply started. |","table":"table-5"},"2214":{"id":"/ai/react-62","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`                          | Fields | Meaning                 |\n| ------------------------------- | ------ | ----------------------- |\n| `\"start-step\"`, `\"finish-step\"` |        | Bracket the model call. |","table":"table-5"},"2215":{"id":"/ai/react-63","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`                                       | Fields                       | Meaning      |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------ |\n| `\"text-start\"`, `\"text-delta\"`, `\"text-end\"` | `id`, plus `delta` on deltas | Answer text. |","table":"table-5"},"2216":{"id":"/ai/react-64","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`                                                      | Fields                       | Meaning                                    |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `\"reasoning-start\"`, `\"reasoning-delta\"`, `\"reasoning-end\"` | `id`, plus `delta` on deltas | Reasoning text, for models that return it. |","table":"table-5"},"2217":{"id":"/ai/react-65","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`                   | Fields                            | Meaning                                                                             |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"tool-input-available\"` | `toolCallId`, `toolName`, `input` | A tool call. `useChat` sends no tools, so this appears only from custom transports. |","table":"table-5"},"2218":{"id":"/ai/react-66","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`     | Fields                                        | Meaning             |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `\"finish\"` | `messageMetadata?: { finishReason?, usage? }` | The reply finished. |","table":"table-5"},"2219":{"id":"/ai/react-67","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#stream-chunks","content":"| `type`    | Fields      | Meaning            |\n| --------- | ----------- | ------------------ |\n| `\"error\"` | `errorText` | The stream failed. |","table":"table-5"},"2220":{"id":"/ai/react-68","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#use-the-prebuilt-component","content":"`AipAgentChat` wraps `useChat` in a styled chat panel. It takes the `PlatformClient` and model API names and builds the model itself:"},"2221":{"id":"/ai/react-69","page_id":"/ai/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/react#use-the-prebuilt-component","content":"Despite the name, it chats with a language model through the Language Model Service, not with an agent built in AIP Agent Studio. For props, render slots, `BaseAipAgentChat`, and theming, see AipAgentChat; for the stylesheet setup, see Prerequisites. To call AIP Agents, see Agents."},"2222":{"id":"/ai/tools","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"page","content":"Tool calling","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","AI","Build with AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools"},"2223":{"id":"/ai/tools-0","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools","content":"Let a Foundry-hosted model call your code to query the Ontology and propose actions, with JSON Schema tools and a confirm-before-apply loop."},"2224":{"id":"/ai/tools-1","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#set-up-the-clients","content":"Set up the clients"},"2225":{"id":"/ai/tools-2","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"Define tools"},"2226":{"id":"/ai/tools-3","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#control-tool-choice","content":"Control tool choice"},"2227":{"id":"/ai/tools-4","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"Read tool calls"},"2228":{"id":"/ai/tools-5","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"Run the loop"},"2229":{"id":"/ai/tools-6","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Keep tool results small"},"2230":{"id":"/ai/tools-7","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#propose-actions-then-confirm","content":"Propose actions, then confirm"},"2231":{"id":"/ai/tools-8","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#stream-with-tools","content":"Stream with tools"},"2232":{"id":"/ai/tools-9","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"Use the AI SDK"},"2233":{"id":"/ai/tools-10","page_id":"/ai/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Safety checklist"},"2234":{"id":"/ai/tools-11","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools","content":"Tools let the model ask your app to run code, such as an Ontology query, and then answer from the result. With `@osdk/aip-core`, the model returns tool calls and your code runs them, so you decide what executes and when."},"2235":{"id":"/ai/tools-12","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools","content":"`@osdk/aip-core` is at version 0.x and its API can change in any minor release. Two limits shape this page:"},"2236":{"id":"/ai/tools-13","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools","content":"Each `generateText` or `streamText` call is one model step. Tools are never executed for you; you run them and loop."},"2237":{"id":"/ai/tools-14","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools","content":"`inputSchema` must be a plain JSON Schema object. A Zod schema is not converted: the tool is sent with empty parameters and a warning. For Zod schemas and an automatic loop, use the AI SDK provider."},"2238":{"id":"/ai/tools-15","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#set-up-the-clients","content":"Tool code needs two clients: the Ontology `Client` to run queries and actions, and a model built on a `PlatformClient`. Create both from one token provider. This Node.js setup uses a service user; the scopes must include `api:use-language-models-execute`."},"2239":{"id":"/ai/tools-16","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#set-up-the-clients","content":"In a browser, use `createPublicOauthClient` with the same scopes, as shown in Generate and stream text."},"2240":{"id":"/ai/tools-17","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"A `ToolSet` maps tool names to definitions. The name is what the model calls, so make it descriptive."},"2241":{"id":"/ai/tools-18","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"| Field         | Type     | Description                                                   |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `description` | `string` | When and why to use the tool. The model reads this to decide. |","table":"table-0"},"2242":{"id":"/ai/tools-19","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"| Field         | Type               | Description                                                   |\n| ------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `inputSchema` | JSON Schema object | The arguments, as `{ type: \"object\", properties, required }`. |","table":"table-0"},"2243":{"id":"/ai/tools-20","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"| Field             | Type                                      | Description                |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `providerOptions` | `Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>` | Provider-specific options. |","table":"table-0"},"2244":{"id":"/ai/tools-21","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#define-tools","content":"`satisfies ToolSet` keeps the literal tool names, so `toolName` on each returned call is typed as `\"searchEmployees\"`."},"2245":{"id":"/ai/tools-22","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#control-tool-choice","content":"| `toolChoice` | Behavior                                                                      |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"auto\"`     | The model decides whether to call a tool. The default when tools are present. |","table":"table-1"},"2246":{"id":"/ai/tools-23","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#control-tool-choice","content":"| `toolChoice` | Behavior                               |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| `\"required\"` | The model must call at least one tool. |","table":"table-1"},"2247":{"id":"/ai/tools-24","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#control-tool-choice","content":"| `toolChoice` | Behavior                       |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| `\"none\"`     | The model must answer in text. |","table":"table-1"},"2248":{"id":"/ai/tools-25","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#control-tool-choice","content":"| `toolChoice`                                    | Behavior                       |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"tool\", toolName: \"searchEmployees\" }` | The model must call that tool. |","table":"table-1"},"2249":{"id":"/ai/tools-26","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"When the model wants a tool, `finishReason` is `\"tool-calls\"` and `toolCalls` lists each call:"},"2250":{"id":"/ai/tools-27","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"| `ToolCall` field | Type     | Description                   |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `toolCallId`     | `string` | Pass it back with the result. |","table":"table-2"},"2251":{"id":"/ai/tools-28","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"| `ToolCall` field | Type     | Description      |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ---------------- |\n| `toolName`       | `string` | The tool to run. |","table":"table-2"},"2252":{"id":"/ai/tools-29","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"| `ToolCall` field | Type      | Description                                                                                     |\n| ---------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `input`          | `unknown` | Arguments parsed from the model's JSON. If the JSON is invalid, the raw string, with a warning. |","table":"table-2"},"2253":{"id":"/ai/tools-30","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#read-tool-calls","content":"`input` is whatever the model produced. It is not validated against `inputSchema`, so check it before use."},"2254":{"id":"/ai/tools-31","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"To finish the answer, append the model's message and a `tool` message with your results, then call the model again. Stop when it answers without tool calls, or after a step limit."},"2255":{"id":"/ai/tools-32","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"`result.response.messages` holds the assistant message, including its tool-call parts. Each `tool-result` part must use the `toolCallId` of the call it answers."},"2256":{"id":"/ai/tools-33","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"A tool result `output` is one of:"},"2257":{"id":"/ai/tools-34","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"| `type`   | `value`  | Sent to the model as |\n| -------- | -------- | -------------------- |\n| `\"text\"` | `string` | The string.          |","table":"table-3"},"2258":{"id":"/ai/tools-35","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"| `type`   | `value`   | Sent to the model as     |\n| -------- | --------- | ------------------------ |\n| `\"json\"` | `unknown` | `JSON.stringify(value)`. |","table":"table-3"},"2259":{"id":"/ai/tools-36","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"| `type`         | `value`  | Sent to the model as                                        |\n| -------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"error-text\"` | `string` | The string. Use it so the model can recover from bad input. |","table":"table-3"},"2260":{"id":"/ai/tools-37","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"| `type`         | `value`   | Sent to the model as     |\n| -------------- | --------- | ------------------------ |\n| `\"error-json\"` | `unknown` | `JSON.stringify(value)`. |","table":"table-3"},"2261":{"id":"/ai/tools-38","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#run-the-loop","content":"| `type`      | `value`                                           | Sent to the model as                                 |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"content\"` | Array of `{ type: \"text\", text }` and media parts | The text parts joined by newlines. Media is dropped. |","table":"table-3"},"2262":{"id":"/ai/tools-39","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Every tool result is sent back as input tokens on the next step."},"2263":{"id":"/ai/tools-40","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Pass `$select` so the query loads only the properties the model needs. See Load objects."},"2264":{"id":"/ai/tools-41","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Set a small `$pageSize` and say the limit in the tool description."},"2265":{"id":"/ai/tools-42","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Map OSDK objects to plain fields, as above, instead of returning whole instances."},"2266":{"id":"/ai/tools-43","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#keep-tool-results-small","content":"Filter on the server with `where` instead of asking the model to filter a long list. See Filter objects."},"2267":{"id":"/ai/tools-44","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#propose-actions-then-confirm","content":"A model can misread a request or be steered by text in the data it reads. Do not apply an action from inside a tool. Have the tool record a proposal, show it to the user, and apply it only after they confirm."},"2268":{"id":"/ai/tools-45","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#propose-actions-then-confirm","content":"Call `runProposalTool` from your loop's `runTool` for `proposeJobTitleChange`, and pass `{ ...tools, ...actionTools }` to `generateText`. `$validateOnly: true` checks the parameters against the action's rules without applying it, so the model learns about invalid input while it can still correct it. Show `proposals` in your UI and call `applyProposal` from the user's confirm button. See Apply actions for the validation result and errors."},"2269":{"id":"/ai/tools-46","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#stream-with-tools","content":"`streamText` takes the same `tools` and `toolChoice`. Tool calls arrive on `fullStream` as `\"tool-call\"` chunks after the text, once the model finishes, and `toolCalls` resolves to the same list. Run them and call `streamText` again with the extended `messages`. `(await result.response)?.messages` holds the assistant message to append."},"2270":{"id":"/ai/tools-47","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"The AI SDK provider in `@osdk/aip-core/ai-sdk` accepts Zod schemas, runs each tool's `execute` for you, and loops until a stop condition. It needs `ai` version 6."},"2271":{"id":"/ai/tools-48","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#use-the-ai-sdk","content":"`execute` runs without asking anyone, so keep action tools on the propose-then-confirm pattern above: `execute` records the proposal and your UI applies it."},"2272":{"id":"/ai/tools-49","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Treat tool `input` as untrusted. Check types and ranges before you query or write."},"2273":{"id":"/ai/tools-50","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Tool calls run with the signed-in user's permissions, or the service user's in Node. Give a service user only the scopes and data access the feature needs."},"2274":{"id":"/ai/tools-51","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Never apply an action, send a message, or delete data without an explicit user confirmation."},"2275":{"id":"/ai/tools-52","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Limit the number of steps so a confused model cannot loop forever."},"2276":{"id":"/ai/tools-53","page_id":"/ai/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/ai/tools#safety-checklist","content":"Text in Ontology data can contain instructions. Do not let tool results grant the model new permissions."},"2277":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"page","content":"Call platform APIs","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Platform SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis"},"2278":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-0","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis","content":"The calling convention for @osdk/foundry functions, including argument order, pagination, errors, binary responses, and preview endpoints."},"2279":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-1","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#import-a-namespace","content":"Import a namespace"},"2280":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-2","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"Argument order"},"2281":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-3","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"Responses"},"2282":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-4","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"Paginate"},"2283":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-5","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#batch-requests","content":"Batch requests"},"2284":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-6","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"Handle errors"},"2285":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-7","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#preview-endpoints","content":"Preview endpoints"},"2286":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-8","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/calling-apis#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"2287":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-9","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis","content":"Every Platform SDK function takes the client first, then the endpoint's path, body, query, and header arguments, in that order. This page covers that convention and how to handle pagination, errors, binary content, and preview endpoints."},"2288":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-10","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#import-a-namespace","content":"Each package exports one namespace per resource, named in the plural: `Users`, `Groups`, `Datasets`, `Files`, `MediaSets`. Each function in a namespace maps to one REST endpoint."},"2289":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-11","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#import-a-namespace","content":"Request and response types, such as `User`, `Group`, and `ListUsersResponse`, are exported by name from the same package. Identifier types such as `UserId` and `PageToken` are strings, so plain string values work wherever they are expected."},"2290":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-12","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"After the client, a function takes up to four groups of arguments, always in this order:"},"2291":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-13","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"| Position | Argument   | Example  |\n| -------- | ---------- | -------- |\n| 1        | The client | `client` |","table":"table-0"},"2292":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-14","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"| Position | Argument                                                    | Example                  |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| 2        | Path parameters, one positional argument each, in URL order | `datasetRid`, `filePath` |","table":"table-0"},"2293":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-15","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"| Position | Argument                                         | Example                                             |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| 3        | The request body, for `POST` and `PUT` endpoints | `{ where: { type: \"queryString\", value: \"jane\" } }` |","table":"table-0"},"2294":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-16","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"| Position | Argument                        | Example                            |\n| -------- | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| 4        | Query parameters, as one object | `{ pageSize: 100, preview: true }` |","table":"table-0"},"2295":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-17","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"| Position | Argument                         | Example                |\n| -------- | -------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| 5        | Header parameters, as one object | `{ ReadToken: token }` |","table":"table-0"},"2296":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-18","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"A function only takes the groups its endpoint has:"},"2297":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-19","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#argument-order","content":"When a function has optional query parameters and you need to pass headers, pass `undefined` or an object for the query parameters first. Your editor shows the parameter names, such as `$queryParams` and `$headerParams`, on hover."},"2298":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-20","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"| Endpoint returns | The function resolves to                                        |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| JSON             | The parsed body, typed, such as `User` or `ListGroupsResponse`. |","table":"table-1"},"2299":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-21","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"| Endpoint returns   | The function resolves to                         |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| No content (`204`) | `undefined`. The return type is `Promise<void>`. |","table":"table-1"},"2300":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-22","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"| Endpoint returns | The function resolves to                                                         |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Binary content   | The `Response`. Read it with `.blob()`, `.arrayBuffer()`, `.text()`, or `.body`. |","table":"table-1"},"2301":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-23","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"Binary endpoints include `Files.content`, `Datasets.readTable`, `MediaSets.read`, and `Users.profilePicture`. Their return type is `Promise<Response>`:"},"2302":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-24","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"Call `URL.revokeObjectURL` when you no longer show the image."},"2303":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-25","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#responses","content":"Upload endpoints such as `Files.upload` and `MediaSets.upload` take the bytes as a `Blob`. A `File` from an `<input type=\"file\">` is a `Blob`, so you can pass it directly."},"2304":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-26","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"List and search endpoints return one page at a time as `{ data, nextPageToken }`. Pass `nextPageToken` back as `pageToken` to get the next page. The last page has no `nextPageToken`."},"2305":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-27","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"| Parameter  | Type     | Description                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `pageSize` | `number` | Preferred page size. The server can return more or fewer items, and some endpoints cap it. |","table":"table-2"},"2306":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-28","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"| Parameter   | Type     | Description                                               |\n| ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pageToken` | `string` | Token from the previous page. Omit it for the first page. |","table":"table-2"},"2307":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-29","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"For `GET` endpoints, such as `Users.list`, these are query parameters. For `POST` endpoints, such as `Users.search`, they go in the body."},"2308":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-30","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"A small async generator turns any paged endpoint into a stream of items:"},"2309":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-31","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"Use it with query-parameter and body pagination alike:"},"2310":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-32","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#paginate","content":"Breaking out of the loop stops further requests."},"2311":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-33","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#batch-requests","content":"Resources with many lookups have a `getBatch` function that takes an array of request elements and returns a `data` map keyed by ID. Each documents its maximum batch size in JSDoc; `Users.getBatch` accepts up to 500:"},"2312":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-34","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"A failed call rejects with a `PalantirApiError`, exported from `@osdk/client`. This includes network failures and error responses that are not JSON; those have no `errorName`, and the underlying error is on `cause`. If the token provider itself throws, the call rejects with a plain `Error`."},"2313":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-35","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field     | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| --------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `message` | `string` | The server's message, or `Failed to fetch <status> <statusText>`. |","table":"table-3"},"2314":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-36","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field       | Type                  | Description                                                                                |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `errorName` | `string \\| undefined` | Stable identifier, such as `UserNotFound` or `ApiFeaturePreviewUsageOnly`. Switch on this. |","table":"table-3"},"2315":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-37","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field       | Type                  | Description                                                                            |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `errorCode` | `string \\| undefined` | Category, such as `NOT_FOUND`, `PERMISSION_DENIED`, `INVALID_ARGUMENT`, or `CONFLICT`. |","table":"table-3"},"2316":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-38","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field              | Type                  | Description                 |\n| ------------------ | --------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `errorDescription` | `string \\| undefined` | Human-readable description. |","table":"table-3"},"2317":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-39","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field        | Type                  | Description  |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | ------------ |\n| `statusCode` | `number \\| undefined` | HTTP status. |","table":"table-3"},"2318":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-40","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field             | Type                  | Description                                                         |\n| ----------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `errorInstanceId` | `string \\| undefined` | Server-side ID for this occurrence. Include it in support requests. |","table":"table-3"},"2319":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-41","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"| Field        | Type                  | Description                                  |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameters` | `object \\| undefined` | Context for the error, such as `{ userId }`. |","table":"table-3"},"2320":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-42","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"Each package exports a type for every error it can return, with the exact `errorName`, `errorCode`, and `parameters`. Import them to see what to expect:"},"2321":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-43","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"Shared errors, such as `ApiFeaturePreviewUsageOnly`, `InvalidPageToken`, and `ApiUsageDenied`, are exported from `@osdk/foundry.core`."},"2322":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-44","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#handle-errors","content":"The client retries `429` and `503` responses up to three times before rejecting. Other errors reject immediately."},"2323":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-45","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#preview-endpoints","content":"Functions tagged `@beta` or `@alpha` in JSDoc call preview endpoints. They take a `preview` query parameter, and the server rejects the call with `ApiFeaturePreviewUsageOnly` unless you set it to `true`:"},"2324":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-46","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#preview-endpoints","content":"`preview` always goes in the query-parameter object, after any body:"},"2325":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-47","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#preview-endpoints","content":"Preview endpoints can change shape between package versions. Pin the package version, and check the changelog when you upgrade."},"2326":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-48","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#next-steps","content":"Users and groups"},"2327":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-49","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#next-steps","content":"Datasets"},"2328":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-50","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#next-steps","content":"Media sets"},"2329":{"id":"/platform/calling-apis-51","page_id":"/platform/calling-apis","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/calling-apis#next-steps","content":"Ontology metadata"},"2330":{"id":"/platform/datasets","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"page","content":"Datasets","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Platform SDK","Recipes"],"tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets"},"2331":{"id":"/platform/datasets-0","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets","content":"Read dataset files and tables, upload files in transactions, and manage branches with @osdk/foundry.datasets."},"2332":{"id":"/platform/datasets-1","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#get-a-dataset","content":"Get a dataset"},"2333":{"id":"/platform/datasets-2","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"Read a table"},"2334":{"id":"/platform/datasets-3","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"List and download files"},"2335":{"id":"/platform/datasets-4","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"Upload a single file"},"2336":{"id":"/platform/datasets-5","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"Upload in a transaction"},"2337":{"id":"/platform/datasets-6","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#delete-a-file","content":"Delete a file"},"2338":{"id":"/platform/datasets-7","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#work-with-branches","content":"Work with branches"},"2339":{"id":"/platform/datasets-8","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#create-a-dataset","content":"Create a dataset"},"2340":{"id":"/platform/datasets-9","page_id":"/platform/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/datasets#reference","content":"Reference"},"2341":{"id":"/platform/datasets-10","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets","content":"`@osdk/foundry.datasets` reads and writes Foundry datasets. Use it to download a file, export a table as CSV or Arrow, upload files, and group several uploads into one transaction."},"2342":{"id":"/platform/datasets-11","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets","content":"Every sample takes a `client` from `createClient` or `createPlatformClient`; see Set up. Reads need the `api:datasets-read` scope and writes need `api:datasets-write`. A dataset is identified by its RID, such as `ri.foundry.main.dataset.<id>`."},"2343":{"id":"/platform/datasets-12","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets","content":"This page describes version 2.78 of `@osdk/foundry.datasets`. In older versions, such as 2.5, `Files.content` and `Datasets.readTable` resolve to a `Blob` instead of a `Response`."},"2344":{"id":"/platform/datasets-13","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#get-a-dataset","content":"`Datasets.get` returns the dataset's `rid`, `name`, and `parentFolderRid`. `Datasets.getSchema` returns its column schema:"},"2345":{"id":"/platform/datasets-14","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#get-a-dataset","content":"`Datasets.getSchema` reads the latest committed version of the default branch. Pass `{ branchName }` or `{ endTransactionRid }` to read another."},"2346":{"id":"/platform/datasets-15","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"`Datasets.readTable` exports a tabular dataset as CSV or Apache Arrow and resolves to a `Response`:"},"2347":{"id":"/platform/datasets-16","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"| Option   | Type               | Description                  |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------- |\n| `format` | `\"CSV\" \\| \"ARROW\"` | Required. The export format. |","table":"table-0"},"2348":{"id":"/platform/datasets-17","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"| Option    | Type       | Description                                                  |\n| --------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `columns` | `string[]` | Required. The columns to include. Pass `[]` for all columns. |","table":"table-0"},"2349":{"id":"/platform/datasets-18","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"| Option     | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `rowLimit` | `number` | The maximum number of rows. Row order is not deterministic. |","table":"table-0"},"2350":{"id":"/platform/datasets-19","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"| Option       | Type     | Description                                                   |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `branchName` | `string` | The branch to read. Defaults to the dataset's default branch. |","table":"table-0"},"2351":{"id":"/platform/datasets-20","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"| Option                                     | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ------------------------------------------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `startTransactionRid`, `endTransactionRid` | `string` | Read the view at, or between, specific transactions. |","table":"table-0"},"2352":{"id":"/platform/datasets-21","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#read-a-table","content":"For `\"ARROW\"`, read the body with `response.arrayBuffer()` and decode it with an Arrow library such as `apache-arrow`. `readTable` does not support views."},"2353":{"id":"/platform/datasets-22","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"`Files.list` lists the files in the latest view of the default branch, one page at a time. `Files.content` downloads one file:"},"2354":{"id":"/platform/datasets-23","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"Each `File` has `path`, `transactionRid`, `sizeBytes` (a string, when known), and `updatedTime`. `Files.get` returns the same metadata for one path."},"2355":{"id":"/platform/datasets-24","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"`Files.list`, `Files.get`, and `Files.content` take the same view options:"},"2356":{"id":"/platform/datasets-25","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"| Option | Reads                                  |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| None   | The latest view of the default branch. |","table":"table-1"},"2357":{"id":"/platform/datasets-26","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"| Option       | Reads                           |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------- |\n| `branchName` | The latest view of that branch. |","table":"table-1"},"2358":{"id":"/platform/datasets-27","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"| Option              | Reads                            |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `endTransactionRid` | The view as of that transaction. |","table":"table-1"},"2359":{"id":"/platform/datasets-28","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"| Option                                        | Reads                                                                                                      |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `startTransactionRid` and `endTransactionRid` | Files changed between the two transactions. Set both to the same RID to see only that transaction's files. |","table":"table-1"},"2360":{"id":"/platform/datasets-29","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#list-and-download-files","content":"To read every page of `Files.list`, use the `paginate` helper from Call platform APIs."},"2361":{"id":"/platform/datasets-30","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"`Files.upload` takes the dataset RID, the file path, and the content as a `Blob`. Without options, it uploads in a new transaction on the default branch and commits it:"},"2362":{"id":"/platform/datasets-31","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"It resolves to the new `File`. If a file already exists at that path, only the newest version is visible afterwards."},"2363":{"id":"/platform/datasets-32","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"| Option       | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ------------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `branchName` | `string` | Upload to this branch in a new transaction, which is committed. |","table":"table-2"},"2364":{"id":"/platform/datasets-33","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"| Option            | Type                                             | Description                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `transactionType` | `\"APPEND\" \\| \"UPDATE\" \\| \"SNAPSHOT\" \\| \"DELETE\"` | With `branchName`, the type of the new transaction. Defaults to `\"UPDATE\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"2365":{"id":"/platform/datasets-34","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"| Option           | Type     | Description                                               |\n| ---------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `transactionRid` | `string` | Upload into an open transaction that you commit yourself. |","table":"table-2"},"2366":{"id":"/platform/datasets-35","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-a-single-file","content":"In a browser, a `File` from `<input type=\"file\">` is a `Blob`, so you can pass it as the content."},"2367":{"id":"/platform/datasets-36","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"To upload several files atomically, open a transaction, upload into it, then commit. If anything fails, abort it so no partial upload becomes visible:"},"2368":{"id":"/platform/datasets-37","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"Create a transaction with `Transactions.create`. Pass the branch as a query parameter, or omit it for the default branch."},"2369":{"id":"/platform/datasets-38","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"Upload each file with `Files.upload`, passing `transactionRid`."},"2370":{"id":"/platform/datasets-39","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"Call `Transactions.commit`, or `Transactions.abort` on failure."},"2371":{"id":"/platform/datasets-40","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"The transaction type decides what the committed view contains:"},"2372":{"id":"/platform/datasets-41","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"| Type       | Effect on the view                                                       |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `SNAPSHOT` | Replaces every file. The view contains only files from this transaction. |","table":"table-3"},"2373":{"id":"/platform/datasets-42","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"| Type     | Effect on the view                                 |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `UPDATE` | Adds files and overwrites files at the same paths. |","table":"table-3"},"2374":{"id":"/platform/datasets-43","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"| Type     | Effect on the view                                  |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `APPEND` | Adds new files. It cannot overwrite existing files. |","table":"table-3"},"2375":{"id":"/platform/datasets-44","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"| Type     | Effect on the view                                                  |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `DELETE` | Removes files. Use it with `Files.deleteFile` and `transactionRid`. |","table":"table-3"},"2376":{"id":"/platform/datasets-45","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#upload-in-a-transaction","content":"A `Transaction` has `rid`, `transactionType`, `status` (`\"OPEN\"`, `\"COMMITTED\"`, or `\"ABORTED\"`), `createdTime`, and `closedTime`. Check a transaction later with `Transactions.get`."},"2377":{"id":"/platform/datasets-46","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#delete-a-file","content":"`Files.deleteFile` removes a file in a new `DELETE` transaction on the default branch, which it commits. The file stays visible in historical views. Pass `branchName` for another branch, or `transactionRid` to delete several files in one open `DELETE` transaction:"},"2378":{"id":"/platform/datasets-47","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#work-with-branches","content":"`Branches` creates, reads, lists, and deletes dataset branches. A new branch can point at a committed transaction:"},"2379":{"id":"/platform/datasets-48","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#work-with-branches","content":"Each `Branch` has a `name` and the `transactionRid` it points to, if any. Delete one with `Branches.deleteBranch(client, datasetRid, branchName)`. The default branch is `master` on most stacks."},"2380":{"id":"/platform/datasets-49","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#create-a-dataset","content":"`Datasets.create` creates an empty dataset in a folder, with a default branch:"},"2381":{"id":"/platform/datasets-50","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#reference","content":"| Function                           | Endpoint                        | Scope               | Returns   |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------- | --------- |\n| `Datasets.get(client, datasetRid)` | `GET /v2/datasets/{datasetRid}` | `api:datasets-read` | `Dataset` |","table":"table-4"},"2382":{"id":"/platform/datasets-51","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#reference","content":"| Function                        | Endpoint            | Scope                | Returns   |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------- | -------------------- | --------- |\n| `Datasets.create(client, bod