                                 | Endpoint                                  | Scope                | Returns  |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------- | -------- |\n| `Branches.create(client, datasetRid, body)` | `POST /v2/datasets/{datasetRid}/branches` | `api:datasets-write` | `Branch` |","table":"table-4"},"2397":{"id":"/platform/datasets-66","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#reference","content":"| Function                                                | Endpoint                                                 | Scope                | Returns |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------- |\n| `Branches.deleteBranch(client, datasetRid, branchName)` | `DELETE /v2/datasets/{datasetRid}/branches/{branchName}` | `api:datasets-write` | `void`  |","table":"table-4"},"2398":{"id":"/platform/datasets-67","page_id":"/platform/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/datasets#reference","content":"All of these are stable. The package also covers views (`Views`) and a dataset's schedules (`Datasets.getSchedules`), and has preview endpoints for transaction history, jobs, and health checks that need `preview: true`, as described in Call platform APIs."},"2399":{"id":"/platform","page_id":"/platform","type":"page","content":"Platform SDK overview","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Platform SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/platform"},"2400":{"id":"/platform-0","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform","content":"The @osdk/foundry packages wrap Foundry platform REST APIs for users, datasets, media sets, builds, and more, alongside the Ontology SDK."},"2401":{"id":"/platform-1","page_id":"/platform","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform#osdk-and-platform-sdk","content":"OSDK and Platform SDK"},"2402":{"id":"/platform-2","page_id":"/platform","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform#packages","content":"Packages"},"2403":{"id":"/platform-3","page_id":"/platform","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform#stable-and-preview-endpoints","content":"Stable and preview endpoints"},"2404":{"id":"/platform-4","page_id":"/platform","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"2405":{"id":"/platform-5","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform","content":"The Platform SDK is a set of `@osdk/foundry.*` packages, one per area of the Foundry API. Use it to call the parts of Foundry that are not Ontology data: users and groups, datasets, media sets, builds, folders, and Ontology metadata."},"2406":{"id":"/platform-6","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#osdk-and-platform-sdk","content":"The Ontology SDK (OSDK) and the Platform SDK can share one client and one token provider. They cover different parts of Foundry."},"2407":{"id":"/platform-7","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#osdk-and-platform-sdk","content":"|            | Ontology SDK                                                           | Platform SDK                                                                                                 |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Use it for | Reading and editing your Ontology: objects, links, actions, functions. | Foundry platform resources: users, groups, markings, datasets, media sets, builds, files, Ontology metadata. |","table":"table-0"},"2408":{"id":"/platform-8","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#osdk-and-platform-sdk","content":"|          | Ontology SDK                                                                   | Platform SDK                                                                                                        |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Packages | `@osdk/client` plus an SDK generated for your Ontology, such as `@my-app/sdk`. | Fixed packages published by Palantir, such as `@osdk/foundry.admin`. The same package works on every Foundry stack. |","table":"table-0"},"2409":{"id":"/platform-9","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#osdk-and-platform-sdk","content":"|       | Ontology SDK                                                                    | Platform SDK                                                                          |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Types | Generated from your object types, so `Employee` has `fullName` and `startDate`. | Generic request and response types from the public API, such as `User` and `Dataset`. |","table":"table-0"},"2410":{"id":"/platform-10","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#osdk-and-platform-sdk","content":"|            | Ontology SDK                   | Platform SDK               |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------- |\n| Call style | `client(Employee).fetchPage()` | `Users.getCurrent(client)` |","table":"table-0"},"2411":{"id":"/platform-11","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#osdk-and-platform-sdk","content":"|        | Ontology SDK                               | Platform SDK                                                                         |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Client | `createClient(baseUrl, ontologyRid, auth)` | The same client, or `createPlatformClient(baseUrl, auth)` when there is no Ontology. |","table":"table-0"},"2412":{"id":"/platform-12","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#osdk-and-platform-sdk","content":"Use the Platform SDK when the OSDK has no equivalent. To read objects, apply actions, or upload media to an object property, use the OSDK."},"2413":{"id":"/platform-13","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#packages","content":"Each package exports one namespace per resource. Install only the packages you call."},"2414":{"id":"/platform-14","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#packages","content":"| Package               | Namespaces                                                                                                                                                  | Purpose                                                                          |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.admin` | `Users`, `Groups`, `GroupMembers`, `GroupMemberships`, `Markings`, `MarkingCategories`, `MarkingMembers`, `Organizations`, `Roles`, `CbacBanners`, and more | Users, groups, memberships, markings, organizations, and classification banners. |","table":"table-1"},"2415":{"id":"/platform-15","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#packages","content":"| Package                   | Namespaces                                                         | Purpose                                       |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.aipagents` | `Agents`, `Agent