---------------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.widgets` | `WidgetSets`, `Releases`, `Repositories`, `WidgetsDevModeSettings`, `WidgetsDevModeSettingsV2` | Custom widget sets, releases, and dev mode. |","table":"table-1"},"2440":{"id":"/platform-40","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#packages","content":"`@osdk/foundry` re-exports every package as a namespace, such as `Admin` and `Datasets`. Prefer the individual packages: they version independently and keep your bundle small."},"2441":{"id":"/platform-41","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#stable-and-preview-endpoints","content":"Every function's JSDoc carries a release tag:"},"2442":{"id":"/platform-42","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#stable-and-preview-endpoints","content":"| Tag       | Meaning | How to call it    |\n| --------- | ------- | ----------------- |\n| `@public` | Stable. | Call it normally. |","table":"table-2"},"2443":{"id":"/platform-43","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#stable-and-preview-endpoints","content":"| Tag     | Meaning                                         | How to call it                                |\n| ------- | ----------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `@beta` | Preview. The shape can change between versions. | Pass `preview: true` in the query parameters. |","table":"table-2"},"2444":{"id":"/platform-44","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#stable-and-preview-endpoints","content":"| Tag      | Meaning                                                                            | How to call it                                |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `@alpha` | Early preview. Expect changes, and the endpoint may not be enabled on every stack. | Pass `preview: true` in the query parameters. |","table":"table-2"},"2445":{"id":"/platform-45","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#stable-and-preview-endpoints","content":"Preview endpoints take an optional `preview` query parameter of type `PreviewMode` (a `boolean`). Without it, the server rejects the request with an `ApiFeaturePreviewUsageOnly` error:"},"2446":{"id":"/platform-46","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#stable-and-preview-endpoints","content":"The calling convention page covers where `preview` goes when an endpoint has a body."},"2447":{"id":"/platform-47","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#next-steps","content":"Install packages, create a client, and request the scopes each API needs."},"2448":{"id":"/platform-48","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#next-steps","content":"Argument order, pagination, errors, and binary responses."},"2449":{"id":"/platform-49","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#next-steps","content":"Look up users, list groups and members, and read markings."},"2450":{"id":"/platform-50","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#next-steps","content":"Read files and tables, and upload in transactions."},"2451":{"id":"/platform-51","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#next-steps","content":"Upload media items and read their content and metadata."},"2452":{"id":"/platform-52","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#next-steps","content":"List object types and action types at runtime."},"2453":{"id":"/platform-53","page_id":"/platform","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform#next-steps","content":"For React hooks that call the admin APIs, see Users and markings in React."},"2454":{"id":"/platform/media-sets","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","type":"page","content":"Media sets","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Platform SDK","Recipes"],"tags":[],"url":"/platform/media-sets"},"2455":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-0","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets","content":"Upload media items, read their content and metadata, and run transformations with @osdk/foundry.mediasets."},"2456":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-1","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/media-sets#identify-a-media-item","content":"Identify a media item"},"2457":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-2","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/media-sets#download-an-item","content":"Download an item"},"2458":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-3","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/media-sets#read-metadata","content":"Read metadata"},"2459":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-4","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/media-sets#pass-a-read-token","content":"Pass a read token"},"2460":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-5","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-an-item","content":"Upload an item"},"2461":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-6","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-into-a-transaction","content":"Upload into a transaction"},"2462":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-7","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-temporary-media","content":"Upload temporary media"},"2463":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-8","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/media-sets#transform-an-item","content":"Transform an item"},"2464":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-9","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"Reference"},"2465":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-10","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets","content":"`@osdk/foundry.mediasets` works with media sets: Foundry collections of images, documents, audio, video, and other files. Use it to upload items to a media set, download them, read their metadata, and convert them with transformations."},"2466":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-11","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets","content":"Every sample takes a `client` from `createClient` or `createPlatformClient`; see Set up. Reads need the `api:mediasets-read` scope, uploads need `api:mediasets-write`, and transformations need `api:mediasets-transform`. All functions are on the `MediaSets` namespace."},"2467":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-12","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets","content":"To read media from an object property or upload a file as an action parameter, use the OSDK instead. It handles the media reference and read token for you. See Media."},"2468":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-13","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#identify-a-media-item","content":"A media set has a RID such as `ri.mio.main.media-set.<id>`, and each item in it has a media item RID. Functions take both as path parameters, in that order."},"2469":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-14","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#identify-a-media-item","content":"When you only have the item's path in the set, look up its RID with `getRidByPath`. It is a preview endpoint:"},"2470":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-15","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#identify-a-media-item","content":"`mediaItemRid` is `undefined` when no item has that path."},"2471":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-16","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#download-an-item","content":"`MediaSets.read` resolves to a `Response` with the item's content:"},"2472":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-17","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#download-an-item","content":"If the set converted the file on upload, `read` returns the converted content. `MediaSets.readOriginal` returns the file as it was uploaded."},"2473":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-18","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#read-metadata","content":"`MediaSets.info` returns basic information, and `MediaSets.metadata` returns details that depend on the media type:"},"2474":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-19","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#read-metadata","content":"| `info` field | Description                                      |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `path`       | The item's path in the media set, if it has one. |","table":"table-0"},"2475":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-20","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#read-metadata","content":"| `info` field | Description            |\n| ------------ | ---------------------- |\n| `mimeType`   | The item's media type. |","table":"table-0"},"2476":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-21","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#read-metadata","content":"| `info` field                     | Description                                                    |\n| -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `originallyUploadedFileMimeType` | The media type of the file as uploaded, when it was converted. |","table":"table-0"},"2477":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-22","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#read-metadata","content":"| `info` field | Description    |\n| ------------ | -------------- |\n| `sizeBytes`  | Size in bytes. |","table":"table-0"},"2478":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-23","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#read-metadata","content":"| `info` field | Description                             |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------- |\n| `viewRid`    | The media set view the item belongs to. |","table":"table-0"},"2479":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-24","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#read-metadata","content":"| `info` field       | Description              |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------ |\n| `logicalTimestamp` | When the item was added. |","table":"table-0"},"2480":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-25","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#read-metadata","content":"`metadata.type` is one of `\"imagery\"`, `\"document\"`, `\"spreadsheet\"`, `\"audio\"`, `\"video\"`, `\"cad\"`, `\"model3d\"`, `\"dicom\"`, `\"email\"`, or `\"untyped\"`. Narrow on it to read type-specific fields, such as `dimensions` for images or `pages` for documents. Every variant has `sizeBytes`."},"2481":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-26","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#pass-a-read-token","content":"A media reference from an Ontology object carries a read token that grants access to that one item. Pass it as the `ReadToken` header parameter, after any query parameters:"},"2482":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-27","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#pass-a-read-token","content":"`read`, `readOriginal`, `info`, and `metadata` take the header object as their fourth argument. Preview functions such as `reference` take query parameters first: `MediaSets.reference(client, mediaSetRid, mediaItemRid, { preview: true }, { ReadToken })`."},"2483":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-28","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-an-item","content":"`MediaSets.upload` adds a file to a media set. It is a preview endpoint, so pass `preview: true`:"},"2484":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-29","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-an-item","content":"| Option          | Type     | Description                                              |\n| --------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `mediaItemPath` | `string` | The item's path in the set. Some media sets require one. |","table":"table-1"},"2485":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-30","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-an-item","content":"| Option                               | Type     | Description                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `branchName`, `branchRid`, `viewRid` | `string` | Where to upload. Set at most one; without any, the item goes to the default branch. |","table":"table-1"},"2486":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-31","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-an-item","content":"| Option          | Type     | Description                         |\n| --------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `transactionId` | `string` | An open transaction to upload into. |","table":"table-1"},"2487":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-32","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-an-item","content":"| Option    | Type      | Description     |\n| --------- | --------- | --------------- |\n| `preview` | `boolean` | Must be `true`. |","table":"table-1"},"2488":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-33","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-an-item","content":"The content is a `Blob`; a `File` from `<input type=\"file\">` works directly. The response has the new `mediaItemRid` and the `mediaSetViewRid`."},"2489":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-34","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-into-a-transaction","content":"Some media sets require uploads in a transaction. `MediaSets.get` returns the set's `transactionPolicy`; when its `type` is `\"batchTransactions\"`, open a transaction, upload, then commit:"},"2490":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-35","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-into-a-transaction","content":"`MediaSets.create` resolves to the transaction ID as a string. Items uploaded in a transaction appear when it is committed; aborting deletes them."},"2491":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-36","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-temporary-media","content":"`MediaSets.uploadMedia` uploads a file that is not yet in any media set, and returns a `MediaReference`. Pass the reference to an action parameter or media property to keep the file; otherwise it is deleted after one hour. It needs `api:ontologies-read` and `api:ontologies-write` instead of the media set scopes:"},"2492":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-37","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#upload-temporary-media","content":"The reference has `mimeType` and `reference.mediaSetViewItem`, with `mediaSetRid`, `mediaSetViewRid`, `mediaItemRid`, and a read `token`. The OSDK uses this endpoint when you pass a file to an action; prefer that path when you are applying an action."},"2493":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-38","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#transform-an-item","content":"Transformations convert a media item, for example resizing an image or extracting text from a document. Start a job with `MediaSets.transform`, poll `getStatus` until it is `\"SUCCESSFUL\"` or `\"FAILED\"`, then download the output with `getResult`. All three are preview endpoints and need `api:mediasets-transform`:"},"2494":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-39","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#transform-an-item","content":"`transformation.type` selects the conversion, such as `\"image\"`, `\"documentToImage\"`, `\"documentToText\"`, `\"audioToText\"`, or `\"videoToImage\"`. Each type has its own options; your editor lists them from the `Transformation` type. To transform an item you can only read through a read token, pass it as the `Token` header parameter."},"2495":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-40","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                            | Scope                | Status | Returns    |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------ | ---------- |\n| `read(client, mediaSetRid, mediaItemRid, headers?)` | `api:mediasets-read` | Stable | `Response` |","table":"table-2"},"2496":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-41","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                                    | Scope                | Status | Returns    |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------ | ---------- |\n| `readOriginal(client, mediaSetRid, mediaItemRid, headers?)` | `api:mediasets-read` | Stable | `Response` |","table":"table-2"},"2497":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-42","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                            | Scope                | Status | Returns                    |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------ | -------------------------- |\n| `info(client, mediaSetRid, mediaItemRid, headers?)` | `api:mediasets-read` | Stable | `GetMediaItemInfoResponse` |","table":"table-2"},"2498":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-43","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                                | Scope                | Status | Returns             |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------ | ------------------- |\n| `metadata(client, mediaSetRid, mediaItemRid, headers?)` | `api:mediasets-read` | Stable | `MediaItemMetadata` |","table":"table-2"},"2499":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-44","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                            | Scope                                         | Status | Returns          |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------ | ---------------- |\n| `uploadMedia(client, blob, { filename }, headers?)` | `api:ontologies-read`, `api:ontologies-write` | Stable | `MediaReference` |","table":"table-2"},"2500":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-45","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                           | Scope                | Status | Returns               |\n| ---------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------ | --------------------- |\n| `get(client, mediaSetRid, query?)` | `api:mediasets-read` | Beta   | `GetMediaSetResponse` |","table":"table-2"},"2501":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-46","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                   | Scope                | Status | Returns                         |\n| ------------------------------------------ | -------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------- |\n| `getRidByPath(client, mediaSetRid, query)` | `api:mediasets-read` | Beta   | `GetMediaItemRidByPathResponse` |","table":"table-2"},"2502":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-47","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                                         | Scope                | Status | Returns          |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------ | ---------------- |\n| `reference(client, mediaSetRid, mediaItemRid, query?, headers?)` | `api:mediasets-read` | Beta   | `MediaReference` |","table":"table-2"},"2503":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-48","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                    | Scope                 | Status | Returns                |\n| ------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------ | ---------------------- |\n| `upload(client, mediaSetRid, blob, query?)` | `api:mediasets-write` | Beta   | `PutMediaItemResponse` |","table":"table-2"},"2504":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-49","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                              | Scope                 | Status | Returns        |\n| ------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------ | -------------- |\n| `create(client, mediaSetRid, query?)` | `api:mediasets-write` | Beta   | Transaction ID |","table":"table-2"},"2505":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-50","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                             | Scope                 | Status | Returns |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------ | ------- |\n| `commit(client, mediaSetRid, transactionId, query?)` | `api:mediasets-write` | Beta   | `void`  |","table":"table-2"},"2506":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-51","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                            | Scope                 | Status | Returns |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------ | ------- |\n| `abort(client, mediaSetRid, transactionId, query?)` | `api:mediasets-write` | Beta   | `void`  |","table":"table-2"},"2507":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-52","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                            | Scope                 | Status | Returns |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------ | ------- |\n| `clear(client, mediaSetRid, query)` | `api:mediasets-write` | Beta   | `void`  |","table":"table-2"},"2508":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-53","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                                               | Scope                     | Status | Returns                      |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------ | ---------------------------- |\n| `transform(client, mediaSetRid, mediaItemRid, body, query?, headers?)` | `api:mediasets-transform` | Beta   | `TransformMediaItemResponse` |","table":"table-2"},"2509":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-54","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                                                | Scope                     | Status | Returns                              |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `getStatus(client, mediaSetRid, mediaItemRid, jobId, query?, headers?)` | `api:mediasets-transform` | Beta   | `GetTransformationJobStatusResponse` |","table":"table-2"},"2510":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-55","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"| Function                                                                | Scope                     | Status | Returns    |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------ | ---------- |\n| `getResult(client, mediaSetRid, mediaItemRid, jobId, query?, headers?)` | `api:mediasets-transform` | Beta   | `Response` |","table":"table-2"},"2511":{"id":"/platform/media-sets-56","page_id":"/platform/media-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/media-sets#reference","content":"Beta functions need `preview: true`. See Preview endpoints."},"2512":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","type":"page","content":"Ontology metadata","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Platform SDK","Recipes"],"tags":[],"url":"/platform/ontology-metadata"},"2513":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-0","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata","content":"List ontologies, object types, link types, action types, and query types at runtime with @osdk/foundry.ontologies, and know when the OSDK is the better fit."},"2514":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-1","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#when-to-use-the-osdk-instead","content":"When to use the OSDK instead"},"2515":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-2","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#identify-the-ontology","content":"Identify the Ontology"},"2516":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-3","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-object-types","content":"List object types"},"2517":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-4","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"Get an object type"},"2518":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-5","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-link-types","content":"List link types"},"2519":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-6","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-action-types","content":"List action types"},"2520":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-7","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-query-types","content":"List query types"},"2521":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-8","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#interfaces-and-full-metadata","content":"Interfaces and full metadata"},"2522":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-9","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"Reference"},"2523":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-10","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata","content":"`@osdk/foundry.ontologies` reads the schema of any Ontology at runtime: its object types, properties, link types, action types, and query types. Use it for tools that work across object types you do not know at build time, such as schema browsers, admin pages, and code generators."},"2524":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-11","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata","content":"Every sample takes a `client` from `createClient` or `createPlatformClient`; see Set up. Metadata reads need the `api:ontologies-read` scope."},"2525":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-12","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#when-to-use-the-osdk-instead","content":"Your generated SDK already contains the schema of every type it includes, checked at compile time. For those types, `client.fetchMetadata` returns runtime metadata without the Platform SDK:"},"2526":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-13","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#when-to-use-the-osdk-instead","content":"| Need                                                             | Use                                        |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| Display names, descriptions, and properties of types in your SDK | `client.fetchMetadata` from `@osdk/client` |","table":"table-0"},"2527":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-14","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#when-to-use-the-osdk-instead","content":"| Need                               | Use                    |\n| ---------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Load, filter, or aggregate objects | The OSDK. See Objects. |","table":"table-0"},"2528":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-15","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#when-to-use-the-osdk-instead","content":"| Need                                                                | Use                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| Discover object types, actions, or queries that are not in your SDK | `@osdk/foundry.ontologies` |","table":"table-0"},"2529":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-16","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#when-to-use-the-osdk-instead","content":"| Need                               | Use                 |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| List the ontologies a user can see | `OntologiesV2.list` |","table":"table-0"},"2530":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-17","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#when-to-use-the-osdk-instead","content":"| Need                                                                          | Use                        |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| Datasources, release status, and other fields `fetchMetadata` does not return | `@osdk/foundry.ontologies` |","table":"table-0"},"2531":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-18","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#when-to-use-the-osdk-instead","content":"`@osdk/foundry.ontologies` also contains the raw object, link, action, and query endpoints that the OSDK calls. Prefer the OSDK for those: it adds types, pagination helpers, caching in React, and result conversion."},"2532":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-19","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#identify-the-ontology","content":"Every function after `OntologiesV2.list` takes the Ontology as its first path parameter: its API name or its RID. With a generated SDK, pass `$ontologyRid`:"},"2533":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-20","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#identify-the-ontology","content":"`OntologiesV2.get(client, ontology)` returns one Ontology's `apiName`, `displayName`, `description`, and `rid`."},"2534":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-21","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-object-types","content":"`ObjectTypesV2.list` returns one page of object types:"},"2535":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-22","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-object-types","content":"| Option                  | Type | Description               |\n| ----------------------- | ---- | ------------------------- |\n| `pageSize`, `pageToken` |      | Pagination. See Paginate. |","table":"table-1"},"2536":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-23","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-object-types","content":"| Option               | Type      | Description                                |\n| -------------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `includeDatasources` | `boolean` | Include each type's backing `datasources`. |","table":"table-1"},"2537":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-24","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-object-types","content":"| Option   | Type     | Description                          |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `branch` | `string` | Read the schema on a Foundry branch. |","table":"table-1"},"2538":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-25","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-object-types","content":"The list endpoint leaves `aliases` empty. Call `ObjectTypesV2.get` to read them."},"2539":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-26","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"`ObjectTypesV2.get` takes the object type's API name:"},"2540":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-27","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"| `ObjectTypeV2` field                                         | Description            |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- |\n| `apiName`, `displayName`, `pluralDisplayName`, `description` | Names and description. |","table":"table-2"},"2541":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-28","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"| `ObjectTypeV2` field | Description          |\n| -------------------- | -------------------- |\n| `rid`                | The object type RID. |","table":"table-2"},"2542":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-29","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"| `ObjectTypeV2` field | Description                           |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `primaryKey`         | API name of the primary key property. |","table":"table-2"},"2543":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-30","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"| `ObjectTypeV2` field | Description                                          |\n| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `titleProperty`      | API name of the property used as the object's title. |","table":"table-2"},"2544":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-31","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"| `ObjectTypeV2` field | Description                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `properties`         | Map from property API name to `PropertyV2`: `dataType` (discriminated by `type`, such as `\"string\"`, `\"integer\"`, `\"date\"`, `\"array\"`), `displayName`, `description`, `rid`, and `typeClasses`. |","table":"table-2"},"2545":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-32","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"| `ObjectTypeV2` field | Description                                                    |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status`             | `\"ACTIVE\"`, `\"ENDORSED\"`, `\"EXPERIMENTAL\"`, or `\"DEPRECATED\"`. |","table":"table-2"},"2546":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-33","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"| `ObjectTypeV2` field | Description    |\n| -------------------- | -------------- |\n| `icon`, `visibility` | Display hints. |","table":"table-2"},"2547":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-34","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"| `ObjectTypeV2` field | Description        |\n| -------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `aliases`            | Alternative names. |","table":"table-2"},"2548":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-35","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#get-an-object-type","content":"| `ObjectTypeV2` field | Description                                                    |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `datasources`        | Backing datasources, when requested with `includeDatasources`. |","table":"table-2"},"2549":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-36","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-link-types","content":"`ObjectTypesV2.listOutgoingLinkTypes` returns the links from an object type to other types:"},"2550":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-37","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-link-types","content":"For the example `Employee`, this lists `lead`, `reports`, and `office`. Each `LinkTypeSideV2` has `apiName`, `displayName`, `objectTypeApiName` (the target type), `cardinality` (`\"ONE\"` or `\"MANY\"`), `foreignKeyPropertyApiName` when the link is backed by a foreign key, `status`, and `linkTypeRid`. `ObjectTypesV2.getOutgoingLinkType` returns one link by API name."},"2551":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-38","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-action-types","content":"`ActionTypesV2.list` returns one page of action types, and `ActionTypesV2.get` returns one by API name:"},"2552":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-39","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-action-types","content":"An `ActionTypeV2` has `apiName`, `displayName`, `description`, `status`, `rid`, `parameters` (a map from parameter ID to `{ displayName, description, dataType, required, typeClasses }`), and `operations`, which describe the objects and links the action creates, modifies, or deletes. `ActionTypesV2.getByRid` looks one up by RID."},"2553":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-40","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#list-query-types","content":"`QueryTypes.list` and `QueryTypes.get` return functions registered in the Ontology. Each `QueryTypeV2` has `apiName`, `displayName`, `description`, `parameters`, `output`, `rid`, and `version`. `list` returns each query at its latest version; pass `{ version }` to `get` for a specific one:"},"2554":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-41","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#interfaces-and-full-metadata","content":"Interface types and full-Ontology metadata are preview endpoints, so pass `preview: true`:"},"2555":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-42","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#interfaces-and-full-metadata","content":"`OntologiesV2.getFullMetadata` returns objects, links, actions, queries, and interfaces in one response. It may omit entities rather than fail, so do not treat a missing type as proof that it does not exist."},"2556":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-43","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                    | Endpoint             | Status |\n| --------------------------- | -------------------- | ------ |\n| `OntologiesV2.list(client)` | `GET /v2/ontologies` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2557":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-44","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                             | Endpoint                        | Status |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `OntologiesV2.get(client, ontology)` | `GET /v2/ontologies/{ontology}` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2558":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-45","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                                 | Endpoint                                     | Status |\n| -------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `OntologiesV2.getFullMetadata(client, ontology, query?)` | `GET /v2/ontologies/{ontology}/fullMetadata` | Beta   |","table":"table-3"},"2559":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-46","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                       | Endpoint                                    | Status |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `ObjectTypesV2.list(client, ontology, query?)` | `GET /v2/ontologies/{ontology}/objectTypes` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2560":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-47","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                                  | Endpoint                                                 | Status |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `ObjectTypesV2.get(client, ontology, objectType, query?)` | `GET /v2/ontologies/{ontology}/objectTypes/{objectType}` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2561":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-48","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                                                    | Endpoint                                             | Status |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `ObjectTypesV2.listOutgoingLinkTypes(client, ontology, objectType, query?)` | `GET .../objectTypes/{objectType}/outgoingLinkTypes` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2562":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-49","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                                                            | Endpoint                               | Status |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `ObjectTypesV2.getOutgoingLinkType(client, ontology, objectType, linkType, query?)` | `GET .../outgoingLinkTypes/{linkType}` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2563":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-50","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                       | Endpoint                                    | Status |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `ActionTypesV2.list(client, ontology, query?)` | `GET /v2/ontologies/{ontology}/actionTypes` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2564":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-51","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                                  | Endpoint                                                 | Status |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `ActionTypesV2.get(client, ontology, actionType, query?)` | `GET /v2/ontologies/{ontology}/actionTypes/{actionType}` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2565":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-52","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                                          | Endpoint                                    | Status |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `ActionTypesV2.getByRid(client, ontology, actionTypeRid, query?)` | `GET .../actionTypes/byRid/{actionTypeRid}` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2566":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-53","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                    | Endpoint                                   | Status |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------ |\n| `QueryTypes.list(client, ontology, query?)` | `GET /v2/ontologies/{ontology}/queryTypes` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2567":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-54","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                                 | Endpoint                                                  | Status |\n| -------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `QueryTypes.get(client, ontology, queryApiName, query?)` | `GET /v2/ontologies/{ontology}/queryTypes/{queryApiName}` | Stable |","table":"table-3"},"2568":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-55","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                            | Endpoint                                       | Status |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `OntologyInterfaces.list(client, ontology, query?)` | `GET /v2/ontologies/{ontology}/interfaceTypes` | Beta   |","table":"table-3"},"2569":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-56","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"| Function                                                          | Endpoint                                                       | Status |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `OntologyInterfaces.get(client, ontology, interfaceType, query?)` | `GET /v2/ontologies/{ontology}/interfaceTypes/{interfaceType}` | Beta   |","table":"table-3"},"2570":{"id":"/platform/ontology-metadata-57","page_id":"/platform/ontology-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/ontology-metadata#reference","content":"All of these need `api:ontologies-read`."},"2571":{"id":"/platform/setup","page_id":"/platform/setup","type":"page","content":"Set up the Platform SDK","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Platform SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/platform/setup"},"2572":{"id":"/platform/setup-0","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup","content":"Install @osdk/foundry packages, create a client with createPlatformClient or reuse an OSDK client, and request the OAuth scopes each API needs."},"2573":{"id":"/platform/setup-1","page_id":"/platform/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/setup#install","content":"Install"},"2574":{"id":"/platform/setup-2","page_id":"/platform/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/setup#create-a-platform-client","content":"Create a platform client"},"2575":{"id":"/platform/setup-3","page_id":"/platform/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/setup#reuse-an-osdk-client","content":"Reuse an OSDK client"},"2576":{"id":"/platform/setup-4","page_id":"/platform/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"Request scopes"},"2577":{"id":"/platform/setup-5","page_id":"/platform/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/setup#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"2578":{"id":"/platform/setup-6","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup","content":"Install the `@osdk/foundry.*` packages you need, create a client, and make sure your token carries the scopes those APIs require."},"2579":{"id":"/platform/setup-7","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#install","content":"Install `@osdk/client` for the client, `@osdk/oauth` for tokens, and one package per API area:"},"2580":{"id":"/platform/setup-8","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#install","content":"Add more packages as you need them, for example `@osdk/foundry.datasets` or `@osdk/foundry.mediasets`. See the package list for every package. Shared types such as `PageToken` live in `@osdk/foundry.core`, which each package depends on; install it directly if you import its types."},"2581":{"id":"/platform/setup-9","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#create-a-platform-client","content":"If your app does not use the Ontology SDK, create a client with `createPlatformClient`:"},"2582":{"id":"/platform/setup-10","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#create-a-platform-client","content":"| Argument  | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| --------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `baseUrl` | `string` | The base URL of your Foundry stack, such as `https://example.palantirfoundry.com`. Requests go to `<baseUrl>/api/v2/...`. An empty string throws `baseUrl cannot be empty`. |","table":"table-0"},"2583":{"id":"/platform/setup-11","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#create-a-platform-client","content":"| Argument        | Type                    | Description                                                                          |\n| --------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `tokenProvider` | `() => Promise<string>` | Returns a bearer token for each request. Usually an OAuth client from `@osdk/oauth`. |","table":"table-0"},"2584":{"id":"/platform/setup-12","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#create-a-platform-client","content":"| Argument  | Type        | Description                                              |\n| --------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `options` | `undefined` | Reserved. Pass `undefined` if you need to set `fetchFn`. |","table":"table-0"},"2585":{"id":"/platform/setup-13","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#create-a-platform-client","content":"| Argument  | Type           | Description                                                         |\n| --------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fetchFn` | `typeof fetch` | The `fetch` used for every request. Defaults to the global `fetch`. |","table":"table-0"},"2586":{"id":"/platform/setup-14","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#create-a-platform-client","content":"The returned `PlatformClient` works only with `@osdk/foundry.*` functions. It has no Ontology, so it cannot load objects or apply actions."},"2587":{"id":"/platform/setup-15","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#reuse-an-osdk-client","content":"A client from `createClient` also works with every platform function. `Client` extends the same `SharedClient` interface that the platform functions accept, so you do not need a second client:"},"2588":{"id":"/platform/setup-16","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#reuse-an-osdk-client","content":"In React, `OsdkProvider` holds this client and the hooks in `@osdk/react/platform-apis` call the admin APIs with it. See Users and markings in React."},"2589":{"id":"/platform/setup-17","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#reuse-an-osdk-client","content":"Both kinds of client add the `Authorization` header to each request and retry a request up to three times, with backoff, when Foundry responds with `429` or `503`."},"2590":{"id":"/platform/setup-18","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"Each function's JSDoc lists the OAuth scopes it needs under **Required Scopes**. Foundry rejects calls from a token that lacks them. The scopes used by the packages on these pages:"},"2591":{"id":"/platform/setup-19","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"| Package               | Read             | Write             |\n| --------------------- | ---------------- | ----------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.admin` | `api:admin-read` | `api:admin-write` |","table":"table-1"},"2592":{"id":"/platform/setup-20","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"| Package                  | Read                | Write                |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------- | -------------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.datasets` | `api:datasets-read` | `api:datasets-write` |","table":"table-1"},"2593":{"id":"/platform/setup-21","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"| Package                   | Read                 | Write                                                                     |\n| ------------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.mediasets` | `api:mediasets-read` | `api:mediasets-write`, plus `api:mediasets-transform` for transformations |","table":"table-1"},"2594":{"id":"/platform/setup-22","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"| Package                    | Read                  | Write                  |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.ontologies` | `api:ontologies-read` | `api:ontologies-write` |","table":"table-1"},"2595":{"id":"/platform/setup-23","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"| Package                    | Read                  | Write                  |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.filesystem` | `api:filesystem-read` | `api:filesystem-write` |","table":"table-1"},"2596":{"id":"/platform/setup-24","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"| Package                       | Read                     | Write                     |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------- |\n| `@osdk/foundry.orchestration` | `api:orchestration-read` | `api:orchestration-write` |","table":"table-1"},"2597":{"id":"/platform/setup-25","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"Some endpoints differ from their package's pattern. For example, `MarkingMembers.list` needs `api:admin-write`, `MediaSets.uploadMedia` needs `api:ontologies-read` and `api:ontologies-write`, and `Groups.listCurrent` needs no scope. Check the JSDoc of each function you call; your editor shows it on hover."},"2598":{"id":"/platform/setup-26","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"Pass the scopes to your OAuth client, and allow each one for your application on **OAuth & scopes** in Developer Console. `@osdk/oauth` only requests the four Ontology scopes by default, so add platform scopes explicitly. A stored refresh token is reused only for the same set of scopes, so changing `scopes` signs users in again. See Authentication."},"2599":{"id":"/platform/setup-27","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#request-scopes","content":"For a server or scheduled job, pass the scopes as the fourth argument of `createConfidentialOauthClient`:"},"2600":{"id":"/platform/setup-28","page_id":"/platform/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/setup#next-steps","content":"Read Call platform APIs for argument order, pagination, and error handling."},"2601":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","type":"page","content":"Users and groups","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Platform SDK","Recipes"],"tags":[],"url":"/platform/users-and-groups"},"2602":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-0","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups","content":"Look up users, search and list them, read group memberships, manage group members, and read markings with @osdk/foundry.admin."},"2603":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-1","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"Get the signed-in user"},"2604":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-2","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/users-and-groups#look-up-users-by-id","content":"Look up users by ID"},"2605":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-3","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/users-and-groups#search-and-list-users","content":"Search and list users"},"2606":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-4","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/users-and-groups#show-a-profile-picture","content":"Show a profile picture"},"2607":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-5","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-group-memberships","content":"Read group memberships"},"2608":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-6","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/users-and-groups#find-groups-and-their-members","content":"Find groups and their members"},"2609":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-7","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/users-and-groups#add-and-remove-group-members","content":"Add and remove group members"},"2610":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-8","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"Read markings"},"2611":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-9","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/platform/users-and-groups#reference","content":"Reference"},"2612":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-10","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups","content":"`@osdk/foundry.admin` reads and manages Foundry users, groups, and markings. Use it to show who is signed in, resolve user IDs to names, check group membership, and list the markings a user can view."},"2613":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-11","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups","content":"Every sample takes a `client` from `createClient` or `createPlatformClient`; see Set up. Reads need the `api:admin-read` scope and writes need `api:admin-write`. In React, the hooks in `@osdk/react/platform-apis` wrap several of these calls; see Users and markings in React."},"2614":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-12","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"`Users.getCurrent` returns the user the token belongs to:"},"2615":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-13","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"A `User` has these fields:"},"2616":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-14","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"| Field | Type     | Description                                                          |\n| ----- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | `string` | The user ID. Other endpoints take this as `userId` or `principalId`. |","table":"table-0"},"2617":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-15","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"| Field      | Type     | Description   |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------- |\n| `username` | `string` | The username. |","table":"table-0"},"2618":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-16","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"| Field       | Type                  | Description |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | ----------- |\n| `givenName` | `string \\| undefined` | First name. |","table":"table-0"},"2619":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-17","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"| Field        | Type                  | Description |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | ----------- |\n| `familyName` | `string \\| undefined` | Last name.  |","table":"table-0"},"2620":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-18","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"| Field   | Type                  | Description    |\n| ------- | --------------------- | -------------- |\n| `email` | `string \\| undefined` | Email address. |","table":"table-0"},"2621":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-19","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"| Field   | Type     | Description                                   |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `realm` | `string` | The authentication realm the user belongs to. |","table":"table-0"},"2622":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-20","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"| Field          | Type                  | Description                             |\n| -------------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `organization` | `string \\| undefined` | RID of the user's primary organization. |","table":"table-0"},"2623":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-21","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"| Field    | Type                    | Description                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `status` | `\"ACTIVE\" \\| \"DELETED\"` | Whether the user is active. |","table":"table-0"},"2624":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-22","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#get-the-signed-in-user","content":"| Field        | Type                       | Description                            |\n| ------------ | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `attributes` | `Record<string, string[]>` | Attributes from the identity provider. |","table":"table-0"},"2625":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-23","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#look-up-users-by-id","content":"`Users.get` takes a user ID. Pass `status: \"DELETED\"` to resolve a user who has been removed, for example the author of an old record:"},"2626":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-24","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#look-up-users-by-id","content":"To resolve many IDs at once, use `Users.getBatch`. It takes up to 500 elements and returns a map keyed by user ID. IDs that do not resolve are missing from the map:"},"2627":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-25","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#search-and-list-users","content":"`Users.search` runs a case-insensitive prefix search on username, given name, and family name. It only returns active users:"},"2628":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-26","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#search-and-list-users","content":"`Users.list` lists every user, one page at a time. Its query parameters:"},"2629":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-27","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#search-and-list-users","content":"| Option    | Type                    | Default      | Description                                                  |\n| --------- | ----------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `include` | `\"ACTIVE\" \\| \"DELETED\"` | Active users | Which users to list. Pass `\"DELETED\"` to list removed users. |","table":"table-1"},"2630":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-28","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#search-and-list-users","content":"| Option     | Type     | Default | Description                                               |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pageSize` | `number` |         | Preferred page size. The server can return more or fewer. |","table":"table-1"},"2631":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-29","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#search-and-list-users","content":"| Option      | Type     | Default | Description                             |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `pageToken` | `string` |         | `nextPageToken` from the previous page. |","table":"table-1"},"2632":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-30","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#search-and-list-users","content":"To read every page, use the `paginate` helper from Call platform APIs."},"2633":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-31","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#show-a-profile-picture","content":"`Users.profilePicture` returns the image as a `Response`:"},"2634":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-32","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#show-a-profile-picture","content":"A user without a picture rejects with a `ProfilePictureNotFound` error."},"2635":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-33","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-group-memberships","content":"`Groups.listCurrent` returns every group the signed-in user belongs to, directly or through another group. It needs no scope, so any signed-in user can call it, but it is a preview endpoint:"},"2636":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-34","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-group-memberships","content":"For any other user, `GroupMemberships.list` returns the IDs of their groups. Set `transitive: true` to include groups they belong to through other groups, then resolve the IDs with `Groups.getBatch`:"},"2637":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-35","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-group-memberships","content":"This reads one page. Paginate with `pageToken` for users in many groups."},"2638":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-36","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-group-memberships","content":"A `Group` has `id`, `name`, `description`, `realm`, `organizations` (organization RIDs), and `attributes`."},"2639":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-37","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#find-groups-and-their-members","content":"`Groups.search` runs a prefix search on group name. `GroupMembers.list` returns a group's members, which can be users or groups:"},"2640":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-38","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#find-groups-and-their-members","content":"| Option       | Type      | Description                       |\n| ------------ | --------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `transitive` | `boolean` | Include members of nested groups. |","table":"table-2"},"2641":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-39","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#find-groups-and-their-members","content":"| Option               | Type      | Description                                          |\n| -------------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `includeExpirations` | `boolean` | Include each member's `expiration`, when one is set. |","table":"table-2"},"2642":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-40","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#find-groups-and-their-members","content":"| Option                  | Type | Description               |\n| ----------------------- | ---- | ------------------------- |\n| `pageSize`, `pageToken` |      | Pagination. See Paginate. |","table":"table-2"},"2643":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-41","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#find-groups-and-their-members","content":"Each member is `{ principalType: \"USER\" | \"GROUP\", principalId, expiration? }`."},"2644":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-42","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#add-and-remove-group-members","content":"Adding and removing members needs `api:admin-write` and permission to manage the group. Both take the group ID and a list of principal IDs, which can be user or group IDs, and resolve to `undefined`:"},"2645":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-43","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#add-and-remove-group-members","content":"`expiration` is optional. Without it, the membership does not expire."},"2646":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-44","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"Markings restrict who can view a resource. `Users.getMarkings` returns the IDs of the markings a user is a member of, and `Markings.list` and `MarkingCategories.list` return the markings and categories the token can see. Join them on `categoryId`:"},"2647":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-45","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"`Markings.list` and `MarkingCategories.list` accept at most 100 per page and include deleted entries unless you pass `includeDeleted: false`. Paginate to read them all. To look up specific markings, use `Markings.get` or `Markings.getBatch`."},"2648":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-46","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"| Marking field | Description     |\n| ------------- | --------------- |\n| `id`          | The marking ID. |","table":"table-3"},"2649":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-47","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"| Marking field | Description                 |\n| ------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `categoryId`  | The category it belongs to. |","table":"table-3"},"2650":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-48","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"| Marking field         | Description   |\n| --------------------- | ------------- |\n| `name`, `description` | Display text. |","table":"table-3"},"2651":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-49","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"| Marking field  | Description                                      |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `organization` | The organization RID, for organization markings. |","table":"table-3"},"2652":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-50","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"| Marking field | Description                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `deleted`     | Whether the marking has been deleted. |","table":"table-3"},"2653":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-51","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"| Marking field              | Description                      |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `createdTime`, `createdBy` | When and by whom it was created. |","table":"table-3"},"2654":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-52","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"Listing who can view a marking, with `MarkingMembers.list`, needs `api:admin-write` because only marking administrators can see its members."},"2655":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-53","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#read-markings","content":"For classification-based access control (CBAC), `CbacBanners.get` returns the banner text and colors for a set of marking IDs. It is a preview endpoint; see the example in Call platform APIs."},"2656":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-54","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#reference","content":"| Function                   | Endpoint                         | Scope            | Status |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ---------------- | ------ |\n| `Users.getCurrent(client)` | `GET /v2/admin/users/getCurrent` | `api:admin-read` | Stable |","table":"table-4"},"2657":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-55","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#reference","content":"| Function                                 | Endpoint                       | Scope            | Status |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ---------------- | ------ |\n| `Users.get(client, userId, { status? })` | `GET /v2/admin/users/{userId}` | `api:admin-read` | Stable |","table":"table-4"},"2658":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-56","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#reference","content":"| Function                           | Endpoint                        | Scope            | Status |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ---------------- | ------ |\n| `Users.getBatch(client, elements)` | `POST /v2/admin/users/getBatch` | `api:admin-read` | Stable |","table":"table-4"},"2659":{"id":"/platform/users-and-groups-57","page_id":"/platform/users-and-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/platform/users-and-groups#reference","co