ut a stored token redirects the browser to Foundry to sign in. After the redirect back to `redirectUrl`, the client exchanges the code, stores the refresh token per `tokenStorage`, and refreshes the access token one minute before it expires."},"3777":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-7","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","content":"An older overload takes `useHistory`, `loginPage`, `postLoginPage`, `scopes`, `fetchFn`, and `ctxPath` as positional arguments. Prefer `options`, which also accepts `refreshTokenMarker`, `tokenStorage`, and `logger`."},"3778":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-8","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#parameters","content":"| Parameter  | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ---------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `clientId` | `string` | The client ID of your Developer Console application. |","table":"table-0"},"3779":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-9","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#parameters","content":"| Parameter | Type     | Description                         |\n| --------- | -------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `url`     | `string` | The base URL of your Foundry stack. |","table":"table-0"},"3780":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-10","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#parameters","content":"| Parameter     | Type     | Description                                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `redirectUrl` | `string` | The redirect URL registered on the application. It must be a route of your app. |","table":"table-0"},"3781":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-11","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#parameters","content":"| Parameter | Type                       | Description |\n| --------- | -------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `options` | `PublicOauthClientOptions` | See below.  |","table":"table-0"},"3782":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-12","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-useHistory","content":"| `useHistory?` | `boolean` | If true, uses `history.replaceState()`, otherwise uses `window.location.assign()` (defaults to true) |\n| ------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3783":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-13","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-loginPage","content":"| `loginPage?` | `string` | Custom landing page URL prior to logging in |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3784":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-14","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-postLoginPage","content":"| `postLoginPage?` | `string` | URL to return to after completed authentication cycle (defaults to `window.location.toString()`) |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3785":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-15","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-scopes","content":"| `scopes?` | `string[]` | OAuth scopes to request. Defaults to `[\"api:read-data\", \"api:write-data\", \"api:use-ontologies-read\", \"api:use-ontologies-write\"]`. |\n| --------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3786":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-16","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-fetchFn","content":"| `fetchFn?` | `((input: RequestInfo \\| URL, init?: RequestInit) => Promise<Response>)` | Custom fetch function to use for requests (defaults to `globalThis.fetch`) |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3787":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-17","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-ctxPath","content":"| `ctxPath?` | `string` | Context path for the authorization server (defaults to \"multipass\") |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3788":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-18","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-refreshTokenMarker","content":"| `refreshTokenMarker?` | `string` | Allows for an additional value to be appended to the local storage key for the refresh token. |\n| --------------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3789":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-19","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-tokenStorage","content":"| `tokenStorage?` | `TokenStorageType` | Controls how refresh tokens are stored. Affects security vs. convenience tradeoff. - `'localStorage'` (default): Tokens persist across browser sessions. Best UX but vulnerable on shared devices. - `'sessionStorage'`: Tokens cleared when browser/tab closes. Recommended for shared devices. Users re-authenticate each browser session. - `'none'`: Tokens never stored. Users re-authenticate on every page load. Most secure but worst UX. Does not request `offline_access` scope. Default: `'localStorage'` |\n| --------------- | ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3790":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-20","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions-logger","content":"| `logger?` | `OauthLogger` | Optional logger for warning messages. If not provided, warnings are silently dropped. Structurally compatible with `@osdk/api`'s `Logger`. |\n| --------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-createPublicOauthClient.ts-PublicOauthClientOptions"},"3791":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-21","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#options","content":"When `scopes` is omitted, the client requests `api:read-data`, `api:write-data`, `api:use-ontologies-read`, and `api:use-ontologies-write`. Unless `tokenStorage` is `\"none\"`, it also requests `offline_access` to get a refresh token."},"3792":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-22","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"`PublicOauthClient`. The interface has no JSDoc, so this table is written by hand."},"3793":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-23","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member | Type                    | Description                                                             |\n| ------ | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `()`   | `() => Promise<string>` | Returns a valid access token, signing in or refreshing first if needed. |","table":"table-1"},"3794":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-24","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member                | Type                        | Description                                                  |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `getTokenOrUndefined` | `() => string \\| undefined` | The current access token without signing in, or `undefined`. |","table":"table-1"},"3795":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-25","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member   | Type                   | Description                                                                                                                         |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `signIn` | `() => Promise<Token>` | Signs in: uses the stored refresh token, completes a pending redirect, or redirects to Foundry. Concurrent calls share one attempt. |","table":"table-1"},"3796":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-26","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member    | Type                  | Description                                                                               |\n| --------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `signOut` | `() => Promise<void>` | Revokes the access token and removes the stored refresh token. Throws when not signed in. |","table":"table-1"},"3797":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-27","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member    | Type                                | Description                                                                                                |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `refresh` | `() => Promise<Token \\| undefined>` | Refreshes the access token with the stored refresh token. Throws when none is stored or the refresh fails. |","table":"table-1"},"3798":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-28","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member             | Type                                 | Description                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `addEventListener` | `(type, listener, options?) => void` | Listens for `\"signIn\"`, `\"signOut\"`, or `\"refresh\"`. `signIn` and `refresh` events carry the `Token` in `detail`. |","table":"table-1"},"3799":{"id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client-29","page_id":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/oauth/create-public-oauth-client#returns","content":"| Member                | Type   