         |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `invalidateObjects(objects)` | Reloads one object instance or an array of them. Interface instances refetch their backing object. |","table":"table-0"},"3976":{"id":"/reference/react/use-observable-client-7","page_id":"/reference/react/use-observable-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-observable-client#returns","content":"| Method                       | Description                                                               |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `invalidateObjectType(type)` | Reloads every cached query for an object type, by definition or API name. |","table":"table-0"},"3977":{"id":"/reference/react/use-observable-client-8","page_id":"/reference/react/use-observable-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-observable-client#returns","content":"| Method                                  | Description                                                                                     |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `invalidateFunction(queryDef, params?)` | Reloads a function's cached result for `params`, or every cached call when `params` is omitted. |","table":"table-0"},"3978":{"id":"/reference/react/use-observable-client-9","page_id":"/reference/react/use-observable-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-observable-client#returns","content":"| Method            | Description                      |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `invalidateAll()` | Reloads everything in the cache. |","table":"table-0"},"3979":{"id":"/reference/react/use-observable-client-10","page_id":"/reference/react/use-observable-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-observable-client#see-also","content":"Cache invalidation"},"3980":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","type":"page","content":"useOsdkAction","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action"},"3981":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-0","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","content":"Apply or validate an action from a component, with pending state, errors, and optional optimistic updates."},"3982":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-1","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#returns","content":"Returns"},"3983":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-2","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#applyaction-arguments","content":"`applyAction` arguments"},"3984":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-3","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#example","content":"Example"},"3985":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-4","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#see-also","content":"See also"},"3986":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-5","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","content":"Returns functions that apply or validate `actionDef` through the shared cache. After an action succeeds, cached objects and lists that it changed are refreshed."},"3987":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-6","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#returns","content":"The result type has little JSDoc, so this table is written by hand."},"3988":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-7","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#returns","content":"| Field         | Type                                                                                                 | Description                                                                                    |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `applyAction` | `(args: ApplyActionParams<Q> \\| ApplyActionParams<Q>[]) => Promise<ActionEditResponse \\| undefined>` | Applies the action. Pass an array to apply a batch. Rethrows on failure after setting `error`. |","table":"table-0"},"3989":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-8","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#returns","content":"| Field            | Type                                                       | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `validateAction` | `(args) => Promise<ActionValidationResponse \\| undefined>` | Validates the parameters without applying the action. A new call cancels the previous one, and the cancelled call resolves to `undefined`. Resolves to `undefined` without validating while `applyAction` is pending. |","table":"table-0"},"3990":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-9","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#returns","content":"| Field  | Type                              | Description                                          |\n| ------ | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `data` | `ActionEditResponse \\| undefined` | The response from the last successful `applyAction`. |","table":"table-0"},"3991":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-10","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#returns","content":"| Field   | Type                                                                           | Description                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `error` | `{ actionValidation?: ActionValidationError; unknown?: unknown } \\| undefined` | The last failure. `actionValidation` is set when the server rejected the parameters; `unknown` holds any other error. Cleared when the next call starts. |","table":"table-0"},"3992":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-11","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#returns","content":"| Field       | Type      | Description                            |\n| ----------- | --------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `isPending` | `boolean` | `true` while `applyAction` is running. |","table":"table-0"},"3993":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-12","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#returns","content":"| Field          | Type      | Description                               |\n| -------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `isValidating` | `boolean` | `true` while `validateAction` is running. |","table":"table-0"},"3994":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-13","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#returns","content":"| Field              | Type                                    | Description                                            |\n| ------------------ | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `validationResult` | `ActionValidationResponse \\| undefined` | The response from the last completed `validateAction`. |","table":"table-0"},"3995":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-14","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#applyaction-arguments","content":"`ApplyActionParams<Q>` is the action's parameters plus:"},"3996":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-15","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#applyaction-arguments","content":"| Field               | Type                               | Description                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$optimisticUpdate` | `(ctx: OptimisticBuilder) => void` | Writes temporary changes to the cache that are rolled back when the action settles. In a batch, every entry's update runs. |","table":"table-1"},"3997":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-16","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#see-also","content":"Actions"},"3998":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-17","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#see-also","content":"Optimistic updates"},"3999":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action-18","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-action#see-also","content":"Errors"},"4000":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","type":"page","content":"useOsdkAggregation","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation"},"4001":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-0","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","content":"Run a server-side aggregation, such as counts or averages grouped by a property, and keep the result cached."},"4002":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-1","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#options","content":"Options"},"4003":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-2","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#returns","content":"Returns"},"4004":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-3","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#example","content":"Example"},"4005":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-4","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#see-also","content":"See also"},"4006":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-5","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","content":"Aggregates every object of `type` that matches `where`, or the objects in `objectSet` when you pass one. `aggregate` takes the same `$select` and `$groupBy` clauses as `ObjectSet.aggregate`."},"4007":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-6","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions-where","content":"| `where?` | `WhereClause<T, RDPs>` | Standard OSDK Where clause to filter objects before aggregation |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions"},"4008":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-7","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions-withProperties","content":"| `withProperties?` | `{ [K in keyof RDPs]: DerivedProperty.Creator<T, RDPs[K]>; }` | Define derived properties (RDPs) to be computed server-side. The derived properties can be used in the where clause and aggregation groupBy/select. |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions"},"4009":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-8","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions-intersectWith","content":"| `intersectWith?` | `{ where: WhereClause<T, RDPs>; }[]` | Intersect the main query with additional filtered object sets. Each entry creates a separate object set with its own where clause, and the final result is the intersection of all sets. |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions"},"4010":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-9","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions-aggregate","content":"| `aggregate` | `A` | Aggregation options including `$groupBy` and `$select` |\n| ----------- | --- | ------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions"},"4011":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-10","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions-dedupeIntervalMs","content":"| `dedupeIntervalMs?` | `number` | The number of milliseconds to wait after the last observed aggregation change. Two uses of `useOsdkAggregation` with the same parameters will only trigger one network request if the second is within `dedupeIntervalMs`. |\n| ------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions"},"4012":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-11","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions-enabled","content":"| `enabled?` | `boolean` | Enable or disable the aggregation. When `false`, the hook does not subscribe or fetch from the server and reports `data: undefined`, `isLoading: false`, and `error: undefined`. `refetch()` is also a no-op while disabled, so it will not invalidate the object type or trigger network requests. Setting it back to `true` re-subscribes and fetches. Default: `true` |\n| ---------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-useOsdkAggregation.ts-UseOsdkAggregationOptions"},"4013":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-12","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#options","content":"The second overload (`UseOsdkAggregationOptionsWithObjectSet`) adds a required `objectSet: ObjectSet<Q>` to aggregate a pivoted, filtered, or composed set. It accepts object types only, not interfaces."},"4014":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-13","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#returns","content":"| Field  | Type                                     | Description                                                                                         |\n| ------ | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `data` | `AggregationsResults<Q, A> \\| undefined` | The aggregation result. An array of groups when `$groupBy` is set, otherwise one object of metrics. |","table":"table-0"},"4015":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-14","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#returns","content":"| Field       | Type      | Description                                         |\n| ----------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `isLoading` | `boolean` | `true` while enabled and the result has not loaded. |","table":"table-0"},"4016":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-15","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#returns","content":"| Field   | Type                 | Description                          |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `error` | `Error \\| undefined` | The error from the last run, if any. |","table":"table-0"},"4017":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-16","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#returns","content":"| Field     | Type                  | Description                                                                          |\n| --------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `refetch` | `() => Promise<void>` | Invalidates cached data for `type` and reruns the aggregation. No-op while disabled. |","table":"table-0"},"4018":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-17","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#see-also","content":"Aggregations"},"4019":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation-18","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-aggregation#see-also","content":"Aggregations in `@osdk/client`"},"4020":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","type":"page","content":"useOsdkClient","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client"},"4021":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client-0","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","content":"Return the OSDK Client passed to the nearest OsdkProvider."},"4022":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client-1","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client#returns","content":"Returns"},"4023":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client-2","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client#example","content":"Example"},"4024":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client-3","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client#see-also","content":"See also"},"4025":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client-4","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","content":"Returns the `client` prop of the surrounding `OsdkProvider`. Use it to build object sets for `useObjectSet` or to call the client directly, for example in an event handler. Calls made directly on the client bypass the shared cache."},"4026":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client-5","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client#returns","content":"`Client`: the client from `createClient` in `@osdk/client`."},"4027":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client-6","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client#see-also","content":"Create a client"},"4028":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client-7","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-client#see-also","content":"createClient"},"4029":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","type":"page","content":"useOsdkFunction","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function"},"4030":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-0","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","content":"Execute a Foundry function and cache its result, refetching when the objects it depends on change."},"4031":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-1","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#options","content":"Options"},"4032":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-2","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#returns","content":"Returns"},"4033":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-3","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#example","content":"Example"},"4034":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-4","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#see-also","content":"See also"},"4035":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-5","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","content":"Runs the function when the component mounts and again when `params` change. Calls with the same function and `params` share one cached result. Use `dependsOn` or `dependsOnObjects` to refetch after actions change related objects."},"4036":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-6","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionOptions-params","content":"| `params?` | `(CompileTimeMetadata<Q>[\"parameters\"] extends Record<string, never> ? undefined : QueryParameterType<CompileTimeMetadata<Q>[\"parameters\"]>)` | Parameters to pass to the function. Must include all required parameters; optional parameters can be omitted. |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionOptions"},"4037":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-7","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionOptions-dependsOn","content":"| `dependsOn?` | `(string \\| ObjectTypeDefinition)[]` | Object types this function depends on. When actions modify objects of these types, the function will automatically refetch. |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionOptions"},"4038":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-8","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionOptions-dependsOnObjects","content":"| `dependsOnObjects?` | `(ObjectSet<ObjectTypeDefinition, never> \\| Osdk.Instance<ObjectTypeDefinition, never, any, {}>)[]` | Specific object instances or ObjectSets this function depends on. When any of these specific objects change, the function will refetch. More fine-grained than dependsOn for precise invalidation control. For ObjectSets, the object type is extracted asynchronously and changes to any object of that type will trigger a refetch. |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionOptions"},"4039":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-9","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionOptions-dedupeIntervalMs","content":"| `dedupeIntervalMs?` | `number` | The number of milliseconds to dedupe identical function calls. Two calls with the same function and params will share results if the second call is within this interval of the first. Default: `2000` |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionOptions"},"4040":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-10","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionOptions-enabled","content":"| `enabled?` | `boolean` | Whether to enable the query. When false, the query will not execute. Useful for: - Dependent queries that need to wait for other data - Conditional queries based on component state Default: `true` |\n| ---------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionOptions"},"4041":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-11","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionResult-data","content":"| `data` | `(CompileTimeMetadata<Q>[\"signature\"] extends (...args: never[]) => infer R ? Awaited<R> : never) \\| undefined` | The function result, or undefined if not yet loaded or on error. |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionResult"},"4042":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-12","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionResult-isLoading","content":"| `isLoading` | `boolean` | True while the function is executing. |\n| ----------- | --------- | ------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionResult"},"4043":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-13","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionResult-error","content":"| `error` | `Error \\| undefined` | Error if the function execution failed. |\n| ------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionResult"},"4044":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-14","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionResult-lastUpdated","content":"| `lastUpdated` | `number` | Timestamp (ms since epoch) of when the result was last fetched. |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionResult"},"4045":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-15","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionResult-refetch","content":"| `refetch` | `() => Promise<void>` | Manually refetch the function. Useful for \"pull to refresh\" or retry patterns. |\n| --------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunction.ts-UseOsdkFunctionResult"},"4046":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-16","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#returns","content":"`isLoading` is `true` only while a request is in flight. On the first render, before the hook subscribes, and while it is disabled, `isLoading` is `false` and `data` is `undefined`, so check both."},"4047":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-17","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#see-also","content":"Functions"},"4048":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function-18","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-function#see-also","content":"useOsdkFunctions"},"4049":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","type":"page","content":"useOsdkFunctions","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions"},"4050":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-0","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","content":"Execute several Foundry functions from one hook and get their results in input order."},"4051":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-1","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#props","content":"Props"},"4052":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-2","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#functionqueryparams","content":"`FunctionQueryParams`"},"4053":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-3","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#returns","content":"Returns"},"4054":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-4","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#example","content":"Example"},"4055":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-5","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#see-also","content":"See also"},"4056":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-6","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","content":"Use it when the number of function calls varies at runtime, which rules out calling `useOsdkFunction` in a loop. Each query shares the cache with `useOsdkFunction`, so identical calls elsewhere do not hit the network twice."},"4057":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-7","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#type-table-useOsdkFunctions.ts-UseOsdkFunctionsProps-queries","content":"| `queries` | `FunctionQueryParams<QueryDefinition<unknown>>[]` | Array of query configurations to execute |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunctions.ts-UseOsdkFunctionsProps"},"4058":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-8","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#type-table-useOsdkFunctions.ts-UseOsdkFunctionsProps-enabled","content":"| `enabled?` | `boolean` | Whether to enable all queries. When false, no queries will execute. Individual query enabled states are also respected. Default: `true` |\n| ---------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunctions.ts-UseOsdkFunctionsProps"},"4059":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-9","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#type-table-useOsdkFunctions.ts-UseOsdkFunctionsProps-maxConcurrent","content":"| `maxConcurrent?` | `number` | Maximum number of queries to execute concurrently. When set, queries are subscribed in batches — the next query starts only after a running one completes (status \"loaded\" or \"error\"). Useful for large payloads that may exceed server time limits. Default: `undefined (all queries run in parallel)` |\n| ---------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkFunctions.ts-UseOsdkFunctionsProps"},"4060":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-10","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#functionqueryparams","content":"| Field             | Type | Description                           |\n| ----------------- | ---- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `queryDefinition` | `Q`  | The function from your generated SDK. |","table":"table-0"},"4061":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-11","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#functionqueryparams","content":"| Field     | Type                        | Description                                                                                                          |\n| --------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `options` | `UseOsdkFunctionOptions<Q>` | The same options as `useOsdkFunction`: `params`, `dependsOn`, `dependsOnObjects`, `dedupeIntervalMs`, and `enabled`. |","table":"table-0"},"4062":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-12","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#returns","content":"An array with one `UseOsdkFunctionResult` per query, in the order of `queries`."},"4063":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-13","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#returns","content":"`queries` is typed with `QueryDefinition<unknown>`, so an entry with typed `params` does not type-check as written, and each result's `data` loses the function's return type. Cast each entry to `UseOsdkFunctionsProps[\"queries\"][number]`, as the example does, and narrow `data` where you read it."},"4064":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions-14","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-functions#see-also","content":"Functions"},"4065":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","type":"page","content":"useOsdkMetadata","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata"},"4066":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata-0","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","content":"Fetch the runtime metadata of an object type, interface, or action, such as display names and property descriptions."},"4067":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata-1","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata#returns","content":"Returns"},"4068":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata-2","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata#example","content":"Example"},"4069":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata-3","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata#see-also","content":"See also"},"4070":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata-4","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","content":"Calls `client.fetchMetadata(type)` and returns the result. The metadata type follows the definition you pass: `ObjectMetadata` for an object type, `InterfaceMetadata` for an interface, and `ActionMetadata` for an action. The result is held in component state, not in the shared cache, so each component that calls the hook fetches once."},"4071":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata-5","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata#returns","content":"| Field     | Type      | Description                       |\n| --------- | --------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `loading` | `boolean` | `true` until the request settles. |","table":"table-0"},"4072":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata-6","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata#returns","content":"| Field      | Type                                                                 | Description                |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `metadata` | `ObjectMetadata \\| InterfaceMetadata \\| ActionMetadata \\| undefined` | The metadata, once loaded. |","table":"table-0"},"4073":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata-7","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata#returns","content":"| Field   | Type                  | Description                              |\n| ------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `error` | `string \\| undefined` | The error message if the request failed. |","table":"table-0"},"4074":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata-8","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-metadata#see-also","content":"Load objects"},"4075":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","type":"page","content":"useOsdkObject","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object"},"4076":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-0","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","content":"Load one object by primary key, or observe an object instance you already have, from the shared cache."},"4077":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-1","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#parameters","content":"Parameters"},"4078":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-2","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#options","content":"Options"},"4079":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-3","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#returns","content":"Returns"},"4080":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-4","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#example","content":"Example"},"4081":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-5","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#see-also","content":"See also"},"4082":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-6","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","content":"Pass a type and primary key to fetch the object, or pass an `Osdk.Instance` to observe it in the cache without a network request. The component re-renders when the cached object changes, for example after an action or an optimistic update."},"4083":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-7","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#parameters","content":"| Parameter | Type | Default | Description                                           |\n| --------- | ---- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `type`    | `Q`  |         | The object type or interface from your generated SDK. |","table":"table-0"},"4084":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-8","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#parameters","content":"| Parameter    | Type                | Default | Description                            |\n| ------------ | ------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `primaryKey` | `PrimaryKeyType<Q>` |         | The primary key of the object to load. |","table":"table-0"},"4085":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-9","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#parameters","content":"| Parameter | Type               | Default | Description                                                                             |\n| --------- | ------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `obj`     | `Osdk.Instance<Q>` |         | An object you already loaded. The hook reads it from the cache only and does not fetch. |","table":"table-0"},"4086":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-10","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#parameters","content":"| Parameter | Type      | Default | Description                                                                      |\n| --------- | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enabled` | `boolean` | `true`  | When `false`, the hook does not subscribe or fetch, and `object` is `undefined`. |","table":"table-0"},"4087":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-11","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#parameters","content":"| Parameter | Type                      | Default | Description |\n| --------- | ------------------------- | ------- | ----------- |\n| `options` | `UseOsdkObjectOptions<Q>` |         | See below.  |","table":"table-0"},"4088":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-12","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#options","content":"The options type has little JSDoc, so this table is written by hand."},"4089":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-13","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#options","content":"| Option    | Type                         | Default        | Description         |\n| --------- | ---------------------------- | -------------- | ------------------- |\n| `$select` | `readonly PropertyKeys<Q>[]` | All properties | Properties to load. |","table":"table-1"},"4090":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-14","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#options","content":"| Option    | Type      | Default | Description                                                                      |\n| --------- | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enabled` | `boolean` | `true`  | When `false`, the hook does not subscribe or fetch, and `object` is `undefined`. |","table":"table-1"},"4091":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-15","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#options","content":"| Option                          | Type      | Default | Description                                                         |\n| ------------------------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$loadPropertySecurityMetadata` | `boolean` | `false` | Loads per-property marking requirements into `$propertySecurities`. |","table":"table-1"},"4092":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-16","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#options","content":"| Option                            | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                       |\n| --------------------------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$includeAllBaseObjectProperties` | `boolean` | `false` | For an interface, loads every property of the underlying object type. No effect for object types. |","table":"table-1"},"4093":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-17","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#returns","content":"| Field    | Type                            | Description                                                              |\n| -------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `object` | `Osdk.Instance<Q> \\| undefined` | The object, or `undefined` before it loads, on error, or while disabled. |","table":"table-2"},"4094":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-18","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#returns","content":"| Field       | Type      | Description                                                                      |\n| ----------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `isLoading` | `boolean` | `true` while enabled and the object has not loaded. `false` once `error` is set. |","table":"table-2"},"4095":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-19","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#returns","content":"| Field   | Type                 | Description                           |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `error` | `Error \\| undefined` | The error from the last load, if any. |","table":"table-2"},"4096":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-20","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#returns","content":"| Field          | Type      | Description                                                                                     |\n| -------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `isOptimistic` | `boolean` | `true` while the cached object reflects an optimistic update that the server has not confirmed. |","table":"table-2"},"4097":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-21","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#returns","content":"| Field         | Type         | Description                         |\n| ------------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------- |\n| `forceUpdate` | `() => void` | Not implemented. Calling it throws. |","table":"table-2"},"4098":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-22","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#see-also","content":"Load objects"},"4099":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object-23","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-object#see-also","content":"Osdk.Instance"},"4100":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","type":"page","content":"useOsdkObjects","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects"},"4101":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-0","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","content":"Load a live, cached list of objects of one type or interface."},"4102":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-1","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#options","content":"Options"},"4103":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-2","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#returns","content":"Returns"},"4104":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-3","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#example","content":"Example"},"4105":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-4","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#see-also","content":"See also"},"4106":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-5","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","content":"Subscribes the component to a list in the shared cache and re-renders when the list or any object in it changes. With `pivotTo`, the list holds the linked type instead of `T`; with `rids`, each object also carries `$rid`."},"4107":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-6","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-rids","content":"| `rids?` | `readonly string[]` | Fetch objects by their RIDs (Resource Identifiers). When provided, starts with a static objectset containing these RIDs. Can be combined with `where` to filter the RID set, and with `orderBy` to sort results. |\n| ------- | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4108":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-7","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-where","content":"| `where?` | `WhereClause<T, RDPs>` | Standard OSDK Where clause with RDP support. When used with `rids`, filters the RID set. When used alone, filters all objects of the type. |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4109":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-8","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-orderBy","content":"| `orderBy?` | `{ [K in PropertyKeys<T>]?: \"asc\" \\| \"desc\" \\| undefined; }` | Sort results by one or more properties. |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4110":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-9","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-pageSize","content":"| `pageSize?` | `number` | The preferred page size for the list. |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4111":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-10","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-withProperties","content":"| `withProperties?` | `{ [K in keyof RDPs]: DerivedProperty.Creator<T, RDPs[K]>; }` | Define derived properties (RDPs) to be computed server-side and attached to each object. These properties will be available on the returned objects alongside their regular properties. |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4112":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-11","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-dedupeIntervalMs","content":"| `dedupeIntervalMs?` | `number` | The number of milliseconds to wait after the last observed list change. Two uses of `useOsdkObjects` with the same parameters will only trigger one network request if the second is within `dedupeIntervalMs`. |\n| ------------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4113":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-12","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-enabled","content":"| `enabled?` | `boolean` | Enable or disable the query. When `false`, the query does not run and the hook returns no data, even if the cache already holds a result. Default: `true` |\n| ---------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4114":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-13","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-intersectWith","content":"| `intersectWith?` | `{ where: WhereClause<T, RDPs>; }[]` | Intersect the results with additional object sets. Each element defines a where clause for an object set to intersect with. The final result will only include objects that match ALL conditions. |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4115":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-14","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-pivotTo","content":"| `pivotTo?` | `LinkNames<T>` | Pivot to related objects through a link. This changes the return type from T to the linked object type. Cannot be combined with `streamUpdates`. The server does not support websocket subscriptions for link-traversal queries. |\n| ---------- | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4116":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-15","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-autoFetchMore","content":"| `autoFetchMore?` | `number \\| boolean` | Causes the list to automatically fetch more as soon as the previous page has been loaded. If a number is provided, it will continue to automatically fetch more until the list is at least that long. - `true`: Fetch all available pages automatically - `number`: Fetch pages until at least this many items are loaded - `undefined` (default): Only fetch the first page, user must call fetchMore() |\n| ---------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4117":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-16","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-streamUpdates","content":"| `streamUpdates?` | `boolean` | Enable streaming updates via websocket subscription. Cannot be combined with `pivotTo`. The server does not support websocket subscriptions for link-traversal queries. |\n| ---------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4118":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-17","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-$select","content":"| `$select?` | `readonly PropertyKeys<T>[]` | Restrict which properties are returned for each object. When provided, only the specified properties will be fetched, reducing payload sizes for list views. |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4119":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-18","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-$loadPropertySecurityMetadata","content":"| `$loadPropertySecurityMetadata?` | `boolean` | When true, loads per-property security metadata (marking requirements) alongside each object. The returned objects will have `$propertySecurities` populated with conjunctive/disjunctive marking requirements per property. |\n| -------------------------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4120":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-19","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-$includeAllBaseObjectProperties","content":"| `$includeAllBaseObjectProperties?` | `boolean` | When true, includes all properties of the underlying concrete object type for interface queries. Has no effect for non-interface queries. |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4121":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-20","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions-resolveToObjectType","content":"| `resolveToObjectType?` | `boolean` |     |\n| ---------------------- | --------- | --- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkObjectsOptions"},"4122":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-21","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult-fetchMore","content":"| `fetchMore` | `(() => Promise<void>) \\| undefined` | Function to fetch more pages (undefined if no more pages) |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult"},"4123":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-22","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult-data","content":"| `data` | `Osdk.Instance<T, \"$allBaseProperties\" \\| EXTRA_OPTIONS, PropertyKeys<T>, RDPs>[] \\| undefined` | The fetched data with derived properties |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult"},"4124":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-23","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult-isLoading","content":"| `isLoading` | `boolean` | Whether data is currently being loaded |\n| ----------- | --------- | -------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult"},"4125":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-24","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult-error","content":"| `error` | `Error \\| undefined` | Any error that occurred during fetching |\n| ------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult"},"4126":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-25","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult-isOptimistic","content":"| `isOptimistic` | `boolean` | Refers to whether the ordered list of objects (only considering the $primaryKey) is optimistic or not. If you need to know if the contents of the list are optimistic you can do that on a per object basis with useOsdkObject |\n| -------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult"},"4127":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-26","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult-totalCount","content":"| `totalCount?` | `string` | The total count of objects matching the query (if available from the API) |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult"},"4128":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-27","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult-hasMore","content":"| `hasMore` | `boolean` |     |\n| --------- | --------- | --- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult"},"4129":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-28","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult-objectSet","content":"| `objectSet` | `ObjectSet<T, RDPs> \\| undefined` |     |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------- | --- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult"},"4130":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-29","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult-refetch","content":"| `refetch` | `() => Promise<void>` |     |\n| --------- | --------------------- | --- |","table":"type-table-useOsdkObjects.ts-UseOsdkListResult"},"4131":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-30","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#see-also","content":"Load objects"},"4132":{"id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects-31","page_id":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-osdk-objects#see-also","content":"Filtering"},"4133":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","type":"page","content":"useStableObjectSet","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Reference","@osdk/react"],"tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set"},"4134":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set-0","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","content":"Return a referentially stable ObjectSet that changes only when its definition changes."},"4135":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set-1","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set#parameters","content":"Parameters"},"4136":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set-2","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set#returns","content":"Returns"},"4137":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set-3","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set#example","content":"Example"},"4138":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set-4","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set#see-also","content":"See also"},"4139":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set-5","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","content":"Returns the same `ObjectSet` instance across renders until the serialized definition, including `where`, `union`, `intersect`, `subtract`, and pivots, changes. Use it instead of `useMemo` when you build an object set inline and pass it to a hook, an effect, or a memoized child."},"4140":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set-6","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set#parameters","content":"| Parameter   | Type                              | Description                                              |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `objectSet` | `ObjectSet<Q, RDPs> \\| undefined` | The object set to stabilize. `undefined` passes through. |","table":"table-0"},"4141":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set-7","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set#returns","content":"`ObjectSet<Q, RDPs> | undefined`: the object set from the first render with the current definition."},"4142":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set-8","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set#see-also","content":"Object sets"},"4143":{"id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set-9","page_id":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/reference/react/use-stable-object-set#see-also","content":"useObjectSet"},"4144":{"id":"/sdk/actions","page_id":"/sdk/actions","type":"page","content":"Actions","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK","Write data"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk/actions"},"4145":{"id":"/sdk/actions-0","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions","content":"Apply Ontology actions with applyAction and batchApplyAction, validate parameters first, read returned edits, and handle ActionValidationError."},"4146":{"id":"/sdk/actions-1","page_id":"/sdk/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/actions#options","content":"Options"},"4147":{"id":"/sdk/actions-2","page_id":"/sdk/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"Parameter values"},"4148":{"id":"/sdk/actions-3","page_id":"/sdk/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/actions#validate-first","content":"Validate first"},"4149":{"id":"/sdk/actions-4","page_id":"/sdk/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/actions#handle-validation-errors","content":"Handle validation errors"},"4150":{"id":"/sdk/actions-5","page_id":"/sdk/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/actions#read-the-edits","content":"Read the edits"},"4151":{"id":"/sdk/actions-6","page_id":"/sdk/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/actions#apply-in-a-batch","content":"Apply in a batch"},"4152":{"id":"/sdk/actions-7","page_id":"/sdk/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/actions#in-react","content":"In React"},"4153":{"id":"/sdk/actions-8","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions","content":"Actions are the way to change Ontology data: they create, modify, and delete objects and links according to rules defined in Foundry. `client(modifyEmployee)` returns an invoker with two methods, `applyAction` for one request and `batchApplyAction` for several."},"4154":{"id":"/sdk/actions-9","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions","content":"`applyAction` rejects when the action fails, so always await it inside `try`/`catch` or attach `.catch`. The parameter names and types come from your generated SDK. In the example SDK, `modifyEmployee` takes `employee` (required), `jobTitle`, and `department`."},"4155":{"id":"/sdk/actions-10","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#options","content":"| Option         | Type      | Default | Description                                               |\n| -------------- | --------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$returnEdits` | `boolean` | `false` | Resolve to the edits the action made. See Read the edits. |","table":"table-0"},"4156":{"id":"/sdk/actions-11","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#options","content":"| Option          | Type      | Default | Description                                                                               |\n| --------------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$validateOnly` | `boolean` | `false` | Check the parameters without applying the action. See Validate first. `applyAction` only. |","table":"table-0"},"4157":{"id":"/sdk/actions-12","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#options","content":"You cannot set both on one call; the types reject it."},"4158":{"id":"/sdk/actions-13","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#options","content":"| Options | `applyAction` resolves to |\n| ------- | ------------------------- |\n| None    | `undefined`               |","table":"table-1"},"4159":{"id":"/sdk/actions-14","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#options","content":"| Options                  | `applyAction` resolves to |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------- |\n| `{ $returnEdits: true }` | `ActionEditResponse`      |","table":"table-1"},"4160":{"id":"/sdk/actions-15","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#options","content":"| Options                   | `applyAction` resolves to  |\n| ------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `{ $validateOnly: true }` | `ActionValidationResponse` |","table":"table-1"},"4161":{"id":"/sdk/actions-16","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#options","content":"When `applyAction` resolves, the action has run. Edits to objects in Object Storage V2 are visible to the next read. Edits in Object Storage V1 are eventually consistent and can take a moment to appear."},"4162":{"id":"/sdk/actions-17","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                              |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object         | A loaded object, its primary key, or `{ $apiName, $primaryKey }`. |","table":"table-2"},"4163":{"id":"/sdk/actions-18","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Interface      | A plain `{ $objectType, $primaryKey }` object, where `$objectType` is the concrete object type. Do not pass a loaded object: the client would send only its primary key. |","table":"table-2"},"4164":{"id":"/sdk/actions-19","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                      |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object set     | An object set, such as `client(Employee).where({ ... })`. |","table":"table-2"},"4165":{"id":"/sdk/actions-20","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Primitive      | A value of the parameter's TypeScript type: `string`, `number`, `boolean`. Dates and timestamps are ISO 8601 strings. `long` and `decimal` accept a `number` or a `string`. |","table":"table-2"},"4166":{"id":"/sdk/actions-21","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                    |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| List           | An array of values of the element type. |","table":"table-2"},"4167":{"id":"/sdk/actions-22","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                          |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Struct         | An object whose keys are the struct's fields. |","table":"table-2"},"4168":{"id":"/sdk/actions-23","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                                                               |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Attachment     | An attachment RID, a `File`, or the result of `createAttachmentUpload`. See Attachments and media. |","table":"table-2"},"4169":{"id":"/sdk/actions-24","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type  | Pass                                                                                         |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Media reference | A `MediaUpload`, a `Media` from an object, or a `MediaReference`. See Attachments and media. |","table":"table-2"},"4170":{"id":"/sdk/actions-25","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"Omit an optional parameter to leave it out of the request. Pass `null` to send an empty value, which clears the property in a modify action:"},"4171":{"id":"/sdk/actions-26","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#parameter-values","content":"Parameter default values configured on the action type are not applied when you call the action from the client. Pass every value you need."},"4172":{"id":"/sdk/actions-27","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#validate-first","content":"`$validateOnly: true` runs the action's submission criteria and parameter constraints without applying it. It resolves to the validation result, valid or not, and does not throw on an invalid result:"},"4173":{"id":"/sdk/actions-28","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#validate-first","content":"The validation result has this shape:"},"4174":{"id":"/sdk/actions-29","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#validate-first","content":"| Field    | Type                   | Description         |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `result` | `\"VALID\" \\| \"INVALID\"` | The overall result. |","table":"table-3"},"4175":{"id":"/sdk/actions-30","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#validate-first","content":"| Field                | Type                                      | Description                                                                                 |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `submissionCriteria` | `{ result, configuredFailureMessage? }[]` | One entry per submission criterion, with the failure message configured on the action type. |","table":"table-3"},"4176":{"id":"/sdk/actions-31","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#validate-first","content":"| Field        | Type                                                         | Description                                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameters` | `Record<string, { result, required, evaluatedConstraints }>` | One entry per parameter. `evaluatedConstraints` lists the checks that ran, such as `range`, `stringLength`, `oneOf`, or `stringRegexMatch`. |","table":"table-3"},"4177":{"id":"/sdk/actions-32","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#handle-validation-errors","content":"When you apply an action whose validation fails, `applyAction` throws an `ActionValidationError` from `@osdk/client`. Its `validation` field holds the same validation result:"},"4178":{"id":"/sdk/actions-33","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#handle-validation-errors","content":"Every other failure, such as a missing permission or an invalid parameter type, rejects with a `PalantirApiError`. See Errors."},"4179":{"id":"/sdk/actions-34","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#read-the-edits","content":"`$returnEdits: true` resolves to the edits the action made:"},"4180":{"id":"/sdk/actions-35","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#read-the-edits","content":"| Field  | Type                           | Description                                                                                            |\n| ------ | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `type` | `\"edits\" \\| \"largeScaleEdits\"` | `\"largeScaleEdits\"` when the action made too many edits to list. Only `editedObjectTypes` is set then. |","table":"table-4"},"4181":{"id":"/sdk/actions-36","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#read-the-edits","content":"| Field                                               | Type                           | Description                                           |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `addedObjects`, `modifiedObjects`, `deletedObjects` | `{ objectType, primaryKey }[]` | The objects the action created, changed, and deleted. |","table":"table-4"},"4182":{"id":"/sdk/actions-37","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#read-the-edits","content":"| Field                        | Type                                                                       | Description                               |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `addedLinks`, `deletedLinks` | `{ linkTypeApiNameAtoB, linkTypeApiNameBtoA, aSideObject, bSideObject }[]` | The links the action created and removed. |","table":"table-4"},"4183":{"id":"/sdk/actions-38","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#read-the-edits","content":"| Field                                      | Type     | Description              |\n| ------------------------------------------ | -------- | ------------------------ |\n| `deletedObjectsCount`, `deletedLinksCount` | `number` | The number of deletions. |","table":"table-4"},"4184":{"id":"/sdk/actions-39","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#read-the-edits","content":"| Field               | Type       | Description                                            |\n| ------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `editedObjectTypes` | `string[]` | The API names of every object type the action touched. |","table":"table-4"},"4185":{"id":"/sdk/actions-40","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#read-the-edits","content":"The edits name objects by type and primary key. To read the new values, load the objects again."},"4186":{"id":"/sdk/actions-41","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#apply-in-a-batch","content":"`batchApplyAction` takes an array of parameter objects for the same action and applies them in one request:"},"4187":{"id":"/sdk/actions-42","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#apply-in-a-batch","content":"Differences from `applyAction`:"},"4188":{"id":"/sdk/actions-43","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#apply-in-a-batch","content":"It accepts `$returnEdits` but not `$validateOnly`."},"4189":{"id":"/sdk/actions-44","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#apply-in-a-batch","content":"It does not throw `ActionValidationError`. If a request in the batch fails, the call rejects with a `PalantirApiError`."},"4190":{"id":"/sdk/actions-45","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#apply-in-a-batch","content":"A batch holds up to 20 requests. Actions that only modify objects in Object Storage V2 and call no functions may have a higher limit. For more, split the array and send several batches."},"4191":{"id":"/sdk/actions-46","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#apply-in-a-batch","content":"Action notifications are not sent for batched requests."},"4192":{"id":"/sdk/actions-47","page_id":"/sdk/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/actions#in-react","content":"`useOsdkAction` from `@osdk/react` wraps `applyAction`, tracks pending and validation state, and refreshes cached objects after the action. See Actions in React."},"4193":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","type":"page","content":"Aggregations","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK","Read data"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk/aggregations"},"4194":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-0","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations","content":"Count, sum, average, and find the min, max, or distinct values of object sets on the server, grouped by exact values, ranges, fixed widths, or durations."},"4195":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-1","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/aggregations#metrics","content":"Metrics"},"4196":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-2","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/aggregations#read-the-result","content":"Read the result"},"4197":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-3","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"Group by"},"4198":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-4","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/aggregations#sort-groups","content":"Sort groups"},"4199":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-5","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/aggregations#aggregate-over-links-and-set-operations","content":"Aggregate over links and set operations"},"4200":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-6","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/aggregations#in-react","content":"In React"},"4201":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-7","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations","content":"`aggregate` computes counts and metrics over an object set on the server and returns only the numbers. It loads no objects, so it is the right tool for totals, averages, and breakdowns, however large the set."},"4202":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-8","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations","content":"`aggregate` takes `$select`, the metrics to compute, and an optional `$groupBy`. Filter first with `where`; every object set method that returns an object set, such as `pivotTo` or `intersect`, can come before it."},"4203":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-9","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#metrics","content":"Each `$select` key is `$count` or `\"<property>:<metric>\"`. The value is a sort direction, described in Sort groups; use `\"unordered\"` when you do not need one."},"4204":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-10","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#metrics","content":"| Metric   | Property types | Result type |\n| -------- | -------------- | ----------- |\n| `$count` | Not applicable | `number`    |","table":"table-0"},"4205":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-11","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#metrics","content":"| Metric       | Property types | Result type           |\n| ------------ | -------------- | --------------------- |\n| `sum`, `avg` | Numeric        | `number \\| undefined` |","table":"table-0"},"4206":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-12","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#metrics","content":"| Metric       | Property types           | Result type                         |\n| ------------ | ------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |\n| `min`, `max` | Numeric, date, timestamp | The property's type, or `undefined` |","table":"table-0"},"4207":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-13","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#metrics","content":"| Metric                | Property types | Result type |\n| --------------------- | -------------- | ----------- |\n| `approximateDistinct` | All            | `number`    |","table":"table-0"},"4208":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-14","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#metrics","content":"| Metric          | Property types | Result type |\n| --------------- | -------------- | ----------- |\n| `exactDistinct` | All            | `number`    |","table":"table-0"},"4209":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-15","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#metrics","content":"A metric that does not apply to the property's type, such as `\"fullName:sum\"`, does not typecheck. `approximateDistinct` is faster on large sets and can be off by a small amount; `exactDistinct` is exact."},"4210":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-16","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#read-the-result","content":"Without `$groupBy`, the result is one object. `$count` is a number, and each property is an object keyed by metric name:"},"4211":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-17","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#read-the-result","content":"With `$groupBy`, the result is an array with one entry per group. Each entry has the group's values under `$group`, plus the same metric fields:"},"4212":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-18","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"`$groupBy` maps each property to a grouping. Several properties group by every combination of their values."},"4213":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-19","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"| Grouping  | Property types | `$group` value       | Description                   |\n| --------- | -------------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `\"exact\"` | All            | The property's value | One group per distinct value. |","table":"table-1"},"4214":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-20","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"| Grouping                 | Property types | `$group` value       | Description         |\n| ------------------------ | -------------- | -------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `{ $exactWithLimit: n }` | All            | The property's value | At most `n` groups. |","table":"table-1"},"4215":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-21","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"| Grouping                                           | Property types | `$group` value       | Description                             |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `{ $exact: { $limit?, $includeNullValue: true } }` | All            | The value, or `null` | Adds a group for objects with no value. |","table":"table-1"},"4216":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-22","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"| Grouping             | Property types | `$group` value           | Description           |\n| -------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------ | --------------------- |\n| `{ $fixedWidth: n }` | Numeric        | The bucket's lower bound | Buckets of width `n`. |","table":"table-1"},"4217":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-23","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"| Grouping                           | Property types           | `$group` value             | Description                                                    |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ $ranges: [[start, end], ...] }` | Numeric, date, timestamp | `{ startValue, endValue }` | One group per range. `start` is inclusive and `end` exclusive. |","table":"table-1"},"4218":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-24","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"| Grouping                   | Property types  | `$group` value     | Description                |\n| -------------------------- | --------------- | ------------------ | -------------------------- |\n| `{ $duration: [n, unit] }` | Date, timestamp | The bucket's start | Buckets of `n` time units. |","table":"table-1"},"4219":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-25","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"`$duration` units:"},"4220":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-26","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"| Property type | Units                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Date          | `\"days\"`, `\"weeks\"`, `\"months\"`, `\"quarters\"`, `\"years\"`, and singular or short forms such as `\"day\"`, `\"wk\"`, `\"mos\"`, `\"yr\"` |","table":"table-2"},"4221":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-27","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"| Property type | Units                                                                                                               |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Timestamp     | The date units, plus `\"seconds\"`, `\"minutes\"`, and `\"hours\"` and their short forms such as `\"sec\"`, `\"min\"`, `\"hr\"` |","table":"table-2"},"4222":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-28","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#group-by","content":"For weeks, months, quarters, and years, `n` must be `1`."},"4223":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-29","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#sort-groups","content":"Set a metric's value in `$select` to `\"asc\"` or `\"desc\"` to order the groups by that metric. `$count: \"desc\"` lists the largest groups first."},"4224":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-30","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#sort-groups","content":"Sorting has two limits, both enforced by the types:"},"4225":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-31","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#sort-groups","content":"With more than one `$groupBy` property, every `$select` value must be `\"unordered\"`."},"4226":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-32","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#sort-groups","content":"With `$exact: { $includeNullValue: true }`, every `$select` value must be `\"unordered\"`."},"4227":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-33","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#aggregate-over-links-and-set-operations","content":"Because `aggregate` runs on any object set, you can aggregate over linked objects or combined sets without loading them:"},"4228":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-34","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#aggregate-over-links-and-set-operations","content":"To attach a per-object aggregate, such as each employee's report count, as a property you can filter and sort on, use derived properties."},"4229":{"id":"/sdk/aggregations-35","page_id":"/sdk/aggregations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/aggregations#in-react","content":"`useOsdkAggregation` from `@osdk/react` runs the same request, caches the result, and loads it again when objects of the type change. See Aggregations in React."},"4230":{"id":"/sdk/derived-properties","page_id":"/sdk/derived-properties","type":"page","content":"Derived properties","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK","Read data"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk/derived-properties"},"4231":{"id":"/sdk/derived-properties-0","page_id":"/sdk/derived-properties","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/derived-properties","content":"Add computed properties to an object set with withProperties, from linked objects, link aggregations, and expressions, then filter and sort on them."},"4232":{"id":"/sdk/derived-proper