/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"| Field     | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| --------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `message` | `string` | The server's message, or `Failed to fetch <status> <statusText>`. |","table":"table-1"},"4286":{"id":"/sdk/errors-15","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"| Field       | Type                  | Description                                                                                           |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `errorCode` | `string \\| undefined` | The category, such as `PERMISSION_DENIED`, `NOT_FOUND`, `INVALID_ARGUMENT`, `CONFLICT`, or `TIMEOUT`. |","table":"table-1"},"4287":{"id":"/sdk/errors-16","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"| Field       | Type                  | Description                                                           |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `errorName` | `string \\| undefined` | The specific error, such as `ObjectTypeNotFound` or `ActionNotFound`. |","table":"table-1"},"4288":{"id":"/sdk/errors-17","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"| Field              | Type                  | Description           |\n| ------------------ | --------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `errorDescription` | `string \\| undefined` | A longer description. |","table":"table-1"},"4289":{"id":"/sdk/errors-18","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"| Field        | Type                  | Description                                            |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `statusCode` | `number \\| undefined` | The HTTP status. `undefined` when no response arrived. |","table":"table-1"},"4290":{"id":"/sdk/errors-19","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"| Field             | Type                  | Description                                                                                                |\n| ----------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `errorInstanceId` | `string \\| undefined` | An ID for this occurrence. Log it, and include it when you report a problem to your Foundry administrator. |","table":"table-1"},"4291":{"id":"/sdk/errors-20","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"| Field        | Type      | Description                                                      |\n| ------------ | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parameters` | `unknown` | Error-specific details, such as the API name that was not found. |","table":"table-1"},"4292":{"id":"/sdk/errors-21","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"On an `UnknownError`, `originalError` holds the underlying error when there is one, such as the `TypeError` from a failed `fetch`."},"4293":{"id":"/sdk/errors-22","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"When no object matches, `fetchOne` and `$link.<link>.fetchOne` reject with a `PalantirApiError` that carries only a message, `Expected a single result but got 0 instead`, and no `statusCode`, `errorCode`, or `errorName`."},"4294":{"id":"/sdk/errors-23","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"Branch on `statusCode` and `errorCode`, which are stable. Use `errorName` for a specific case. Do not parse `message`."},"4295":{"id":"/sdk/errors-24","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#palantirapierror","content":"A `NOT_FOUND` error can also mean that the user cannot see a resource that exists."},"4296":{"id":"/sdk/errors-25","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#actionvalidationerror","content":"`applyAction` throws `ActionValidationError` when the server ran the action's submission criteria and parameter constraints and they failed. It is not a `PalantirApiError`. Its `validation` field has `result`, `submissionCriteria`, and `parameters`. See Actions for the shape and a message helper."},"4297":{"id":"/sdk/errors-26","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#actionvalidationerror","content":"`batchApplyAction` does not throw it. A batch that fails validation rejects with a `PalantirApiError`."},"4298":{"id":"/sdk/errors-27","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#methods-that-return-a-result","content":"Three methods resolve to a `Result` instead of rejecting:"},"4299":{"id":"/sdk/errors-28","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#methods-that-return-a-result","content":"| Method                                     | On               |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------- |\n| `fetchOneWithErrors(primaryKey, options?)` | Object type sets |","table":"table-2"},"4300":{"id":"/sdk/errors-29","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#methods-that-return-a-result","content":"| Method                          | On               |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `fetchPageWithErrors(options?)` | Every object set |","table":"table-2"},"4301":{"id":"/sdk/errors-30","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#methods-that-return-a-result","content":"| Method                                      | On           |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| `$link.<link>.fetchOneWithErrors(options?)` | Single links |","table":"table-2"},"4302":{"id":"/sdk/errors-31","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#methods-that-return-a-result","content":"A `Result` is `{ value }` on success or `{ error }` on failure, where `error` is an `Error`. Narrow it with `isOk` from `@osdk/client`:"},"4303":{"id":"/sdk/errors-32","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#methods-that-return-a-result","content":"`error` is the same error the throwing variant would have thrown, so the narrowing above still applies."},"4304":{"id":"/sdk/errors-33","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#retries","content":"The client retries a request that fails with `429 Too Many Requests` or `503 Service Unavailable`, up to three times, unless the response sets the header `QoS-Retry-Hint: do-not-retry`. The delays grow exponentially from about one second, with random jitter. Other errors, including network failures, are not retried. Your code sees the error only after the last attempt."},"4305":{"id":"/sdk/errors-34","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#errors-before-a-request","content":"These throw a plain `Error` before any request is sent:"},"4306":{"id":"/sdk/errors-35","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#errors-before-a-request","content":"| Error                  | Cause                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Invalid ontology RID` | `createClient` got an Ontology RID string that does not start with `ri.`. If you pass a `Promise`, the check runs when it resolves and surfaces as an unhandled rejection instead. |","table":"table-3"},"4307":{"id":"/sdk/errors-36","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#errors-before-a-request","content":"| Error                     | Cause                                                                                      |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `baseUrl cannot be empty` | `createClient` got an empty base URL. A malformed URL throws a `TypeError` from `new URL`. |","table":"table-3"},"4308":{"id":"/sdk/errors-37","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#errors-before-a-request","content":"| Error                                                                | Cause                                                                   |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Cannot filter on property \"<name>\" with an undefined or null value` | A `where` clause had a `null` or `undefined` value. See Filter objects. |","table":"table-3"},"4309":{"id":"/sdk/errors-38","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#errors-before-a-request","content":"| Error                                                              | Cause                                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `A WhereClause Filter with multiple clauses/fields is not allowed` | One property in a `where` clause had more than one operator. |","table":"table-3"},"4310":{"id":"/sdk/errors-39","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#errors-before-a-request","content":"| Error                                          | Cause                                                                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Object does not implement interface '<name>'` | `$as` was called with an interface the object type does not implement. See Interfaces. |","table":"table-3"},"4311":{"id":"/sdk/errors-40","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#errors-before-a-request","content":"| Error                                      | Cause                                            |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `Union return types are not yet supported` | A function returned a union type. See Functions. |","table":"table-3"},"4312":{"id":"/sdk/errors-41","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#patterns","content":"Await every call inside `try`/`catch`, or attach `.catch`. A rejected promise that nothing handles crashes a Node.js process and logs an unhandled rejection in the browser."},"4313":{"id":"/sdk/errors-42","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#patterns","content":"Catch `ActionValidationError` before `PalantirApiError`, and show the validation messages to the user. Other action errors usually need a retry or an administrator."},"4314":{"id":"/sdk/errors-43","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#patterns","content":"For loads where a missing object is expected, use the `WithErrors` variants instead of catching."},"4315":{"id":"/sdk/errors-44","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#patterns","content":"In long jobs, log `errorInstanceId` and `errorName` with each failure, and keep going instead of stopping at the first error."},"4316":{"id":"/sdk/errors-45","page_id":"/sdk/errors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/errors#patterns","content":"For errors in `@osdk/react` hooks, see Loading and errors."},"4317":{"id":"/sdk/filtering","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"page","content":"Filter objects","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK","Read data"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering"},"4318":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-0","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering","content":"Reference for where clauses in @osdk/client, covering comparison, set, null, text, array, date, geospatial, and logical operators, with examples."},"4319":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-1","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#how-a-clause-combines","content":"How a clause combines"},"4320":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-2","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"Operator reference"},"4321":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-3","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#comparison-and-sets","content":"Comparison and sets"},"4322":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-4","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#text","content":"Text"},"4323":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-5","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#fuzzy-matching","content":"Fuzzy matching"},"4324":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-6","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#phonetic-matching","content":"Phonetic matching"},"4325":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-7","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#interval-rules","content":"Interval rules"},"4326":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-8","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#arrays","content":"Arrays"},"4327":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-9","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#dates-and-timestamps","content":"Dates and timestamps"},"4328":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-10","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#geospatial-filters","content":"Geospatial filters"},"4329":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-11","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#combine-clauses","content":"Combine clauses"},"4330":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-12","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#title-and-primary-key","content":"Title and primary key"},"4331":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-13","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#struct-properties","content":"Struct properties"},"4332":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-14","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#vector-search","content":"Vector search"},"4333":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-15","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/filtering#type-a-clause","content":"Type a clause"},"4334":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-16","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering","content":"`where` narrows an object set on the server. It takes a clause object and returns a new object set, so you can chain it with other `where` calls, links, aggregations, and any load method."},"4335":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-17","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering","content":"`where` sends no request by itself. The filter runs when you call `fetchPage`, `asyncIter`, `aggregate`, or another method that loads data."},"4336":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-18","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#how-a-clause-combines","content":"Each key of the clause is a property name, `$title`, `$primaryKey`, or one of `$and`, `$or`, `$not`."},"4337":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-19","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#how-a-clause-combines","content":"Several keys in one clause must all match. `{ department: \"Engineering\", salary: { $gte: 150_000 } }` is an AND."},"4338":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-20","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#how-a-clause-combines","content":"A bare value means equality. `{ department: \"Engineering\" }` is the same as `{ department: { $eq: \"Engineering\" } }`."},"4339":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-21","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#how-a-clause-combines","content":"Each property takes one operator. `{ salary: { $gte: 100_000, $lt: 200_000 } }` does not typecheck, and throws at runtime. Use `$and` for a range."},"4340":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-22","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#how-a-clause-combines","content":"Chained `where` calls also combine with AND."},"4341":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-23","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#how-a-clause-combines","content":"The value must not be `null` or `undefined`. The client throws `Cannot filter on property \"<name>\" with an undefined or null value`. To match missing values, use `$isNull: true`."},"4342":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-24","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator | Property types     | Value                          | Matches                                       |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `$eq`    | Non-array, non-geo | A value of the property's type | Equal values. Also written as the bare value. |","table":"table-0"},"4343":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-25","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator | Property types     | Value                          | Matches                    |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ | -------------------------- |\n| `$ne`    | Non-array, non-geo | A value of the property's type | Values that are not equal. |","table":"table-0"},"4344":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-26","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator | Property types     | Value              | Matches                                                      |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `$in`    | Non-array, non-geo | An array of values | Any value in the array. An empty array matches every object. |","table":"table-0"},"4345":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-27","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator  | Property types | Value     | Matches                                                 |\n| --------- | -------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$isNull` | All            | `boolean` | `true`: the property has no value. `false`: it has one. |","table":"table-0"},"4346":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-28","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator                     | Property types                      | Value                          | Matches                                                                                      |\n| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$gt`, `$gte`, `$lt`, `$lte` | Numbers, strings, dates, timestamps | A value of the property's type | Greater than, greater or equal, less than, less or equal. Strings compare lexicographically. |","table":"table-0"},"4347":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-29","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator      | Property types | Value                                    | Matches                                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$startsWith` | `string`       | `string`, or `{ term, phoneticSearch? }` | Values that contain the terms adjacent and in order, with the last term matched as a prefix. The match can start anywhere in the value. |","table":"table-0"},"4348":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-30","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator           | Property types | Value                                                              | Matches                                                    |\n| ------------------ | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$containsAnyTerm` | `string`       | `string`, `{ term, fuzzySearch? }`, or `{ term, phoneticSearch? }` | Values that contain any of the whitespace-separated terms. |","table":"table-0"},"4349":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-31","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator            | Property types | Value                                                              | Matches                                          |\n| ------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `$containsAllTerms` | `string`       | `string`, `{ term, fuzzySearch? }`, or `{ term, phoneticSearch? }` | Values that contain all the terms, in any order. |","table":"table-0"},"4350":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-32","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator                   | Property types | Value                                    | Matches                                                   |\n| -------------------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$containsAllTermsInOrder` | `string`       | `string`, or `{ term, phoneticSearch? }` | Values that contain all the terms, adjacent and in order. |","table":"table-0"},"4351":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-33","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator    | Property types | Value            | Matches                                                                  |\n| ----------- | -------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `$interval` | `string`       | An interval rule | Term proximity, ordering, prefix, and fuzzy matches. See Interval rules. |","table":"table-0"},"4352":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-34","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator        | Property types | Value    | Matches                                                                       |\n| --------------- | -------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$matchesRegex` | `string`       | `string` | Beta. Values that match the regular expression, in the Foundry search syntax. |","table":"table-0"},"4353":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-35","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator    | Property types   | Value                                     | Matches                                        |\n| ----------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `$contains` | Array properties | An element value, or a filter on elements | Arrays with at least one element that matches. |","table":"table-0"},"4354":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-36","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator  | Property types         | Value                              | Matches                                         |\n| --------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `$within` | `geopoint`, `geoshape` | Distance, bounding box, or polygon | Shapes inside the area. See Geospatial filters. |","table":"table-0"},"4355":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-37","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator      | Property types         | Value                   | Matches                       |\n| ------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `$intersects` | `geopoint`, `geoshape` | Bounding box or polygon | Shapes that overlap the area. |","table":"table-0"},"4356":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-38","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator | Property types | Value               | Matches                          |\n| -------- | -------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `$and`   | Clause         | An array of clauses | Objects that match every clause. |","table":"table-0"},"4357":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-39","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator | Property types | Value               | Matches                                 |\n| -------- | -------------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `$or`    | Clause         | An array of clauses | Objects that match at least one clause. |","table":"table-0"},"4358":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-40","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"| Operator | Property types | Value      | Matches                               |\n| -------- | -------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `$not`   | Clause         | One clause | Objects that do not match the clause. |","table":"table-0"},"4359":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-41","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"Boolean properties accept `$eq`, `$ne`, `$in`, and `$isNull`. Array properties accept only `$contains` and `$isNull`."},"4360":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-42","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#operator-reference","content":"`$in: []` matches every object, not none. When the array comes from user input, check for an empty array before you add the filter."},"4361":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-43","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#text","content":"The text operators match whole terms, the whitespace-separated words of the value, rather than raw substrings. `$startsWith` is a term match too: `{ fullName: { $startsWith: \"ada lov\" } }` matches `Ada Lovelace`, and also `Countess Ada Lovelace`."},"4362":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-44","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#fuzzy-matching","content":"`$containsAnyTerm` and `$containsAllTerms` also take `{ term, fuzzySearch: true }`, which matches terms within a small edit distance, such as a typo:"},"4363":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-45","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#phonetic-matching","content":"Every text operator also takes `{ term, phoneticSearch: true }`, which matches similarly pronounced terms, such as `Jon` and `John`. The property must support phonetic search, set with `supportsPhonetic` in Ontology as code. `fuzzySearch` and `phoneticSearch` cannot both be `true`; use `$or` to combine them."},"4364":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-46","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#interval-rules","content":"`$interval` takes one rule. Rules nest through `$and` and `$or`:"},"4365":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-47","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#interval-rules","content":"| Rule  | Fields                                                     | Matches                                                                                                             |\n| ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Match | `$match: string`, `$ordered: boolean`, `$maxGaps?: number` | The terms of `$match`. `$ordered: true` requires them in order. `$maxGaps` limits the number of words between them. |","table":"table-1"},"4366":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-48","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#interval-rules","content":"| Rule   | Fields                                      | Matches                                                     |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Prefix | `$match: string`, `$prefixOnLastTerm: true` | The terms in order, with the last term matched as a prefix. |","table":"table-1"},"4367":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-49","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#interval-rules","content":"| Rule  | Fields                                  | Matches                                                   |\n| ----- | --------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Fuzzy | `$fuzzy: string`, `$fuzziness?: number` | A term within `$fuzziness` edits (0, 1, or 2; default 2). |","table":"table-1"},"4368":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-50","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#interval-rules","content":"| Rule | Fields                                                           | Matches         |\n| ---- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| All  | `$and: IntervalRule[]`, `$ordered: boolean`, `$maxGaps?: number` | Every sub-rule. |","table":"table-1"},"4369":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-51","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#interval-rules","content":"| Rule | Fields                | Matches                |\n| ---- | --------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Any  | `$or: IntervalRule[]` | At least one sub-rule. |","table":"table-1"},"4370":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-52","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#arrays","content":"On an array property, `$contains` matches objects where at least one element matches. Pass an element value, or a filter that each element is tested against. `$isNull` is the only other operator:"},"4371":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-53","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#arrays","content":"To require several elements, combine `$contains` filters with `$and`."},"4372":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-54","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#dates-and-timestamps","content":"Date and timestamp properties take ISO 8601 strings: `\"2024-01-31\"` for dates and `\"2024-01-31T09:00:00Z\"` for timestamps. They accept `$eq`, `$ne`, `$in`, `$isNull`, and the range operators:"},"4373":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-55","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#geospatial-filters","content":"Coordinates are `[longitude, latitude]`, as in GeoJSON. The samples assume `Office` has a `geopoint` property named `location`."},"4374":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-56","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#geospatial-filters","content":"| Filter                        | Value                                                               | Matches                                   |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `$within: { $distance, $of }` | `$distance: [number, unit]`, `$of: [lon, lat]` or a GeoJSON `Point` | Points within the distance of the center. |","table":"table-2"},"4375":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-57","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#geospatial-filters","content":"| Filter                                  | Value                        | Matches                         |\n| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `$within: { $bbox }` or `$within: bbox` | `[west, south, east, north]` | Shapes inside the bounding box. |","table":"table-2"},"4376":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-58","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#geospatial-filters","content":"| Filter                  | Value                                               | Matches                    |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `$within: { $polygon }` | Polygon coordinates: an array of rings, each closed | Shapes inside the polygon. |","table":"table-2"},"4377":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-59","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#geospatial-filters","content":"| Filter             | Value               | Matches                    |\n| ------------------ | ------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `$within: polygon` | A GeoJSON `Polygon` | Shapes inside the polygon. |","table":"table-2"},"4378":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-60","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#geospatial-filters","content":"| Filter                                          | Value                        | Matches                               |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `$intersects: { $bbox }` or `$intersects: bbox` | `[west, south, east, north]` | Shapes that overlap the bounding box. |","table":"table-2"},"4379":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-61","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#geospatial-filters","content":"| Filter                                                | Value                                       | Matches                          |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `$intersects: { $polygon }` or `$intersects: polygon` | Polygon coordinates, or a GeoJSON `Polygon` | Shapes that overlap the polygon. |","table":"table-2"},"4380":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-62","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#geospatial-filters","content":"Distance units are `\"m\"`, `\"meter\"`, `\"meters\"`, `\"km\"`, `\"kilometer\"`, `\"kilometers\"`, `\"cm\"`, `\"centimeter\"`, `\"centimeters\"`, `\"mile\"`, `\"miles\"`, `\"foot\"`, `\"feet\"`, `\"inch\"`, `\"inches\"`, `\"yard\"`, `\"yards\"`, `\"nautical_mile\"`, `\"nauticalMile\"`, and `\"nautical miles\"`."},"4381":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-63","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#combine-clauses","content":"`$and`, `$or`, and `$not` take clauses and nest to any depth:"},"4382":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-64","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#title-and-primary-key","content":"`$title` filters on the object type's title property and `$primaryKey` on its primary key, without naming them. Both are useful in code that works across object types:"},"4383":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-65","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#struct-properties","content":"A struct property filters on one field at a time: `{ address: { city: \"Denver\" } }` applies the field's own operators to `address.city`. To filter on two fields, combine two clauses with `$and`. On an array of structs, wrap the field filter in `$contains`: `{ addresses: { $contains: { city: \"Denver\" } } }`."},"4384":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-66","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#vector-search","content":"`nearestNeighbors(query, numNeighbors, property)` returns an object set of the objects whose vector property is closest to the query. `query` is text, which the server embeds with the property's model, or a vector with the property's dimension. `numNeighbors` is between 1 and 500. To get the closest first, and a `$score` on each object, load the result with `$orderBy: \"relevance\"`."},"4385":{"id":"/sdk/filtering-67","page_id":"/sdk/filtering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/filtering#type-a-clause","content":"Build a clause outside the call with the `WhereClause` type from `@osdk/client`:"},"4386":{"id":"/sdk/functions","page_id":"/sdk/functions","type":"page","content":"Functions","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK","Logic"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk/functions"},"4387":{"id":"/sdk/functions-0","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions","content":"Execute Foundry functions (queries) with executeFunction, pass objects and object sets as parameters, and read struct, object, and object set results."},"4388":{"id":"/sdk/functions-1","page_id":"/sdk/functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/functions#execute-a-function","content":"Execute a function"},"4389":{"id":"/sdk/functions-2","page_id":"/sdk/functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"Parameter values"},"4390":{"id":"/sdk/functions-3","page_id":"/sdk/functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"Return values"},"4391":{"id":"/sdk/functions-4","page_id":"/sdk/functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/functions#object-results","content":"Object results"},"4392":{"id":"/sdk/functions-5","page_id":"/sdk/functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/functions#object-set-results","content":"Object set results"},"4393":{"id":"/sdk/functions-6","page_id":"/sdk/functions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/functions#in-react","content":"In React"},"4394":{"id":"/sdk/functions-7","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions","content":"Functions published to the Ontology, called queries in the API, appear in your generated SDK next to object types and actions. `client(myFunction).executeFunction(params)` runs one on the server and resolves to its typed return value."},"4395":{"id":"/sdk/functions-8","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions","content":"The samples use these functions, which stand in for functions in your own SDK:"},"4396":{"id":"/sdk/functions-9","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions","content":"| Function         | Parameters | Returns   |\n| ---------------- | ---------- | --------- |\n| `countEmployees` | None       | `integer` |","table":"table-0"},"4397":{"id":"/sdk/functions-10","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions","content":"| Function             | Parameters           | Returns                         |\n| -------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `getEmployeeMetrics` | `department: string` | Struct `{ headcount: integer }` |","table":"table-0"},"4398":{"id":"/sdk/functions-11","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions","content":"| Function        | Parameters                  | Returns  |\n| --------------- | --------------------------- | -------- |\n| `summarizeTeam` | `team: ObjectSet<Employee>` | `string` |","table":"table-0"},"4399":{"id":"/sdk/functions-12","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions","content":"| Function        | Parameters                              | Returns               |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `getTopEarners` | `department: string`, `limit?: integer` | `ObjectSet<Employee>` |","table":"table-0"},"4400":{"id":"/sdk/functions-13","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions","content":"| Function     | Parameters           | Returns    |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ---------- |\n| `getManager` | `employee: Employee` | `Employee` |","table":"table-0"},"4401":{"id":"/sdk/functions-14","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#execute-a-function","content":"`executeFunction` takes one object with a key per parameter, or no argument when the function has no parameters. Nullable parameters are optional. It rejects with a `PalantirApiError` when the function fails or times out on the server; see Errors."},"4402":{"id":"/sdk/functions-15","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#execute-a-function","content":"If your SDK was generated with a pinned function version, the client calls that version. Otherwise it calls the latest published version."},"4403":{"id":"/sdk/functions-16","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                                                                                                         |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Primitive      | A value of the parameter's TypeScript type. Dates and timestamps are ISO 8601 strings. `long` and `decimal` accept a `number` or a `string`. |","table":"table-1"},"4404":{"id":"/sdk/functions-17","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                              |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object         | A loaded object, its primary key, or `{ $apiName, $primaryKey }`. |","table":"table-1"},"4405":{"id":"/sdk/functions-18","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                                                                                        |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Interface      | An object loaded through the interface, or `{ $objectType, $primaryKey }`, where `$objectType` is the concrete object type. |","table":"table-1"},"4406":{"id":"/sdk/functions-19","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                                                                           |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object set     | An object set, such as `client(Employee).where({ ... })`. The server receives its definition, not its objects. |","table":"table-1"},"4407":{"id":"/sdk/functions-20","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                     |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| List, set      | An array, or a `Set` for set parameters. |","table":"table-1"},"4408":{"id":"/sdk/functions-21","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                          |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Struct         | An object whose keys are the struct's fields. |","table":"table-1"},"4409":{"id":"/sdk/functions-22","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                                                      |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Map            | An object keyed by the map's keys. For object keys, use each object's `$objectSpecifier`. |","table":"table-1"},"4410":{"id":"/sdk/functions-23","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                                                                 |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Attachment     | An attachment RID, a `File`, or the result of `createAttachmentUpload`. The client uploads it first. |","table":"table-1"},"4411":{"id":"/sdk/functions-24","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"| Parameter type  | Pass                                                              |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Media reference | A `MediaUpload`, a `Media` from an object, or a `MediaReference`. |","table":"table-1"},"4412":{"id":"/sdk/functions-25","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#parameter-values","content":"Pass an object set to let the function work on a filtered set without loading it in the client:"},"4413":{"id":"/sdk/functions-26","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type | You get                                                                                 |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Primitive   | The value. `long` and `decimal` are strings; dates and timestamps are ISO 8601 strings. |","table":"table-2"},"4414":{"id":"/sdk/functions-27","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type | You get   |\n| ----------- | --------- |\n| List, set   | An array. |","table":"table-2"},"4415":{"id":"/sdk/functions-28","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type | You get         |\n| ----------- | --------------- |\n| Struct      | A plain object. |","table":"table-2"},"4416":{"id":"/sdk/functions-29","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type | You get                                                                              |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Map         | A plain object keyed by the map's keys. Object keys become object specifier strings. |","table":"table-2"},"4417":{"id":"/sdk/functions-30","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type | You get                                                                                      |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object      | An object reference with `$apiName`, `$objectType`, and `$primaryKey`. It has no properties. |","table":"table-2"},"4418":{"id":"/sdk/functions-31","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type | You get                                                               |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Object set  | An object set. Load it with `fetchPage`, `asyncIter`, or `aggregate`. |","table":"table-2"},"4419":{"id":"/sdk/functions-32","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type | You get                                     |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| Attachment  | An `Attachment`. See Attachments and media. |","table":"table-2"},"4420":{"id":"/sdk/functions-33","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type     | You get                               |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Media reference | A `Media`. See Attachments and media. |","table":"table-2"},"4421":{"id":"/sdk/functions-34","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type                 | You get            |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| Two-dimensional aggregation | `{ key, value }[]` |","table":"table-2"},"4422":{"id":"/sdk/functions-35","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type                   | You get                               |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Three-dimensional aggregation | `{ key, groups: { key, value }[] }[]` |","table":"table-2"},"4423":{"id":"/sdk/functions-36","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"| Return type                                 | You get     |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| Nullable, when the function returns nothing | `undefined` |","table":"table-2"},"4424":{"id":"/sdk/functions-37","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#return-values","content":"Union return types are not supported: the client throws `Union return types are not yet supported`."},"4425":{"id":"/sdk/functions-38","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#object-results","content":"A returned object is a reference, not a loaded object. Load it by primary key to read its properties:"},"4426":{"id":"/sdk/functions-39","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#object-set-results","content":"A returned object set is like any other. Filter, sort, page, and aggregate it before loading:"},"4427":{"id":"/sdk/functions-40","page_id":"/sdk/functions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/functions#in-react","content":"`useOsdkFunction` from `@osdk/react` executes a function, caches the result by its parameters, and can refetch when objects it depends on change. See Functions in React."},"4428":{"id":"/sdk","page_id":"/sdk","type":"page","content":"TypeScript SDK overview","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk"},"4429":{"id":"/sdk-0","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk","content":"Query objects, apply actions, and run functions from any TypeScript runtime with @osdk/client, in Node.js scripts, servers, Vue, or any framework."},"4430":{"id":"/sdk-1","page_id":"/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk#install","content":"Install"},"4431":{"id":"/sdk-2","page_id":"/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk#example","content":"Example"},"4432":{"id":"/sdk-3","page_id":"/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk#one-entry-point-clientdefinition","content":"One entry point: `client(definition)`"},"4433":{"id":"/sdk-4","page_id":"/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk#relation-to-osdkreact","content":"Relation to `@osdk/react`"},"4434":{"id":"/sdk-5","page_id":"/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"In this section"},"4435":{"id":"/sdk-6","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk","content":"`@osdk/client` reads and edits your Ontology from any JavaScript runtime with `fetch`: Node.js scripts and servers, serverless functions, and browser apps in any framework. It has no UI dependency. Your generated SDK supplies typed definitions for your object types, interfaces, actions, and functions, and the client runs them."},"4436":{"id":"/sdk-7","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#install","content":"Your generated SDK comes from your Foundry npm registry. Set up `.npmrc` as described in Installation, then:"},"4437":{"id":"/sdk-8","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#install","content":"Create one client for your app with `createClient`, as described in Create a client. Authentication covers the token provider. The samples in this section import that client from `./client`."},"4438":{"id":"/sdk-9","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#example","content":"The query runs on the server and returns typed objects. Each `applyAction` call validates and applies one edit. In real code, wrap it in `try`/`catch`, as shown in Actions."},"4439":{"id":"/sdk-10","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#one-entry-point-clientdefinition","content":"Call `client` with a definition from your SDK. What it returns depends on the definition:"},"4440":{"id":"/sdk-11","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#one-entry-point-clientdefinition","content":"| You pass                           | You get                                    | Main methods                                                                                         |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| An object type, such as `Employee` | An object set of every object of that type | `fetchOne`, `fetchPage`, `asyncIter`, `where`, `aggregate`, `pivotTo`, `withProperties`, `subscribe` |","table":"table-0"},"4441":{"id":"/sdk-12","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#one-entry-point-clientdefinition","content":"| You pass                       | You get                                          | Main methods                |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------- |\n| An interface, such as `Worker` | An object set over every type that implements it | The same, except `fetchOne` |","table":"table-0"},"4442":{"id":"/sdk-13","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#one-entry-point-clientdefinition","content":"| You pass                            | You get           | Main methods                      |\n| ----------------------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| An action, such as `modifyEmployee` | An action invoker | `applyAction`, `batchApplyAction` |","table":"table-0"},"4443":{"id":"/sdk-14","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#one-entry-point-clientdefinition","content":"| You pass           | You get            | Main methods      |\n| ------------------ | ------------------ | ----------------- |\n| A function (query) | A function invoker | `executeFunction` |","table":"table-0"},"4444":{"id":"/sdk-15","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#one-entry-point-clientdefinition","content":"Object sets are lazy descriptions. `where`, `pivotTo`, `union`, and `withProperties` return new object sets without sending a request. A request goes out when you call a method that loads data: `fetchOne`, `fetchPage`, `asyncIter`, `aggregate`, or `subscribe`."},"4445":{"id":"/sdk-16","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#one-entry-point-clientdefinition","content":"`client.fetchMetadata(definition)` loads the definition from Foundry at runtime, such as an object type's `displayName`, `description`, and `icon`, or an interface's `implementedBy`."},"4446":{"id":"/sdk-17","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#relation-to-osdkreact","content":"`@osdk/react` is built on this client. Its hooks accept the same `where` clauses, derived property definitions, and action parameters, and add a shared cache that keeps components current after actions and live updates. In a React app, use the hooks for data you render and call the client directly for one-off work, such as exports. See Objects in React."},"4447":{"id":"/sdk-18","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#relation-to-osdkreact","content":"Outside React, framework guides show how to wire the client in Node.js and Vue."},"4448":{"id":"/sdk-19","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Load objects\" href=\"/sdk/objects\">fetchOne, fetchPage, asyncIter, $select, sorting, and the object shape.</Card>"},"4449":{"id":"/sdk-20","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Filter objects\" href=\"/sdk/filtering\">Every where operator, with examples.</Card>"},"4450":{"id":"/sdk-21","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Links and object sets\" href=\"/sdk/links\">Follow links, pivot sets, and combine them.</Card>"},"4451":{"id":"/sdk-22","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Interfaces\" href=\"/sdk/interfaces\">Query across object types and convert between views.</Card>"},"4452":{"id":"/sdk-23","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Aggregations\" href=\"/sdk/aggregations\">Counts, metrics, and group-bys on the server.</Card>"},"4453":{"id":"/sdk-24","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Derived properties\" href=\"/sdk/derived-properties\">Compute properties at query time with withProperties.</Card>"},"4454":{"id":"/sdk-25","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Actions\" href=\"/sdk/actions\">Apply, validate, and batch edits.</Card>"},"4455":{"id":"/sdk-26","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Functions\" href=\"/sdk/functions\">Run Foundry functions and read their results.</Card>"},"4456":{"id":"/sdk-27","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Attachments and media\" href=\"/sdk/media\">Download and upload files.</Card>"},"4457":{"id":"/sdk-28","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Subscriptions\" href=\"/sdk/subscriptions\">Receive live updates for an object set.</Card>"},"4458":{"id":"/sdk-29","page_id":"/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk#in-this-section","content":"<Card title=\"Errors\" href=\"/sdk/errors\">Error types, retries, and handling patterns.</Card>"},"4459":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","type":"page","content":"Interfaces","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK","Read data"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk/interfaces"},"4460":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-0","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces","content":"Query objects of every type that implements an interface, convert between interface and object views with $as, and narrow object sets with narrowToType."},"4461":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-1","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/interfaces#query-an-interface","content":"Query an interface"},"4462":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-2","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/interfaces#what-an-interface-object-set-supports","content":"What an interface object set supports"},"4463":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-3","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-one-object-with-as","content":"Convert one object with `$as`"},"4464":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-4","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-an-object-set-with-narrowtotype","content":"Convert an object set with `narrowToType`"},"4465":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-5","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/interfaces#read-interface-metadata","content":"Read interface metadata"},"4466":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-6","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/interfaces#pass-interface-objects-to-actions","content":"Pass interface objects to actions"},"4467":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-7","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces","content":"An interface describes properties that several object types share. Querying an interface returns objects of every type that implements it, viewed through the interface's properties. You can then convert each object to its concrete type."},"4468":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-8","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces","content":"In the example SDK, the interface `Worker` has one property, `name`. `Employee` implements it, with `fullName` as `name`."},"4469":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-9","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#query-an-interface","content":"`client(Worker)` is an object set over every object that implements `Worker`. Filter, sort, and select by the interface's property names:"},"4470":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-10","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#query-an-interface","content":"On an interface object, `$apiName` is the interface (`\"Worker\"`) and `$objectType` is the object's concrete type (`\"Employee\"`). `$primaryKey` is the concrete object's primary key."},"4471":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-11","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#what-an-interface-object-set-supports","content":"| Method  | Supported | Notes                        |\n| ------- | --------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `where` | Yes       | On interface property names. |","table":"table-0"},"4472":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-12","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#what-an-interface-object-set-supports","content":"| Method                                          | Supported | Notes                                     |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `fetchPage`, `fetchPageWithErrors`, `asyncIter` | Yes       | Accept `$includeAllBaseObjectProperties`. |","table":"table-0"},"4473":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-13","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#what-an-interface-object-set-supports","content":"| Method      | Supported | Notes                        |\n| ----------- | --------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `aggregate` | Yes       | On interface property names. |","table":"table-0"},"4474":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-14","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#what-an-interface-object-set-supports","content":"| Method      | Supported | Notes              |\n| ----------- | --------- | ------------------ |\n| `subscribe` | Yes       | See Subscriptions. |","table":"table-0"},"4475":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-15","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#what-an-interface-object-set-supports","content":"| Method         | Supported | Notes                                      |\n| -------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `narrowToType` | Yes       | Converts to an object type set. See below. |","table":"table-0"},"4476":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-16","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#what-an-interface-object-set-supports","content":"| Method    | Supported | Notes                               |\n| --------- | --------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `pivotTo` | Yes       | For links defined on the interface. |","table":"table-0"},"4477":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-17","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#what-an-interface-object-set-supports","content":"| Method                           | Supported                             | Notes                                    |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `union`, `intersect`, `subtract` | With other sets of the same interface | Not with object type sets. Narrow first. |","table":"table-0"},"4478":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-18","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#what-an-interface-object-set-supports","content":"| Method                           | Supported | Notes                                                                                                                                     |\n| -------------------------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fetchOne`, `fetchOneWithErrors` | No        | Typed `never`. A primary key is unique only within one object type, so load by key from the object type: `client(Employee).fetchOne(id)`. |","table":"table-0"},"4479":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-19","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-one-object-with-as","content":"`$as(Employee)` returns the concrete view of an interface object, with the object type's property names. `$as(Worker)` goes the other way:"},"4480":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-20","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-one-object-with-as","content":"`$as` makes no request. It only exposes the properties that were loaded:"},"4481":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-21","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-one-object-with-as","content":"From an interface fetch, the concrete view has only the properties that the interface maps to, such as `fullName`. Reading `salary` is a type error."},"4482":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-22","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-one-object-with-as","content":"To get every property of the object type, pass `$includeAllBaseObjectProperties: true` to `fetchPage` or `asyncIter`. Then `$as(Employee)` has all `Employee` properties."},"4483":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-23","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-one-object-with-as","content":"`$includeAllBaseObjectProperties` cannot be combined with `$select`."},"4484":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-24","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-one-object-with-as","content":"`$as` throws when:"},"4485":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-25","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-one-object-with-as","content":"The target is an object type other than the object's own. Check `$objectType` first, as above."},"4486":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-26","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-one-object-with-as","content":"The target interface is not implemented by the object type."},"4487":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-27","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-one-object-with-as","content":"Converting an interface object to its object type, when one of the interface's properties is implemented by something other than a plain property of the object type. The message tells you to load the object type directly."},"4488":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-28","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-an-object-set-with-narrowtotype","content":"`narrowToType` converts a whole object set on the server, and keeps only objects of the given type:"},"4489":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-29","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#convert-an-object-set-with-narrowtotype","content":"From an interface, pass a type that implements it. From an object type, pass an interface it implements. Other types do not typecheck."},"4490":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-30","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#read-interface-metadata","content":"`client.fetchMetadata(Worker)` loads the interface definition from Foundry, including `implementedBy`, the API names of the object types that implement it:"},"4491":{"id":"/sdk/interfaces-31","page_id":"/sdk/interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/interfaces#pass-interface-objects-to-actions","content":"An action parameter of an interface type takes a plain object with the concrete type and primary key, such as `{ $objectType: worker.$objectType, $primaryKey: worker.$primaryKey }`. Pass that object, not the loaded `worker` itself. See Actions."},"4492":{"id":"/sdk/links","page_id":"/sdk/links","type":"page","content":"Links and object sets","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK","Read data"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk/links"},"4493":{"id":"/sdk/links-0","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links","content":"Traverse links from an object with $link, pivot whole object sets with pivotTo, and combine object sets with union, intersect, and subtract."},"4494":{"id":"/sdk/links-1","page_id":"/sdk/links","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/links#follow-a-link-from-an-object","content":"Follow a link from an object"},"4495":{"id":"/sdk/links-2","page_id":"/sdk/links","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/links#one-to-one-and-many-to-one-links","content":"One-to-one and many-to-one links"},"4496":{"id":"/sdk/links-3","page_id":"/sdk/links","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/links#one-to-many-and-many-to-many-links","content":"One-to-many and many-to-many links"},"4497":{"id":"/sdk/links-4","page_id":"/sdk/links","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/links#pivot-an-object-set","content":"Pivot an object set"},"4498":{"id":"/sdk/links-5","page_id":"/sdk/links","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/links#combine-object-sets","content":"Combine object sets"},"4499":{"id":"/sdk/links-6","page_id":"/sdk/links","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/links#load-links-in-bulk","content":"Load links in bulk"},"4500":{"id":"/sdk/links-7","page_id":"/sdk/links","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/links#in-react","content":"In React"},"4501":{"id":"/sdk/links-8","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links","content":"Links connect objects of one type to objects of another, such as an `Employee` to their `Office`. You can follow a link from one loaded object with `$link`, or from a whole object set with `pivotTo`. Object sets also combine with `union`, `intersect`, and `subtract`, all on the server."},"4502":{"id":"/sdk/links-9","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links","content":"In the example SDK, `Employee` has three links: `lead` (one `Employee`), `reports` (many `Employee`), and `office` (one `Office`). `Office` has `occupants` (many `Employee`)."},"4503":{"id":"/sdk/links-10","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#follow-a-link-from-an-object","content":"Every object has a `$link` field with one entry per link type. What the entry is depends on the link's cardinality:"},"4504":{"id":"/sdk/links-11","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#follow-a-link-from-an-object","content":"| Link                  | `$link` entry          | Methods                                              |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| One, such as `office` | A single-link accessor | `fetchOne(options?)`, `fetchOneWithErrors(options?)` |","table":"table-0"},"4505":{"id":"/sdk/links-12","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#follow-a-link-from-an-object","content":"| Link                    | `$link` entry                    | Methods                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Many, such as `reports` | An object set of the linked type | Everything an object set has: `where`, `fetchPage`, `asyncIter`, `aggregate`, `pivotTo`, and more |","table":"table-0"},"4506":{"id":"/sdk/links-13","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#one-to-one-and-many-to-one-links","content":"`fetchOne` takes `$select` and `$includeRid`. It rejects when the object has no linked object, with a `PalantirApiError` whose message is `Expected a single result but got 0 instead`. If the link is optional, use `fetchOneWithErrors` and check the result:"},"4507":{"id":"/sdk/links-14","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#one-to-many-and-many-to-many-links","content":"A many link is an object set, so you can filter, sort, page, and aggregate it before loading anything:"},"4508":{"id":"/sdk/links-15","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#one-to-many-and-many-to-many-links","content":"`$link` sends no request until you call a load method. You do not need to `$select` anything for `$link` to work: the link resolves from the object's primary key."},"4509":{"id":"/sdk/links-16","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#pivot-an-object-set","content":"`pivotTo(link)` returns the set of objects linked to any object in the source set. Use it to traverse links for many objects in one request instead of one request per object:"},"4510":{"id":"/sdk/links-17","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#pivot-an-object-set","content":"The result has no duplicates: an office with ten engineers appears once. Pivots chain, and the result is a full object set:"},"4511":{"id":"/sdk/links-18","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#pivot-an-object-set","content":"The link name must exist on the source type. `pivotTo(\"occupants\")` on an `Employee` set does not typecheck."},"4512":{"id":"/sdk/links-19","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#combine-object-sets","content":"`union`, `intersect`, and `subtract` take one or more object sets of the same type and return a new object set. Nothing loads until you call a load method:"},"4513":{"id":"/sdk/links-20","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#combine-object-sets","content":"| Method          | Returns                     |\n| --------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `a.union(b, c)` | Objects in any of the sets. |","table":"table-1"},"4514":{"id":"/sdk/links-21","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#combine-object-sets","content":"| Method              | Returns               |\n| ------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `a.intersect(b, c)` | Objects in every set. |","table":"table-1"},"4515":{"id":"/sdk/links-22","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#combine-object-sets","content":"| Method             | Returns                                            |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `a.subtract(b, c)` | Objects in `a` that are in none of the other sets. |","table":"table-1"},"4516":{"id":"/sdk/links-23","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#combine-object-sets","content":"The sets must be of the same object type. An `Employee` set and a `Worker` interface set do not combine; see Interfaces to convert between them with `narrowToType`."},"4517":{"id":"/sdk/links-24","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#load-links-in-bulk","content":"`experimental_asyncIterLinks(links)` iterates over the links of every object in a set and yields `{ source, target, linkType }`, where `source` and `target` carry `$apiName` and `$primaryKey`. It is experimental and may change. Use it to build an in-memory graph:"},"4518":{"id":"/sdk/links-25","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#load-links-in-bulk","content":"Limits:"},"4519":{"id":"/sdk/links-26","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#load-links-in-bulk","content":"Links can be stale: a returned primary key may no longer exist."},"4520":{"id":"/sdk/links-27","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#load-links-in-bulk","content":"The server loads source objects in pages. If one page has more than 100,000 links, the result for that page is cut off at 100,000."},"4521":{"id":"/sdk/links-28","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#load-links-in-bulk","content":"Object Storage V1 links are not supported and throw."},"4522":{"id":"/sdk/links-29","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#load-links-in-bulk","content":"Interface links are not supported."},"4523":{"id":"/sdk/links-30","page_id":"/sdk/links","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/links#in-react","content":"`@osdk/react` wraps these calls in hooks that cache and update: `useLinks` for `$link`, and `useObjectSet` for pivots and set operations. See Links in React and Object sets in React."},"4524":{"id":"/sdk/media","page_id":"/sdk/media","type":"page","content":"Attachments and media","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK","More"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk/media"},"4525":{"id":"/sdk/media-0","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media","content":"Read attachment and media reference properties with fetchContents and fetchMetadata, and upload files by passing them to action parameters."},"4526":{"id":"/sdk/media-1","page_id":"/sdk/media","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/media#read-an-attachment","content":"Read an attachment"},"4527":{"id":"/sdk/media-2","page_id":"/sdk/media","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/media#read-a-media-reference","content":"Read a media reference"},"4528":{"id":"/sdk/media-3","page_id":"/sdk/media","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/media#upload-through-an-action","content":"Upload through an action"},"4529":{"id":"/sdk/media-4","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media","content":"Objects store files in two property types. Attachment properties hold files uploaded through actions. Media reference properties point to items in a Foundry media set, such as images, documents, audio, and video. Both load lazily: the object holds a handle, and you download the content when you need it."},"4530":{"id":"/sdk/media-5","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media","content":"The samples assume `Employee` has an attachment property `resume` and a media reference property `photo`, and that an action `updateEmployeeFiles` takes `employee`, `resume` (attachment), and `photo` (media reference)."},"4531":{"id":"/sdk/media-6","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-an-attachment","content":"An attachment property is an `Attachment`:"},"4532":{"id":"/sdk/media-7","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-an-attachment","content":"| Member | Type     | Description         |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------- |\n| `rid`  | `string` | The attachment RID. |","table":"table-0"},"4533":{"id":"/sdk/media-8","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-an-attachment","content":"| Member            | Type                          | Description                                            |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `fetchMetadata()` | `Promise<AttachmentMetadata>` | Loads `rid`, `filename`, `sizeBytes`, and `mediaType`. |","table":"table-0"},"4534":{"id":"/sdk/media-9","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-an-attachment","content":"| Member            | Type                | Description                                                              |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `fetchContents()` | `Promise<Response>` | Downloads the file. Read it with `blob()`, `arrayBuffer()`, or `text()`. |","table":"table-0"},"4535":{"id":"/sdk/media-10","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-a-media-reference","content":"A media reference property is a `Media`:"},"4536":{"id":"/sdk/media-11","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-a-media-reference","content":"| Member            | Type                     | Description                                                       |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fetchMetadata()` | `Promise<MediaMetadata>` | Loads `mediaType`, `sizeBytes`, and `path` when the item has one. |","table":"table-1"},"4537":{"id":"/sdk/media-12","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-a-media-reference","content":"| Member                 | Type                         | Description                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `fetchFullMetadata?()` | `Promise<MediaFullMetadata>` | Loads type-specific metadata, such as page count for documents and dimensions for images. Optional in the type, but every `Media` the client returns has it. |","table":"table-1"},"4538":{"id":"/sdk/media-13","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-a-media-reference","content":"| Member            | Type                | Description         |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `fetchContents()` | `Promise<Response>` | Downloads the item. |","table":"table-1"},"4539":{"id":"/sdk/media-14","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-a-media-reference","content":"| Member                | Type             | Description                                                                                                |\n| --------------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getMediaReference()` | `MediaReference` | The reference itself: the MIME type and the media set item it points to. Pass it to an action or function. |","table":"table-1"},"4540":{"id":"/sdk/media-15","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-a-media-reference","content":"`itemMetadata.type` is one of `\"document\"`, `\"imagery\"`, `\"audio\"`, `\"video\"`, `\"dicom\"`, `\"email\"`, `\"model3d\"`, `\"spreadsheet\"`, or `\"untyped\"`. When the server returns a type this client version does not know, `type` is `\"unknown\"` and the payload is on `raw`."},"4541":{"id":"/sdk/media-16","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#read-a-media-reference","content":"`fetchContents` resolves to a standard `Response`. A non-2xx status does not reject, so check `response.ok`."},"4542":{"id":"/sdk/media-17","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#upload-through-an-action","content":"The client does not write files to objects directly. Pass the file as an action parameter, and the client uploads it before it applies the action:"},"4543":{"id":"/sdk/media-18","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#upload-through-an-action","content":"| Parameter type | Pass                                                                                      |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Attachment     | `createAttachmentUpload(blob, fileName)`, a `File`, or the RID of an existing attachment. |","table":"table-2"},"4544":{"id":"/sdk/media-19","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#upload-through-an-action","content":"| Parameter type  | Pass                                                                                                |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Media reference | A `MediaUpload` (`{ data: blob, fileName }`), a `Media` from another object, or a `MediaReference`. |","table":"table-2"},"4545":{"id":"/sdk/media-20","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#upload-through-an-action","content":"`openAsBlob` needs Node.js 19.8 or later."},"4546":{"id":"/sdk/media-21","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#upload-through-an-action","content":"A `File` from an `<input type=\"file\">` already has a name, so you can pass it as is."},"4547":{"id":"/sdk/media-22","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#upload-through-an-action","content":"To reuse a file that is already in Foundry, pass its handle instead of uploading again:"},"4548":{"id":"/sdk/media-23","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#upload-through-an-action","content":"Uploads are temporary until an action links them to an object. If the action fails, or you never apply one, Foundry deletes the uploaded file after one hour."},"4549":{"id":"/sdk/media-24","page_id":"/sdk/media","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/media#upload-through-an-action","content":"Functions accept the same values for attachment and media reference parameters. See Functions."},"4550":{"id":"/sdk/objects","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"page","content":"Load objects","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK","Read data"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects"},"4551":{"id":"/sdk/objects-0","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects","content":"Load one object by primary key, page through object sets, iterate over every object, select properties, sort, and read the Osdk.Instance shape."},"4552":{"id":"/sdk/objects-1","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#load-one-object","content":"Load one object"},"4553":{"id":"/sdk/objects-2","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#without-exceptions","content":"Without exceptions"},"4554":{"id":"/sdk/objects-3","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"Load a page"},"4555":{"id":"/sdk/objects-4","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#page-through-results","content":"Page through results"},"4556":{"id":"/sdk/objects-5","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#load-every-object","content":"Load every object"},"4557":{"id":"/sdk/objects-6","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#paging-and-consistency","content":"Paging and consistency"},"4558":{"id":"/sdk/objects-7","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#select-properties","content":"Select properties"},"4559":{"id":"/sdk/objects-8","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#sort","content":"Sort"},"4560":{"id":"/sdk/objects-9","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"The object shape"},"4561":{"id":"/sdk/objects-10","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#copy-with-changes","content":"Copy with changes"},"4562":{"id":"/sdk/objects-11","page_id":"/sdk/objects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/objects#type-objects-in-your-code","content":"Type objects in your code"},"4563":{"id":"/sdk/objects-12","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects","content":"An object set from `client(Employee)` loads objects in three ways: one object by primary key, one page at a time, or every object with an async iterator. This page covers each method, its options, and the shape of the objects it returns."},"4564":{"id":"/sdk/objects-13","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects","content":"The samples import a client from `./client`. See Create a client to set one up."},"4565":{"id":"/sdk/objects-14","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-one-object","content":"`fetchOne` takes a primary key and resolves to the object:"},"4566":{"id":"/sdk/objects-15","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-one-object","content":"| Option    | Type             | Default                        | Description                                             |\n| --------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$select` | `PropertyKeys[]` | The API's default property set | Properties to load. The primary key is always returned. |","table":"table-0"},"4567":{"id":"/sdk/objects-16","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-one-object","content":"| Option        | Type      | Default | Description                         |\n| ------------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `$includeRid` | `boolean` | `false` | Adds `$rid` to the returned object. |","table":"table-0"},"4568":{"id":"/sdk/objects-17","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-one-object","content":"`fetchOne` rejects when no object has that primary key, or when you cannot see it. The error is a `PalantirApiError` with the message `Expected a single result but got 0 instead` and no `statusCode` or `errorName`."},"4569":{"id":"/sdk/objects-18","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-one-object","content":"`fetchOne` exists only on object types. Interface object sets do not have it; see Interfaces."},"4570":{"id":"/sdk/objects-19","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#without-exceptions","content":"`fetchOneWithErrors` takes the same arguments and resolves to a `Result` instead of rejecting. Narrow it with `isOk`:"},"4571":{"id":"/sdk/objects-20","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#without-exceptions","content":"A `Result` is either `{ value }` or `{ error }`, where `error` is an `Error`. See Errors for the error types."},"4572":{"id":"/sdk/objects-21","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"`fetchPage` resolves to one page of objects:"},"4573":{"id":"/sdk/objects-22","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"| Option    | Type             | Default                        | Description                                |\n| --------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `$select` | `PropertyKeys[]` | The API's default property set | Properties to load. See Select properties. |","table":"table-1"},"4574":{"id":"/sdk/objects-23","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"| Option     | Type                                             | Default   | Description           |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------ | --------- | --------------------- |\n| `$orderBy` | `{ [property]: \"asc\" \\| \"desc\" } \\| \"relevance\"` | Unordered | Sort order. See Sort. |","table":"table-1"},"4575":{"id":"/sdk/objects-24","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"| Option      | Type     | Default        | Description                                                                       |\n| ----------- | -------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$pageSize` | `number` | Server default | Objects in this page. It does not limit the total; continue with `nextPageToken`. |","table":"table-1"},"4576":{"id":"/sdk/objects-25","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"| Option           | Type     | Default | Description                                 |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `$nextPageToken` | `string` |         | The `nextPageToken` from the previous page. |","table":"table-1"},"4577":{"id":"/sdk/objects-26","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"| Option      | Type      | Default | Description                                                                |\n| ----------- | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$snapshot` | `boolean` | `false` | Pages through one consistent view of the data. See Paging and consistency. |","table":"table-1"},"4578":{"id":"/sdk/objects-27","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"| Option        | Type      | Default | Description                 |\n| ------------- | --------- | ------- | --------------------------- |\n| `$includeRid` | `boolean` | `false` | Adds `$rid` to each object. |","table":"table-1"},"4579":{"id":"/sdk/objects-28","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"| Option                            | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                     |\n| --------------------------------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$includeAllBaseObjectProperties` | `boolean` | `false` | Interface object sets only. Loads every property of the underlying object type. See Interfaces. |","table":"table-1"},"4580":{"id":"/sdk/objects-29","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"The page has three fields:"},"4581":{"id":"/sdk/objects-30","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"| Field  | Type              | Description               |\n| ------ | ----------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `data` | `Osdk.Instance[]` | The objects in this page. |","table":"table-2"},"4582":{"id":"/sdk/objects-31","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"| Field           | Type                  | Description                                                                   |\n| --------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `nextPageToken` | `string \\| undefined` | Pass as `$nextPageToken` to load the next page. `undefined` on the last page. |","table":"table-2"},"4583":{"id":"/sdk/objects-32","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"| Field        | Type     | Description                                    |\n| ------------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `totalCount` | `string` | The number of objects in the set, as a string. |","table":"table-2"},"4584":{"id":"/sdk/objects-33","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-a-page","content":"`fetchPageWithErrors` takes the same options and resolves to a `Result` of the page instead of rejecting."},"4585":{"id":"/sdk/objects-34","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#page-through-results","content":"Pass each page's `nextPageToken` into the next request until it is `undefined`:"},"4586":{"id":"/sdk/objects-35","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#page-through-results","content":"Keep the other options the same on every page. Only `$nextPageToken` changes."},"4587":{"id":"/sdk/objects-36","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-every-object","content":"`asyncIter` loads page after page until it has every object in the set, and yields them one at a time:"},"4588":{"id":"/sdk/objects-37","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-every-object","content":"`asyncIter` accepts `$select`, `$orderBy`, `$includeRid`, and `$includeAllBaseObjectProperties`. It requests pages of 10,000 objects and always requests a snapshot."},"4589":{"id":"/sdk/objects-38","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-every-object","content":"Before you iterate over a large object type:"},"4590":{"id":"/sdk/objects-39","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-every-object","content":"Pass `$select` with only the properties you read. Loading unused properties costs bandwidth and server time, and reading fewer properties afterwards does not undo it."},"4591":{"id":"/sdk/objects-40","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-every-object","content":"Handle each object as it arrives. Collecting every object into an array makes memory grow with the size of the set."},"4592":{"id":"/sdk/objects-41","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-every-object","content":"For counts, sums, and group-bys, use `aggregate`. It runs on the server and loads no objects."},"4593":{"id":"/sdk/objects-42","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#load-every-object","content":"For a sample or the first N objects, use `fetchPage` with `$pageSize`."},"4594":{"id":"/sdk/objects-43","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#paging-and-consistency","content":"| Method                     | Loads                                    | Snapshot                                           |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fetchPage({ $pageSize })` | One page. Continue with `nextPageToken`. | Only with `$snapshot: true`, passed on every page. |","table":"table-3"},"4595":{"id":"/sdk/objects-44","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#paging-and-consistency","content":"| Method        | Loads                                   | Snapshot |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| `asyncIter()` | Every matching object, page after page. | Always.  |","table":"table-3"},"4596":{"id":"/sdk/objects-45","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#paging-and-consistency","content":"| Method               | Loads                          | Snapshot        |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------ | --------------- |\n| `aggregate({ ... })` | Counts, sums, and groups only. | Not applicable. |","table":"table-3"},"4597":{"id":"/sdk/objects-46","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#paging-and-consistency","content":"Without a snapshot, later pages can repeat or skip objects if objects are added, removed, or edited between requests. A snapshot configured for a function run still applies, whatever you pass."},"4598":{"id":"/sdk/objects-47","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#paging-and-consistency","content":"With a snapshot, every page of a non-stream-backed object type reflects the same point in time, so a completed traversal returns each object exactly once. Paging fails if the snapshot expires or the server detects a paging inconsistency (`PagingInconsistencyDetected`). Stream-backed object types do not keep a snapshot across pages: changes during a traversal can make it fail, and exactly-once traversal is not guaranteed."},"4599":{"id":"/sdk/objects-48","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#paging-and-consistency","content":"If an `asyncIter` traversal of a frequently updated object type fails:"},"4600":{"id":"/sdk/objects-49","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#paging-and-consistency","content":"Aggregate instead, if you only need a summary."},"4601":{"id":"/sdk/objects-50","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#paging-and-consistency","content":"Select fewer properties and filter the set so the traversal finishes sooner."},"4602":{"id":"/sdk/objects-51","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#paging-and-consistency","content":"Loop over `fetchPage` without a snapshot and de-duplicate by `$primaryKey`. De-duplication removes repeated objects but cannot recover skipped ones."},"4603":{"id":"/sdk/objects-52","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#select-properties","content":"Without `$select`, the server returns its default property set for the object type. Vector properties, for example, are not in it. With `$select`, the result type narrows to the properties you asked for, so reading anything else is a type error:"},"4604":{"id":"/sdk/objects-53","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#select-properties","content":"Rules for `$select`:"},"4605":{"id":"/sdk/objects-54","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#select-properties","content":"The primary key is always returned, as a property and as `$primaryKey`."},"4606":{"id":"/sdk/objects-55","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#select-properties","content":"Ontology-defined derived properties are not returned by default. Name them in `$select`."},"4607":{"id":"/sdk/objects-56","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#select-properties","content":"Derived properties you add with `withProperties` are returned when `$select` is omitted. If you pass `$select`, name them in it too."},"4608":{"id":"/sdk/objects-57","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#sort","content":"`$orderBy` maps property names to `\"asc\"` or `\"desc\"`. With several keys, the first key sorts first and later keys break ties:"},"4609":{"id":"/sdk/objects-58","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#sort","content":"When you pass `$select`, every `$orderBy` key must also be in `$select`. Otherwise the call does not typecheck."},"4610":{"id":"/sdk/objects-59","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#sort","content":"`$orderBy: \"relevance\"` sorts by how well each object matches the text filters in your `where` clause, and adds a numeric `$score` to each object:"},"4611":{"id":"/sdk/objects-60","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"Each object is an `Osdk.Instance`: its properties plus a few `$` fields. Objects are frozen, so assigning to a property throws in strict mode."},"4612":{"id":"/sdk/objects-61","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Field         | Type                 | Description                                |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `$primaryKey` | The primary key type | The object's primary key, such as `12345`. |","table":"table-4"},"4613":{"id":"/sdk/objects-62","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Field      | Type     | Description                                                                                    |\n| ---------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$apiName` | `string` | The API name of the type you queried: the object type, or the interface for interface queries. |","table":"table-4"},"4614":{"id":"/sdk/objects-63","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Field         | Type     | Description                                                                                      |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `$objectType` | `string` | The API name of the object's concrete object type. Differs from `$apiName` on interface objects. |","table":"table-4"},"4615":{"id":"/sdk/objects-64","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Field    | Type                  | Description                                    |\n| -------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `$title` | `string \\| undefined` | The value of the object type's title property. |","table":"table-4"},"4616":{"id":"/sdk/objects-65","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Field  | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$rid` | `string` | The object's RID. Present only when you pass `$includeRid: true`. |","table":"table-4"},"4617":{"id":"/sdk/objects-66","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Field              | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$objectSpecifier` | `string` | A string that identifies the object across types. |","table":"table-4"},"4618":{"id":"/sdk/objects-67","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Field   | Type     | Description                              |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `$link` | `object` | Accessors for linked objects. See Links. |","table":"table-4"},"4619":{"id":"/sdk/objects-68","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Field | Type                      | Description                                                                                                |\n| ----- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$as` | `(type) => Osdk.Instance` | Views the object as an interface it implements, or an interface object as its object type. See Interfaces. |","table":"table-4"},"4620":{"id":"/sdk/objects-69","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Field    | Type                          | Description                                                    |\n| -------- | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `$clone` | `(changes?) => Osdk.Instance` | Returns a copy, optionally with some property values replaced. |","table":"table-4"},"4621":{"id":"/sdk/objects-70","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"Nullable properties are typed `T | undefined`. Property values use these TypeScript types:"},"4622":{"id":"/sdk/objects-71","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Property type | TypeScript type |\n| ------------- | --------------- |\n| `string`      | `string`        |","table":"table-5"},"4623":{"id":"/sdk/objects-72","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Property type                                 | TypeScript type |\n| --------------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `integer`, `short`, `byte`, `float`, `double` | `number`        |","table":"table-5"},"4624":{"id":"/sdk/objects-73","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Property type     | TypeScript type |\n| ----------------- | --------------- |\n| `long`, `decimal` | `string`        |","table":"table-5"},"4625":{"id":"/sdk/objects-74","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Property type | TypeScript type |\n| ------------- | --------------- |\n| `boolean`     | `boolean`       |","table":"table-5"},"4626":{"id":"/sdk/objects-75","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Property type       | TypeScript type              |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `date`, `timestamp` | `string`, in ISO 8601 format |","table":"table-5"},"4627":{"id":"/sdk/objects-76","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Property type    | TypeScript type |\n| ---------------- | --------------- |\n| Array properties | `T[]`           |","table":"table-5"},"4628":{"id":"/sdk/objects-77","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Property type | TypeScript type |\n| ------------- | --------------- |\n| `geopoint`    | GeoJSON `Point` |","table":"table-5"},"4629":{"id":"/sdk/objects-78","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Property type | TypeScript type  |\n| ------------- | ---------------- |\n| `geoshape`    | GeoJSON geometry |","table":"table-5"},"4630":{"id":"/sdk/objects-79","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Property type | TypeScript type                          |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `attachment`  | `Attachment`. See Attachments and media. |","table":"table-5"},"4631":{"id":"/sdk/objects-80","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#the-object-shape","content":"| Property type    | TypeScript type                     |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `mediaReference` | `Media`. See Attachments and media. |","table":"table-5"},"4632":{"id":"/sdk/objects-81","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#copy-with-changes","content":"`$clone` builds a new local object. It does not write to Foundry; use an action for that. It throws if the changes include a different primary key:"},"4633":{"id":"/sdk/objects-82","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#type-objects-in-your-code","content":"Use `Osdk.Instance<Employee>` from `@osdk/client`, or the generated alias `Employee.OsdkInstance`. Narrow the properties with the third type argument, and add `\"$rid\"` as the second to include the RID:"},"4634":{"id":"/sdk/objects-83","page_id":"/sdk/objects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/objects#type-objects-in-your-code","content":"A function that takes `Osdk.Instance<Employee, never, \"fullName\">` accepts any `Employee` loaded with at least `fullName`."},"4635":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","type":"page","content":"Subscriptions","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","TypeScript SDK","More"],"tags":[],"url":"/sdk/subscriptions"},"4636":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-0","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions","content":"Receive live updates when objects in an object set are added, changed, or removed, with subscribe, its four callbacks, and unsubscribe."},"4637":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-1","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/subscriptions#callbacks","content":"Callbacks"},"4638":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-2","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/subscriptions#options","content":"Options"},"4639":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-3","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/subscriptions#updates","content":"Updates"},"4640":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-4","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/subscriptions#keep-a-local-copy-current","content":"Keep a local copy current"},"4641":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-5","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/subscriptions#connection","content":"Connection"},"4642":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-6","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/sdk/subscriptions#in-react","content":"In React"},"4643":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-7","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions","content":"`subscribe` opens a live connection to an object set. The server pushes each change to an object in the set, so you can keep a local copy current without polling."},"4644":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-8","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions","content":"`subscribe` works on any object set, including filtered sets, pivots, and interfaces. It returns immediately with `{ unsubscribe }`; the connection opens in the background."},"4645":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-9","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#callbacks","content":"All callbacks are optional."},"4646":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-10","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#callbacks","content":"| Callback                     | Called when                                                                  |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSuccessfulSubscription()` | The server accepted the subscription. Changes from here on reach `onChange`. |","table":"table-0"},"4647":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-11","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#callbacks","content":"| Callback           | Called when                                |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `onChange(update)` | An object in the set changed. See Updates. |","table":"table-0"},"4648":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-12","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#callbacks","content":"| Callback        | Called when                                                                                                                 |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onOutOfDate()` | The client cannot account for every change, for example after the connection dropped and reconnected. Reload the whole set. |","table":"table-0"},"4649":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-13","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#callbacks","content":"| Callback                                 | Called when                                                                                                                    |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onError({ subscriptionClosed, error })` | Something failed. When `subscriptionClosed` is `true`, no more updates arrive. When it is `false`, the subscription continues. |","table":"table-0"},"4650":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-14","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#callbacks","content":"An exception thrown inside `onChange` or another callback does not stop the subscription. The client reports it to `onError` with `subscriptionClosed: false`. If `onError` itself throws, the client closes the subscription."},"4651":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-15","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#options","content":"| Option       | Type             | Default                    | Description                                                   |\n| ------------ | ---------------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `properties` | `PropertyKeys[]` | Every property of the type | The properties to receive. `update.object` is typed to these. |","table":"table-1"},"4652":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-16","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#options","content":"| Option       | Type      | Default | Description                                                                                                       |\n| ------------ | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `includeRid` | `boolean` | `false` | Adds `$rid` to each updated object. Not available when `properties` includes a geotime series reference property. |","table":"table-1"},"4653":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-17","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#options","content":"Request only the properties you display. Without `properties`, each update can carry every property of the type."},"4654":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-18","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#updates","content":"`onChange` receives `{ object, state }`:"},"4655":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-19","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#updates","content":"| `state`              | Meaning                                                                                                                           |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"ADDED_OR_UPDATED\"` | The object was created, was edited, or now matches the set's filter. `object` has the latest values of the subscribed properties. |","table":"table-2"},"4656":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-20","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#updates","content":"| `state`     | Meaning                                                                            |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"REMOVED\"` | The object was deleted, or no longer matches the filter. Drop it by `$primaryKey`. |","table":"table-2"},"4657":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-21","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#updates","content":"Updates to a geotime series reference property arrive as separate updates that carry only the primary key and that property. Merge each update into your copy of the object rather than replacing it, so a property missing from an update keeps its last value."},"4658":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-22","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#keep-a-local-copy-current","content":"Load the set once the subscription is live, apply each change, and reload on `onOutOfDate`:"},"4659":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-23","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#keep-a-local-copy-current","content":"Loading after `onSuccessfulSubscription`, not before, means a change made while the first load runs still reaches `onChange`."},"4660":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-24","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#connection","content":"All subscriptions from one client share a single WebSocket. When the connection drops, the client reconnects with exponential backoff, resubscribes, and calls `onOutOfDate` on each subscription it restored. In Node.js, the client uses the `ws` package, so no polyfill is needed."},"4661":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-25","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#connection","content":"Call `unsubscribe` when you no longer need updates, such as when a component unmounts or a request handler finishes. An open subscription keeps the connection open."},"4662":{"id":"/sdk/subscriptions-26","page_id":"/sdk/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdk/subscriptions#in-react","content":"`useOsdkObjects` and `useObjectSet` accept `streamUpdates: true`, which subscribes for you and writes each change into the shared cache. See Objects in React."},"4663":{"id":"/components/action-form","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"page","content":"ActionForm","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Components","Data"],"tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form"},"4664":{"id":"/components/action-form-0","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form","content":"ActionForm renders form fields from an OSDK action definition, validates input in the browser, and applies the action on submit."},"4665":{"id":"/components/action-form-1","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#import","content":"Import"},"4666":{"id":"/components/action-form-2","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#basic-usage","content":"Basic Usage"},"4667":{"id":"/components/action-form-3","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"Props Reference"},"4668":{"id":"/components/action-form-4","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#choosing-actionform-vs-baseform","content":"Choosing ActionForm vs BaseForm"},"4669":{"id":"/components/action-form-5","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"Default Field Rendering"},"4670":{"id":"/components/action-form-6","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#unsupported-features","content":"Unsupported Features"},"4671":{"id":"/components/action-form-7","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#custom-field-definitions","content":"Custom Field Definitions"},"4672":{"id":"/components/action-form-8","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#sections","content":"Sections"},"4673":{"id":"/components/action-form-9","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#rich-dropdown-labels","content":"Rich dropdown labels"},"4674":{"id":"/components/action-form-10","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#scoped-object-select-fields","content":"Scoped object select fields"},"4675":{"id":"/components/action-form-11","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#behavior-notes","content":"Behavior Notes"},"4676":{"id":"/components/action-form-12","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#examples","content":"Examples"},"4677":{"id":"/components/action-form-13","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#controlled-form-state","content":"Controlled form state"},"4678":{"id":"/components/action-form-14","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#custom-submit-handling","content":"Custom submit handling"},"4679":{"id":"/components/action-form-15","page_id":"/components/action-form","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/action-form#styling","content":"Styling"},"4680":{"id":"/components/action-form-16","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#basic-usage","content":"[!NOTE]\n`@my-app/sdk` is a placeholder for your generated SDK package. `./client` (used in scoped object-select examples below) is the file in your app where you exported the OSDK client returned by `createClient(...)`. Replace both with the actual paths in your project."},"4681":{"id":"/components/action-form-17","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#basic-usage","content":"`ActionForm` fetches action metadata, renders fields for the action parameters, runs client-side validation, and calls the OSDK action when the user submits. The form title is hidden by default. Pass `showFormTitle={true}` to show it; the title uses `formTitle` when provided, otherwise the action display name, otherwise the action API name."},"4682":{"id":"/components/action-form-18","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"`ActionForm` is a discriminated union: provide both `formState` and `onFormStateChange` for controlled mode, or omit both for uncontrolled mode."},"4683":{"id":"/components/action-form-19","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"Type parameters: `Q extends ActionDefinition<unknown>`"},"4684":{"id":"/components/action-form-20","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                              |\n| ----------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `formTitle` | `string` | Title shown in the form header. Omit to hide the header. |","table":"table-0"},"4685":{"id":"/components/action-form-21","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name               | Type      | Description                                             |\n| ------------------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `isSubmitDisabled` | `boolean` | Whether the submit button is disabled. Default `false`. |","table":"table-0"},"4686":{"id":"/components/action-form-22","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name               | Type | Description                                                                                            |\n| ------------------ | ---- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `actionDefinition` | `Q`  | **Required.** The OSDK action definition. Its parameters drive the rendered fields and the submission. |","table":"table-0"},"4687":{"id":"/components/action-form-23","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name            | Type      | Description                                          |\n| --------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `showFormTitle` | `boolean` | Whether to show the form title. Defaults to `false`. |","table":"table-0"},"4688":{"id":"/components/action-form-24","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name       | Type                                                                                                                                        | Description                                                                                                     |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSubmit` | `(formState: FormState<Q>, applyAction: (formState: FormState<Q>) => Promise<ActionEditResponse \\| undefined>) => Promise<unknown> \\| void` | If supplied, this will override the default submit action. By default, the action's applyAction will be called. |","table":"table-0"},"4689":{"id":"/components/action-form-25","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name                   | Type                                          | Description                                                                    |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onValidationResponse` | `(results: ActionValidationResponse) => void` | Called when the validation response is returned from a validateOnly submission |","table":"table-0"},"4690":{"id":"/components/action-form-26","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name        | Type                                                 | Description                                                                        |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSuccess` | `(results: ActionEditResponse \\| undefined) => void` | Called when the action is successfully executed from a non-validateOnly submission |","table":"table-0"},"4691":{"id":"/components/action-form-27","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name      | Type                         | Description                                                         |\n| --------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onError` | `(error: FormError) => void` | Called when action metadata fails to load or form submission fails. |","table":"table-0"},"4692":{"id":"/components/action-form-28","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name                   | Type                                    | Description                            |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `formFieldDefinitions` | `ReadonlyArray<FormFieldDefinition<Q>>` | Custom flat list of field definitions. |","table":"table-0"},"4693":{"id":"/components/action-form-29","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name                     | Type                                      | Description                                                      |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `formContentDefinitions` | `ReadonlyArray<ActionFormContentItem<Q>>` | Ordered list of fields and sections that define the form layout. |","table":"table-0"},"4694":{"id":"/components/action-form-30","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name        | Type           | Description                                                         |\n| ----------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `formState` | `FormState<Q>` | The current form values. If provided, the form state is controlled. |","table":"table-0"},"4695":{"id":"/components/action-form-31","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#props-reference","content":"| Name                | Type                                                           | Description                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onFormStateChange` | `(updater: (prevState: FormState<Q>) => FormState<Q>) => void` | Called when a field value changes, with a state updater. Required when the form state is controlled; also fires in uncontrolled mode so callers can observe changes. |","table":"table-0"},"4696":{"id":"/components/action-form-32","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#choosing-actionform-vs-baseform","content":"| Use case                                                                 | Use this API |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------ |\n| Render a form directly from an OSDK action and submit with `applyAction` | `ActionForm` |","table":"table-1"},"4697":{"id":"/components/action-form-33","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#choosing-actionform-vs-baseform","content":"| Use case                                     | Use this API                             |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| Override generated fields for an OSDK action | `ActionForm` with `formFieldDefinitions` |","table":"table-1"},"4698":{"id":"/components/action-form-34","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#choosing-actionform-vs-baseform","content":"| Use case                                              | Use this API |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| Build a form from manually-authored field definitions | `BaseForm`   |","table":"table-1"},"4699":{"id":"/components/action-form-35","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#choosing-actionform-vs-baseform","content":"| Use case                                                                | Use this API                               |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| Group an OSDK action's fields into sections, or order standalone fields | `ActionForm` with `formContentDefinitions` |","table":"table-1"},"4700":{"id":"/components/action-form-36","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#choosing-actionform-vs-baseform","content":"| Use case                                          | Use this API |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| Build a custom form layout without an OSDK action | `BaseForm`   |","table":"table-1"},"4701":{"id":"/components/action-form-37","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"When `formFieldDefinitions` is omitted, `ActionForm` derives one field per action parameter from action metadata."},"4702":{"id":"/components/action-form-38","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"| Action parameter type | Default field component | Default behavior       |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `string`              | `TEXT_INPUT`            | Single-line text input |","table":"table-2"},"4703":{"id":"/components/action-form-39","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"| Action parameter type | Default field component | Default behavior         |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `boolean`             | `RADIO_BUTTONS`         | True/False radio options |","table":"table-2"},"4704":{"id":"/components/action-form-40","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"| Action parameter type       | Default field component | Default behavior |\n| --------------------------- | ----------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `integer`, `double`, `long` | `NUMBER_INPUT`          | Numeric input    |","table":"table-2"},"4705":{"id":"/components/action-form-41","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"| Action parameter type   | Default field component | Default behavior |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `datetime`, `timestamp` | `DATETIME_PICKER`       | Date picker      |","table":"table-2"},"4706":{"id":"/components/action-form-42","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"| Action parameter type          | Default field component | Default behavior |\n| ------------------------------ | ----------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `attachment`, `mediaReference` | `FILE_PICKER`           | File picker      |","table":"table-2"},"4707":{"id":"/components/action-form-43","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"| Action parameter type | Default field component | Default behavior                               |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"object\" }`  | `OBJECT_SELECT`         | Object selector for the referenced object type |","table":"table-2"},"4708":{"id":"/components/action-form-44","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"| Action parameter type   | Default field component | Default behavior             |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `{ type: \"objectSet\" }` | `OBJECT_SET`            | Read-only object set summary |","table":"table-2"},"4709":{"id":"/components/action-form-45","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"| Action parameter type                          | Default field component | Default behavior                           |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `marking`, `geohash`, `geoshape`, `objectType` | `UNSUPPORTED`           | Disabled field recommending a custom field |","table":"table-2"},"4710":{"id":"/components/action-form-46","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"| Action parameter type                         | Default field component | Default behavior                           |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `{ type: \"interface\" }`, `{ type: \"struct\" }` | `UNSUPPORTED`           | Disabled field recommending a custom field |","table":"table-2"},"4711":{"id":"/components/action-form-47","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#default-field-rendering","content":"Required validation is inferred from the action parameter's nullability. Additional client-side validation comes from field-specific props such as `min`, `max`, `minLength`, `maxLength`, and `maxSize`."},"4712":{"id":"/components/action-form-48","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#unsupported-features","content":"`ActionForm` is a lightweight OSDK component and does not yet match the full ActionForm in Foundry. The table below lists the main gaps to account for when adopting it."},"4713":{"id":"/components/action-form-49","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#unsupported-features","content":"| Feature                   | Current behavior                                                                                                                                        | Workaround                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Backend action validation | The form does not call backend validation before submit and does not process validation-derived displays, allowed values, defaults, or section results. | Use `formFieldDefinitions` validation props, field-level `validate`, `onSubmit`, and `onError` for app-owned checks and submission error handling. |","table":"table-3"},"4714":{"id":"/components/action-form-50","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#unsupported-features","content":"| Feature                               | Current behavior                                                                                                            | Workaround                                                                                                           |\n| ------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Unsupported generated parameter types | `marking`, `geohash`, `geoshape`, `objectType`, `interface`, and `struct` render as disabled unsupported fields by default. | Override those parameters with `fieldComponent: \"CUSTOM\"` or another compatible component in `formFieldDefinitions`. |","table":"table-3"},"4715":{"id":"/components/action-form-51","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#unsupported-features","content":"| Feature                         | Current behavior                                                                                                                                                                                              | Workaround                                                                                               |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Action-authored layout metadata | Action-defined sections, form content ordering, section validation, and layout toggles are not read from metadata. Fields render in metadata parameter order unless fully replaced by `formFieldDefinitions`. | Group fields with `formContentDefinitions` sections, or control field order with `formFieldDefinitions`. |","table":"table-3"},"4716":{"id":"/components/action-form-52","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#unsupported-features","content":"| Feature                                     | Current behavior                                                                                                 | Workaround                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Conditional logic and dynamic display state | Backend-driven hidden, disabled, required, and allowed-value rules are not evaluated as the user edits the form. | Encode static display state in field definitions, or manage dynamic state in your app and pass updated `formFieldDefinitions` / controlled `formState`. |","table":"table-3"},"4717":{"id":"/components/action-form-53","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#unsupported-features","content":"| Feature               | Current behavior                                                                                                                        | Workaround                                                                                                                  |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Defaults and prefills | Backend prefills, type-class defaults, current timestamp defaults, and validation-derived default values are not applied automatically. | Provide `defaultValue` in field definitions, seed controlled `formState`, or compute defaults in app code before rendering. |","table":"table-3"},"4718":{"id":"/components/action-form-54","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#custom-field-definitions","content":"Use `formFieldDefinitions` when the default rendering for a parameter is not the UI you want. The list is a complete replacement: include every parameter that should appear in the form."},"4719":{"id":"/components/action-form-55","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#sections","content":"Use `formContentDefinitions` instead of `formFieldDefinitions` to group fields into sections. Each item is either `{ type: \"field\", definition }` or `{ type: \"section\", key, definition }`, and items render in array order. Like `formFieldDefinitions`, the list replaces the generated fields."},"4720":{"id":"/components/action-form-56","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#sections","content":"| Section option | Default | Description      |\n| -------------- | ------- | ---------------- |\n| `title`        |         | Section heading. |","table":"table-4"},"4721":{"id":"/components/action-form-57","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#sections","content":"| Section option | Default | Description             |\n| -------------- | ------- | ----------------------- |\n| `description`  |         | Text under the heading. |","table":"table-4"},"4722":{"id":"/components/action-form-58","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#sections","content":"| Section option | Default | Description                |\n| -------------- | ------- | -------------------------- |\n| `fields`       |         | The fields in the section. |","table":"table-4"},"4723":{"id":"/components/action-form-59","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#sections","content":"| Section option       | Default | Description       |\n| -------------------- | ------- | ----------------- |\n| `collapsedByDefault` | `false` | Starts collapsed. |","table":"table-4"},"4724":{"id":"/components/action-form-60","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#sections","content":"| Section option | Default | Description          |\n| -------------- | ------- | -------------------- |\n| `showTitleBar` | `true`  | Shows the title bar. |","table":"table-4"},"4725":{"id":"/components/action-form-61","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#sections","content":"| Section option | Default | Description         |\n| -------------- | ------- | ------------------- |\n| `columnCount`  | `1`     | `1` or `2` columns. |","table":"table-4"},"4726":{"id":"/components/action-form-62","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#sections","content":"| Section option | Default | Description                                                    |\n| -------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `style`        | `\"box\"` | `\"box\"` renders a bordered card, `\"minimal\"` only the heading. |","table":"table-4"},"4727":{"id":"/components/action-form-63","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#rich-dropdown-labels","content":"Use `itemToStringLabel` for the dropdown's text behavior: search matching, accessibility labels, fallback item keys, and default visual text. Add `renderItemLabel` when the visible label needs richer React content while preserving the same string behavior."},"4728":{"id":"/components/action-form-64","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#scoped-object-select-fields","content":"`OBJECT_SELECT` can load options from either an object type or a pre-scoped object set. Pass `objectType` for an unfiltered selector, or pass `objectSet` to limit selectable options. The two are mutually exclusive. Search text is applied within the object set, and the current value is not automatically cleared when it is outside that set."},"4729":{"id":"/components/action-form-65","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#scoped-object-select-fields","content":"For a completely custom field, use `fieldComponent: \"CUSTOM\"` and provide `customRenderer`:"},"4730":{"id":"/components/action-form-66","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#behavior-notes","content":"`formFieldDefinitions` replaces generated fields. Passing one custom field means only that field renders."},"4731":{"id":"/components/action-form-67","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#behavior-notes","content":"Pass `formFieldDefinitions` or `formContentDefinitions`, not both."},"4732":{"id":"/components/action-form-68","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#behavior-notes","content":"`fieldKey` must match the action parameter key; submitted form state uses the same keys."},"4733":{"id":"/components/action-form-69","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#behavior-notes","content":"`fieldComponentProps` should not include `value`, `onChange`, or `id`; form state wiring provides those."},"4734":{"id":"/components/action-form-70","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#behavior-notes","content":"Controlled mode requires both `formState` and `onFormStateChange`."},"4735":{"id":"/components/action-form-71","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#behavior-notes","content":"Use `onSubmit` for custom submission behavior. If `onSubmit` is omitted, `ActionForm` calls `applyAction` and then `onSuccess`."},"4736":{"id":"/components/action-form-72","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#styling","content":"`ActionForm` is built on `BaseForm`, so the form layout and field styling use the same CSS variables documented in CSSVariables.md."},"4737":{"id":"/components/action-form-73","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#styling","content":"`ActionForm` does not add outer padding by default. Apply internal spacing by setting the form padding variables on the form or a wrapper element:"},"4738":{"id":"/components/action-form-74","page_id":"/components/action-form","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/action-form#styling","content":"Use `--osdk-form-content-padding-inline` to apply shared horizontal padding to the header, fields, and footer. Use `--osdk-form-content-padding-block` to control vertical padding for the form fields section. For card-style outer spacing, apply margin, border, background, and border radius to the wrapper rather than the form itself."},"4739":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"page","content":"AipAgentChat","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Components","Experimental"],"tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat"},"4740":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-0","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat","content":"AipAgentChat renders an AI chat interface backed by a Foundry language model through useChat from @osdk/react/experimental/aip."},"4741":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-1","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#import","content":"Import"},"4742":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-2","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#basic-usage","content":"Basic Usage"},"4743":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-3","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#minimal-example","content":"Minimal Example"},"4744":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-4","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#pinned-model","content":"Pinned model"},"4745":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-5","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#with-model-picker-controlled","content":"With model picker (controlled)"},"4746":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-6","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#with-model-picker-uncontrolled","content":"With model picker (uncontrolled)"},"4747":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-7","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#custom-render","content":"Custom render"},"4748":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-8","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#drop-down-to-baseaipagentchat","content":"Drop down to BaseAipAgentChat"},"4749":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-9","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#drop-further-usechat-directly","content":"Drop further: useChat directly"},"4750":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-10","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#props-reference","content":"Props Reference"},"4751":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-11","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#theming","content":"Theming"},"4752":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-12","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat","content":"Importing the component is sufficient. You do not need to import `useChat` or\n`foundryModel` yourself."},"4753":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-13","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#import","content":"**`AipAgentChat`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts a\nFoundry `PlatformClient` and an LMS model API name; constructs the\nlanguage-model handle, drives `useChat`, and renders the chat UI."},"4754":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-14","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#import","content":"**`BaseAipAgentChat`** — Lower-level OSDK-agnostic component that\naccepts `messages`, `status`, and `onSendMessage` directly. Use this\nwhen you already manage chat state yourself (a custom hook, a\nnon-OSDK backend, etc.)."},"4755":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-15","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#minimal-example","content":"The simplest way to use `AipAgentChat` is with just a platform client;\n`model` and `defaultModel` are both optional and fall back to `\"gpt-4o\"`:"},"4756":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-16","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#with-model-picker-uncontrolled","content":"The component manages model state internally; `onModelChange` is a\nnon-controlling listener (analytics, persistence, etc.)."},"4757":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-17","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#drop-down-to-baseaipagentchat","content":"`BaseAipAgentChat` is OSDK-agnostic — the consumer drives the chat by\npassing the current `messages`, `status`, `error`, and an `onSendMessage`\ncallback that resolves once the user's message has been forwarded.\nUse it for non-OSDK backends, custom transports, or unit tests."},"4758":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-18","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#drop-further-usechat-directly","content":"For full control over the chat hook (regenerate, custom transports), call\n`useChat` from `@osdk/react/experimental/aip` yourself and feed the result\ninto your own UI. `useChat` is text-only: it does not run tools or multi-step\nagent loops."},"4759":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-19","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#props-reference","content":"See `AipAgentChatApi.ts` for\nthe full prop list with JSDoc. `client` is the only required prop.\n`model` (controlled) and `defaultModel` (uncontrolled) are both\noptional; if neither is supplied the chat falls back to the first\nentry of `availableModels` (when provided), or to `\"gpt-4o\"`. Notable\noptional props:"},"4760":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-20","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#props-reference","content":"`availableModels` + `onModelChange` — render a model picker in the\ncomposer footer."},"4761":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-21","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#props-reference","content":"`system` — system prompt prepended to every request."},"4762":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-22","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#props-reference","content":"`initialMessages` — seed conversation snapshot."},"4763":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-23","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#props-reference","content":"`enableAutoScroll` (default `true`) — auto-pin to the bottom of the\nmessage list as new tokens arrive."},"4764":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-24","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#props-reference","content":"`renderEmptyState` / `renderMessage` — render overrides."},"4765":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-25","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#props-reference","content":"`onError`, `onFinish` — listeners forwarded to `useChat`."},"4766":{"id":"/components/aip-agent-chat-26","page_id":"/components/aip-agent-chat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/aip-agent-chat#theming","content":"CSS variables are documented in\n`docs/CSSVariables.md` under **AIP\nAgent Chat**. The `--osdk-aip-agent-chat-*` namespace covers the\ncontainer, spacing, message bubbles, composer, empty state, and the\n3-dot streaming loader. Defaults live in\n`src/tokens/component-tokens/aip-agent-chat.css`;\ncolor, spacing, and radius tokens derive from `--osdk-*` semantic\ntokens, so brand overrides applied at the `--osdk-*` layer flow through\nautomatically."},"4767":{"id":"/components/css-variables","page_id":"/components/css-variables","type":"page","content":"CSS Variables API Reference","breadcrumbs":["OSDK TypeScript","Components","Theming"],"tags":[],"url":"/components/css-variables"},"4768":{"id":"/components/css-variables-0","page_id":"/components/css-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/css-variables","content":"Reference for the CSS custom properties in @osdk/react-components, from Blueprint token mappings to per-component tokens."},"4769":{"id":"/components/css-variables-1","page_id":"/components/css-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/css-variables#overview","content":"Overview"},"4770":{"id":"/components/css-variables-2","page_id":"/components/css-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/components/css-variables#token-architecture","content":"Token Architecture"},"4771":{"id":"/components/css-variables-3","page_i