eful for `MULTI_SELECT`, which already has its own inline search field. Defaults to `true`. |","table":"table-7"},"6267":{"id":"/components/filter-list-135","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-filter-definition","content":"| Name | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ---- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id` | `string` | Optional unique identifier for stable keying across filter reorders. Set it explicitly when that derived value would collide, e.g. two filters on the same property.<br /><br />This is the key used in `defaultFilterStates`; `getFilterKey(definition)` returns it. Defaults to a value derived from the definition (its `key`, or its link and property names) |","table":"table-7"},"6268":{"id":"/components/filter-list-136","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-filter-definition","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description                                                                                                                |\n| ----------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `isVisible` | `boolean` | Controls whether this filter is rendered. When false, the 