's state on mount, FilterList owns the state from then on Defaults to `undefined (filter starts empty)`. |","table":"table-7"},"6274":{"id":"/components/filter-list-142","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-filter-definition","content":"| Name          | Type    | Description                                      |\n| ------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `filterState` | `State` | **Deprecated** — Rename to `defaultFilterState`. |","table":"table-7"},"6275":{"id":"/components/filter-list-143","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-filter-definition","content":"| Name          | Type                                                             | Description                                                                             |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `renderInput` | `(props: CustomFilterInputRendererProps<Q, State>) => ReactNode` | Render the input portion of the filter Used when rendering within a filter item wrapper |","table":"table-7"},"6276":{"id":"/components/filter-list-144","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-filter-definition","content":"| Name         | Type                                                            | Description                                                                              |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `renderItem` | `(props: CustomFilterItemRendererProps<Q, State>) => ReactNode` | Render the complete filter item Used when you need full control over the item appearance |","table":"table-7"},"6277":{"id":"/components/filter-list-145","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-filter-definition","content":"| Name            | Type                                            | Description                                                                                                        |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `toWhereClause` | `(state: State) => WhereClause<Q> \\| undefined` | **Required.** Convert filter state to a WhereClause for filtering Required for the filter to affect the object set |","table":"table-7"},"6278":{"id":"/components/filter-list-146","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"When using `type: \"STATIC_VALUES\"`, the definition supports:"},"6279":{"id":"/components/filter-list-147","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"Type parameters: `Q extends ObjectTypeDefinition`, `C extends StaticValuesComponentType = StaticValuesComponentType`"},"6280":{"id":"/components/filter-list-148","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name          | Type      | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `searchField` | `boolean` | When `false`, the header monocle (search-values icon) is hidden even for filter components that ordinarily support in-filter search. Useful for `MULTI_SELECT`, which already has its own inline search field. Defaults to `true`. |","table":"table-8"},"6281":{"id":"/components/filter-list-149","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ---- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id` | `string` | Optional unique identifier for stable keying across filter reorders. Set it explicitly when that derived value would collide, e.g. two filters on the same property.<br /><br />This is the key used in `defaultFilterStates`; `getFilterKey(definition)` returns it. Defaults to a value derived from the definition (its `key`, or its link and property names) |","table":"table-8"},"6282":{"id":"/components/filter-list-150","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description                                                                                                                |\n| ----------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `isVisible` | `boolean` | Controls whether this filter is rendered. When false, the filter is hidden but its state is preserved. Defaults to `true`. |","table":"table-8"},"6283":{"id":"/components/filter-list-151","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name   | Type              | Description   |\n| ------ | ----------------- | ------------- |\n| `type` | `\"STATIC_VALUES\"` | **Required.** |","table":"table-8"},"6284":{"id":"/components/filter-list-152","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ----- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `key` | `string` | **Required.** Key used for state management and auto WHERE clause generation. When `toWhereClause` is not provided, this is used as the property key in the generated WHERE clause. |","table":"table-8"},"6285":{"id":"/components/filter-list-153","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                  |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | Display label for the filter |","table":"table-8"},"6286":{"id":"/components/filter-list-154","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name              | Type | Description                                       |\n| ----------------- | ---- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `filterComponent` | `C`  | **Required.** The filter component type to render |","table":"table-8"},"6287":{"id":"/components/filter-list-155","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name                 | Type                            | Description                                                                                                              |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `defaultFilterState` | `FilterStateByComponentType[C]` | Seeds the filter's state on mount, FilterList owns the state from then on Defaults to `undefined (filter starts empty)`. |","table":"table-8"},"6288":{"id":"/components/filter-list-156","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name          | Type                            | Description                                      |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `filterState` | `FilterStateByComponentType[C]` | **Deprecated** — Rename to `defaultFilterState`. |","table":"table-8"},"6289":{"id":"/components/filter-list-157","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name     | Type       | Description                                                                                                                       |\n| -------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `values` | `string[]` | **Required.** The static list of values to display in the filter component. These are rendered directly without OSDK aggregation. |","table":"table-8"},"6290":{"id":"/components/filter-list-158","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name          | Type                           | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `renderValue` | `(value: string) => ReactNode` | Custom display function for filter values. Replaces the default string display in dropdown items, chips, and listogram rows. When the function returns a string, that string is also used for search matching within filter dropdowns. When it returns a non-string `ReactNode`, search falls back to the raw value. |","table":"table-8"},"6291":{"id":"/components/filter-list-159","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ----------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `showCount` | `boolean` | Show aggregation counts next to filter option values. Applies to LISTOGRAM, SINGLE_SELECT, and MULTI_SELECT components. Defaults to `true for LISTOGRAM and MULTI_SELECT, false for SINGLE_SELECT`. |","table":"table-8"},"6292":{"id":"/components/filter-list-160","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name       | Type                     | Description                                                                                      |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `colorMap` | `Record<string, string>` | Maps filter values to colors for visual differentiation. Used by LISTOGRAM (per-row bar colors). |","table":"table-8"},"6293":{"id":"/components/filter-list-161","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name              | Type                                                                          | Description                                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `listogramConfig` | `{ displayMode?: \"full\" \\| \"count\" \\| \"minimal\"; maxVisibleItems?: number; }` | Configuration for LISTOGRAM display mode. Only applies when filterComponent is \"LISTOGRAM\". |","table":"table-8"},"6294":{"id":"/components/filter-list-162","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#static-values-filter-definition","content":"| Name            | Type                                                  | Description                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toWhereClause` | `(state: FilterState) => WhereClause<Q> \\| undefined` | Optional custom WHERE clause generator. When provided, this is used instead of auto-generating a WHERE clause from the `key` and filter state. |","table":"table-8"},"6295":{"id":"/components/filter-list-163","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"When using `type: \"PROPERTY\"` or `type: \"LINKED_PROPERTY\"`, specify a `filterComponent`:"},"6296":{"id":"/components/filter-list-164","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component   | Best For                        | State Type    |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `LISTOGRAM` | Categorical data with bar chart | `EXACT_MATCH` |","table":"table-9"},"6297":{"id":"/components/filter-list-165","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component       | Best For              | State Type |\n| --------------- | --------------------- | ---------- |\n| `SINGLE_SELECT` | Single value dropdown | `SELECT`   |","table":"table-9"},"6298":{"id":"/components/filter-list-166","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component      | Best For                          | State Type |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| `MULTI_SELECT` | Multi-select dropdown with search | `SELECT`   |","table":"table-9"},"6299":{"id":"/components/filter-list-167","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component   | Best For                         | State Type    |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `TEXT_TAGS` | Tag-based input with suggestions | `EXACT_MATCH` |","table":"table-9"},"6300":{"id":"/components/filter-list-168","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component       | Best For                       | State Type      |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------ | --------------- |\n| `CONTAINS_TEXT` | Free-text search on a property | `CONTAINS_TEXT` |","table":"table-9"},"6301":{"id":"/components/filter-list-169","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component      | Best For                         | State Type     |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `NUMBER_RANGE` | Min/max range slider for numbers | `NUMBER_RANGE` |","table":"table-9"},"6302":{"id":"/components/filter-list-170","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component    | Best For          | State Type   |\n| ------------ | ----------------- | ------------ |\n| `DATE_RANGE` | Date range picker | `DATE_RANGE` |","table":"table-9"},"6303":{"id":"/components/filter-list-171","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component | Best For              | State Type |\n| --------- | --------------------- | ---------- |\n| `TOGGLE`  | Boolean on/off toggle | `TOGGLE`   |","table":"table-9"},"6304":{"id":"/components/filter-list-172","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component     | Best For           | State Type |\n| ------------- | ------------------ | ---------- |\n| `SINGLE_DATE` | Single date picker | `SELECT`   |","table":"table-9"},"6305":{"id":"/components/filter-list-173","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component    | Best For             | State Type |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ---------- |\n| `MULTI_DATE` | Multiple date picker | `SELECT`   |","table":"table-9"},"6306":{"id":"/components/filter-list-174","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#filter-components","content":"| Component  | Best For                  | State Type |\n| ---------- | ------------------------- | ---------- |\n| `TIMELINE` | Date range with start/end | `TIMELINE` |","table":"table-9"},"6307":{"id":"/components/filter-list-175","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#combining-with-objecttable","content":"FilterList owns its filter state. Read the clause out with `onFilterClauseChanged` and pass it to `ObjectTable`:"},"6308":{"id":"/components/filter-list-176","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"`onFilterListChanged` reports the state the list mounted with and every change\nafter it — a filter set, a filter removed, or a reset — as an event with a\n`reason` (what happened) and a `snapshot` (everything derived from the resulting\nstate), so you don't need to wire up `onFilterStateChanged`,\n`onFilterClauseChanged` and `onEffectiveObjectSet` separately and reconcile\ntheir firings:"},"6309":{"id":"/components/filter-list-177","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"| `event.reason.type`         | Extra fields | Fires when                                     |\n| --------------------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"FILTER_LIST_INITIALIZED\"` | —            | The list mounted, once, before any interaction |","table":"table-10"},"6310":{"id":"/components/filter-list-178","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"| `event.reason.type`      | Extra fields            | Fires when                        |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `\"FILTER_STATE_CHANGED\"` | `filterKey`, `newState` | The user changed a filter's value |","table":"table-10"},"6311":{"id":"/components/filter-list-179","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"| `event.reason.type` | Extra fields | Fires when                         |\n| ------------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `\"FILTER_REMOVED\"`  | `filterKey`  | A filter was removed from the list |","table":"table-10"},"6312":{"id":"/components/filter-list-180","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"| `event.reason.type`   | Extra fields | Fires when                                |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `\"FILTER_LIST_RESET\"` | —            | The reset button restored the mount state |","table":"table-10"},"6313":{"id":"/components/filter-list-181","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"`filteredObjectSet` is `undefined` when no `objectSet` prop is supplied."},"6314":{"id":"/components/filter-list-182","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"`\"FILTER_LIST_INITIALIZED\"` reports the state seeded from `defaultFilterStates`\nand from each definition's `defaultFilterState`, so the initial clause and\nfiltered `ObjectSet` arrive without waiting for a first interaction. If you only\ncare about the current state and not what caused it, ignore `reason` — every\n`snapshot` carries the full `filterClause` and `filteredObjectSet`:"},"6315":{"id":"/components/filter-list-183","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#reading-everything-from-one-callback","content":"Changes are reported as they happen, with no debounce, so an analytics handler\nsees every distinct interaction. Free-text and range inputs debounce their own\nkeystrokes, so typing reports once per pause rather than once per character. If\nyou need coarser batching than that — one network request per burst, say —\ndebounce your own handler."},"6316":{"id":"/components/filter-list-184","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#addremove-filters-uncontrolled-mode","content":"Use `addFilterMode=\"uncontrolled\"` with `isVisible: false` on some filters to let users add and remove filters dynamically:"},"6317":{"id":"/components/filter-list-185","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#addremove-filters-uncontrolled-mode","content":"Filters marked `isVisible: false` appear in the \"Add filter\" popover. Users can add them to the list and remove visible filters via the close button. Reset restores the original visibility."},"6318":{"id":"/components/filter-list-186","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#removable-filters-controlled-mode","content":"When `addFilterMode=\"controlled\"` and `onFilterRemoved` is provided, each filter shows a remove button on hover. The consumer manages the definitions array:"},"6319":{"id":"/components/filter-list-187","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#prefiltered-objectset","content":"Pass a `.where()` objectSet to scope filter dropdown values. For example, to only show Engineering employees:"},"6320":{"id":"/components/filter-list-188","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#prefiltered-objectset","content":"The filter dropdowns will only show job titles and locations that exist within the Engineering department."},"6321":{"id":"/components/filter-list-189","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#keyword-search-filter","content":"Add a full-text search filter that searches across multiple properties:"},"6322":{"id":"/components/filter-list-190","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-listogram-colors","content":"Assign colors to specific values in a listogram:"},"6323":{"id":"/components/filter-list-191","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-value-rendering","content":"Use `renderValue` to customize how filter values are displayed and searched. The returned string replaces the raw value for both display and search matching. This is useful for showing human-readable names instead of IDs:"},"6324":{"id":"/components/filter-list-192","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-value-rendering","content":"`renderValue` works with `LISTOGRAM`, `SINGLE_SELECT`, and `MULTI_SELECT` filter components. For `MULTI_SELECT`, it applies to both dropdown items and selected chips. Searching within a filter dropdown matches against the `renderValue` output."},"6325":{"id":"/components/filter-list-193","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#custom-value-rendering","content":"For best performance, memoize `renderValue` with `useCallback` to avoid unnecessary re-renders:"},"6326":{"id":"/components/filter-list-194","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#listogram-display-modes","content":"Control how much detail each listogram row shows:"},"6327":{"id":"/components/filter-list-195","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#limiting-visible-items","content":"By default, LISTOGRAM filters show at most 5 items with a \"View all\" link. Override with `maxVisibleItems`:"},"6328":{"id":"/components/filter-list-196","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#collapsible-panel","content":"The collapse control is available by default and `FilterList` owns the collapsed\nstate, so collapsing works with no wiring at all:"},"6329":{"id":"/components/filter-list-197","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#collapsible-panel","content":"Start collapsed with `defaultCollapsed`. `onCollapsedChange` fires in both\nmodes; in uncontrolled mode it is purely a listener on top of the built-in\nbehavior, so the panel keeps collapsing and expanding on its own. Use it when\nthe surrounding layout needs to react:"},"6330":{"id":"/components/filter-list-198","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#collapsible-panel","content":"To own the state yourself, pass `collapsed` instead of `defaultCollapsed`. That\nswitches the feature into controlled mode: the prop is the source of truth, the\ncomponent keeps no internal state, and the panel only moves when you re-render\nwith a new value in response to `onCollapsedChange`. If both are supplied,\n`collapsed` wins."},"6331":{"id":"/components/filter-list-199","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#collapsible-panel","content":"`onCollapsedChange` is only an event listener — it never enables the control and\nnever takes over the state. Availability is governed by `enableCollapse` alone."},"6332":{"id":"/components/filter-list-200","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#collapsible-panel","content":"Pass `enableCollapse={false}` to pin the panel open and remove the control\nentirely; `collapsed` and `defaultCollapsed` are then ignored."},"6333":{"id":"/components/filter-list-201","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#drag-and-drop-sorting","content":"Enable reordering of filters via drag and drop:"},"6334":{"id":"/components/filter-list-202","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#exclude-toggle","content":"LISTOGRAM and TEXT_TAGS filters support an exclude/include toggle. Hover a filter item and click the three-dot menu to toggle between \"Keeping\" and \"Excluding\" modes. When excluding, selected values are excluded from results and appear with a strikethrough."},"6335":{"id":"/components/filter-list-203","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#styling","content":"FilterList uses CSS custom properties included in `@osdk/react-components/styles.css` for theming. Override `--osdk-*` tokens to customize FilterList without affecting other components, or override `--bp-*` tokens for global theming."},"6336":{"id":"/components/filter-list-204","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#styling","content":"Use the `className` prop for scoped styling:"},"6337":{"id":"/components/filter-list-205","page_id":"/components/filter-list","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/filter-list#styling","content":"For a full reference of CSS tokens, see the CSS Variables documentation."},"6338":{"id":"/components/filter-list-206","page_id":"/compone