he `columnDefinitions` prop."},"6475":{"id":"/components/object-table-80","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"Type parameters: `Q extends ObjectOrInterfaceDefinition`, `RDPs extends Record<string, SimplePropertyDef> = {}`, `FunctionColumns extends Record<string, QueryDefinition<{}>> = Record<string, never>`"},"6476":{"id":"/components/object-table-81","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name         | Type | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------ | ---- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `objectType` | `Q`  | **Required.** The object or interface type of the object If objectSet is not provided, objects will be fetched based on this type. |","table":"table-0"},"6477":{"id":"/components/object-table-82","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name        | Type           | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ----------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `objectSet` | `ObjectSet<Q>` | The set of objects to show in the table. If provided, the table fetches through this object set instead of fetching based on objectType. Supported for both object and interface types.<br /><br />For an interface object set, rows expose the interface's declared properties; the underlying concrete object's non-interface properties are not loaded. Use objectType-based fetching if you need those. |","table":"table-0"},"6478":{"id":"/components/object-table-83","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                | Type                                                | Description                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `columnDefinitions` | `Array<ColumnDefinition<Q, RDPs, FunctionColumns>>` | Ordered list of column definitions to show in the table<br /><br />If not provided, all of the properties of the object type will be shown in default order. |","table":"table-0"},"6479":{"id":"/components/object-table-84","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name               | Type                  | Description |\n| ------------------ | --------------------- | ----------- |\n| `objectSetOptions` | `ObjectSetOptions<Q>` |             |","table":"table-0"},"6480":{"id":"/components/object-table-85","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name               | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dedupeIntervalMs` | `number` | Minimum time between fetch requests in milliseconds. Increasing this value reduces redundant network calls when the same data is requested multiple times in quick succession. Defaults to `60_000 1 minute`. |","table":"table-0"},"6481":{"id":"/components/object-table-86","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name            | Type      | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `streamUpdates` | `boolean` | Enable streaming updates via websocket subscription. When true, the table will automatically update when matching objects are added, updated, or removed in Foundry.<br /><br />Limitations: `streamUpdates` cannot be used together with `pivotTo` or `withProperties`. The server does not support websocket subscriptions for link-traversal or derived-property queries. Those queries still fetch data normally but won't receive real-time updates. Defaults to `false`. |","table":"table-0"},"6482":{"id":"/components/object-table-87","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                            |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `pageSize` | `number` | Number of objects to fetch per page. Defaults to `50`. |","table":"table-0"},"6483":{"id":"/components/object-table-88","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name     | Type                   | Description                                                  |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `filter` | `WhereClause<Q, RDPs>` | The current where clause to filter the objects in the table. |","table":"table-0"},"6484":{"id":"/components/object-table-89","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                 | Type      | Description                                                                                                              |\n| -------------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `enableColumnConfig` | `boolean` | Whether the column configuration dialog for column visibility and ordering is available to the user. Defaults to `true`. |","table":"table-0"},"6485":{"id":"/components/object-table-90","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                  | Type      | Description                                                    |\n| --------------------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enableColumnPinning` | `boolean` | Whether columns can be pinned by the user. Defaults to `true`. |","table":"table-0"},"6486":{"id":"/components/object-table-91","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                   | Type      | Description                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enableColumnResizing` | `boolean` | Whether columns can be resized by the user. Defaults to `true`. |","table":"table-0"},"6487":{"id":"/components/object-table-92","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                        | Type                                                                                                                    | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onColumnVisibilityChanged` | `(newStates: Array<{ columnId: PropertyKeys<Q> \\| keyof RDPs \\| keyof FunctionColumns; isVisible: boolean; }>) => void` | Called when the column visibility or ordering changed.<br /><br />If provided, the table will allow the user to show/hide columns. |","table":"table-0"},"6488":{"id":"/components/object-table-93","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                     | Type                                                                                                                                     | Description                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onColumnsPinnedChanged` | `(newStates: Array<{ columnId: PropertyKeys<Q> \\| keyof RDPs \\| keyof FunctionColumns; pinned: \"left\" \\| \"right\" \\| \"none\"; }>) => void` | Called when the pinned columns change.<br /><br />If provided, the table will allow the user to pin/unpin columns. |","table":"table-0"},"6489":{"id":"/components/object-table-94","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name             | Type                                                                                                   | Description                      |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------- |\n| `onColumnResize` | `(columnId: PropertyKeys<Q> \\| keyof RDPs \\| keyof FunctionColumns, newWidth: number \\| null) => void` | Called when a column is resized. |","table":"table-0"},"6490":{"id":"/components/object-table-95","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                  | Type                                                                         | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onColumnHeaderClick` | `(columnId: PropertyKeys<Q> \\| keyof RDPs \\| keyof FunctionColumns) => void` | Called when a column header is clicked.<br /><br />The columnId matches the `locator.id` configured on the column definition. The dropdown menu trigger is excluded — clicking the chevron opens the header menu instead of firing this callback. |","table":"table-0"},"6491":{"id":"/components/object-table-96","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name             | Type      | Description                                                    |\n| ---------------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enableOrdering` | `boolean` | Whether the table is sortable by the user. Defaults to `true`. |","table":"table-0"},"6492":{"id":"/components/object-table-97","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name             | Type                                                                              | Description                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultOrderBy` | `Array<{ property: PropertyKeys<Q> \\| keyof RDPs; direction: \"asc\" \\| \"desc\"; }>` | The default order by clause to sort the objects in the table. If provided without orderBy prop, the sorting is uncontrolled. If both orderBy and defaultOrderBy are provided, orderBy takes precedence. |","table":"table-0"},"6493":{"id":"/components/object-table-98","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name      | Type                                                                              | Description                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `orderBy` | `Array<{ property: PropertyKeys<Q> \\| keyof RDPs; direction: \"asc\" \\| \"desc\"; }>` | The current order by clause to sort the objects in the table. If provided, the sorting is controlled. If both orderBy and defaultOrderBy are provided, orderBy takes precedence. |","table":"table-0"},"6494":{"id":"/components/object-table-99","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name               | Type                                                                                                    | Description                                                                      |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onOrderByChanged` | `(newOrderBy: Array<{ property: PropertyKeys<Q> \\| keyof RDPs; direction: \"asc\" \\| \"desc\"; }>) => void` | Called when the order by clause is changed. Required when sorting is controlled. |","table":"table-0"},"6495":{"id":"/components/object-table-100","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name            | Type                               | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `selectionMode` | `\"single\" \\| \"multiple\" \\| \"none\"` | Selection mode for the table rows.<br /><br />If multiple, a checkbox will be shown for each row to allow selecting multiple rows as well as a top-level checkbox in the header to select all rows. Defaults to `\"none\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"6496":{"id":"/components/object-table-101","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name           | Type                  | Description                                                                             |\n| -------------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `selectedRows` | `PrimaryKeyType<Q>[]` | The currently selected rows in the table. If provided, the row selection is controlled. |","table":"table-0"},"6497":{"id":"/components/object-table-102","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name            | Type      | Description                                                                                                                                           |\n| --------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `isAllSelected` | `boolean` | Indicates whether all rows are selected in controlled mode. When true, the table will show all rows as selected regardless of the selectedRows array. |","table":"table-0"},"6498":{"id":"/components/object-table-103","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                    | Type                                            | Description                                                                                          |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRowSelectionChanged` | `(change: RowSelectionChange<Q, RDPs>) => void` | Called when the row selection changes, with a `RowSelectionChange` payload describing the new state. |","table":"table-0"},"6499":{"id":"/components/object-table-104","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                     | Type                                             | Description                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onLoadedObjectsChanged` | `(change: LoadedObjectsChange<Q, RDPs>) => void` | Called when the set of loaded rows changes — as pages are fetched, when streamed updates arrive, and after a refetch — with a `LoadedObjectsChange` payload. |","table":"table-0"},"6500":{"id":"/components/object-table-105","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name         | Type                        | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------ | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `focusedRow` | `PrimaryKeyType<Q> \\| null` | The primary key of the row to render as visually focused (the \"last interacted\" row). When provided, focus state is controlled by the caller.<br /><br />Stored as a primary key rather than a full object so the focus does not go stale when the underlying row data changes.<br /><br />Pass `null` to render no row as focused. |","table":"table-0"},"6501":{"id":"/components/object-table-106","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                  | Type                                                                                   | Description                                                                                                                                |\n| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onFocusedRowChanged` | `(row: Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs> \\| null) => void` | Called when the focused row changes — fires in both controlled and uncontrolled modes so callers can observe focus without taking it over. |","table":"table-0"},"6502":{"id":"/components/object-table-107","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name       | Type                   | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `editMode` | `\"always\" \\| \"manual\"` | Controls the edit mode behavior of the table. - \"always\": Editable cells are immediately in edit mode on row clicked. - \"manual\": User can toggle edit mode on/off via the Edit Table button. Defaults to `\"manual\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"6503":{"id":"/components/object-table-108","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name             | Type      | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ---------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `showEditFooter` | `boolean` | Whether to render the bottom edit footer that hosts the \"Edit Table\" / \"Cancel\" / \"Submit Edits\" buttons and the edit-state indicators (modification count, validation errors). Defaults to true whenever the table has at least one column declared editable (i.e. any column with `editable: true` or `editable: (object) => boolean`). When `false`, the \"Edit Table\" and \"Submit Edits\" buttons will not be shown. |","table":"table-0"},"6504":{"id":"/components/object-table-109","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                 | Type                                                                                                   | Description                                                           |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onCellValueChanged` | `(info: CellEditInfo<Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs>, unknown>) => void` | Called after the value of a cell is edited and committed by the user. |","table":"table-0"},"6505":{"id":"/components/object-table-110","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name            | Type                                                                                                                  | Description                                                              |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onSubmitEdits` | `(edits: CellEditInfo<Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs>, unknown>[]) => Promise<boolean>` | If provided, the \"Submit Edits\" button will be shown in the edit footer. |","table":"table-0"},"6506":{"id":"/components/object-table-111","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name         | Type                                                                              | Description                   |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `onRowClick` | `(object: Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs>) => void` | Called when a row is clicked. |","table":"table-0"},"6507":{"id":"/components/object-table-112","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name                    | Type                                                                                                          | Description                                                              |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `renderCellContextMenu` | `(row: Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs>, cellValue: unknown) => React.ReactNode` | If provided, will render this context menu when right clicking on a cell |","table":"table-0"},"6508":{"id":"/components/object-table-113","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `rowHeight` | `number` | The height of each row in pixels. Defaults to `40`. |","table":"table-0"},"6509":{"id":"/components/object-table-114","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name               | Type                    | Description                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `renderEmptyState` | `() => React.ReactNode` | Render override for the empty state. Called when the table has no rows and no error. When omitted, a default \"No Data\" indicator is rendered. |","table":"table-0"},"6510":{"id":"/components/object-table-115","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name               | Type                                                                                                             | Description                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getRowAttributes` | `(object: Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs>) => Record<string, string \\| undefined>` | Returns extra HTML attributes (typically `data-*`) to apply to each row element. Use this to drive conditional row styling |","table":"table-0"},"6511":{"id":"/components/object-table-116","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name       | Type                                    | Description                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tableRef` | `React.Ref<ObjectTableHandle<Q, RDPs>>` | Imperative handle for programmatic table actions. Pass a ref (`useRef<ObjectTableHandle<Q, RDPs>>(null)`) to call `ObjectTableHandle` methods such as `ObjectTableHandle.getSnapshot`. |","table":"table-0"},"6512":{"id":"/components/object-table-117","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#props-reference","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description |\n| ----------- | -------- | ----------- |\n| `className` | `string` |             |","table":"table-0"},"6513":{"id":"/components/object-table-118","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#object-set-options","content":"The `objectSetOptions` prop combines the table's object set with others before fetching:"},"6514":{"id":"/components/object-table-119","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#object-set-options","content":"Type parameters: `Q extends ObjectOrInterfaceDefinition`"},"6515":{"id":"/components/object-table-120","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#object-set-options","content":"| Name    | Type             | Description               |\n| ------- | ---------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `union` | `ObjectSet<Q>[]` | Object sets to union with |","table":"table-1"},"6516":{"id":"/components/object-table-121","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#object-set-options","content":"| Name        | Type             | Description                   |\n| ----------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `intersect` | `ObjectSet<Q>[]` | Object sets to intersect with |","table":"table-1"},"6517":{"id":"/components/object-table-122","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#object-set-options","content":"| Name       | Type             | Description                  |\n| ---------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `subtract` | `ObjectSet<Q>[]` | Object sets to subtract from |","table":"table-1"},"6518":{"id":"/components/object-table-123","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"Each entry in `columnDefinitions` is a `ColumnDefinition`. The `locator` identifies what the column shows (see Column Locator Types); the remaining fields control appearance and behavior."},"6519":{"id":"/components/object-table-124","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"Type parameters: `Q extends ObjectOrInterfaceDefinition`, `RDPs extends Record<string, SimplePropertyDef> = {}`, `FunctionColumns extends Record<string, QueryDefinition<{}>> = Record<string, never>`"},"6520":{"id":"/components/object-table-125","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description         |\n| ----------- | --------- | ------------------- |\n| `isVisible` | `boolean` | Defaults to `true`. |","table":"table-2"},"6521":{"id":"/components/object-table-126","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name     | Type                          | Description         |\n| -------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `pinned` | `\"left\" \\| \"right\" \\| \"none\"` | Defaults to `none`. |","table":"table-2"},"6522":{"id":"/components/object-table-127","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description |\n| ------- | -------- | ----------- |\n| `width` | `number` |             |","table":"table-2"},"6523":{"id":"/components/object-table-128","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------- |\n| `minWidth` | `number` |             |","table":"table-2"},"6524":{"id":"/components/object-table-129","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------- |\n| `maxWidth` | `number` |             |","table":"table-2"},"6525":{"id":"/components/object-table-130","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description |\n| ----------- | --------- | ----------- |\n| `resizable` | `boolean` |             |","table":"table-2"},"6526":{"id":"/components/object-table-131","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description |\n| ----------- | --------- | ----------- |\n| `orderable` | `boolean` |             |","table":"table-2"},"6527":{"id":"/components/object-table-132","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name         | Type                                                                                                                                                                     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `renderCell` | `(object: Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs>, locator: ColumnDefinitionLocator<Q, RDPs, FunctionColumns>, value: unknown) => React.ReactNode` | Custom renderer for the cell value.<br /><br />This changes only how the cell's value is displayed; the value itself is unchanged. To change the value, use `getCellValue` (and declare its `cellValueType`) — `renderCell` then receives that value as its third argument. The two can be combined.<br /><br /> `renderCell` is used only when the cell is read-only. When cells are actually editable, the in-built edit component takes over. |","table":"table-2"},"6528":{"id":"/components/object-table-133","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `columnName` | `string` | If provided, this will be used in the column header. If both columnName and renderHeader are provided, renderHeader will take precedence in the table header. columnName will still be used in other parts where the column name is displayed.<br /><br />If not provided, for a property column, the property displayName will be used for other columns, the id will be used. |","table":"table-2"},"6529":{"id":"/components/object-table-134","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name           | Type                    | Description                                                                                                                                                               |\n| -------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `renderHeader` | `() => React.ReactNode` | If provided, this will be used to render the header component. When both columnName and renderHeader are provided, renderHeader will take precedence in the table header. |","table":"table-2"},"6530":{"id":"/components/object-table-135","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name       | Type                                                                                              | Description                                                                                                        |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `editable` | `\\| true \\| ((object: Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs>) => boolean)` | `editable` can be a boolean or a predicate that receives the row's object and returns whether the cell is editable |","table":"table-2"},"6531":{"id":"/components/object-table-136","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name              | Type                                                                             | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `editFieldConfig` | `EditFieldConfig<Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs>>` | Configuration for the cell editor component.<br /><br />When provided, the column uses the specified field component (e.g. dropdown) instead of the default auto-detected text/number input.<br /><br />`getFieldComponentProps` receives the row's object and a map of any pending edits for that row (keyed by column id), and returns the props to pass to the field component. Editor configuration can depend on the current row or on other in-progress edits within the row. |","table":"table-2"},"6532":{"id":"/components/object-table-137","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name           | Type                                               | Description                                                 |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `validateEdit` | `(value: unknown) => Promise<string \\| undefined>` | Additional function to validate the cell value during edit. |","table":"table-2"},"6533":{"id":"/components/object-table-138","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name      | Type                                                                              | Description                                                                                                                                           |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `locator` | `\\| PropertyColumnLocator<Q> \\| RdpColumnLocator<Q, RDPs> \\| CustomColumnLocator` | **Required.** What the column shows — a property, a linked object property (derived property), or a custom column — and that locator's configuration. |","table":"table-2"},"6534":{"id":"/components/object-table-139","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name            | Type                    | Description                                                                                                             |\n| --------------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cellValueType` | `BaseWirePropertyTypes` | The cell value's data type. Constrains what `getCellValue` may return, and selects the editor for an `editable` column. |","table":"table-2"},"6535":{"id":"/components/object-table-140","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-definition-structure","content":"| Name           | Type                                                                                                                                                                                                           | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `getCellValue` | `(object: Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs>, locator: ColumnDefinitionLocator<Q, RDPs, FunctionColumns>) => PropertyValueWireToClient[BaseWirePropertyTypes] \\| null \\| undefined` | Derives the cell's value from the row's object. Without it the column reads the property named by `locator.id`.<br /><br />Use this to change what the cell's value _is_ — what it returns is the value the table renders, edits, and passes on to `renderCell`. Use `renderCell` to change only how that value is displayed. The two can be combined. |","table":"table-2"},"6536":{"id":"/components/object-table-141","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editable","content":"`editable` accepts either a boolean or a function `(rowData) => boolean`:"},"6537":{"id":"/components/object-table-142","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editable","content":"`editable: true` — every cell in the column is editable."},"6538":{"id":"/components/object-table-143","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editable","content":"`editable: (rowData) => boolean` — configurable per row. The function receives the row's data and returns whether the cell should be editable."},"6539":{"id":"/components/object-table-144","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editable","content":"When `editable` is a function, the column is still considered \"potentially editable\" at the table level — the bottom edit-mode bar is shown so users can enter and exit edit mode. The per-row predicate decides whether each cell renders the editor or the read-only value."},"6540":{"id":"/components/object-table-145","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"When `editable` is truthy, columns default to a text or number input (auto-detected from the property type). Use `editFieldConfig` to specify a different editor component."},"6541":{"id":"/components/object-table-146","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"**Supported editor components:**"},"6542":{"id":"/components/object-table-147","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| `fieldComponent` | Description                              | Renders                                                      |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `\"DROPDOWN\"`     | A select dropdown or searchable combobox | `Select` (default) or `Combobox` (when `isSearchable: true`) |","table":"table-3"},"6543":{"id":"/components/object-table-148","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| `fieldComponent` | Description               | Renders          |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `\"DATE_PICKER\"`  | A date or datetime picker | `DatetimePicker` |","table":"table-3"},"6544":{"id":"/components/object-table-149","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"Without `editFieldConfig`, editable columns use a text input for string properties and a number input for numeric properties (`double`, `integer`, `long`, `float`, `decimal`, `byte`, `short`)."},"6545":{"id":"/components/object-table-150","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"`getFieldComponentProps` receives the row's data and returns the props passed to the field component, so editor configuration can vary per row (e.g. dropdown items computed from the row's state)."},"6546":{"id":"/components/object-table-151","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"`editFieldConfig` is a discriminated union on `fieldComponent`. Each variant's `getFieldComponentProps` returns the config for that editor:"},"6547":{"id":"/components/object-table-152","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"**`fieldComponent: \"DROPDOWN\"`** — `getFieldComponentProps` returns:"},"6548":{"id":"/components/object-table-153","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"Type parameters: `V = unknown`"},"6549":{"id":"/components/object-table-154","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name    | Type  | Description                                     |\n| ------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `items` | `V[]` | **Required.** Available items for the dropdown. |","table":"table-4"},"6550":{"id":"/components/object-table-155","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name                | Type                               | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `itemToStringLabel` | `(item: V \\| undefined) => string` | Converts an item to a display string. Defaults to `String()`.<br /><br />`item` may be `undefined` when the cell has no value yet — the formatter is responsible for producing a sensible label in that case. |","table":"table-4"},"6551":{"id":"/components/object-table-156","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name        | Type                  | Description                                                                                                             |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `itemToKey` | `(item: V) => string` | Returns a unique string key for a list item. Used as the React `key`. Falls back to the item's index when not provided. |","table":"table-4"},"6552":{"id":"/components/object-table-157","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name          | Type                      | Description                                                                                                                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `isItemEqual` | `(a: V, b: V) => boolean` | Custom equality check for item values. Defaults to `Object.is`. Required when items are objects to ensure correct selection matching. |","table":"table-4"},"6553":{"id":"/components/object-table-158","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name           | Type      | Description                                                                                                                                          |\n| -------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `isSearchable` | `boolean` | Whether the dropdown allows searching/filtering. When true, renders a Combobox with a search input. When false (default), renders a Select dropdown. |","table":"table-4"},"6554":{"id":"/components/object-table-159","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | Placeholder text shown when no value is selected. |","table":"table-4"},"6555":{"id":"/components/object-table-160","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name         | Type      | Description                              |\n| ------------ | --------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `isMultiple` | `boolean` | Whether multiple values can be selected. |","table":"table-4"},"6556":{"id":"/components/object-table-161","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"**`fieldComponent: \"DATE_PICKER\"`** — `getFieldComponentProps` returns:"},"6557":{"id":"/components/object-table-162","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name  | Type   | Description                            |\n| ----- | ------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| `min` | `Date` | The earliest date the user can select. |","table":"table-5"},"6558":{"id":"/components/object-table-163","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name  | Type   | Description                          |\n| ----- | ------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `max` | `Date` | The latest date the user can select. |","table":"table-5"},"6559":{"id":"/components/object-table-164","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name       | Type      | Description                                           |\n| ---------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `showTime` | `boolean` | Whether to show a time picker alongside the calendar. |","table":"table-5"},"6560":{"id":"/components/object-table-165","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name               | Type      | Description                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `closeOnSelection` | `boolean` | Whether to close the popover after selecting a date. Defaults to true when `showTime` is false, false when `showTime` is true. |","table":"table-5"},"6561":{"id":"/components/object-table-166","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | Placeholder text shown when no value is selected. |","table":"table-5"},"6562":{"id":"/components/object-table-167","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name         | Type                     | Description                                                                                                              |\n| ------------ | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `formatDate` | `(date: Date) => string` | Formats a Date for display in the input field when not editing. Provide a matching `parseDate` if using a custom format. |","table":"table-5"},"6563":{"id":"/components/object-table-168","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#editfieldconfig","content":"| Name        | Type                                  | Description                                                                       |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parseDate` | `(text: string) => Date \\| undefined` | Parses a user-typed string back into a Date. Must be the inverse of `formatDate`. |","table":"table-5"},"6564":{"id":"/components/object-table-169","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#columnname-vs-renderheader","content":"**`columnName`**: If provided, this string is used as the column header text. If not provided, property columns default to the property's `displayName`, and other column types default to the `id`."},"6565":{"id":"/components/object-table-170","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#columnname-vs-renderheader","content":"**`renderHeader`**: If provided, this function renders the header component. When both `columnName` and `renderHeader` are provided, `renderHeader` takes precedence in the table header, but `columnName` is still used in other places where the column name is displayed (e.g., the column configuration dialog, multi-sort dialog)."},"6566":{"id":"/components/object-table-171","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#1-property-column","content":"Displays a property from the object type:"},"6567":{"id":"/components/object-table-172","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#2-derived-property-rdp-column","content":"Displays a computed property:"},"6568":{"id":"/components/object-table-173","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#3-function-column","content":"Displays values computed by an OSDK function (query). This is equivalent to Workshop's function-backed columns. The function must accept an ObjectSet parameter and return a map of results keyed per object."},"6569":{"id":"/components/object-table-174","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#3-function-column","content":"| Property | Type         | Required | Description                          |\n| -------- | ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `type`   | `\"function\"` | Yes      | Identifies this as a function column |","table":"table-6"},"6570":{"id":"/components/object-table-175","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#3-function-column","content":"| Property | Type                    | Required | Description                         |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `id`     | `keyof FunctionColumns` | Yes      | Key in the FunctionColumns type map |","table":"table-6"},"6571":{"id":"/components/object-table-176","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#3-function-column","content":"| Property          | Type              | Required | Description                          |\n| ----------------- | ----------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `queryDefinition` | `QueryDefinition` | Yes      | The OSDK query definition to execute |","table":"table-6"},"6572":{"id":"/components/object-table-177","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#3-function-column","content":"| Property            | Type                    | Required | Description                                             |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getFunctionParams` | `(objectSet) => params` | Yes      | Computes function parameters from the current ObjectSet |","table":"table-6"},"6573":{"id":"/components/object-table-178","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#3-function-column","content":"| Property | Type                 | Required | Description                                              |\n| -------- | -------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getKey` | `(object) => string` | Yes      | Generates a lookup key for each object in the result map |","table":"table-6"},"6574":{"id":"/components/object-table-179","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#3-function-column","content":"| Property   | Type                     | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getValue` | `(cellData?) => unknown` | No       | Extracts a display value from the raw function result per object. `cellData` is `undefined` when the object has no result (e.g., loading or missing from the function output) |","table":"table-6"},"6575":{"id":"/components/object-table-180","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#3-function-column","content":"| Property           | Type     | Required | Description                                                                                                           |\n| ------------------ | -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dedupeIntervalMs` | `number` | No       | Minimum time (ms) between re-fetches of the same function with the same parameters. Defaults to `300_000` (5 minutes) |","table":"table-6"},"6576":{"id":"/components/object-table-181","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#4-custom-column","content":"Displays header and cell with the provided custom renderers."},"6577":{"id":"/components/object-table-182","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-6-hidden-columns","content":"Use `isVisible: false` to define columns that are hidden by default but can be toggled visible by the user:"},"6578":{"id":"/components/object-table-183","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-9-filtering-on-object-properties-and-derived-properties-rdps","content":"You can filter by object properties and derived properties by including them in the `WhereClause`:"},"6579":{"id":"/components/object-table-184","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-11-controlled-row-selection","content":"**Key points about select all behavior:**"},"6580":{"id":"/components/object-table-185","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-11-controlled-row-selection","content":"The `isSelectAll` field in the `onRowSelectionChanged` payload indicates whether the change was triggered by the \"select all\" checkbox"},"6581":{"id":"/components/object-table-186","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-11-controlled-row-selection","content":"When `isAllSelected` is `true`, the table shows all rows as selected regardless of the `selectedRows` array content"},"6582":{"id":"/components/object-table-187","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-11-controlled-row-selection","content":"This allows efficient handling of \"select all\" without loading all object IDs"},"6583":{"id":"/components/object-table-188","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-11-controlled-row-selection","content":"Individual row selections automatically set `isAllSelected` to `false`"},"6584":{"id":"/components/object-table-189","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-11-controlled-row-selection","content":"After \"select all\", new rows loaded via scroll (`fetchMore`) stay visually checked and `onRowSelectionChanged` refires with the expanded selection so controlled callers stay in sync"},"6585":{"id":"/components/object-table-190","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#listening-to-selection-changes","content":"`onRowSelectionChanged` is the preferred callback. It fires with a single payload covering everything you usually need:"},"6586":{"id":"/components/object-table-191","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-12-custom-column-type","content":"In a custom column type, you can render anything in the column by passing in renderHeader and renderCell props."},"6587":{"id":"/components/object-table-192","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-13-editable-table","content":"Enable inline editing with validation, dropdown selectors, and bulk submission:"},"6588":{"id":"/components/object-table-193","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"**Edit Modes**:"},"6589":{"id":"/components/object-table-194","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"`manual` (default): User clicks \"Edit Table\" button to enter edit mode"},"6590":{"id":"/components/object-table-195","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"`always`: Table is always in edit mode"},"6591":{"id":"/components/object-table-196","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"**Editor Components**:"},"6592":{"id":"/components/object-table-197","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"**Text input** (default): For string properties"},"6593":{"id":"/components/object-table-198","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"**Number input** (auto-detected): For numeric properties (`double`, `integer`, `long`, `float`, `decimal`, `byte`, `short`)"},"6594":{"id":"/components/object-table-199","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"**Dropdown (Select)**: Fixed list of options via `editFieldConfig` with `fieldComponent: \"DROPDOWN\"`"},"6595":{"id":"/components/object-table-200","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"**Dropdown (Combobox)**: Searchable list via `isSearchable: true` in `fieldComponentProps`"},"6596":{"id":"/components/object-table-201","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"**Validation**:"},"6597":{"id":"/components/object-table-202","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"Use `validateEdit` on columns for async validation"},"6598":{"id":"/components/object-table-203","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"Validation errors are shown with an error icon and tooltip"},"6599":{"id":"/components/object-table-204","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"Works with all editor types including dropdowns"},"6600":{"id":"/components/object-table-205","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"**Edit State Management**:"},"6601":{"id":"/components/object-table-206","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"Edits are tracked locally until submitted"},"6602":{"id":"/components/object-table-207","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"Modified cells are visually highlighted"},"6603":{"id":"/components/object-table-208","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"\"Cancel\" button discards all pending edits"},"6604":{"id":"/components/object-table-209","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"**Bulk Submission**:"},"6605":{"id":"/components/object-table-210","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"When `onSubmitEdits` is provided, a \"Submit Edits\" button appears"},"6606":{"id":"/components/object-table-211","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"All edits are submitted together"},"6607":{"id":"/components/object-table-212","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#key-features-of-editable-tables","content":"Return `true` from `onSubmitEdits` to clear edits after successful submission"},"6608":{"id":"/components/object-table-213","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#per-row-configuration-for-editable-and-fieldcomponentprops","content":"Pass a function to `editable` to gate editing per row, and a `getFieldComponentProps` function to compute editor props from the row's data:"},"6609":{"id":"/components/object-table-214","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-14-custom-column-configuration-dialog","content":"Use the `ColumnConfigDialog` component to create a custom column configuration experience:"},"6610":{"id":"/components/object-table-215","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-14-custom-column-configuration-dialog","content":"This example demonstrates:"},"6611":{"id":"/components/object-table-216","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-14-custom-column-configuration-dialog","content":"Using the `ColumnConfigDialog` component for custom column management"},"6612":{"id":"/components/object-table-217","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-14-custom-column-configuration-dialog","content":"Tracking column visibility and order in component state"},"6613":{"id":"/components/object-table-218","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-14-custom-column-configuration-dialog","content":"Providing a custom button to open the dialog"},"6614":{"id":"/components/object-table-219","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-14-custom-column-configuration-dialog","content":"Disabling the built-in column configuration to avoid conflicts"},"6615":{"id":"/components/object-table-220","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-14-custom-column-configuration-dialog","content":"Managing hidden columns that can be toggled visible by users"},"6616":{"id":"/components/object-table-221","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-15-function-backed-columns","content":"Display values computed by OSDK functions (queries) alongside regular property columns. Function columns automatically handle loading states, caching, and deduplication."},"6617":{"id":"/components/object-table-222","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#example-15-function-backed-columns","content":"Multiple function columns sharing the same `queryDefinition` are automatically deduplicated into a single API call. Use different `getValue` functions to extract different fields from the same result:"},"6618":{"id":"/components/object-table-223","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-pinning","content":"Pin columns to the left or right side of the table:"},"6619":{"id":"/components/object-table-224","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-resizing","content":"Control whether columns can be resized:"},"6620":{"id":"/components/object-table-225","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#column-resizing","content":"Listen to resize events:"},"6621":{"id":"/components/object-table-226","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#disable-filtering-or-sorting","content":"Disable filtering or sorting globally:"},"6622":{"id":"/components/object-table-227","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#disable-filtering-or-sorting","content":"Or per column:"},"6623":{"id":"/components/object-table-228","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#custom-row-height","content":"Adjust row height for better readability:"},"6624":{"id":"/components/object-table-229","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-and-conditional-row-styling","content":"Use `getRowAttributes` to apply custom HTML attributes (typically `data-*` attributes) to each `<tr>` element. This is the recommended pattern for conditional row styling — for example, changing a row's background color based on the underlying object's state."},"6625":{"id":"/components/object-table-230","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-and-conditional-row-styling","content":"Entries whose value is `undefined` are skipped, so you can include attributes conditionally without emitting empty values."},"6626":{"id":"/components/object-table-231","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-and-conditional-row-styling","content":"Then drive your row styling in CSS using attribute selectors. Row background colors come from `--osdk-table-row-bg-default` (and `--osdk-table-row-bg-alternate` for odd zebra rows) — overriding both on a `<tr>` for matching rows takes precedence:"},"6627":{"id":"/components/object-table-232","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-and-conditional-row-styling","content":"Notes:"},"6628":{"id":"/components/object-table-233","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-and-conditional-row-styling","content":"Combine multiple attribute selectors to express priority (the most specific selector wins, per normal CSS rules)."},"6629":{"id":"/components/object-table-234","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#row-attributes-and-conditional-row-styling","content":"The table sets its own attributes (`data-selected`, `data-focused`, `data-row-parity`, `data-pinned`) on rows and cells. Avoid using these names in `getRowAttributes` since they would override the built-in behavior."},"6630":{"id":"/components/object-table-235","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#loading-and-empty-states","content":"The ObjectTable automatically handles:"},"6631":{"id":"/components/object-table-236","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#loading-and-empty-states","content":"**Loading state**: Shows skeleton rows while data is loading"},"6632":{"id":"/components/object-table-237","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#loading-and-empty-states","content":"**Empty state**: Shows appropriate message when no data matches filters"},"6633":{"id":"/components/object-table-238","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#loading-and-empty-states","content":"**Error state**: Displays error messages if data fetching fails"},"6634":{"id":"/components/object-table-239","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#loading-and-empty-states","content":"No additional configuration needed - these states are built-in!"},"6635":{"id":"/components/object-table-240","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#infinite-scrolling","content":"The ObjectTable automatically implements infinite scroll pagination, with page size of 50. As users scroll down, more data is loaded seamlessly. No configuration required!"},"6636":{"id":"/components/object-table-241","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#observing-loaded-objects","content":"`onLoadedObjectsChanged` reports which rows the table currently holds. It fires once the first page has loaded and again each time the loaded rows or the total count change — as further pages are fetched, when streamed updates arrive, after a refetch, and as function-backed column values fill in. It's a listener only; the table keeps loading whether or not you pass it."},"6637":{"id":"/components/object-table-242","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#observing-loaded-objects","content":"The payload is a `LoadedObjectsChange<Q, RDPs>`:"},"6638":{"id":"/components/object-table-243","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#observing-loaded-objects","content":"| Field           | Type                                                              | Description                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `loadedObjects` | `Osdk.Instance<Q, \"$allBaseProperties\", PropertyKeys<Q>, RDPs>[]` | Rows loaded so far, in display order. Rows the user hasn't scrolled to yet are absent. Each row also carries its function-backed column values. |","table":"table-7"},"6639":{"id":"/components/object-table-244","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#observing-loaded-objects","content":"| Field        | Type                  | Description                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `totalCount` | `string \\| undefined` | Total objects matching the object set, or `undefined` when the API didn't report one. A string, matching `getSnapshot()`'s `totalCount`. |","table":"table-7"},"6640":{"id":"/components/object-table-245","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#observing-loaded-objects","content":"Compare `loadedObjects.length` against `totalCount` to tell whether more rows remain. To get **every** matching row rather than the loaded ones, use `getSnapshot()` instead — it pages through the whole object set."},"6641":{"id":"/components/object-table-246","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#observing-loaded-objects","content":"Memoize the handler (`useCallback`) if it closes over state, as you would any other prop."},"6642":{"id":"/components/object-table-247","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#exporting-data","content":"Pass a `tableRef` to obtain an `ObjectTableHandle<Q, RDPs>`. Its `getSnapshot()` method loads **all** matching rows and returns a format-agnostic snapshot of the table's columns, rows, and total match count, so you can export to CSV, JSON, the clipboard, or anywhere else. When the total row count exceeds `rowLimit` (default `10_000`), the returned promise rejects (with a string error message); otherwise every matching row is loaded."},"6643":{"id":"/components/object-table-248","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#exporting-data","content":"The snapshot reflects the table's current column visibility, ordering, and pinning. Property, derived-property, and function-backed columns are all included. Custom-rendered columns have no underlying value and are omitted. Each row exposes a `getValue(columnId)` accessor; cells are the raw value, or the thrown `Error` instance if a function-backed cell failed to load (the promise still resolves with the rest of the snapshot)."},"6644":{"id":"/components/object-table-249","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#exporting-data","content":"The snapshot also carries `totalCount` — the number of objects matching the underlying object set as reported by the API, encoded as a string (or `undefined` when no count was provided). It may exceed the number of loaded rows, so it's handy for surfacing \"exported N of M\"."},"6645":{"id":"/components/object-table-250","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#exporting-data","content":"`getSnapshot()` accepts an optional `{ rowLimit }` that bounds the snapshot size — when the total row count exceeds it, the promise rejects with a string error message. `row.getValue(columnId)` returns the raw cell value (or the thrown `Error` instance for failed function-backed cells, or `undefined` for unknown column ids) — your formatter handles the rest."},"6646":{"id":"/components/object-table-251","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"`ObjectTable` is assembled from a set of building-block hooks that are exported so you can build a **fully custom table** while keeping OSDK data fetching, sorting, selection, editing, and snapshot behavior. Reach for these when you need markup or interactions that `ObjectTable`'s props don't cover."},"6647":{"id":"/components/object-table-252","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"The hooks are unopinionated about rendering — they produce the state and column definitions you feed into your own `@tanstack/react-table` instance, which you construct in your app:"},"6648":{"id":"/components/object-table-253","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"[!WARNING]\n**Match the `@tanstack/react-table` version.** `@osdk/react-components` bundles its own copy of `@tanstack/react-table`, and the hook return types (`ColumnDef`, `Table`, `SortingState`, `OnChangeFn`, …) come from that copy. TanStack types are **invariant** in their type parameters, and this package augments `@tanstack/react-table` via `declare module` (adding table/column `meta` fields). If your app resolves a **different** `@tanstack/react-table` version than the one this package uses, you may hit confusing type errors — e.g. a `ColumnDef` or `Table` produced by these hooks reported as not assignable to the one from your copy, or the augmented `meta` fields missing."},"6649":{"id":"/components/object-table-254","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"Install a version that matches the one this package depends on (see `@tanstack/react-table` in `@osdk/react-components`'s `package.json`) — and dedupe so a single copy is resolved (e.g. a pnpm `overrides` / npm `overrides` / yarn `resolutions` entry if a transitive dependency pulls in another version)."},"6650":{"id":"/components/object-table-255","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"Available hooks (import from `@osdk/react-components/object-table`):"},"6651":{"id":"/components/object-table-256","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook                 | Responsibility                                                                             |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `useObjectTableData` | Loads rows (by type or from an object set), applies filter/sort/derived + function columns |","table":"table-8"},"6652":{"id":"/components/object-table-257","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook            | Responsibility                                                                   |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useColumnDefs` | Builds TanStack column definitions from `columnDefinitions` (or object metadata) |","table":"table-8"},"6653":{"id":"/components/object-table-258","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook              | Responsibility                                      |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useTableSorting` | Controlled/uncontrolled sort state ↔ OSDK `orderBy` |","table":"table-8"},"6654":{"id":"/components/object-table-259","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook              | Responsibility                                                   |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useRowSelection` | Single/multiple/range row selection (controlled or uncontrolled) |","table":"table-8"},"6655":{"id":"/components/object-table-260","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook                 | Responsibility                         |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `useSelectionColumn` | The leading checkbox column definition |","table":"table-8"},"6656":{"id":"/components/object-table-261","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook                                                           | Responsibility                                     |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useColumnPinning` / `useColumnResize` / `useColumnVisibility` | Column pinning, sizing, and visibility/order state |","table":"table-8"},"6657":{"id":"/components/object-table-262","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook            | Responsibility                            |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `useFocusedRow` | Controlled/uncontrolled focused-row state |","table":"table-8"},"6658":{"id":"/components/object-table-263","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook                      | Responsibility                                                  |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useLoadedObjectsChanged` | Fires a callback when the loaded rows or the total count change |","table":"table-8"},"6659":{"id":"/components/object-table-264","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook               | Responsibility                                              |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useEditableTable` | Cell-edit session state (pending edits, validation, submit) |","table":"table-8"},"6660":{"id":"/components/object-table-265","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook                     | Responsibility                        |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| `useFunctionColumnsData` | Fetches function-backed column values |","table":"table-8"},"6661":{"id":"/components/object-table-266","page_id":"/components/object-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/components/object-table#headless-hooks","content":"| Hook                     | Responsibility                                                |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------