mnDef` or `Table` produced by these hooks reported as not assignable to the one from your copy, or the augmented `meta` fields missing."],[6071,"@osdk/react documentation"],[6756,"@osdk/react documentation"],[7059,"@osdk/react-components provides Ontology-aware React components that take OSDK types and handle data loading, caching, and state for you."],[6981,"@osdk/react-components styles every component through three layers of CSS custom properties that you can override to theme your app."],[3821,"@osdk/react/platform-apis"],[3884,"@osdk/react/testing"],[4753,"**`AipAgentChat`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts a\nFoundry `PlatformClient` and an LMS model API name; constructs the\nlanguage-model handle, drives `useChat`, and renders the chat UI."],[4754,"**`BaseAipAgentChat`** — Lower-level OSDK-agnostic component that\naccepts `messages`, `status`, and `onSendMessage` directly. Use this\nwhen you already manage chat state yourself (a custom hook, a\nnon-OSDK backend, etc.)."],[6117,"**`BaseEmailViewer`** — Lower-level component that accepts a pre-parsed `ParsedEmail` object."],[6355,"**`BaseImageViewer`** — Lower-level component that accepts a URL string directly. Use this when you already have the image source."],[6379,"**`BaseMarkdownViewer`** — Lower-level component that accepts a markdown string directly."],[6830,"**`BasePdfViewer`** — Lower-level component that accepts the PDF source directly as a URL string, `ArrayBuffer`, `Uint8Array`, or `Blob`. Use this when you already have the PDF source."],[6967,"**`BaseSpreadsheetViewer`** — Lower-level component that accepts a pre-parsed `ParsedSpreadsheet` object."],[7022,"**`BaseTiffViewer`** — Lower-level component that accepts raw `Uint8Array` bytes directly."],[7046,"**`BaseVideoViewer`** — Lower-level component that accepts a URL string directly. Use this when you already have the video source."],[7127,"**`BaseXmlViewer`** — Lower-level component that accepts an XML string directly."],[6564,"**`columnName`**: If provided, this string is used as the column header text. If not provided, property columns default to the property's `displayName`, and other column types default to the `id`."],[6116,"**`EmailViewer`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts an OSDK `Media` object, parses the .eml contents, and renders the email."],[6556,"**`fieldComponent: \"DATE_PICKER\"`** — `getFieldComponentProps` returns:"],[6547,"**`fieldComponent: \"DROPDOWN\"`** — `getFieldComponentProps` returns:"],[6354,"**`ImageViewer`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts an OSDK `Media` object, handles fetching the image contents, and renders via a native `<img>` element."],[6378,"**`MarkdownViewer`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts an OSDK `Media` object, handles fetching the markdown text, and renders via `BaseMarkdownViewer`."],[6829,"**`PdfViewer`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts an OSDK `Media` object, handles fetching the PDF contents, and renders the viewer."],[242,"**`refetch` scope.** On `useOsdkObjects`, `useObjectSet`, and `useOsdkAggregation`, `refetch` invalidates the whole object type, so every list and aggregation of that type refetches. On `useOsdkFunction`, it refetches only that function call with those parameters. To refetch more narrowly, use the methods in Cache invalidation."],[6565,"**`renderHeader`**: If provided, this function renders the header component. When both `columnName` and `renderHeader` are provided, `renderHeader` takes precedence in the table header, but `columnName` is still used in other places where the column name is displayed (e.g., the column configuration dialog, multi-sort dialog)."],[6966,"**`SpreadsheetViewer`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts an OSDK `Media` object, parses the spreadsheet, and renders it."],[7021,"**`TiffViewer`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts an OSDK `Media` object, handles fetching the TIFF contents, and renders via `BaseTiffViewer`."],[244,"**`useObjectSet`.** When the object set changes, `data` keeps the last loaded result until the new set loads."],[245,"**`useOsdkFunction`.** `isLoading` is `true` only while a request is in flight, so the first render can report `isLoading: false` with no data. Treat `data === undefined && error == null` as the initial state, or check `lastUpdated === 0`."],[246,"**`useOsdkMetadata`.** It uses `loading`, not `isLoading`, and `error` is the error's message as a string, not an `Error`. It does not retry after a failure."],[243,"**`useOsdkObject`.** `isLoading` is `false` as soon as `error` is set."],[7045,"**`VideoViewer`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts an OSDK `Media` object, handles fetching the video contents, and renders with native browser controls."],[7126,"**`XmlViewer`** — Primary component for OSDK usage. Accepts an OSDK `Media` object, fetches the XML text, and renders it."],[1325,"**A `tsconfig.json` in `.osdk`.** After generating, the plugin runs `tsc` with `.osdk` as the working directory and fails if it exits with an error."],[2795,"**Actions applied with `useOsdkAction`.** The server reports which objects the action added, modified, and deleted. The cache refetches those objects, and every list, link, aggregation, and function that depends on their types re-evaluates."],[1606,"**Allow the origin.** Ask your Foundry administrator to allow `http://localhost:8080` for CORS on your environment."],[6049,"**Banner data** — the classification string, text color, and background colors"],[6053,"**Base layer** (`BaseCbacPicker`, `BaseCbacBanner`, `BaseCbacPickerDialog`) — pure UI with no OSDK dependency, accepts primitive data directly"],[4919,"**Blueprint Token Mappings**: OSDK-namespaced aliases to Blueprint's design tokens"],[6944,"**Blueprint tokens (`--bp-*`)** — the underlying Blueprint design tokens that most `--osdk-*` tokens map to. Override these for consistent theming across **both Blueprint and OSDK components**. (A few `--osdk-*` tokens hold raw values rather than mapping to a `--bp-*` token — override those `--osdk-*` tokens directly.)"],[6386,"**Bold**, _italic_, and ~~strikethrough~~ text"],[6880,"**Building block components** — Assemble a custom layout using `PdfViewerContent`, `PdfViewerToolbar`, etc."],[6604,"**Bulk Submission**:"],[1612,"**Callback route.** Your app renders a route at the redirect path, so the OAuth client can complete sign-in."],[2870,"**Clear logs**, in the same menu, empties the feed. It does not reset the other devtools metrics."],[1610,"**Client ID.** The client ID passed to `createPublicOauthClient` matches the one on your application's **OAuth & scopes** page in Developer Console."],[6950,"**Color contrast (WCAG AA):** 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text."],[1078,"**Compile.** The `maker` CLI imports that file and writes the IR to `ontology.json`, plus `value-types.json` when you define value types."],[2915,"**Components.** The injected Fiber hook attributes each `@osdk/react` hook to the component that mounted it. The hook must install before React loads. If React loads first, the panel still works but shows a notice that component inspection is unavailable."],[6879,"**Components** (`PdfViewer` / `BasePdfViewer`) — Drop-in viewers with full UI out of the box."],[6038,"**Conjunctive** categories: adds or removes the marking (checkbox behavior)"],[2916,"**Console.** The monitor captures `console` calls made while the page is open."],[953,"**Create the client once.** Import `client` from `src/client.ts` in every component. Do not call `createClient` inside `setup`."],[6683,"**CSS variables**"],[6694,"**CSS variables**"],[6709,"**CSS variables**"],[6720,"**CSS variables**"],[6681,"**Data attributes**"],[6692,"**Data attributes**"],[6704,"**Data attributes**"],[6717,"**Data attributes**"],[2818,"**Declare function dependencies.** `dependsOn` and `dependsOnObjects` let the cache rerun functions after actions, so you do not invalidate them by hand."],[205,"**Declare function dependencies.** Prefer `dependsOn` and `dependsOnObjects` over invalidating functions by hand."],[1480,"**Deduplicated requests.** Components that ask for the same objects with the same options share one cache entry and one request."],[1077,"**Define.** You write object types, links, actions, interfaces, shared property types, and value types in `.ontology/ontology.mts`. Each `define*` call validates its input and registers the type."],[1079,"**Develop locally.** In a Vite app, `@osdk/vite-plugin-oac` runs `maker` on every change, converts the IR to Ontology metadata, generates an SDK into `.osdk/src`, and answers OSDK requests from the dev server with seeded data."],[247,"**Disabled hooks.** With `enabled: false` (or `false` as the last argument to `useOsdkObject`), `isLoading` is `false` and no request is sent."],[6046,"**Disallowed markings** — which markings are blocked based on the current selection"],[6039,"**Disjunctive** categories: replaces the existing selection in that category (radio behavior)"],[6951,"**Distinct interactive states:** rest, hover, active, selected, and focused should each be visually distinguishable — the default `--osdk-table-row-bg-*` and `--osdk-table-row-border-color-*` tokens are designed to meet WCAG AA; preserve that intent in custom themes."],[2819,"**Do not invalidate on mount.** Calling `invalidateAll` or `invalidateObjectType` in a mount effect refetches on every navigation and defeats the cache."],[954,"**Do not reach for `@osdk/react`.** Its hooks need React. For a shared cache in Vue, use the observable client below."],[6875,"**Download button** — downloads the PDF (hidden by default, enable with `enableDownload`)"],[6595,"**Dropdown (Combobox)**: Searchable list via `isSearchable: true` in `fieldComponentProps`"],[6594,"**Dropdown (Select)**: Fixed list of options via `editFieldConfig` with `fieldComponent: \"DROPDOWN\"`"],[6588,"**Edit Modes**:"],[6600,"**Edit State Management**:"],[6591,"**Editor Components**:"],[6632,"**Empty state**: Shows appropriate message when no data matches filters"],[796,"**Enables package exports** (`resolver.unstable_enablePackageExports: true`), because the OSDK packages publish their entry points, such as `@osdk/client/observable`, through the `exports` field."],[6865,"**Enter** — next match"],[6633,"**Error state**: Displays error messages if data fetching fails"],[6867,"**Escape** — close search bar"],[2868,"**Filter logs** searches the serialized arguments of each entry."],[299,"**Fixes without regenerating.** A bug fix in `@osdk/client` reaches you through a dependency update. You do not need to regenerate the SDK."],[1037,"**From the API.** Call the endpoint with a token that can read the ontology, and save the response."],[1036,"**From the OSDK CLI.** `osdk unstable typescript generate` with `--foundryUrl`, `--clientId`, and `--ontologyWritePath ontology-full-metadata.json` signs you in, fetches the metadata, and writes it to that path while it generates an SDK."],[1484,"**Function dependencies.** `useOsdkFunction` reruns a function when objects it depends on change, using `dependsOn` for object types or `dependsOnObjects` for specific instances."],[2798,"**Functions with `dependsOn` or `dependsOnObjects`.** They rerun after actions edit what they declare. See Call functions."],[6881,"**Hooks** — Build entirely custom components. The hooks do all the heavy lifting."],[6045,"**Implied markings** — which markings are automatically included based on the current selection"],[1007,"**Install the same version of all three.** If `@osdk/react` is `2.83.0`, use `@osdk/client@2.83.0` and `@osdk/api@2.83.0`."],[2817,"**Invalidate the narrowest thing you can.** `invalidateObjects` is cheaper than `invalidateObjectType`, which is cheaper than `invalidateAll`."],[6341,"**Keep filter lists focused** -- show 3-8 filters; too many filters overwhelm users"],[204,"**Keep one source of truth.** Do not copy OSDK data into Redux, TanStack Query, or component state. Copies miss optimistic updates and action edits."],[2820,"**Keep OSDK data in the cache.** Copying it into component state, Redux, or another query library creates a second copy that invalidation and optimistic updates do not reach."],[1008,"**Keep prereleases together.** A prerelease `@osdk/react`, such as `-beta.3`, needs the same prerelease of `@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api`. Pairing it with stable releases breaks."],[952,"**Key lists by `$primaryKey`.** It is unique within an object type and stable across fetches."],[6579,"**Key points about select all behavior:**"],[203,"**Let actions drive updates.** Do not call `invalidate*` after `applyAction`. The cache already handles the edits."],[2816,"**Let actions drive updates.** If a change comes from `useOsdkAction`, do not invalidate afterward. It refetches data that is already fresh."],[5924,"**Leverage the mapping**: Since OSDK tokens map to Blueprint tokens, changing a Blueprint token will automatically affect all OSDK tokens that reference it."],[2797,"**Lists with `streamUpdates: true`.** The server pushes changes over a WebSocket."],[1483,"**Live data.** `streamUpdates: true` keeps a list current over a WebSocket subscription instead of polling."],[6631,"**Loading state**: Shows skeleton rows while data is loading"],[798,"**Loads `.env.development` with `dotenv`** and adds `react-native-svg-transformer` for `.svg` imports."],[6338,"**Memoize filterDefinitions** -- define the array outside the component or wrap in `useMemo` to avoid unnecessary re-renders"],[1616,"**Missing scopes.** The OAuth client requests `api:read-data`, `api:write-data`, `api:use-ontologies-read`, and `api:use-ontologies-write` by default. Other APIs need more. For example, the user and marking hooks in `@osdk/react/platform-apis` need `api:admin-read`. Add the scope to the application in Developer Console, then request it:"],[951,"**Never mutate an object to update the UI.** Assigning to `employee.jobTitle` throws in strict mode. Apply an action, then fetch again."],[1479,"**Normalized object cache.** Each object, such as `Employee:42`, is stored once. When it changes, every list, link, and detail view that contains it re-renders with the new values."],[6593,"**Number input** (auto-detected): For numeric properties (`double`, `integer`, `long`, `float`, `decimal`, `byte`, `short`)"],[298,"**One runtime.** Several generated SDKs share the same `@osdk/client` code instead of each shipping its own."],[1482,"**Optimistic updates with rollback.** Pass `$optimisticUpdate` to `applyAction` to show the expected result immediately. If the action fails, the cache restores the previous state."],[2796,"**Optimistic updates.** They are removed when the action finishes. See Optimistic updates."],[4920,"**OSDK Component Tokens**: Component-specific semantic tokens"],[6052,"**OSDK layer** (`CbacPicker`, `CbacPickerDialog`) — fetches data using `@osdk/react` hooks, converts it to primitive props, passes to the base layer"],[6943,"**OSDK tokens (`--osdk-*`)** — every visual property used inside OSDK components resolves through a token prefixed with `--osdk-` (e.g. `--osdk-table-header-bg`, `--osdk-form-section-content-padding-inline`). Override these to theme **OSDK components only**, leaving other Blueprint components in your app untouched."],[6856,"**Outline** (`\"outline\"`) — Shows the document's table of contents. If the PDF has embedded bookmarks, those are displayed with their original nesting and bold/italic styling. If no bookmarks exist, headings are automatically extracted from the text content based on font size."],[5921,"**Override at the right level**:"],[5918,"**Override Blueprint tokens** to change the entire design system"],[5917,"**Override OSDK tokens directly** for quick customization"],[6870,"**Page navigation** — previous/next buttons and a page number input"],[6339,"**Persist filter state with `defaultFilterStates`** -- read changes out via `onFilterStateChanged`, key them with the exported `getFilterKey(definition)`, and pass them back through `defaultFilterStates` to rehydrate after navigation. `serializeFilterStates` / `deserializeFilterStates` handle the `Date` round-trip for you"],[1323,"**pnpm.** The plugin runs `maker`, `osdk`, and `tsc` with `pnpm exec`, so pnpm must be on your `PATH` and each binary must be installed in your project."],[1387,"**Primary key.** Must be a primitive type, such as `string` or `integer`, and cannot be `editOnly`. Every object needs a unique value."],[1607,"**Proxy through Vite.** Forward `/api` and `/multipass/api` to Foundry from the dev server, and set `VITE_FOUNDRY_API_URL=http://localhost:8080`. Requests then go to your own origin, so CORS does not apply. See Proxy Foundry requests in development."],[1611,"**Redirect URL.** The redirect URL matches one listed on the same page exactly, including protocol, port, and path, such as `http://localhost:8080/auth/callback`."],[2914,"**Requests and cache.** The devtools wrap the observable client that `OsdkProvider` creates and record the cache reads, network requests, and actions that pass through it. Data you load with raw `fetch`, `axios`, or another state library does not appear."],[6047,"**Required marking groups** — which additional markings must be selected for the classification to be valid"],[797,"**Resolves `@osdk` packages with the `browser`, `require`, and `import` conditions**, so Metro picks their browser builds on every platform."],[1618,"**Resources outside the application's scope.** The object type, action, or function is not included in the application's Ontology SDK resources in Developer Console."],[6872,"**Rotate controls** — rotate all pages left (counter-clockwise) or right (clockwise) in 90° increments"],[6874,"**Search button** — opens the search bar"],[2850,"**Search ontology** matches component names and the object types and actions they use."],[6866,"**Shift+Enter** — previous match"],[1080,"**Ship.** The IR file is the artifact. None of these packages uploads or installs it into a Foundry stack."],[6873,"**Sidebar toggle** — open/close the sidebar panel"],[297,"**Smaller bundles.** Each definition is a small named export. Bundlers drop the ones you do not import, so the SDK's cost scales with what you use, not with the size of the Ontology."],[950,"**Store results in `shallowRef`.** OSDK objects are frozen. Vue does not wrap frozen objects in reactive proxies, so changes are never detected inside them anyway. Replace the whole value when new data arrives."],[6541,"**Supported editor components:**"],[6592,"**Text input** (default): For string properties"],[6855,"**Thumbnails** (`\"thumbnails\"`) — Renders page thumbnails. Click a thumbnail to jump to that page."],[1388,"**Title.** Must be a primitive type, or a struct whose `mainValue` is primitive."],[1613,"**Token provider.** The client receives the OAuth client as its token provider: `createClient(foundryUrl, ontologyRid, auth)`."],[1481,"**Updates after actions.** An action's response lists the objects it added, modified, and deleted. The cache reloads those objects and re-evaluates affected lists against their `where` clauses, with no manual invalidation."],[1009,"**Upgrade them in one command.** Bump the three packages together, and include `@osdk/react-components` if you use it:"],[6342,"**Use `addFilterMode=\"uncontrolled\"` for progressive disclosure** -- start with a few visible filters and let users add more as needed"],[5920,"**Use CSS Layers**: Always import the default tokens into a layer, then add your custom overrides in a higher-priority layer. This ensures your custom theme takes precedence without specificity issues."],[6340,"**Use objectSet constraints to scope filter values** -- pass a prefiltered objectSet (e.g. `client(Employee).where(...)`) so filter dropdowns only show relevant values"],[206,"**Use the devtools.** The Cache panel shows entries, hits, and misses in a running app."],[1619,"**User permissions.** The signed-in user cannot see the data or apply the action. Requests made with a public OAuth client act as the signed-in user and never exceed that user's access."],[6048,"**Validation (`isValid`)** — whether the current selection satisfies all constraints"],[6596,"**Validation**:"],[1324,"**Vite** and a Node.js version that can import `.mts` files natively: 22.18 or later, or 23.6 or later."],[1010,"**Your generated SDK has a peer dependency on `@osdk/client`.** It is set to the client version that generated it, so install an `@osdk/client` that satisfies the SDK's peer range. When you upgrade the client across many versions, generate a new SDK version too."],[6871,"**Zoom controls** — zoom in/out in 25% steps (range: 25%–500%)"],[1097,"`--apiNamespace com.example` prefixes the API names of the object types, interfaces, shared property types, and action types you define, so `Employee` becomes `com.example.Employee`. Pass names without the prefix in your definitions. Link type API names are not prefixed, and value types are prefixed only when you set `namespacePrefix: true`."],[553,"`--ontologyPath` takes an Ontology metadata file written by `--ontologyWritePath`."],[552,"`--ontologyWritePath` saves the loaded metadata so you can regenerate later without signing in."],[442,"`--token <token>`"],[446,"`--token` and `--tokenFile` cannot be used together. The token must be a JWT. Without one, the command exits with `No token found.`"],[443,"`--tokenFile <path>`, a file whose contents are the token"],[214,"`.validation`, not `.message`"],[1576,"`\"<name>\" is not exported by @osdk/client/…/observable.js`"],[6314,"`\"FILTER_LIST_INITIALIZED\"` reports the state seeded from `defaultFilterStates`\nand from each definition's `defaultFilterState`, so the initial clause and\nfiltered `ObjectSet` arrive without waiting for a first interaction. If you only\ncare about the current state and not what caused it, ignore `reason` — every\n`snapshot` carries the full `filterClause` and `filteredObjectSet`:"],[6784,"`\"system\"` is the only mode where the resolved theme can change without anyone calling `setTheme` — it reacts to the OS preference flipping while your app is open."],[3744,"`() => Promise<string>`: resolves to `\"PUBLIC\"`."],[1977,"`@osdk/agents` is for code that runs inside a Foundry agent, not for apps that call one. Foundry injects an Ontology `Client` and a `PlatformClient` into each invocation; `@osdk/agents/experimental` reads them."],[3699,"`@osdk/aip-core`"],[2235,"`@osdk/aip-core` is at version 0.x and its API can change in any minor release. Two limits shape this page:"],[2002,"`@osdk/aip-core` is at version 0.x, and its API can change in any minor release. The current release runs one model call per request: there is no built-in multi-step tool loop, no structured (JSON) output, and only text content parts are sent. Image and file parts are dropped with a warning."],[2001,"`@osdk/aip-core` sends chat completions to the Foundry Language Model Service (LMS) with the same auth, governance, and usage tracking as the rest of your OSDK app. Use `generateText` for a complete answer and `streamText` to render tokens as they arrive."],[710,"`@osdk/api`, `@osdk/client`, and `@osdk/react` are released together with one version number. Install the same version of all three, and keep prereleases together. Your generated SDK has a peer dependency on `@osdk/client`, so generate a new SDK version when you upgrade the client across many versions."],[1596,"`@osdk/api`, `@osdk/client`, and `@osdk/react` share one version number. Install the same version of all three, and keep prereleases together:"],[374,"`@osdk/cli` as a dev dependency."],[423,"`@osdk/cli` deploys your app to Foundry website hosting, manages its versions, publishes widget sets, keeps branched SDKs in sync, and generates SDKs from an Ontology. This page lists every command and flag."],[3697,"`@osdk/client`"],[654,"`@osdk/client` and `@osdk/api` are peer dependencies as well; install them as described in Installation."],[725,"`@osdk/client` changelog"],[2003,"`@osdk/client` is a peer dependency. `@osdk/aip-core` brings in `@osdk/language-models` itself."],[4435,"`@osdk/client` reads and edits your Ontology from any JavaScript runtime with `fetch`: Node.js scripts and servers, serverless functions, and browser apps in any framework. It has no UI dependency. Your generated SDK supplies typed definitions for your object types, interfaces, actions, and functions, and the client runs them."],[813,"`@osdk/client` runs in Node.js without a browser or bundler, so you can query the Ontology and apply actions from scripts, backend services, scheduled jobs, and serverless functions. This page covers what changes outside the browser: authentication, module format, `fetch`, and configuration."],[1006,"`@osdk/client`, `@osdk/api`, and `@osdk/react` are released together and share a version number. `@osdk/react` imports its cache runtime from `@osdk/client/observable`, which is tied to the exact release line, so a mismatch fails at build time even when npm's peer ranges are satisfied."],[557,"`@osdk/foundry-sdk-generator` loads the resources you name from Foundry and writes a compiled npm package with ESM, CommonJS, and bundled type definitions."],[2612,"`@osdk/foundry.admin` reads and manages Foundry users, groups, and markings. Use it to show who is signed in, resolve user IDs to names, check group membership, and list the markings a user can view."],[1950,"`@osdk/foundry.aipagents` is the Platform SDK package for AIP Agents. It works with the `Client` from `createClient` or a `PlatformClient`; see Platform SDK setup."],[2341,"`@osdk/foundry.datasets` reads and writes Foundry datasets. Use it to download a file, export a table as CSV or Arrow, upload files, and group several uploads into one transaction."],[2465,"`@osdk/foundry.mediasets` works with media sets: Foundry collections of images, documents, audio, video, and other files. Use it to upload items to a media set, download them, read their metadata, and convert them with transformations."],[2531,"`@osdk/foundry.ontologies` also contains the raw object, link, action, and query endpoints that the OSDK calls. Prefer the OSDK for those: it adds types, pagination helpers, caching in React, and result conversion."],[2523,"`@osdk/foundry.ontologies` reads the schema of any Ontology at runtime: its object types, properties, link types, action types, and query types. Use it for tools that work across object types you do not know at build time, such as schema browsers, admin pages, and code generators."],[2440,"`@osdk/foundry` re-exports every package as a namespace, such as `Admin` and `Datasets`. Prefer the individual packages: they version independently and keep your bundle small."],[645,"`@osdk/integration-testing` is a `0.x` package and depends on the experimental `--experimentalOntologyMetadata` generator flag. Its API may change between releases."],[644,"`@osdk/integration-testing` starts a local Ontology server from the Foundry CLI, fills it with seed objects and links, and gives you a real `Client` connected to it. Use it to test code that queries objects, filters, and follows links end to end, without a Foundry stack. To test React components with mocks instead, see Testing."],[2112,"`@osdk/language-models` is not superseded: `@osdk/aip-core` depends on it for the proxy URL. Use `@osdk/aip-core` for a provider-neutral API, and `@osdk/language-models` when you want a provider's own SDK."],[2079,"`@osdk/language-models` is the lower-level package `@osdk/aip-core` is built on. It returns Foundry's provider-compatible proxy URLs, so you can point an OpenAI, Anthropic, or Google SDK at Foundry instead of the provider. Use it when you need a provider feature `@osdk/aip-core` does not cover yet, such as the OpenAI Responses API or embeddings."],[1033,"`@osdk/maker-import` turns the metadata of an ontology that already exists in Foundry into TypeScript modules. Import those modules into your `.ontology/ontology.mts` file to link to, implement, or reuse existing types without redefining them."],[1081,"`@osdk/maker` installs a `maker` binary. For local development, also install the Vite plugin; see Local development."],[3698,"`@osdk/oauth`"],[726,"`@osdk/react-components` changelog"],[6051,"`@osdk/react-components` follows the same pattern as `@osdk/react-components`:"],[5925,"`@osdk/react-components` ships built-in dark-theme overrides that activate when `[data-bp-color-scheme=\"dark\"]` is set on an ancestor element (typically `<html>`) — matching Blueprint's own convention so the OSDK + Blueprint tokens flip together. The supported way to set the attribute is `<OsdkThemeProvider>` from `@osdk/react-components/experimental/theme`; see OsdkThemeProvider for the full reference, including `defaultTheme=\"system\"` (the default, follows `prefers-color-scheme`), runtime toggles via `useOsdkTheme`, and controlled mode for integrating with an external theme store."],[711,"`@osdk/react-components`, `@osdk/react-devtools`, and `@osdk/oauth` have their own version numbers. Upgrade them alongside the three core packages. See Version compatibility."],[2890,"`@osdk/react-devtools` adds a panel to your `@osdk/react` app during development. Use it to see which components own OSDK hooks, how often reads hit the cache, and what your app logs to the console."],[2891,"`@osdk/react-devtools` is experimental. Its panels and metrics can change between minor versions."],[978,"`@osdk/react-devtools` ships a Vite plugin that injects an inspection panel into your app during `vite dev` and does nothing in production builds:"],[3696,"`@osdk/react/platform-apis`"],[3695,"`@osdk/react`"],[2169,"`@osdk/react` already depends on `@osdk/aip-core`; install it directly because your code imports `foundryModel` from it. `useChat` does not read from `OsdkProvider`, so it works inside or outside one."],[724,"`@osdk/react` changelog"],[791,"`@osdk/react` does not touch the DOM, so its hooks