ers accept an object instance or its primary key:"],[130,"`applyAction` throws `ActionValidationError` when the parameters fail validation, with the details in `error.validation`. `batchApplyAction` takes an array of parameter objects and applies them in one request."],[4296,"`applyAction` throws `ActionValidationError` when the server ran the action's submission criteria and parameter constraints and they failed. It is not a `PalantirApiError`. Its `validation` field has `result`, `submissionCriteria`, and `parameters`. See Actions for the shape and a message helper."],[838,"`applyAction` throws `ActionValidationError` when validation fails, with details in `error.validation`. Other request failures, such as a missing permission, throw `PalantirApiError` from `@osdk/client`. Catching per object lets the rest of the run continue."],[3995,"`ApplyActionParams<Q>` is the action's parameters plus:"],[4588,"`asyncIter` accepts `$select`, `$orderBy`, `$includeRid`, and `$includeAllBaseObjectProperties`. It requests pages of 10,000 objects and always requests a snapshot."],[835,"`asyncIter` fetches page after page until every matching object has loaded. It reads from a consistent snapshot, so each object arrives once even when data changes during the loop. Page size is chosen by the client; `asyncIter` has no `$pageSize` option."],[4587,"`asyncIter` loads page after page until it has every object in the set, and yields them one at a time:"],[3204,"`autoFetchMore: true` on a large object type can take a long time and hold every object in memory. Prefer a number, or `fetchMore` on demand. For counts, sums, and group-bys, use `useOsdkAggregation` instead of loading objects."],[4760,"`availableModels` + `onModelChange` — render a model picker in the\ncomposer footer."],[4757,"`BaseAipAgentChat` is OSDK-agnostic — the consumer drives the chat by\npassing the current `messages`, `status`, `error`, and an `onSendMessage`\ncallback that resolves once the user's message has been forwarded.\nUse it for non-OSDK backends, custom transports, or unit tests."],[7018,"`BaseTiffViewerProps`"],[7097,"`BaseWorkshopModule` accepts an explicit `branchRid`. When no branch is supplied, it opens on main, including when Workshop previously remembered another branch in the browser session."],[840,"`batchApplyAction` applies an array of parameter objects in one request, which is faster than one request per object. It does not support `$validateOnly`. Send the edits in chunks:"],[4297,"`batchApplyAction` does not throw it. A batch that fails validation rejects with a `PalantirApiError`."],[4186,"`batchApplyAction` takes an array of parameter objects for the same action and applies them in one request:"],[1962,"`blockingContinue` resolves with `agentMarkdownResponse`, `parameterUpdates`, `totalTokensUsed`, `interruptedOutput`, and `sessionTraceId`."],[2378,"`Branches` creates, reads, lists, and deletes dataset branches. A new branch can point at a committed transaction:"],[388,"`branchPlugin()` adds a meta tag to the `<head>` of your HTML:"],[378,"`branchPlugin()` takes no options."],[4445,"`client.fetchMetadata(definition)` loads the definition from Foundry at runtime, such as an object type's `displayName`, `description`, and `icon`, or an interface's `implementedBy`."],[132,"`client.fetchMetadata(definition)` returns runtime metadata, such as display names and descriptions, for an object type, interface, action, or function:"],[4490,"`client.fetchMetadata(Worker)` loads the interface definition from Foundry, including `implementedBy`, the API names of the object types that implement it:"],[4469,"`client(Worker)` is an object set over every object that implements `Worker`. Filter, sort, and select by the interface's property names:"],[3402,"`client` must be a `PlatformClient` from `createPlatformClient`. A string `model` is an LMS model API name, such as `\"gpt-4o\"`. To use a registered model, pass `{ type: \"registeredModel\", registeredModelRid }`."],[3547,"`Client`, a function with one call signature per definition kind, plus `fetchMetadata`."],[4026,"`Client`: the client from `createClient` in `@osdk/client`."],[6407,"`columnName` vs `renderHeader`"],[3760,"`ConfidentialOauthClient`:"],[668,"`create` throws when an object of that type with the same primary key already exists, and when the properties do not match the metadata. A non-primary-key property set to `undefined` is allowed, even when the metadata marks it required, and is left empty."],[73,"`createAuthlessClient()` returns a token provider that sends a fixed public token, for apps that let anyone view data without a Foundry account:"],[79,"`createClient`"],[398,"`createClient` resolves the branch once, when you create the client:"],[825,"`createClient` takes the same arguments in Node as in the browser; see Create a client for every option. Only an explicit `UNSTABLE_DO_NOT_USE_BRANCH` sets the branch in Node, because there is no page URL or meta tag to read it from."],[97,"`createClient` throws `Invalid ontology RID` when `ontologyRid` is a string that does not start with `ri.`."],[1621,"`createClient` throws this when its second argument does not start with `ri.`. The value is often empty, an API name, or a placeholder from an env file. Pass the full Ontology RID, such as `ri.ontology.main.ontology.<uuid>`. Find it on the **Ontology SDK** page of your application in Developer Console, or import `$ontologyRid` from your generated SDK."],[64,"`createConfidentialOauthClient` uses the client credentials grant with a client ID and secret from a confidential application in Developer Console. Requests run as that application's service user, not as a person."],[2086,"`createFetch` replaces the `Authorization` header on each request, so the client keeps working after the token from `getFoundryToken` expires. The proxy accepts each provider's native request format; Foundry's LLM-provider compatible APIs documentation lists the supported endpoints."],[1728,"`create