eateSeedWithMetadata` from `@osdk/seed-helpers` builds seed data without a server, and returns it with whatever your function returns. `create` returns a reference with the object's properties, `$apiName`, and `$primaryKey`; `link` connects two references by link name."],[3165,"`data` is `undefined` until the first page arrives. After that, `isLoading` can be `true` while `data` still holds the previous result, for example while the hook revalidates after an action. Keep rendering `data` during those refreshes instead of replacing the list with a spinner. Loading and errors covers the pattern in depth."],[2697,"`data` is an `ActionEditResponse`: a summary of what the action changed, not a value returned by the action's logic."],[2380,"`Datasets.create` creates an empty dataset in a folder, with a default branch:"],[2344,"`Datasets.get` returns the dataset's `rid`, `name`, and `parentFolderRid`. `Datasets.getSchema` returns its column schema:"],[2345,"`Datasets.getSchema` reads the latest committed version of the default branch. Pass `{ branchName }` or `{ endTransactionRid }` to read another."],[2346,"`Datasets.readTable` exports a tabular dataset as CSV or Apache Arrow and resolves to a `Response`:"],[1430,"`datasources` says where property values come from. Without it, a dataset backs every property. Give an object type one base datasource (`dataset`, `stream`, `restrictedView`, or `direct`) plus any number of `derived` datasources; `defineObject` throws if you list more than one `dataset`, `stream`, or `restrictedView`. Properties not mapped by a `derived` datasource come from the base datasource."],[3906,"`DebouncedCallback<TArgs>`, a function with the same arguments as `callback` and two methods:"],[176,"`dedupeIntervalMs` defaults to `2000` on `useOsdkObjects`, `useObjectSet`, `useLinks`, `useOsdkAggregation`, and `useOsdkFunction`. If two components mount the same query within that window, the second one reuses the first request."],[6763,"`defaultTheme` modes