le refreshes yourself."],[71,"The client requests a new token when the current one expires. There is no refresh token or browser storage. It supports `signIn()`, `signOut()`, `getTokenOrUndefined()`, and `signIn` and `signOut` events, but not `refresh()`."],[2322,"The client retries `429` and `503` responses up to three times before rejecting. Other errors reject immediately."],[4304,"The client retries a request that fails with `429 Too Many Requests` or `503 Service Unavailable`, up to three times, unless the response sets the header `QoS-Retry-Hint: do-not-retry`. The delays grow exponentially from about one second, with random jitter. Other errors, including network failures, are not retried. Your code sees the error only after the last attempt."],[259,"The client retries requests that fail with `429` or `503` up to three times, with exponential backoff, before the error reaches your hook."],[46,"The client starts sign-in on the first request, so pages that load OSDK data trigger it automatically. To keep a route from rendering until the user is signed in, check for a token first. `getTokenOrUndefined()` returns the current access token synchronously, or `undefined` if there is none or it has expired:"],[1983,"The clients exist only while an invocation runs. Call `getClient()` and `getPlatformClient()` inside your handlers, not at module load and not from work that outlives the invocation."],[6328,"The collapse control is available by default and `FilterList` owns the collapsed\nstate, so collapsing works with no wiring at all:"],[387,"The command reads dist tags from your registry, so it needs the same `.npmrc` and `FOUNDRY_TOKEN` as a normal install. A `401` from the registry fails with `Not authorized to read <pkg>`. See Installation."],[437,"The command-line flag."],[230,"The component checks `error` separately from `data`. A refresh can fail after earlier data loaded, so both can be set at once."],[4756,"The component manages model state internally; `onMode