ets ship in a **widget set**, a Foundry resource with a RID such as `ri.widgetregistry..widget-set.<id>`. One project builds one widget set, and each HTML entrypoint in its Vite config becomes one widget in the set. You deploy the set as numbered versions, and the host loads the scripts and stylesheets that the version's manifest lists."],[839,"With `{ $validateOnly: true }`, `applyAction` returns the validation result instead of applying the action. Its `result` is `\"VALID\"` or `\"INVALID\"`."],[4226,"With `$exact: { $includeNullValue: true }`, every `$select` value must be `\"unordered\"`."],[4211,"With `$groupBy`, the result is an array with one entry per group. Each entry has the group's values under `$group`, plus the same metric fields:"],[2766,"With `enabled: false`, the hook does not fetch and returns `data: undefined`, `isLoading: false`, and `error: undefined`. `refetch` does nothing while disabled."],[608,"With `git-describe`, the CLI strips `tagPrefix` from the result, or a leading `v` when there is no prefix. The result depends on where you are relative to the newest tag:"],[3047,"With `useObjectSet`, call `pivotTo` on the object set you pass in. The result is then typed as the linked type, which the hook's own `pivotTo` option does not do:"],[4598,"With a snapshot, every page of a non-stream-backed object type reflects the same point in time, so a completed traversal returns each object exactly once. Paging fails if the snapshot expires or the server detects a paging inconsistency (`PagingInconsistencyDetected`). Stream-backed object types do not keep a snapshot across pages: changes during a traversal can make it fail, and exactly-once traversal is not guaranteed."],[6370,"With a string"],[7121,"With a string"],[6348,"With a URL"],[7039,"With a URL"],[6806,"With a URL, ArrayBuffer, Uint8Array, or Blob"],[1865,"With an empty `tagPrefix`, the build uses the most recent tag reachable from `HEAD` and strips a leading `v`, so `v1.4.0` becomes `1.4.0`. With a prefix such as `widgets/`, it only matches tags that start with the prefix and strips it, so `widgets/1.4.0` becomes `1.4.0`. Commits after the tag and uncommitted changes add a suffix such as `1.4.0-3-g1a2b3c4-dirty`. The build fails if git is missing, the directory is not a repository, or no tag matches."],[6807,"With annotations and sidebar"],[6078,"With MIME type override"],[4745,"With model picker (controlled)"],[4746,"With model picker (uncontrolled)"],[4225,"With more than one `$groupBy` property, every `$select` value must be `\"unordered\"`."],[6774,"With no props the provider follows `prefers-color-scheme` and re-renders when the OS preference changes. To override the OS at runtime, descendants call `setTheme` from `useOsdkTheme`."],[6107,"With OSDK Media"],[6347,"With OSDK Media"],[6369,"With OSDK Media"],[6805,"With OSDK Media"],[6956,"With OSDK Media"],[7015,"With OSDK Media"],[7038,"With OSDK Media"],[7120,"With OSDK Media"],[6957,"With parsed data"],[6108,"With parsed email data"],[7016,"With raw bytes"],[6400,"With Selection"],[6928,"With Tailwind CSS v4"],[6077,"With viewer-specific props"],[1877,"Without `--token` or `--tokenFile`, the CLI reads `FOUNDRY_TOKEN`. The deprecated `FOUNDRY_SDK_AUTH_TOKEN` still works with a warning. The token must be a JWT."],[1191,"Without `--write-locks`, maker fails when an interface has opted in and no lockfile exists, or when the lockfile is out of date."],[4210,"Without `$groupBy`, the result is one object. `$count` is a number, and each property is an object keyed by metric name:"],[122,"Without `$select`, the response includes the type's default properties. Select only what you read. `$pageSize` sizes each page; it does not cap the total."],[3193,"Without `$select`, the server returns its default property set for each object. Pass `$select` with only the properties the component reads; the primary key is always included."],[4603,"Without `$select`, the server returns its default property set for the object