he provider."],[5975,"Wrapping your app with `OsdkProvider`"],[6166,"Wrapping your app with `OsdkProvider`"],[6468,"Wrapping your app with `OsdkProvider`"],[1905,"Wraps `children` in an error boundary. An uncaught render error shows its stack trace, plus troubleshooting tips when `NODE_ENV` is not `production`. Add your own error boundary inside `FoundryWidget` to show a custom message instead."],[3809,"Wraps your app so `@osdk/react` hooks can reach the client. The provider builds an `ObservableClient` from `client`, which holds the shared cache, and rebuilds it whenever `client` changes."],[633,"Write a test"],[1067,"Write an ontology"],[4909,"XML Viewer"],[7116,"XmlViewer"],[7117,"XmlViewer displays XML from an OSDK Media object, or a string you provide, in a styled monospace <pre><code> block."],[7124,"XmlViewerProps"],[713,"Yes, with `@osdk/client` and a confidential OAuth client. `createConfidentialOauthClient` from `@osdk/oauth` uses the client credentials grant, so requests act as the application's service user, not a signed-in person:"],[708,"Yes. `@osdk/client` has no UI dependency and works in any browser or JavaScript runtime with `fetch`. Create a client with `createClient` and call `client(Employee).fetchPage()`, `client(modifyEmployee).applyAction()`, and so on. See Use the client without React."],[715,"Yes. `@osdk/create-app` has React, Vue, and Expo templates, plus a React template for public apps without sign-in. Choose one at the prompt, or pass it directly:"],[2975,"you call `refetch`, or invalidate it through the observable client (see Invalidate the cache),"],[221,"You call `refetch`, or something invalidates the entry."],[2725,"You can also apply an action with the `Client` from `useOsdkClient`. This bypasses the cache: components do not update until you invalidate the affected data yourself (see Invalidate the cache). Prefer `useOsdkAction` in components."],[6708,"You can also attach custom `data-*` attributes per row with the `getRowAttributes` prop — see Row Attributes and Conditional Row Styling."],[3178,"You can also filter on `$primaryKey`, for example `{ $primaryKey: { $in: [101, 102] } }`, without knowing the name of the primary key property."],[1478,"You can call `@osdk/client` from any data layer, including TanStack Query. `@osdk/react` adds behavior that a generic request cache cannot reproduce because it understands Ontology objects:"],[6578,"You can filter by object properties and derived properties by including them in the `WhereClause`:"],[621,"You cannot delete the live version. To take the site offline, clear the live version with `osdk site version unset`; the site is unreachable until you set one again."],[4157,"You cannot set both on one call; the types reject it."],[3087,"You combined sets with `union`, `intersect`, or `subtract`."],[2896,"You do not add any JSX. During `vite dev`, the plugin injects two scripts into `index.html`: one that installs a React Fiber hook, and one that imports the panel:"],[2794,"You do not need to invalidate after:"],[1722,"You do not need to publish a widget set before developing on it. To place the widget in a Workshop module, publish a version once so the widget appears in Workshop's **Widget setup** panel. See Build and publish."],[1595,"You might also see the same error for `unstable-do-not-use.js` or a path in `@osdk/api`. `@osdk/react` imports its runtime from `@osdk/client/observable`, and your installed `@osdk/client` or `@osdk/api` comes from a different release than your `@osdk/react`."],[461,"You must pass `--version` or `--autoVersion`, or set `site.autoVersion` in `foundry.config.json`. When the deploy succeeds, the CLI prints the live URL, `https://<subdomain>`. With `--uploadOnly`, it prints `https://<subdomain>/.system/preview?previewVersion=<version>` instead."],[1503,"You need Node.js and an application in Foundry Developer Console. The CLI asks for these values, so collect them first:"],[1459,"You pick the Ontology resources your app 